#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Kidnapped">
#. <location>enter</location>
#. <chance>15</chance>
#. <cond>
#. if player.misnDone("Kidnapped") or player.misnActive("Kidnapped") then
#. return false
#. end
#. if system.cur() ~= system.get("Arcturus") then
#. return false
#. end
#. local misn_test = require "misn_test"
#. if not misn_test.mercenary(true) then
#. return false
#. end
#. return misn_test.reweight_active()
#. </cond>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Kidnapping</campaign>
#. <tier>3</tier>
#. </notes>
#. </event>
#. --
#.
#. Event for kidnapped mission.
#. --
#. Non-persistent state
#. Create Mom and Dad in their spaceship, and have them come from the planet Brooks in Arcturus system, following the player.
#. Test for claim here
#. Pa and Ma are hailing the player!
#. Pa and Ma have been hailed. The mission can begin, and panma should land on the planet Brooks
msgid ""
"\"Hello {player}, thank you so much for answering our hail! We really could "
"use your help,\" says a haggard sounding man over the comm. \"It's about our "
"children, my wife's and mine. We were out on a family vacation to Antica, "
"you see, and we were attacked by a gang of pirates…\"\n"
"\"And he thought he could out-fly them,\" a woman's voice pipes up. \"My "
"husband used to be a bit of a pilot, but that was back when we were still "
"dating. He would fly all the way to the Apez system to see me! Before we had "
"children…\" The woman trails off."
msgstr ""
"\"Hola {player}, ¡muchas gracias por responder a nuestra llamada! Nos "
"vendría muy bien tu ayuda\", dice un hombre que suena cansado a través del "
"comunicador. \"Es sobre nuestros hijos, los de mi mujer y los míos. "
"Estábamos de vacaciones familiares en Antica, y fuimos atacados por una "
"banda de piratas...\"\n"
"\"Y el pensó que podía dejarlos atras\", se oye una voz de mujer. \"Mi "
"marido solía pilotar naves, pero eso era cuando éramos novios. ¡Volaba todo "
"el camino hasta el sistema Apez para verme! Claro que eso era antes de tener "
"hijos...\" Su voz se va apagando."

msgid ""
"The man quickly speaks up again. \"The pirates disabled our ship and we "
"thought we were goners, but when they boarded us, they took our three "
"children and left us! I tried to fight them, but they had my children with "
"knives to their necks… what was I supposed to do? So we got a tow back to "
"Brooks, but now we need to find someone who will rescue our children. We've "
"heard of your skills; will you please help us?\""
msgstr ""
"El hombre se apresura a hablar de nuevo. \"Los piratas incapacitaron nuestra "
"nave y pensamos que ibamos a morir, pero cuando nos abordaron solo se "
"llevaron a nuestros tres hijos y nos abandonaron. Intenté luchar contra "
"ellos, pero tenían a mis hijos con cuchillos en el cuello… ¿qué se suponia "
"que debía hacer? Al final conseguimos un remolque de vuelta a Brooks, pero "
"ahora necesitamos encontrar a alguien que rescate a nuestros hijos. Hemos "
"oído hablar de tus habilidades; ¿podrías ayudarnos?\""

msgid "Rescue those children!"
msgstr "¡Rescatar a los niños!"

msgid "Politely refuse"
msgstr "Negarse educadamente"

msgid ""
"You can hear that the the man is quite disappointed. \"I'm sure you have a "
"good reason to not want to help us. Perhaps you have something else more "
"pressing…\" Before the comm is cut you can hear the woman beginning to sob "
"and the man consoling her."
msgstr ""
"Se puede oír que el hombre está bastante decepcionado. \"Estoy seguro de que "
"tienes una buena razón para no querer ayudarnos. Quizás tengas algo más "
"urgente…\" Antes de que se corte la comunicación, se oye a la mujer empezar "
"a sollozar y al hombre consolarla."

msgid ""
"The two parents immediately begin thanking you quite profusely, spending a "
"few hectostu simply telling you how much they truly appreciate your "
"assistance. After a while, you realize that if these children are going to "
"be rescued this cycle, you are going to need to get started sooner rather "
"than later. \"Yes, quite right,\" the father replies. \"No need to delay any "
"longer than absolutely necessary. I don't know a whole lot, but you should "
"be able to eavesdrop on some pirates at a bar. The bar on {pnt} in the {sys} "
"system has been known to serve pirates occasionally, so stopping there would "
"be a good course of action. We will anticipate your return. Again, this "
"means so much to us.\" Before you know it, the two parents are at it again, "
"thanking you like it's all they know how to do. Before it gets really bad, "
"you bid farewell, break communication, and get on your way."
msgstr ""

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Levo Pirates">
#. <unique/>
#. <location>load</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. </event>
#. --
#.
#. Save Levo!
#.
#. Creates a small blockade of pirates in the Levo system. The player has to
#. clear them to be able to land.
#.
#. This is triggered on "load" to be able to claim the system so that other
#. missions don't mess with it. Furthermore, the spob is set as restricted to
#. avoid having missions go to it, but it gets cleared when the event is
#. finished.
#. --
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Levo Pirates Epilogue">
#. <unique/>
#. <location>land</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <spob>Levo</spob>
#. <cond>player.evtDone("Levo Pirates")</cond>
#. </event>
#. --
#.
#. Epilogue for saving Levo.
#. --
msgid "Red Goatee"
msgstr "Perilla Roja"

msgid ""
"\"You aren't with the pirates are you?\"\n"
"After a quick confirmation they continue.\n"
"\"Help us! Some pirate called '{pirate}' is trying to dominate us!\""
msgstr ""
"\"No estás con los piratas, ¿verdad?\"\n"
"Tras una rápida confirmación continúan.\n"
"\"¡Ayudanos! ¡Un pirata llamado '{pirate}' está intentando dominarnos!\""

msgid "\"Please clear out marauders in the system and we'll let you land!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Por favor, elimina a los merodeadores del sistema y te dejaremos "
"aterrizar!\""

msgid ""
"The communication abruptly cuts off. It seems like they could use your help."
msgstr ""
"La comunicación se corta bruscamente. Parece que les vendría bien tu ayuda."

msgid "Levo Citizen"
msgstr "Ciudadano Levo"

msgid "Brave Pilot Breaks Levo Blockade"
msgstr "Piloto Valiente Rompe el Bloqueo de Levo"

msgid ""
"A brave pilot known as the 'Saviour of Levo' has broken a failed pirate "
"blockade in the system of Levo. Local authorities praise the hero who "
"stepped in when nobody else would."
msgstr ""
"Un valiente piloto conocido como el \"Salvador de Levo\" ha roto un bloqueo "
"pirata fallido en el sistema Levo. Las autoridades locales elogian al héroe "
"que intervino cuando nadie más lo hacía."

msgid "Marauders Out of Control?"
msgstr "Merodeadores, ¿fuera de control?"

msgid ""
"Marauder '{pirate}' was defeated after attempting to dominate the {sys} "
"system. Local pirate warlords express anger at such rashness which can lead "
"to more patrols in nearby systems. \"Dominating in this day and age? Gotta "
"get with the times!\" says Captain of the Pink Demon."
msgstr ""
"El merodeador '{pirate}' fue derrotado tras intentar dominar el sistema "
"{sys}. Los caudillos piratas locales expresan su enfado ante tal temeridad, "
"lo que puede provocar más patrullas en los sistemas cercanos. \"¿Dominar en "
"estos tiempos? Hay que adaptarse a los tiempos\", dice el capitán del "
"Demonio Rosa."

msgid "You land and quickly find yourself surrounded by ecstatic locals."
msgstr "Aterrizas y rápidamente te encuentras rodeado de lugareños extasiados."

msgid ""
"A more distinguished individual comes out to shake your hand.\n"
"\"Thanks you for saving us!\""
msgstr ""
"Un individuo más distinguido sale a estrecharle la mano.\n"
"\"¡Gracias por salvarnos!\""

msgid ""
"\"We usually don't see any weird stuff here in {spb}, so we were just "
"minding our business when some pirate called {pirate} hailed us and told us "
"they were going to dominate us!\""
msgstr ""
"\"No solemos ver cosas raras aquí en {spb}, así que estábamos ocupándonos de "
"nuestros asuntos cuando un pirata llamado {pirate} ¡nos llamó y nos dijo que "
"iban a dominarnos!\""

msgid ""
"\"I have no idea how they managed to get here without being eliminated by "
"Imperial or Soromid forces. Bunch of useless lots they are, the Great Houses."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"No tengo ni idea de cómo se las arreglaron para llegar hasta aquí sin ser "
"eliminados por las fuerzas del Imperio o los Soromida. Un montón de inútiles "
"son, las Grandes Casas.\""

msgid ""
"\"We've been stuck like this for almost 2 cycles until you came along. I "
"can't believe how lawless the Galaxy has become. Back in the day we didn't "
"have so many ruffians with delusions of grandeur flying around.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hemos estado atrapados así durante casi 2 ciclos hasta que llegaste tú. No "
"puedo creer lo anárquica que se ha vuelto la Galaxia. Antes no había tantos "
"rufianes con delirios de grandeza volando por ahí.\""

msgid ""
"\"At {spb}, we let no good dead go unrewarded. Here, take some credits for "
"your troubles\""
msgstr ""
"\"En {spb}, no dejamos ningún buen muerto sin recompensa. Toma, coge algunos "
"créditos por las molestias\""

msgid ""
"\"Say, it's not much, but as the saviour of {spb}, we would love to host a "
"small banquet in your honour.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oye, no es mucho, pero como salvador de {spb}, nos encantaría ofrecerte un "
"pequeño banquete en tu honor.\""

msgid "Accept the invitation."
msgstr "Aceptas la invitación."

msgid "Decline to join in."
msgstr "Declinas la invitación."

msgid ""
"You join in a short celebration which features a great assortment of local "
"fish cuisine and lagers. It is quite enjoyable, and once it's done you get "
"back on your way."
msgstr ""
"Te unes a una breve celebración en la que se ofrece un gran surtido de "
"platos locales de pescado y cervezas rubias. Es bastante agradable, y una "
"vez terminada vuelves a ponerte en camino."

msgid "You politely decline and go on your way."
msgstr "Te niegas cortésmente y sigues tu camino."

#. Add some news
msgid ""
"You helped clear a pirate blockade at the {sys} system. The locals were very "
"grateful for your help."
msgstr ""
"Ayudaste a despejar un bloqueo pirata en el sistema {sys}. Los lugareños "
"estaban muy agradecidos por tu ayuda."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Majesteka Stowaways Aboard">
#. <location>land</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <spob>Majesteka II</spob>
#. <unique />
#. </event>
#. --
#.
#. Some kids sneak onto your ship if you land on Majesteka II.
#. --
msgid ""
"You are flying around, minding your own business when suddenly, {shipai} "
"materializes in front of you."
msgstr ""
"Estás ocupándote de tus asuntos cuando, de repente, {shipai} se materializa "
"en frente de tí."

msgid ""
"For some reason, they are speaking in a very low volume, almost as if "
"whispering.\n"
"\"{playername}, it seems that we have a situation aboard the ship.\""
msgstr ""
"Por alguna razón, está hablando en un volumen muy bajo, casi como si "
"susurrara.\n"
"\"{playername}, parece que tenemos una situación a bordo de la nave.\""

msgid "\"What is it?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué es eso?\""

msgid "\"Did you have another 'accident' with ship oil?\""
msgstr "\" ¿Tuviste otro \"accidente\" con aceite de nave?\""

msgid ""
"\"Wait, how did you kn…?!?\"\n"
"They quickly change the topic.\n"
"\"About the situation aboard the ship.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Espera, ¿cómo supiste...?\"\n"
"Rápidamente cambia de tema.\n"
"\"Sobre la situación a bordo de la nave.\""

msgid ""
"\"I have detected alien lifeforms in the cargo holds! These are completely "
"unrelated to the fungus growing in the spoiled food rations. You should go "
"investigate!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡He detectado formas de vida alienígena en las bodegas de carga! No tienen "
"nada que ver con los hongos que crecen en las raciones de comida "
"estropeadas. ¡Deberías ir a investigar!\""

msgid ""
"You begrudgingly go to investigate the cargo holds. As you are about to open "
"the door, you hear some weird noises. Seems like {ainame} was right this "
"time."
msgstr ""
"A regañadientes, vas a investigar las bodegas de carga. Cuando estás a punto "
"de abrir la puerta, oyes unos ruidos extraños. Parece que {ainame} tenía "
"razón esta vez."

msgid "Ask who is there"
msgstr "Preguntar quién está ahí"

msgid "Walk in casually"
msgstr "Andar como si nada"

msgid "Draw your weapon and barge in"
msgstr "Desenfundar tu arma y entrar"

msgid ""
"You ask if anybody is there, but don't get any response. It is probably best "
"to go in and check."
msgstr ""
"Pregunta si hay alguien, pero no obtienes respuesta. Probablemente lo mejor "
"sea entrar y comprobarlo."

msgid ""
"You walk in casually and turn on the lights to see what is going on. A quick "
"inspection doesn't turn up anything. You turn around to leave the ship when "
"suddenly something jumps on your back!"
msgstr ""
"Entras despreocupadamente y enciendes las luces para ver qué pasa. Una "
"rápida inspección no revela nada. Te das la vuelta para abandonar la nave "
"cuando, de repente, ¡algo salta sobre tu espalda!"

msgid ""
"You fumble around and slam your back into a wall and it drops off with a "
"resounding thud. Another unknown object jumps onto your leg and you manage "
"to kick it off!"
msgstr ""
"Andas a tientas y te golpeas la espalda contra una pared, cayendo lo que sea "
"con un ruido sordo. ¡ otro objeto desconocido salta sobre tu pierna y "
"consigues apartarlo de una patada!"

msgid ""
"You recompose yourself and look around and find two small kids unconscious "
"on the floor. They look really dirty and are covered in rags. When did they "
"get on your ship?"
msgstr ""
"Te recompones y miras a tu alrededor y encuentras a dos niños pequeños "
"inconscientes en el suelo. Parecen muy sucios y están cubiertos de harapos. "
"¿Cuándo llegaron a tu nave?"

msgid ""
"Seeing as they don't seem like much of a threat, you get some water and "
"splash it on their faces to wake them up. They slowly wake up and "
"immediately run and try to hide in a corner. You slowly calm them down and "
"coax them to tell you what is going on."
msgstr ""
"Como no parecen una gran amenaza, coges un poco de agua y se la echas en la "
"cara para despertarlos. Se despiertan lentamente e inmediatamente corren a "
"esconderse en un rincón. Poco a poco, los calmas y los convences para que te "
"cuenten lo que esta pasando."

msgid ""
"You barge in with your weapon drawn, ready to shoot whatever sort of space "
"monster awaiting you. You catch a quick motion in the corner of the eye and "
"shoot a low power warning shot. Suddenly, you hear what appears to be "
"sobbing."
msgstr ""
"Irrumpes con el arma desenfundada, listo para disparar a cualquier tipo de "
"monstruo espacial que te aguarde. Captas un rápido movimiento con el rabillo "
"del ojo y disparas un tiro de advertencia de baja potencia. De repente, oyes "
"lo que parecen ser sollozos."

msgid ""
"You carefully approach with your weapon still in hand and find yourself face "
"to face with two small kids covered in rags. One is bawling their heart out "
"while the other is hugging them trying to calm them down. They look at your "
"fearfully."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas cuidadosamente con el arma en la mano y te encuentras cara a cara "
"con dos niños pequeños cubiertos de harapos. Uno llora a gritos y el otro lo "
"abraza para intentar calmarlo. Te miran con miedo."

msgid ""
"Seeing that they don't seem like much of a threat, you lower your weapon and "
"try to calm them down. Once they are not panicked anymore, you coax them to "
"tell you what is going on."
msgstr ""
"Al ver que no representan una gran amenaza, bajas el arma e intentas "
"calmarlos. Una vez que ya no están aterrorizados, les convences para que te "
"cuenten lo que ocurre."

msgid ""
"It seems like they are a pair of orphans from {spob} who stowed away in the "
"cargo hold while you were landed. They don't really have anywhere to go and "
"don't want to end up like their parent and wanted to at least try to get "
"away from there for a better life."
msgstr ""
"Parece que son un par de huérfanos de {spob} que viajaron de polizones en la "
"bodega de carga mientras tú desembarcabas. En realidad no tienen adonde ir y "
"no quieren acabar como sus padres y querían al menos intentar alejarse de "
"allí para tener una vida mejor."

msgid ""
"Seeing that your ship is no place to raise a couple of orphans, you have to "
"make a decision of what to do with them."
msgstr ""
"Viendo que tu nave no es lugar para criar a un par de huérfanos, tienes que "
"tomar una decisión sobre qué hacer con ellos."

msgid "Try to find a good place for them"
msgstr "Intentar encontrar un buen lugar para ellos"

msgid "Drop them off on the nearest planet"
msgstr "Dejarlos en el planeta más cercano"

#. {_([[Dump them out the airlock]]), "03_airlock"},
msgid ""
"You decide to drop them off next time you land to get rid of the problem as "
"soon as possible. At the end of the day, you are not here to supervise "
"orphans, and any place will be a better future for them."
msgstr ""
"Decides dejarlos la siguiente vez que aterrices para deshacerte del problema "
"lo antes posible. A fin de cuentas, no estás aquí para supervisar huérfanos, "
"y cualquier lugar será un futuro mejor para ellos."

msgid ""
"You decide to take the orphans to a better place and give them a promising "
"future. However, first things first, you decide to wash them down and give "
"them some of your old clothes. Last thing you want to get is an infestation "
"of space lice."
msgstr ""
"Decides llevar a los huérfanos a un lugar mejor y darles un futuro "
"prometedor. Sin embargo, lo primero es lo primero: decides lavarlos y "
"cederles algo de tu ropa vieja. Lo último que quieres es una infestación de "
"piojos espaciales."

msgid ""
"Once you get hygiene out of the way, you give them some drawing utensils to "
"keep them distracted while you fly them to a better home."
msgstr ""
"Una vez eliminada esta cuestión del higiene, les das algunos utensilios de "
"dibujo para que se distraigan mientras los llevas volando a un hogar mejor."

msgid ""
"You land again on {spob} to drop off the orphans at their home world. You "
"figure it is the environment that they grew up in and are most accustomed "
"to, and will probably be best for them."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas de nuevo en {spob} para dejar a los huérfanos en su mundo natal. "
"Crees que es el entorno en el que han crecido y al que están más "
"acostumbrados, y que probablemente será lo mejor para ellos."

msgid ""
"The orphans become quiet and sad when they realize they are back to where "
"they came from. However, knowing their battle to be lost they get off your "
"ship and disappear into the grimy darkness."
msgstr ""
"Los huérfanos se quedan callados y tristes cuando se dan cuenta de que han "
"vuelto al lugar de donde vinieron. Sin embargo, sabiendo que su batalla está "
"perdida, bajan de tu nave y desaparecen en la mugrienta oscuridad."

msgid ""
"With the orphans out of the way, you can now get back to your adventures, "
"however, you have a small nagging feeling that maybe that was not the best "
"for the orphans."
msgstr ""
"Con los huérfanos fuera de tu camino, ahora puedes volver a tus aventuras, "
"sin embargo, tienes una pequeña sensación persistente de que tal vez eso no "
"fue lo mejor para los huérfanos."

msgid "You returned a pair of stowaway orphans to their home planet of {spob}."
msgstr ""
"Has devuelto a un par de huérfanos polizones a su planeta natal en {spob}."

msgid ""
"You land and promptly get the orphans off your ship. Being their first times "
"they are off their home world they are in amaze at all the things out there. "
"With a boundless sense of wonder and curiosity, they disappear. At least "
"they made it away from {spob}."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas y enseguida sacas a los huérfanos de tu nave. Al ser la primera "
"vez que salen de su mundo natal, se quedan asombrados de todo lo que hay ahí "
"fuera. Con un ilimitado sentido de la maravilla y la curiosidad, "
"desaparecen. Al menos lograron alejarse de {spob}."

msgid ""
"You took a pair of stowaway orphans from {spob} to {curspob} in the {cursys}."
msgstr ""
"Llevaste un par de huérfanos polizones de {spob} a {curspob} en el {cursys}."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="P-1587 Dragon Awake">
#. <location>load</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <cond>player.evtDone("P-1587 Dragon Intro")</cond>
#. <unique />
#. </event>
#. --
msgid "Haze Leviathan"
msgstr ""

#. So plasma burst gets used
#. Make more dragon-y
#. The scales have 20 absorb over S&K war plating
#. Keep your distance if you wanna live
#. I assume some of the trinkets it's covered in have a scrambling/jamming effect
#. To make up for the cooldown_mod
#. To make stealth bombing slightly harder
#. The faster you take it down, the shorter the volley in phase 2 will be
#. If player is in a small ship then something fishy is going on (stealth bomber?) and phase 2 is hardened against stealth bombers, so trigger it earlier)
#. Clear debuffs and jam lockons to live a bit longer
#. Basically no more armour regen
#. But what remains of the armour will be putting up a fight
#. Volley of hellfire be upon ye
#. Dodging it is an option though!
#. ~3/4 chance for Imperators to be jammed
#. So in a proper fight the shield regen boost won't do much, but if you're a stealth bomber, then uh oh
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="P-1587 Dragon Epilogue">
#. <location>land</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <spob>P-1587</spob>
#. <cond>player.evtDone("P-1587 Dragon Awake")</cond>
#. <unique />
#. </event>
#. --
msgid ""
"You return to where the pile of {goods} lays scattered and damaged over the "
"planetary surface. Looks like you won't be able to recover any."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You give the area one last scan before giving up, which, lo and behold, "
"seems to bring up something other than damaged goods. It has an odd shape, "
"almost like an egg! Could this be?!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You race to get a closer look at the object, however, it seems to be "
"exfoliated scales from the feral bioship that inhabited the mountain of "
"luxury goods. Taking a closer look at them, they seem like they could be "
"useful as makeshift armour on your ships."
msgstr ""

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="P-1587 Dragon Intro">
#. <location>land</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <spob>P-1587</spob>
#. <unique />
#. </event>
#. --
#. Very low chance
#. We have to claim with the next event, inclusive should be fine
msgid ""
"As you perform a premilinary scan of {spb}, it seems as there's a large "
"abnormality on the planet's surface. Upon further inspection, it's a large "
"pile of {goods}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A secondary scan confirms that your eyes aren't deceiving you, and there "
"seems to be a lot of {goods} just abandoned on the surface. The amount is "
"utterly ridiculous, and it seems it won't fit all in your ship, but you can "
"try to take as much as you want.\n"
"\n"
"What do you do?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You return to the pile of {goods}, as impressive as ever.\n"
"\n"
"What do you want to do?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Take {goods}"
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave it alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "Leave it alone. (No free space)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Shoot at the pile."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some things are best not trifled with. You decide to leave the pile alone "
"and take your leave."
msgstr ""

msgid "Take how much?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Take how many tonnes of {goods}?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You load up on {amount} of {goods}. Seems like there's still plenty left."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You are loading the {goods} when you hear a large rumble. Wait, the mountain "
"of {goods} is moving!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You make a mad dash to your ships and scramble to your cockpit as the floor "
"seems to collapse under you."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The moment your ship's weapon systems lock on the pile, the ground starts to "
"shake. {spb} shouldn't have siesmic activity."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you try to process the situation, there's an explosion of {goods}, which "
"are now falling like rain. Seems like it's your call to get out of here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You slam down on your thrusters and quickly leave {spb} behind, only for "
"your ship's sensors to indicate you are being followed. What the hell is "
"that?"
msgstr ""

#. Will be marked as finished if awoken
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Quai Pirates">
#. <unique/>
#. <location>load</location>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. </event>
#. --
#.
#. Small blockade of pirates in the Quai system that persist until
#. eliminated
#. --
msgid "Brunette Goatee"
msgstr "Perilla Morena"

msgid "\"You look far away from home, kitten.\""
msgstr "\"Pareces muy lejos de casa, gatita\""

msgid ""
"You're not sure what they mean by kitten, but you notice something weird on "
"their face. What is up with that goatee?"
msgstr ""
"No estás seguro de lo que quieren decir con gatito, pero notas algo raro en "
"su cara. ¿Qué pasa con esa perilla?"

msgid ""
"\"You see, you're in {pirate} territory now. Pay {creds} or we'll turn you "
"to scrap metal and sell your parts!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Verás, ahora estás en territorio {pirate}. ¡Paga {creds} o te "
"convertiremos en chatarra y venderemos tus partes!\""

msgid "\"Wait, I thought I was in Sirius space?\""
msgstr "\"Espera, ¿pensaba que estaba en el espacio Sirio?\""

msgid "\"Wait, did you paint the goatee on your face?\""
msgstr "\"Espera, ¿te has pintado una perilla en la cara?\""

msgid "\"Hey, I'm just passing by, I mean no trouble.\""
msgstr "\"Eh, sólo pasaba por aquí, no quiero problemas.\""

msgid "\"You threaten a fellow pirate?\""
msgstr "\"¿Amenazaste a un compañero pirata?\""

msgid ""
"\"You made the right choice. Enjoy your stay but you'll have to repay on "
"reentry!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Has tomado la decisión correcta. ¡Disfruta de tu estancia, pero tendrás "
"que pagar al volver!\""

msgid ""
"\"Sirius? They have their heads to stuck up in their collective asses and "
"can't deal with our raw firepower. You're in {pirate} space now!\""
msgstr ""
"¿\" Sirio \"? Tienen la cabeza demasiado metida en el culo y no pueden hacer "
"frente a nuestra potencia de fuego. ¡Ahora estás en espacio {pirate}!\""

msgid ""
"\"Think of this as a mutual business agreement. Nothing wrong about business "
"between friends?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Piensa en esto como un acuerdo de negocios mutuo. ¿No hay nada malo en los "
"negocios entre amigos?\""

msgid "\"You may mean no trouble, but I sure as hell do. Now pay up!\""
msgstr "\"Puede que no quieras causar problemas, pero yo sí. ¡Ahora paga!\""

msgid ""
"They suddenly get flustered and when they speak again they seem to forcibly "
"lower their voice.\n"
"\"Wha... what are you insinuating? That I don't live up to my name with my "
"fabulous brunette goatee?!\""
msgstr ""
"De repente se ponen nerviosos y cuando vuelven a hablar parecen bajar la voz "
"a la fuerza.\n"
"\"¿Qué... qué estás insinuando? ¡¿Que no hago honor a mi nombre con mi "
"fabulosa perilla morena?!\""

msgid ""
"Looking closely, it's clear that it is drawn on. Seems to be something like "
"crayon?"
msgstr ""
"Mirándolo de cerca, está claro que está dibujado. ¿Parece ser algo como "
"crayón?"

msgid "Crayon Goatee"
msgstr "Perilla de Crayón"

#. Much more aggressive
msgid "\"Brunette Goatee? More like Crayon Goatee!\""
msgstr "\"¿Perilla morena? ¡Más bien Perilla de Crayón!\""

msgid ""
"Blood swells to their face like a ripened tomato, making the crayon goatee "
"even more obvious."
msgstr ""
"La sangre se le hincha en su cara como un tomate maduro, haciendo aún más "
"evidente la perilla de crayón."

msgid ""
"\"Get him! The bastard is not getting out alive. I want their head as my "
"table stand!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Atrápadlo! El bastardo no sale vivo de aquí. ¡Quiero su cabeza como "
"pisapapeles en mi mesa!\""

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Refuel">
#. <location>none</location>
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. </event>
#. --
#. Time between spam in seconds
#, fuzzy
msgid "Come fast, I'm under attack!"
msgstr "¡Estamos bajo ataque!"

#. Took too much damage
#, fuzzy
msgid "Under attack! I'm outta here."
msgstr "¡Bajo ataque! ¡Solicito apoyo!"

#. Nice work
#, fuzzy
msgid "Thanks a bunch!"
msgstr "¡Gracias!"

#. Reward time
msgid "You receive {reward} for {fuel} u of fuel."
msgstr ""

#. Done, time to go away
#. Stop refuelling again
#. We don't reset the vulnerability so it's more likely they get away and we
#. have a happy ending
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <event name="Shadowcomm">
#. <location>enter</location>
#. <chance>3</chance>
#. <cond>system.cur():presence("hostile") &lt; 60 and player.misnDone("Shadowrun") and not (player.misnDone("Shadow Vigil") or player.misnActive("Shadow Vigil")) and not (system.cur() == system.get("Pas")) and system.cur():presence("Independent") &gt; 20</cond>
#. <notes>
#. <done_misn name="Shadowrun"/>
