msgid ""
"The night sky always draws our eyes. People look up with a question, or in "
"wonder, and sometimes with a dream: to venture forth among the stars."
msgstr ""
"El cielo nocturno siempre atrae nuestras miradas. La gente mira hacia arriba "
"con preguntas, asombrados, y a veces con sueños: aventurarse entre las "
"estrellas."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From Earth, the first spacefarers spied tiny jewels shining with the light "
"of distant suns, far away but so clear. To reach out and grasp one would "
"only cost a lifetime. Cheap at the price."
msgstr ""
"Desde la Tierra, los primeros viajeros espaciales divisaron pequeñas joyas "
"que brillaban con la luz de soles distantes, muy alejados pero tan nítidos. "
"Alcanzar una y aferrarla sólo costaría una vida. Barato para su precio."

msgid ""
"So men and women locked their sleeping bodies into hulking metal boxes. They "
"hurled themselves out into the void. On arrival, they decanted and woke to "
"find new stars staring coldly down from stranger skies."
msgstr ""
"Por ello, hombres y mujeres encerraron sus cuerpos dormidos en enormes cajas "
"de metal. Se lanzaron al vacío. Y al llegar, se decantaron y se despertaron "
"para encontrar nuevas estrellas mirándoles fríamente desde cielos más "
"extraños."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The first wave of explorers crept from star to star at sub-light speeds, "
"until the invention of the hyperspace drive spurred a second growth. Then "
"civilization spread, as it always has, with exponential enthusiasm -- "
"ripples in the dark sea of space."
msgstr ""
"La primera oleada de exploradores se arrastró de estrella en estrella a "
"velocidades sublumínicas, hasta que la invención del motor hiperespacial "
"impulsó un segundo crecimiento. En ese momento la civilización se extendió, "
"como siempre lo ha hecho, con un entusiasmo exponencial, ondas a través del "
"oscuro mar del espacio."

msgid ""
"However, the heroic age of discovery lasted only as long as human curiosity "
"outpaced greed. Too soon, conflict erupted on the colonies. Land, fuel, "
"food, and distrust sowed the seeds of discord. Once begun, the fever of war "
"spread from world to world and became a holocaust."
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, la época heroica de los descubrimientos sólo duró el tiempo que "
"la curiosidad humana superó a la codicia. Rápidamente estalló el conflicto "
"en las colonias. La tierra, el combustible, los alimentos y la desconfianza "
"sembraron las semillas de la discordia. Una vez comenzada, la fiebre de la "
"guerra se expandió de mundo en mundo y se convirtió en un holocausto."

msgid ""
"After a hundred years of interstellar conflict, on the ashes that remained, "
"at last a new order built its foundations."
msgstr ""
"Tras cien años de conflicto interestelar, sobre las cenizas que "
"permanecieron, finalmente una nueva orden construyó sus cimientos."

msgid ""
"A man named Daedris asserted dominion over the exhausted worlds. He founded "
"a Galactic Empire and named himself its ruler. Under the iron fist of his "
"military, relations between planets resumed; abandoned trade routes saw "
"traffic for the first time in living memory."
msgstr ""
"Un hombre llamado Daedris afirmó su dominio sobre los mundos exhaustos. "
"Fundó un Imperio Galáctico y se nombró a sí mismo su soberano. Bajo el puño "
"de hierro de su ejército, se reanudaron las relaciones entre los planetas; "
"las rutas comerciales abandonadas retornaron desde tiempos que ya no se "
"recordaban."

msgid ""
"Scholars call it the zenith: technology leapt forward, culture flourished, "
"irradiated rock was cleansed and dead planets brought back to life. Peace "
"reigned in an imperial golden age."
msgstr ""
"Los académicos lo llamaron el cenit: la tecnología avanzó a pasos "
"agigantados, la cultura floreció, las rocas irradiadas fueron limpiadas y "
"los planetas muertos volvieron a la vida. La paz reinó en una edad de oro "
"imperial."

msgid ""
"After Daedris, under his successors, the light of the empire waned. Civil "
"strife and religious division weakened social bonds. The great projects of "
"the imperium went awry. In some regions, administration fell into the hands "
"of other powers. The Great Houses now policed the space lanes."
msgstr ""
"Después de Daedris, bajo sus sucesores, la luz del imperio se desvaneció. "
"Las disputas civiles y la división religiosa debilitaron los vínculos "
"sociales. Los grandes proyectos del imperio se torcieron. En algunas "
"regiones, la administración cayó en manos de otras fuerzas. Las Grandes "
"Casas ahora vigilaban las rutas espaciales."

msgid "Rise and fall, the rhythm of history."
msgstr "Ascenso y caída, el ritmo de la historia."

msgid "But the march of history stumbled over the unknown, over the Incident."
msgstr ""
"Pero la marcha de la historia se tropezó con lo desconocido, con el "
"Incidente."

msgid "It tore the heart out of the Empire."
msgstr "Hizo trizas el corazón del Imperio."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"From Earth, a cataclysmic explosion ripped through space, annihilating "
"stars, vaporizing worlds. Billions died. Dozens of systems disappeared into "
"the mysterious nebula left behind. Now the great, galaxy-spanning "
"civilization survives as a shadow of its former glory."
msgstr ""
"Desde la Tierra, una explosión cataclísmica rasgó el espacio, aniquilando "
"estrellas, vaporizando mundos. Miles de millones de personas murieron. "
"Decenas de sistemas desaparecieron en la misteriosa nebulosa que quedó tras "
"de sí. Ahora, la gran civilización que abarca toda la galaxia sobrevive como "
"una sombra de su antigua gloria."

msgid "What else remains? Questions."
msgstr "¿Qué otra cosa nos queda? Preguntas."

msgid ""
"Ten Standard Cycles have passed in a universe ruled by the shards of a "
"decaying empire. After the Incident, corruption and piracy run rampant, but "
"where there is chaos, there is also opportunity."
msgstr ""
"Diez Ciclos Estándar han pasado en un universo gobernado por los fragmentos "
"de un imperio en decadencia. Tras el Incidente, la corrupción y la piratería "
"campan a sus anchas, pero donde hay caos, también hay oportunidades."

msgid "Welcome to the universe of Naev..."
msgstr "Bienvenido al universo de Naev..."

#. Drone
#. event ends on player leaving the system or landing
#. only mark done if the player found the jump
msgid "You have noticed something strange…"
msgstr "Has notado algo extraño…"

msgid "What was that?"
msgstr "¿Qué fue eso?"

msgid "There is nothing of worth left on the ship."
msgstr "No queda nada de valor en la nave."

msgid "The ship consists of nothing more than a bare hull."
msgstr "La nave no consiste más que en un casco desnudo."

msgid "The ship has already been scavenged."
msgstr "La nave ya ha sido saqueada."

msgid "There is not much left besides the hull of the ship."
msgstr "No queda mucho más que el casco de la nave."

msgid "The ship looks like it has been picked clean."
msgstr "La nave parece haber sido limpiada."

#. luacheck: globals boardothers
msgid ""
"You board the ship and don't see much of value. As you are about to give up "
"and go back to your ship, something in the corner of your eye catches your "
"attention."
msgstr ""
"Subes a la nave y no ves nada de valor. Cuando estás a punto de rendirte y "
"volver a tu nave, algo en el rabillo del ojo te llama la atención."

msgid ""
"You find a paper notebook stuck in a part of damaged hull. Most people use "
"the ship computers to store notes and information and rarely rely on "
"physical storage."
msgstr ""
"Encuentras un cuaderno de papel clavado en una parte del casco dañado. La "
"mayoría de la gente utiliza los ordenadores de la nave para almacenar notas "
"e información y rara vez confía en el almacenamiento físico."

msgid "You begin to read the passages."
msgstr "Empiezas a leer los pasajes."

msgid ""
"UST 602:1914\n"
"\n"
"Although my peers will likely make fun of me if they find out, I have "
"decided to start a paper log of my upcoming travels aboard the Beagle. It "
"was hard to find a place selling paper notebooks, as everyone uses holopads, "
"but I was able to find a small place at an antique shop on Antica. For such "
"primitive technology, it was very expensive.\n"
"\n"
"I look forward to starting my travels next decaperiod! It will be my first "
"time leaving Arcturus in ages!"
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1914\n"
"\n"
"Aunque es probable que mis compañeros se burlen de mí si se enteran, he "
"decidido empezar un diario de papel de mis próximos viajes a bordo del "
"Beagle. Fue difícil encontrar un lugar que vendiera cuadernos de papel, ya "
"que todo el mundo utiliza holopads, pero pude encontrar un pequeño lugar en "
"una tienda de antigüedades en Antica. Para una tecnología tan primitiva, "
"resultó muy caro.\n"
"\n"
"¡Estoy deseando empezar mis viajes en el próximo decaperíodo! ¡Será la "
"primera vez que salga de Arcturus en años!"

msgid ""
"UST 602:1928\n"
"\n"
"I have met the crew. They seem fairly friendly except for the big silent "
"guy. I wonder if it will all work out… I just have to stop messing things up "
"this time.\n"
"\n"
"My room is a bit small, but as expected. My roommate seems like a quiet "
"person. I'm not sure if I'll be able to get used to all this floating around "
"in zero-gravity though."
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1928\n"
"\n"
"He conocido a la tripulación. Parecen bastante amistosos, excepto el tipo "
"grande y silencioso. Me pregunto si todo saldrá bien... Sólo tengo que dejar "
"de arruinar las cosas esta vez.\n"
"\n"
"Mi habitación es un poco pequeña, pero como era de esperar. Mi compañero de "
"cuarto parece una persona tranquila. Aunque no estoy seguro de si podré "
"acostumbrarme a todo esto de flotar en gravedad cero."

msgid ""
"UST 602:1971\n"
"\n"
"We are on route to the Delta Pavonis system.\n"
"\n"
"Things haven't been working too well. There was a leak in one of the "
"radiators. We almost got fried, but my roommate was able to fix it in time."
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1971\n"
"\n"
"Estamos en ruta hacia el sistema Delta Pavonis.\n"
"\n"
"Las cosas no han funcionado muy bien. Había una fuga en uno de los "
"radiadores. Casi nos quedamos fritos, pero mi compañero de cuarto pudo "
"arreglarlo a tiempo."

msgid ""
"UST 602:1980\n"
"\n"
"The Captain got in a fight with the provider that was supposed to give us "
"the cargo to take to the Qex system… I don't know what we'll do if this trip "
"gets cancelled… It will look horrible on my Curriculum Vitae…"
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1980\n"
"\n"
"El capitán se ha peleado con el proveedor que debía darnos la carga para "
"llevarla al sistema Qex... No sé qué haremos si este viaje se cancela... "
"Quedará fatal en mi Iurrículum…"

msgid ""
"UST 602:1983\n"
"\n"
"It seems like we got another commission, but we have to go to some place "
"called Hatter in Soromid space… The navigator claims he knows a shortcut, "
"but I have a bad feeling about this.\n"
"\n"
"I want to run back home, but I can't quit so early. They would never stop "
"making fun of me. Maybe Soromid space will be interesting?\n"
"\n"
"We leave for Dune next period."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"UST 602:1995\n"
"\n"
"We have made it to Arrakis in the Dune system.\n"
"\n"
"The sand is awful here. It gets in everything and everywhere, so I decided "
"to cut short my visit of the local area. It's also nice to be in the ship "
"alone. Much quieter and more peaceful."
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1995\n"
"\n"
"Hemos llegado a Arrakis, en el sistema Duna.\n"
"\n"
"La arena es horrible aquí. Se mete en todo y en todas partes, así que he "
"decidido acortar mi visita a la zona. También es agradable estar solo en la "
"nave. Mucho más tranquilo y pacífico."

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"(This page consists of scribbled drawings of the ship and people. A person "
"captioned \"Captain\" is drawn with horns coming out of his head.)"
msgstr ""
"UST (la fecha está en blanco)\n"
"\n"
"(Esta página consiste en dibujos garabateados de la nave y de las personas. "
"Se dibuja una persona con el título \"Capitán\" con cuernos que salen de su "
"cabeza.)"

msgid ""
"UST 602:1999\n"
"\n"
"We have finished loading the cargo, which consists of some sort of bottles "
"of something like sand? The Captain said it is very expensive and was "
"yelling at us all the time while we were loading the cargo.\n"
"\n"
"I have decided that once this is over I will try to find a new job. I don't "
"think I will ever get used to the Captain's temper.\n"
"\n"
"Since it seems like the navigator has a bit of a hangover, we leave in 5 "
"periods."
msgstr ""
"UST 602:1999\n"
"\n"
"Hemos terminado de cargar la mercancía, que consiste en una especie de "
"botellas de algo parecido a la arena. El capitán ha dicho que es muy caro y "
"nos ha estado gritando todo el tiempo mientras cargábamos la mercancía.\n"
"\n"
"He decidido que una vez que esto termine trataré de encontrar un nuevo "
"trabajo. No creo que me acostumbre nunca al temperamento del capitán.\n"
"\n"
"Como parece que el navegante tiene un poco de resaca, partimos en 5 períodos."

msgid ""
"UST 602:2008\n"
"\n"
"It was very hard to wake the navigator and we are behind schedule again. I "
"hate getting yelled at.\n"
"\n"
"We are on on our way to Soromid space, but I don't think the navigator is in "
"much condition to fly."
msgstr ""
"UST 602:2008\n"
"\n"
"Ha sido muy duro despertar al navegante y volvemos a ir con retraso. Odio "
"que me griten.\n"
"\n"
"Estamos de camino al espacio Soromida, pero no creo que el navegante esté en "
"condiciones de volar."

msgid ""
"UST 602:2011\n"
"\n"
"(the writing is much more frantic)\n"
"We are being shot at! There's pirates all over! This is not what I signed up "
"for!\n"
"\n"
"WE'RE GOING TO DIE! WE'RE GOING TO DIE! WE'RE GOING TO DIE!\n"
"(The writing gets abruptly cut off.)\n"
msgstr ""
"UST 602:2011\n"
"\n"
"(la escritura es mucho más frenética)\n"
"¡Nos están disparando! ¡Hay piratas por todas partes! ¡Esto no es para lo "
"que me apunté!\n"
"\n"
"¡VAMOS A MORIR! ¡VAMOS A MORIR! ¡VAMOS A MORIR!\n"
"(La escritura se corta abruptamente.)\n"

msgid ""
"UST 602.2020\n"
"\n"
"This is awful! We are hiding out in an asteroid field. Our cockpit was blown "
"out and the navigator and captain are dead.\n"
"\n"
"I have no idea what to do. It is very hard to write in my space suit, but I "
"don't think the atmosphere unit is going to last long."
msgstr ""
"UST 602.2020\n"
"\n"
"¡Esto es horrible! Estamos escondidos en un campo de asteroides. Nuestra "
"cabina fue volada y el navegante y el capitán están muertos.\n"
"\n"
"No tengo ni idea de qué hacer. Es muy difícil escribir en mi traje espacial, "
"pero no creo que la unidad de atmósfera vaya a durar mucho."

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"Something is scratching at the hull. It sounds like a weird animal. I "
"haven't seen any living person in I don't know how long.\n"
"\n"
"There is no atmosphere and I can't take off my suit any more. I don't see "
"any way out."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"I have lost all notion of time.\n"
"\n"
"They are all around. I don't really understand what they are. They look like "
"small ships, but they are slowly and mechanically tearing apart the ship.\n"
"\n"
"I'm going to die aren't I?"
msgstr ""
"UST (la fecha está en blanco)\n"
"\n"
"He perdido la noción del tiempo.\n"
"\n"
"Están por todas partes. No entiendo muy bien lo que son. Parecen pequeñas "
"naves, pero están destrozando la nave lenta y mecánicamente.\n"
"\n"
"Voy a morir, ¿verdad?"

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"I'm getting cold. I think the heating unit is malfunctioning.\n"
"\n"
"I may have finally lost my mind. There are weird ships prying and removing "
"the ship components. They seem to behave like some sort of pack of wild "
"animals."
msgstr ""
"UST (la fecha está en blanco)\n"
"\n"
"Tengo frío. Creo que la unidad de calefacción está funcionando mal.\n"
"\n"
"Puede que finalmente haya perdido la cabeza. Hay naves extrañas que hurgan y "
"remueven los componentes de la nave. Parecen comportarse como una especie de "
"manada de animales salvajes."

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"I don't feel hunger any more. The numbness sensation is spreading.\n"
"\n"
"The ships don't seem to pay me much attention as they come and go. They "
"remind me of ants back home."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"(There are lots of weird scribbles on the page, however, you can make some "
"sort of map with an area indicated by a big X. It seems like you could "
"investigate this.)\n"
msgstr ""
"UST (la fecha está en blanco)\n"
"\n"
"(Hay muchos garabatos extraños en la página, sin embargo, se puede hacer una "
"especie de mapa con un área indicada por una gran X. Esto se podría "
"investigar).\n"

msgid ""
"UST (the date is blank)\n"
"\n"
"A---s--hm---t---\n"
"\n"
"(It seems like it is the end of the written part of the notebook.)"
msgstr ""
"UST (la fecha está en blanco)\n"
"\n"
"A---s--hm---t---\n"
"\n"
"(Parece que es el final de la parte escrita del cuaderno.)"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You tune your ship sensors to pick up the most minuscule of disturbances and "
"focus on the area indicated by the notebook. You are about to give up when "
"you detect an anomaly. It looks like you can use this to jump, but where "
"could it lead?"
msgstr ""
"Afinas los sensores de tu nave para captar la más minúscula de las "
"perturbaciones y te centras en la zona indicada por el cuaderno. Estás a "
"punto de rendirte cuando detectas una anomalía. Parece que puedes utilizarla "
"para saltar, pero ¿a dónde puede llevar?"

