msgid "Captain Hamfresser"
msgstr "Capitán Hamfresser"

msgid ""
"A tall, and very large, cyborg soldier sits against a wall, right next to "
"the emergency exit. He loudly drinks an orange juice through a pink straw "
"and suspiciously examines the other customers. By the power of his glare he "
"cleared a large area around him as people seem to prefer to move away "
"instead of meeting his half-robotic gaze. Unfortunately, he matches the "
"description of your contact, which means you will have to overcome your fear "
"and talk to him."
msgstr ""
"Un soldado cibernético, alto y muy grande, se sienta contra una pared, justo "
"al lado de la salida de emergencia. Bebe ruidosamente un zumo de naranja con "
"una pajita rosa y examina con recelo a los demás clientes. Con la fuerza de "
"su mirada, despeja una amplia zona a su alrededor, ya que la gente parece "
"preferir alejarse en lugar de encontrarse con su mirada medio robótica. Por "
"desgracia, coincide con la descripción de tu contacto, lo que significa que "
"tendrás que superar tu miedo y hablar con él."

msgid ""
"This planet belongs to Lord Battleaddict. You will be captured if you land "
"here. The mission failed."
msgstr ""
"Este planeta pertenece a Señor AdictoABatalla. Serás capturado si aterrizas "
"aquí. La misión fracasará."

#. Report back
msgid "Major Tam and Captain Leblanc"
msgstr "El Mayor Tam y el Capitán Leblanc"

msgid "Major Tam and Captain Leblanc seem to be waiting for you."
msgstr "El Mayor Tam y el Capitán Leblanc parecen estar esperándote."

#. Epilogue
msgid "Your employers"
msgstr "Tus empleadores"

msgid "Tam and Leblanc are congratulating their general."
msgstr "Tam y Leblanc felicitan a tu general."

msgid "New passengers"
msgstr "Nuevos pasajeros"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"H... hi\", you say, waving timidly. \"Are you Captain Hamfresser?\". The "
"soldier answers \"Of course, as it is written on my name tag.\" Next to his "
"Captain's insignia, and the logo of the Dvaered Space Infantry (a mace with "
"wings), he points to a small label on his chest that reads \"Hamfresser\". "
"Hamfresser looks at you from top to bottom \"You're the private pilot, "
"right? Tell me your ship's dock number, and I'll meet you there. Oh, and "
"please make room for {tonnes} of cargo.\"\n"
"   The captain then gets up, delicately puts his empty glass on the counter, "
"and leaves. While his hairbrushes the ceiling, you wonder if {tonnes} are "
"enough to accommodate him. When you arrive at the dock, you see Hamfresser, "
"with five other soldiers and two androids that load a huge and strange "
"machine into your ship. \"Hey,\" you say, \"what are you doing with your... "
"your death machine?\" Hamfresser approaches and answers at low voice \"But, "
"mate, this is not a death machine, It's just a bomb. Or even just a bomblet."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"H... hola\", dices, saludando tímidamente. \"¿Es usted el capitán "
"Hamfresser?\". El soldado responde \"Por supuesto, como está escrito en mi "
"placa de identificación\". Junto a su insignia de capitán, y el logotipo de "
"la Infantería Espacial Dvaered (una maza con alas), señala una pequeña "
"etiqueta en su pecho que dice \"Hamfresser\". Hamfresser te mira de arriba a "
"abajo \"Eres el piloto privado, ¿verdad? Dígame el número de muelle de su "
"nave y nos encontraremos allí. Ah, y por favor, haga sitio para {tonnes} de "
"carga.\"\n"
"El capitán se levanta, deja delicadamente su vaso vacío sobre el mostrador y "
"se va. Mientras su pelo roza el techo, te preguntas si las {tonnes} son "
"suficientes para acomodarlo. Cuando llegas al muelle, ves a Hamfresser, con "
"otros cinco soldados y dos androides que cargan una enorme y extraña máquina "
"en tu nave. \"Oye\", dices, \"¿qué haces con tu... tu máquina de la muerte?"
"\". Hamfresser se acerca y responde en voz baja \"Pero, amigo, esto no es "
"una máquina de la muerte, es sólo una bomba. O incluso sólo una bombita.\""

msgid ""
"\"Very well,\" you acquiesce, \"do what you have to do.\" Once the cargo is "
"loaded and the team has taken their places in the cabin, you start to talk "
"with the captain. \"And I suppose this bomblet is destined for "
"Battleaddict's Goddard. How are we supposed to put it there? Are we going to "
"pretend it's a gift from the High Command to his granddaughter?\". "
"Hamfresser looks at you surprised. \"No... that's not what the Major... do "
"you think it could work?\" You realize it would take too long to explain "
"that it was a sarcastic comment (assuming that this guy knew what sarcasm "
"is) and simply ask him to explain the major's plan.\n"
"   \"Last period, we intercepted a message from Battleaddict to a plumber. "
"His cruiser has issues with sewage disposal, and he requested an "
"intervention. So, we abducted the plumber, and we disguised an EMP bomb as a "
"replacement sewage disposal. We will dock with his ship, plant the bomb, "
"repair the breakdown (so he won't suspect us) and leave. Private Ling here "
"is a Goddard-plumber, so she will lead us.\" A young and smiling soldier "
"raises her hand, and says \"Hi\"."
msgstr ""
"\"Muy bien\", aceptas, \"haz lo que tengas que hacer\". Una vez que la carga "
"está cargada y el equipo ha ocupado sus lugares en la cabina, empiezas a "
"hablar con el capitán. \"Supongo que esta bomba está destinada al Goddard de "
"AdictoABatalla. ¿Cómo se supone que la pondremos allí? ¿Vamos a fingir que "
"es un regalo del Alto Mando a su nieta?\". Hamfresser te mira sorprendido. "
"\"No... eso no es lo que el Mayor... ¿crees que podría funcionar?\". Te das "
"cuenta de que te llevaría demasiado tiempo explicar que era un comentario "
"sarcástico (suponiendo que este tipo supiera lo que es el sarcasmo) y "
"simplemente le pides que te explique el plan del mayor.\n"
"   \"El último periodo, interceptamos un mensaje de AdictoABatalla a un "
"fontanero. Su crucero tiene problemas con la evacuación de aguas residuales "
"y solicitó una intervención. Así que secuestramos al fontanero y disfrazamos "
"una bomba PEM de reemplazo para la eliminación de aguas residuales. "
"Atracaremos en su nave, colocaremos la bomba, repararemos la avería (para "
"que no sospeche de nosotros) y nos iremos. La soldado Ling es fontanera de "
"Goddard, así que nos guiará\". Una joven y sonriente soldado levanta la mano "
"y dice \"Hola\"."

msgid ""
"While you wonder whether the plan is insanely brilliant or dead stupid, "
"Hamfresser begins the introductions. \"This is Sergeant Nikolov, she is my "
"second in command, this is Private Tronk, from my squad, and Corporal "
"Therus, our medical support. Oh, and the guy in the corner over there is "
"Lieutenant Strafer. He is a pilot from Special Operations. He is here in "
"case we need to switch to plan B.\" As you ask what plan B is, Hamfresser "
"simply answers, \"you don't want to switch to plan B.\n"
"   \"As usual, Lord Battleaddict's cruiser should be in orbit around {pnt} "
"in {sys}\"."
msgstr ""
"Mientras te preguntas si el plan es increíblemente brillante o muy estúpido, "
"Hamfresser comienza las presentaciones. \"Esta es la sargento Nikolov, es mi "
"segunda al mando, este es el soldado Tronk, de mi escuadrón, y el cabo "
"Therus, nuestro apoyo médico. Ah, y el tipo de la esquina es el teniente "
"Strafer. Es un piloto de Operaciones Especiales. Está aquí en caso de que "
"necesitemos cambiar al plan B\". Al preguntar cuál es el plan B, Hamfresser "
"se limita a responder: \"no querrás cambiar al plan B.\n"
"   \"Como siempre, el crucero del Señor AdictoABatalla debería estar en "
"órbita alrededor del {pnt} en {sys}\"."

msgid "Bomb"
msgstr "Bomba"

msgid "A gift from the High Command to Lord Battleaddict."
msgstr "Un regalo del Alto Mando al Señor AdictoABatalla."

msgid "Not enough free space"
msgstr "No hay suficiente espacio libre"

msgid ""
"Your ship does not have enough free space. Come back with {tonnes} free."
msgstr "Su nave no tiene suficiente espacio libre. Vuelva con {tonnes} libres."

msgid "Go to {sys}, approach {pnt}, and wait for the Phalanx"
msgstr "Ve a {sys}, acércate a {pnt}, y espera a la Falange"

msgid "Disable and board the Phalanx"
msgstr "Incapacitar y abordar la Falange"

msgid "Report back on {pnt} in {sys}"
msgstr "Informe sobre {pnt} en {sys}"

#. Fighter duel
#. Entering (Dvaer)
#. Flowers
msgid "General Klank"
msgstr "General Klank"

msgid "Colonel Urnus"
msgstr "Coronel Urnus"

#. To avoid being in the range
#. Equips a Goddard for a duel, with or without repeating railguns
#. TODO switch to equipopt
msgid "Not far from the goal"
msgstr "No muy lejos de la meta"

msgid ""
"As you finish your jump, Lieutenant Strafer approaches your radar screen "
"\"Battleaddict's Goddard should be around {pnt}. I guess he should be adding "
"nanobond plating and repeating railguns everywhere he can by now. There "
"should be a few patrol ships around him that will control our security "
"clearance.\" Hamfresser gives instructions to the team: \"Everyone put your "
"plumber suits on. Nikolov, switch the decoder on so that we can monitor the "
"transmissions of the escort ships. It could tell us if we're detected.\""
msgstr ""
"Mientras terminas de saltar, el Teniente Strafer se acerca a tu pantalla de "
"radar \"El Goddard de AdictoABatalla debería estar por {pnt}. Supongo que ya "
"debe estar añadiendo revestimientos de nanovínculo y cañones de riel de "
"repetición en todos los lugares que pueda. Debería haber unas cuantas naves "
"de patrulla a su alrededor que controlarán nuestra autorización de "
"seguridad\". Hamfresser da instrucciones al equipo: \"Pónganse todos los "
"trajes de fontanero. Nikolov, enciende el decodificador para que podamos "
"controlar las transmisiones de las naves de escolta. Podría indicarnos si "
"nos detectan.\""

msgid "We're safe now"
msgstr "Ahora estamos a salvo"

msgid ""
"Once the ship returns to its normal speed after jumping, Hamfresser says: "
"\"Strange, I wouldn't have believed we'd survive this one. Would you, "
"Strafer?\" The lieutenant answers \"I agree, captain. I guess we've got a "
"good pilot.\" As you ask them why, then, they were not scared, Hamfresser "
"answers: \"Of course we were scared! Who would not be? But we are trained "
"not to show our fear. It tends to distract the pilots.\"\n"
"   A few seconds later, you receive an encoded inter-system message from "
"Major Tam: \"Plan A has leaked. Please switch to plan C. Do not jump in "
"{sys} by any means. For your information, the leak is under control and the "
"source has been dealt with.\" The voice makes a pause and continues: \"I "
"really hope this messages catches you before you enter {sys}. Otherwise, may "
"Dvaerius, the patron saint of mace rockets, have mercy on your souls...\" "
"\"Good old Tamtam,\" Hamfresser says smiling, \"he always worries too much "
"about us.\""
msgstr ""
"Una vez que la nave vuelva a su velocidad normal tras el salto, Hamfresser "
"dice: \"Extraño, no habría creído que sobreviviríamos a esto. ¿Y tú, Strafer?"
"\" El teniente responde \"Estoy de acuerdo, capitán. Creo que tenemos un "
"buen piloto\". Al preguntarles por qué, entonces, no estaban asustados, "
"Hamfresser responde \"¡Claro que estábamos asustados! ¿Quién no lo estaría? "
"Pero estamos entrenados para no mostrar nuestro miedo. Tiende a distraer a "
"los pilotos\".\n"
"   Unos segundos después, recibes un mensaje codificado entre sistemas del "
"Mayor Tam: \"El plan A se ha filtrado. Por favor, cambien al plan C. No "
"salten en {sys} de ninguna manera. Para su información, la fuga está bajo "
"control y se ha tratado la fuente\". La voz hace una pausa y continúa: "
"\"Realmente espero que estos mensajes te atrapen antes de que entres en "
"{sys}. De lo contrario, que Dvaerius, el santo patrón de los cohetes maza, "
"se apiade de vuestras almas...\" \"El bueno de Tamtam\", dice Hamfresser "
"sonriendo, \"siempre se preocupa demasiado por nosotros.\""

msgid "Plan C"
msgstr "Plan C"

msgid ""
"\"All right, everyone, we're now heading to {pnt} in {sys}. According to our "
"intelligence, there should be a Phalanx from Battleaddict's fleet that will "
"take off from there soon. Its name is 'Gorgon'. It is on its way back from a "
"transport mission. According to the analysts, there should be enough free "
"space in this ship for our bomb. We will disable the ship, neutralize the "
"pilot, and load our material. After that, {player} will report back to the "
"Major on {duel_pnt} and the rest of the team will execute the remainder of "
"the plan. I, or Sergeant Nikolov, will brief you once we're in the Phalanx.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Muy bien, todos, ahora nos dirigimos a {pnt} en {sys}. Según nuestra "
"inteligencia, debería haber una Falange de la flota de AdictoABatalla que "
"despegará de allí pronto. Su nombre es 'Gorgona'. Viene de vuelta de una "
"misión de transporte. Según los analistas, debería haber suficiente espacio "
"libre en esta nave para nuestra bomba. Incapacitaremos la nave, "
"neutralizaremos al piloto y cargaremos nuestro material. Después de eso, "
"{player} informará al Mayor sobre {duel_pnt} y el resto del equipo ejecutará "
"el resto del plan. Yo, o el sargento Nikolov, les informaremos una vez que "
"estemos en la Falange.\""

#. Battleaddict agrees for the player to approach
msgid "You're controlled"
msgstr "Estás controlado"

msgid ""
"As you approach the lighter ships that protect the cruiser, a Vendetta hails "
"you. Hamfresser answers \"We're Johnson and Jhonson, associate plumbers. "
"We've an appointment with Mr. Battleaddict. It's about a sewage disposal "
"problem.\" The fighter pilot answers: \"It's all right citizen, your "
"transponder code is correct. You may pass.\" You ease your ship forwards "
"while Hamfresser greets the pilot with an obsequious \"Thank you, mister "
"officer.\"\n"
"   \"By the way,\" says Lieutenant Strafer once the communication has been "
"closed, \"This cruiser probably has no turreted weapons, in anticipation of "
"the duel, so I would recommend to approach it from the back, just in case.\""
msgstr ""
"Al acercarte a las naves más ligeras que protegen el crucero, una Vendetta "
"te llama. Hamfresser responde \"Somos Johnson y Jhonson, fontaneros "
"asociados. Tenemos una cita con el señor AdictoABatalla. Se trata de un "
"problema de evacuación de aguas residuales\". El piloto de caza responde: "
"\"Está bien ciudadano, su código de transpondedor es correcto. Puede "
"pasar\". Haces avanzar Tu nave mientras Hamfresser saluda al piloto con un "
"obsequioso \"Gracias, señor oficial\".\n"
"\"Por cierto\", dice el teniente Strafer una vez cerrada la comunicación, "
"\"este crucero probablemente no tenga armas de torreta, en previsión del "
"duelo, así que recomendaría acercarse por la parte trasera, por si acaso.\""

msgid "We told you not to use a combat ship!"
msgstr "¡Te dijimos que no usaras una nave de combate!"

msgid ""
"As you approach, Lieutenant Strafer looks at your radar screen. \"We are in "
"a combat ship. We told you not to use a combat ship. Now, they are going to "
"attack us! Why did you have to use a combat ship? We'll have to abort the "
"mission now. All because of your bloody combat ship!\""
msgstr ""
"Al acercarse, el Teniente Strafer mira la pantalla de su radar. \"Estamos en "
"una nave de combate. Les dijimos que no usaran una nave de combate. Ahora, "
"¡van a atacarnos! ¿Por qué has tenido que utilizar una nave de combate? "
"Ahora tendremos que abortar la misión. ¡Todo por culpa de tu maldita nave de "
"combate!\""

#. Battleaddict sees that the player is not a plumber
msgid "That could have worked"
msgstr "Eso podría haber funcionado"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"While on approach, you get a better look at the surface of the cruiser. You "
"see a dozen shuttles transporting material and tools from the planet to the "
"ship. As you get closer, you remark that the cruiser looks like a huge "
"construction site with workers in spacesuits welding nanobond reinforcement "
"plates on the hull. Behind you, you hear the chatter of the escort ships, "
"which Hamfresser and his team are anxiously listening to: \"Hey, Zog, I'm "
"getting concerned about my daughter. Her teacher told me she was non-violent "
"with her classmates. Do you think I should see a specialist?\" \"Meh, I "
"don't know, honestly. The new holomovies are to blame. There is always less "
"violence and more love in there. The government should take measures.\"\n"
"   Suddenly, a message makes everyone come to a halt: \"So, Colonel, when do "
"we take those fake plumbers out? I look forward to using my shredders a bit!"
"\" \"Shut up, Corporal!\" \"Oah, come on, I'm on the encoded channel. The "
"plumbers aren't able to break our code.\" \"But they're NOT plumbers, stupid!"
"\"\n"
"   Hamfresser looks at you and declares \"We're aborting the mission. Get us "
"out of this system, {player}!\" Strangely enough, none of the soldiers seem "
"to show any sign of panic."
msgstr ""
"Mientras te acercas, puedes ver mejor la superficie del crucero. Ves una "
"docena de lanzaderas que transportan material y herramientas desde el "
"planeta hasta la nave. Al acercarte, observas que el crucero parece una "
"enorme obra de construcción con trabajadores en trajes espaciales soldando "
"placas de refuerzo de nanovínculo en el casco. Detrás de ti oyes el parloteo "
"de las naves de escolta, que Hamfresser y su equipo escuchan ansiosamente: "
"\"Oye, Zog, me estoy preocupando por mi hija. Su profesora me ha dicho que "
"no es violenta con sus compañeros. ¿Crees que debería ver a un especialista?"
"\". \"Meh, no lo sé, sinceramente. La culpa la tienen las nuevas "
"holopelículas. Siempre hay menos violencia y más amor en ellas. El gobierno "
"debería tomar medidas\".\n"
"   De repente, un mensaje hace que todos se detengan: \"Entonces, Coronel, "
"¿cuándo eliminamos a esos falsos fontaneros? Tengo ganas de usar un poco mis "
"trituradoras\". \"¡Cállate, Cabo!\" \"Vamos, estoy en el canal codificado. "
"Los fontaneros no son capaces de descifrar nuestro código\". \"¡Pero si NO "
"son fontaneros, estúpido!\"\n"
"   Hamfresser te mira y declara \"Abortamos la misión. Sácanos de este "
"sistema, {player}\". Extrañamente, ninguno de los soldados parece mostrar "
"ningún signo de pánico."

msgid "Jump out. Do NOT land in this system"
msgstr "Salta. NO aterrice en este sistema"

#. Test civilian ships
#. Spawn the Phalanx to disable
msgid "Gorgon"
msgstr "Gorgona"

#. Go towards Battleaddict's place
#. TODO switch to equipopt
#. TODO: not possible to jump out nor land
#. Decide if the Phalanx flees or fight
#. Makes the carceral convoy enter the system
#. escort[4] = pilot.add( "Za'lek Heavy Drone", "Za'lek", mem.prevsys, nil, {ai="collective"} )
#. TODO: not possible to jump nor to land
#. Hooks for the interception target
#. Hack so that Strafer attacks them and not the Sting
#. Decide between fight or runaway
msgid "Just try to catch me, you pirate!"
msgstr "¡Intenta atraparme, pirata!"

msgid "You made a very big mistake!"
msgstr "¡Has cometido un gran error!"

msgid "Boarding"
msgstr "Abordaje"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All the members of the commando unit have put on their battle suits. "
"Hamfresser gives the final orders. \"Nikolov, Tronk, and I will enter first "
"and clear the area. Remember, we don't have our usual Dudley combat "
"androids. We're stuck with the two useless plumber bots and the few security "
"droids of {player}'s ship so we'll have to get our hands dirty. Corvettes "
"are typically protected by a few 629 Spitfires and an occasional 711 "
"Grillmeister. That's not very much, but still enough to send the inattentive "
"soldier ad patres.\"\n"
"   When the corvette's airlock falls under Nikolov's circular saw, the "
"captain waves and the small team enters the ship. You hear shots and "
"explosions coming from further and further into the enemy ship. Finally, you "
"hear a laconic message coming from the disabled corvette: \"Strafer here, "
"everything went well. We'll now transfer the cargo into the Phalanx... Now "
"that the manoeuvre is finished, you may leave.\" Happy to have survived the "
"operation so far, you start your engines and respond \"Good luck, folks!\" "
"The lieutenant answers \"Thanks, citizen, I'm glad to have met you.\""
msgstr ""
"Todos los miembros de la unidad de comandos se han puesto sus trajes de "
"combate. Hamfresser da las últimas órdenes. \"Nikolov, Tronk y yo entraremos "
"primero y despejaremos la zona. Recordad que no tenemos a nuestros androides "
"de combate habituales Dudley. Estamos atascados con los dos inútiles robots "
"fontaneros y los pocos droides de seguridad de la nave de {player}, así que "
"tendremos que ensuciarnos las manos. Las corbetas suelen estar protegidas "
"por unos pocos Spitfires 629 y un ocasional Grillmeister 711. No es mucho, "
"pero sí lo suficiente para enviar al soldado desatento ad patres.\"\n"
"   Cuando la esclusa de la corbeta cae bajo la sierra circular de Nikolov, "
"el capitán saluda y el pequeño equipo entra en la nave. Se oyen disparos y "
"explosiones que provienen cada vez más del interior de la nave enemiga. "
"Finalmente, oyes un lacónico mensaje procedente de la corbeta incapacitada: "
"\"Aquí Strafer, todo ha ido bien. Ahora transferiremos la carga a la "
"Falange... Ahora que la maniobra está terminada, pueden marcharse\". Feliz "
"de haber sobrevivido a la operación hasta ahora, enciendes los motores y "
"responde \"¡Buena suerte, amigos!\". El teniente responde \"Gracias, "
"ciudadano, me alegro de haberte conocido.\""

#. Prevent the player form actually boarding the ship
#. It's ours now!
#. Mission failed: phalanx died
#. Reset the zlk standing
#. Don't care after boarding
msgid "Mission Failed: target destroyed"
msgstr "Misión Fallida: objetivo destruido"

msgid ""
"You were supposed to disable that ship, not to destroy it. How are you "
"supposed to transport the bomb now?"
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías inutilizar esa nave, no destruirla. ¿Cómo se supone "
"que vas a transportar la bomba ahora?"

#. Mission failed: phalanx escaped
#. Don't care after boarding
msgid "Mission Failed: target escaped"
msgstr "Misión Fallida: el objetivo ha escapado"

msgid ""
"You were supposed to disable that ship, not to let it escape. How are you "
"supposed to transport the bomb now?"
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías incapacitar esa nave, no dejarla escapar. ¿Cómo se "
"supone que vas a transportar la bomba ahora?"

msgid "Ready to attend to the show?"
msgstr "¿Listo para asistir al espectáculo?"

msgid ""
"As you sit at the table, Tam starts to speak: \"I got a message from Captain "
"Hamfresser. Apparently, everything went according to plan this time. They "
"should have docked with the Goddard, allegedly to add their mission log to "
"the central database. Then they planted the bomb in the plumbing, close to "
"the central unit, and they faked an accident while landing on {pnt}. I guess "
"they should be hiking somewhere on the planet's surface by now, looking for "
"the opportunity to steal an unfortunate civilian's Llama in order to make "
"their trip back.\n"
"   \"Our boss, General Klank, is ready for the duel. The Captain and I are "
"his duel witnesses, so we should be joining our pageantry ships by now. Oh, "
"and the duel commissioner is someone you already know, Colonel Urnus. In "
"about a period, Lord Battleaddict should arrive, so if you take off soon, "
"you will see the duel.\""
msgstr ""
"Mientras te sientas en la mesa, Tam empieza a hablar: \"Recibí un mensaje "
"del Capitán Hamfresser. Al parecer, esta vez todo ha ido según lo previsto. "
"Debían acoplarse a la Goddard, supuestamente para añadir su registro de "
"misión a la base de datos central. Luego colocaron la bomba en las tuberías, "
"cerca de la unidad central, y fingieron un accidente al aterrizar en {pnt}. "
"Supongo que ahora deben estar de excursión en algún lugar de la superficie "
"del planeta, buscando la oportunidad de robar la Llama de un civil "
"desafortunado para poder hacer su viaje de vuelta.\n"
"   \"Nuestro jefe, el General Klank, está listo para el duelo. El Capitán y "
"yo somos sus testigos del duelo, así que ya deberíamos estar uniéndonos a "
"nuestras naves de representación. Ah, y el comisario del duelo es alguien "
"que ya conoces, el Coronel Urnus. En aproximadamente un período, Señor "
"AdictoABatalla debería llegar, así que si despegas pronto, verás el duelo.\""

msgid "Attend to the duel"
msgstr "Atiende al duelo"

#. Starts the duel
msgid "Here we go"
msgstr "Aquí vamos"

msgid ""
"Colonel Urnus's ship broadcasts the message: \"I, Colonel Urnus, have been "
"requested by both parties of this duel to be today's commissioner. I hereby "
"solemnly swear, as an officer of the Dvaered Army, to be respectful of our "
"laws and our customs, and I have never worked under the command nor as a "
"commander of either of the generals involved in this duel. I have verified "
"the pedigree of the four witnesses and I can attest they are respectable "
"officers of the Dvaered Army. Lord Battleaddict, General Klank, before "
"proceeding with combat, I must ask you one last time: Are you sure your "
"disagreement cannot be solved by any other means?\"\n"
"   A formal silence follows the words of the colonel, but soon Battleaddict "
"and Klank respond: \"It cannot, Mister Commissioner.\" Urnus continues: \"I "
"am witness to the fact that this duel conforms to the rules established by "
"our ancestors. I have inspected both ships and I attest that I observed no "
"irregularities. Let the fight begin. May the most virtuous one of you "
"survive.\""
msgstr ""
"La nave del Coronel Urnus emite el mensaje: \"Yo, el Coronel Urnus, he sido "
"solicitado por ambas partes de este duelo para ser el comisario de hoy. Juro "
"solemnemente, como oficial del Ejército Dvaered, ser respetuoso con nuestras "
"leyes y nuestras costumbres, y que nunca he trabajado bajo el mando ni como "
"comandante de ninguno de los generales implicados en este duelo. He "
"verificado el pedigrí de los cuatro testigos y puedo dar fe de que son "
"respetables oficiales del Ejército Dvaered. Señor AdictoABatalla, General "
"Klank, antes de proceder al combate, debo preguntarles una última vez: "
"¿Están seguros de que su desacuerdo no puede resolverse por otros medios?\"\n"
"   Un silencio formal sigue a las palabras del coronel, pero pronto "
"AdictoABatalla y Klank responden: \"No puede, señor comisario\". Urnus "
"continúa: \"Soy testigo de que este duelo se ajusta a las reglas "
"establecidas por nuestros antepasados. He inspeccionado ambas naves y doy fe "
"de que no he observado ninguna irregularidad. Que comience el combate. Que "
"sobreviva el más virtuoso de vosotros.\""

#. Actually it should not be necessary, but...
msgid "Let the fight begin!"
msgstr "¡Que comience la lucha!"

msgid "Come on, boss!"
msgstr "¡Vamos, jefe!"

msgid "DESTROY HIM!"
msgstr "¡DESTRÚYELO!"

msgid "You're the best, boss!"
msgstr "¡Eres el mejor, jefe!"

msgid "Yeah!"
msgstr "¡Sí!"

#. Disables the ships
#. Explosion and such
msgid "Damn!"
msgstr "¡Maldita sea!"

msgid "Oooooo..."
msgstr "Oooooo..."

msgid "What the?"
msgstr "¿Qué?"

msgctxt "fw01"
msgid "Come on!"
msgstr "¡Vamos!"

msgid "Hey, they have put a bomb in the general's ship as well!"
msgstr "¡Oye, también han puesto una bomba en la nave del general!"

msgid ""
"The electricians! We've called electricians recently! They planted the bomb!"
msgstr ""
"¡Los electricistas! ¡Hemos llamado a los electricistas recientemente! ¡Ellos "
"pusieron la bomba!"

msgid "Cheaters!"
msgstr "¡Tramposos!"

msgid "Cheaters yourselves!"
msgstr "¡Tramposos vosotros!"

msgid "Hey, Battleaddict, it seems we are both down..."
msgstr "Hey, AdictoABatala, parece que ambos estamos caidos..."

msgid "I still want to kill you!"
msgstr "¡Todavía quiero matarte!"

msgid "So do I."
msgstr "Yo también."

msgid "Luckily enough, I've got my Vendetta in the fighter bay."
msgstr "Por suerte, tengo mi Vendetta en la bahía de cazas."

msgid "Shall we continue?"
msgstr "¿Continuamos?"

msgid "Of course, we shall!"
msgstr "¡Claro que sí!"

#. Prevent both Goddards from colliding with Vendetta's ammo. Set the AI so that they don't get stuck.
#. atk_drone
#. Actually it should not be necessary, but...
#. Prevent them from staying on the top of their ships
#. camera.set(klank2, true)
msgid "Aha! In your freaking ugly face!"
msgstr "¡Ajá! ¡En tu maldita y fea cara!"

msgid "You're the best, general!"
msgstr "¡Eres el mejor, general!"

msgid "Nooooo!"
msgstr "¡Nooooo!"

msgid "General Klank won the duel!"
msgstr "¡El General Klank ganó el duelo!"

#. Epilogue
msgid "A good thing done"
msgstr "Una cosa bien hecha"

msgid ""
"As you approach, the major tells General Klank that you are the private "
"pilot they hired recently. \"I see,\" says the general \"so you are one of "
"the people I have to thank for still being alive now.\" You answer that he "
"apparently would not have needed help if Battleaddict had not cheated as "
"well, and he responds: \"Damn fake electricians; I should have suspected "
"something. Anyway, citizen, rest assured that we will need your services "
"again.\" A group of generals approach and congratulate Klank. He stands up "
"and leaves with them, loudly exchanging dubious pleasantries.\n"
"   Major Tam speaks to you: \"Apparently, Battleaddict had a commando unit "
"dress like electricians and hide an EMP bomb in the General's Goddard. It "
"exploded during the fight, just like our own bomb. And now both ships have "
"their systems ruined. Well, anyway, thank you for your help, here are "
"{credits} for you!\""
msgstr ""
"Al acercarse, el mayor le dice al general Klank que usted es el piloto "
"privado que contrataron recientemente. \"Ya veo\", dice el general, \"así "
"que usted es una de las personas a las que tengo que agradecer que siga vivo "
"ahora\". Tú le respondes que, al parecer, no habría necesitado ayuda si "
"AdictoABatalla no hubiera hecho trampas también, y él responde \"Malditos "
"falsos electricistas; debería haber sospechado algo. De todos modos, "
"ciudadano, ten por seguro que volveremos a necesitar tus servicios\". Un "
"grupo de generales se acerca y felicita a Klank. Éste se levanta y se marcha "
"con ellos, intercambiando en voz alta dudosas cortesías.\n"
"   El Mayor Tam te habla: \"Al parecer, AdictoABatalla hizo que una unidad "
"de comandos se vistiera de electricista y escondiera una bomba PEM en el "
"Goddard del general. Explotó durante el combate, igual que nuestra propia "
"bomba. Y ahora ambas naves tienen sus sistemas arruinados. Bueno, de todos "
"modos, gracias por tu ayuda, ¡aquí tienes {credits} para ti!\""

msgid ""
"Major Tam's superior, General Klank, had a Goddard duel with Lord "
"Battleaddict. You took part in an operation to sabotage Battleaddict's "
"cruiser. Lord Battleaddict sabotaged Klank's cruiser as well, but at the end "
"of the day, General Klank won the duel."
msgstr ""
"El superior del Mayor Tam, el General Klank, tuvo un duelo Goddard con Lord "
"AdictoABatalla. Participó en una operación para sabotear el crucero de "
"AdictoABatalla. Señor AdictoABatalla también saboteó el crucero de Klank, "
"pero al final, el general Klank ganó el duelo."

#. This ensures the next mission will be available only once the traitor event is done
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Dvaered Escape">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>2</priority>
#. <chance>10</chance>
#. <done>Dvaered Sabotage</done>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <cond>var.peek("loyal2klank") == true</cond>
#. <faction>Dvaered</faction>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Frontier Invasion</campaign>
#. <done_evt name="Betray General Klank">If you don't betray</done_evt>
#. <provides name="General Klank wants his 10M back">If you get into debt</provides>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Dvaered Escape
#. -- This is the third mission of the Frontier War Dvaered campaign.
#. -- The player has to set up the evasion of a Goddard executive.
#. -- This executive will then help House Dvaered on the diplomatic point of view.
#.
#. Stages :
#. 0) Goto find Hamfresser
#. 1) Goto the interception (intsys)
#. 2) Start to run away
#. 3) Goto an hospital
#. 4) Runaway
#. 5) Player has been hailed by Captain HewHew
#. 6) Player has met the Empire and Pirate agent, but did not accept any of their offers (yet?)
#. 7) Accepted Empire solution: can cross blockade of dealsys->dealjump
#. 8) Accepted Pirate solution: can cross any blockade
#. 9) Accepted Pirate solution: can cross any blockade, but has paid cash
#. --
#. Non-persistent state
#. Forward-declared functions
#. common hooks
#. TODO: add news comments about all this
msgid ""
"Hamfresser and his team are gathered at a table. The captain drinks from his "
"favourite pink straw while incessantly scanning the room."
msgstr ""
"Hamfresser y su equipo están reunidos en una mesa. El capitán bebe de su "
"pajita rosa preferida mientras escudriña incesantemente la sala."

msgid ""
"The captain sits alone at a distant table. He nervously chews his pink straw "
"while waiting for your signal to infiltrate the hospital."
msgstr ""
"El capitán se sienta solo en una mesa lejana. Mastica nerviosamente su "
"pajita rosa mientras espera tu señal para infiltrarse en el hospital."

msgid ""
"The second in command of Hamfresser's squad seems to be as laid back as a "
"Totoran gladiator on cocaine. Clearly, open spaces like this bar with many "
"people around are not suited to commandos, who are used to seeing strangers "
"as potential hostiles."
msgstr ""
"El segundo al mando del escuadrón de Hamfresser parece tan relajado como un "
"gladiador totorano drogado con cocaína. Está claro que los espacios abiertos "
"como este bar con mucha gente alrededor no son adecuados para los comandos, "
"que están acostumbrados a ver a los extraños como potenciales hostiles."

msgid ""
"The young cyborg sits to the right of his captain and looks suspiciously at "
"his glass of sparkling water."
msgstr ""
"El joven cyborg se sienta a la derecha de su capitán y mira con recelo su "
"vaso de agua con gas."

msgid ""
"This soldier is the team's medic. As such, she seems to be slightly less "
"combat-ready than the others, but her large, cybernetically-enhanced arms "
"still make her look like she could crush a bull."
msgstr ""
"Esta soldado es la médica del equipo. Como tal, parece estar ligeramente "
"menos preparada para el combate que los demás, pero sus grandes brazos "
"mejorados cibernéticamente hacen que parezca que podría aplastar a un toro."

msgid ""
"The pilot is the only one in the group who looks like the kind of person "
"with whom you are used to working. His presence, along with the others, "
"makes the group even stranger."
msgstr ""
"El piloto es el único del grupo que parece el tipo de persona con la que "
"estás acostumbrado a trabajar. Su presencia, junto con la de los demás, hace "
"que el grupo sea aún más extraño."

msgid ""
"Captain Leblanc is the top pilot of General Klank's task force. Her presence "
"in this bar means that the High Command needs your help."
msgstr ""
"El Capitán Leblanc es el mejor piloto del grupo de trabajo del General "
"Klank. Su presencia en este bar significa que el Alto Mando necesita tu "
"ayuda."

msgid "A difficult mission"
msgstr "Una misión difícil"

msgid ""
"As you approach, Leblanc recognizes you. \"Hello, citizen. Fancy meeting you "
"here! The Major told me I would end up finding you by checking all the "
"shifty places in Dvaered space. We need your services once more. But, this "
"time, it will be sort of a bit... More illegal.\" You wonder how something "
"could be more illegal than helping black ops commandos assassinate a pilot, "
"steal a corvette, and sabotage a warlord's cruiser. And, so, you answer:"
msgstr ""
"Al acercarse, Leblanc te reconoce. \"Hola, ciudadano. Es un placer "
"encontrarte aquí. El Mayor me dijo que acabaría encontrándote revisando "
"todos los lugares sospechosos del espacio Dvaered. Necesitamos tus servicios "
"una vez más. Pero, esta vez, será un poco... Más ilegal\". Te preguntas cómo "
"puede ser algo más ilegal que ayudar a los comandos de operaciones "
"encubiertas a asesinar a un piloto, robar una corbeta y sabotear el crucero "
"de un señor de la guerra. Y, entonces, respondes:"

msgid ""
"\"As you wish, citizen. After all, one can not obligate people to do their "
"duty...\""
msgstr ""
"\"Como quiera, ciudadano. Después de todo, no se puede obligar a la gente a "
"cumplir con su deber...\""

msgid "The problem to solve"
msgstr "El problema a resolver"

msgid ""
"\"Alright,\" Leblanc says, \"Here is the situation: before we prepare for "
"our military operations, we need to protect our backs. Major Tam believes "
"that the House Goddard is the key to ensure that the Empire will not thwart "
"our plan. Tam would explain it much better than I, but as Goddard is right "
"in between our space and Imperial space, they really have much to lose in "
"case of a direct conflict. What is more, as we are House Goddard's best "
"customer, they tend to appreciate us. For example, we recently paid 6M "
"credits to repair all the electronics in Klank's and Battleaddict's "
"Goddards.\n"
"   However, not all members of Goddard's executive board share the same "
"opinion on our Frontier invasion projects. Mr. Danftang, their Public "
"Relations Manager, in particular, used to see it as an opportunity to sell "
"more cruisers to the High Command and was very favourable to the invasion. "
"However, he was recently arrested by the Za'lek police for unclear reasons. "
"Many suspect Goddard's shareholders of trying to settle the score. As you "
"may have guessed at this point, our mission is to help this man escape from "
"Za'lek prison.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Muy bien\", dice Leblanc, \"Esta es la situación: antes de prepararnos "
"para nuestras operaciones militares, necesitamos proteger nuestras espaldas. "
"El Mayor Tam cree que la Casa Goddard es la clave para que el Imperio no "
"frustre nuestro plan. Tam lo explicaría mucho mejor que yo, pero como "
"Goddard está justo en medio de nuestro espacio y el espacio imperial, "
"realmente tienen mucho que perder en caso de un conflicto directo. Además, "
"como somos el mejor cliente de la Casa Goddard, suelen apreciarnos. Por "
"ejemplo, hace poco pagamos 6 millones de créditos para reparar toda la "
"electrónica de los Goddard de Klank y AdictoABatalla.\n"
"   Sin embargo, no todos los miembros de la junta directiva de Goddard "
"comparten la misma opinión sobre nuestros proyectos de invasión de la "
"frontera. El Sr. Danftang, su director de relaciones públicas, en "
"particular, solía verlo como una oportunidad para vender más cruceros al "
"Alto Mando y era muy favorable a la invasión. Sin embargo, recientemente fue "
"detenido por la policía Za'lek por razones poco claras. Muchos sospechan que "
"los accionistas de Goddard intentan ajustar cuentas. Como habrás adivinado a "
"estas alturas, nuestra misión es ayudar a este hombre a escapar de la "
"prisión Za'lek.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"The target is currently in a Za'lek VIP holding cell on {pripla} in "
"{prisys}. He will be transferred to {zlkpla} in {zlksys} for a preliminary "
"interview with the judge. The Za'lek don't expect anybody to try to free him "
"through violence, so they aren't taking too many precautions.\n"
"   \"Major Tam has planned the operation. First, you will pick up Hamfresser "
"and his team on {hampla} in {hamsys}. I'll be there too, and then we will "
"fly in formation to {intsys} and set up the ambush. It would be preferable "
"if you would make sure that your ship doesn't outrun my Vendetta. The convoy "
"should be a few drones and a corvette. We will destroy the drones and "
"disable the corvette in order to let the commando unit enter the ship and "
"recover the target. Tam has insisted that he doesn't want us to kill anybody "
"as it could irritate the Za'lek a bit too much. After that, we will have to "
"jump out of the system and to return to {reppla} separately.\n"
"   \"A fake transponder will be installed on both our ships. This will "
"ensure that, provided we don't do anything stupid on our way back, we will "
"not be recognized as hostile by the Za'lek patrols and ground control "
"services. So we should be able to refuel without any problem on Za'lek "
"planets.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El objetivo se encuentra actualmente en una celda VIP de Za'lek en "
"{pripla} en {prisys}. Será trasladado a {zlkpla} en {zlksys} para una "
"entrevista preliminar con el juez. Los Za'lek no esperan que nadie intente "
"liberarlo mediante la violencia, así que no están tomando demasiadas "
"precauciones.\n"
"   \"El Mayor Tam ha planeado la operación. Primero, recogerás a Hamfresser "
"y su equipo en {hampla} en {hamsys}. Yo también estaré allí, y luego "
"volaremos en formación hasta {intsys} y prepararemos la emboscada. Sería "
"preferible que te aseguraras de que tu nave no sobrepasa a mi Vendetta. La "
"caravana debería ser de unos pocos drones y una corbeta. Destruiremos los "
"drones e inutilizaremos la corbeta para que la unidad de comandos pueda "
"entrar en la nave y recuperar el objetivo. Tam ha insistido en que no quiere "
"que matemos a nadie ya que podría irritar demasiado a los Za'lek. Después, "
"tendremos que saltar fuera del sistema y volver a {reppla} por separado.\n"
"  \"Se instalará un transpondedor falso en nuestras dos naves. Esto "
"asegurará que, siempre que no hagamos ninguna estupidez en nuestro camino de "
"vuelta, no seremos reconocidos como hostiles por las patrullas Za'lek y los "
"servicios de control en tierra. Así que deberíamos poder repostar sin "
"problemas en los planetas Za'lek.\""

msgid "You will help a Goddard executive to evade his Za'lek prison."
msgstr "Ayudarás a un ejecutivo de Goddard a evadir su prisión Za'lek."

msgid "Hopefully something better than Gauss Guns..."
msgstr "Esperemos que sea algo mejor que las armas Gauss..."

