"por lo ocurrido. Ahora deberían aceptarte en su espacio.\"\n"
"  El comandante empieza a marcharse, pero luego vuelve \"Oh, casi me olvido "
"de pagarte. Jeje. Aquí tienes {credits}.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You explain to the major the problems you encountered. \"I guess it must "
"have been very hard, and risky, to skirt the blockade, congratulations! Oh, "
"and by the way, I made sure the Za'lek don't blame you personally for what "
"happened. They should accept you in their space now.\"\n"
"   The major starts to go away, but then comes back \"Oh, I almost forgot to "
"pay you. Hehe. Here are {credits}.\""
msgstr ""
"Le explicas al mayor los problemas que has encontrado. Le hablas del extraño "
"trato que el Imperio intentó hacer contigo. \"Sí, los servicios de "
"inteligencia Imperiales son formidables. Es muy difícil ocultarles nuestras "
"intenciones. Hiciste bien en no aceptar su oferta. Supongo que debe haber "
"sido muy difícil, y arriesgado, eludir el bloqueo Imperial, ¡felicidades! "
"Ah, y por cierto, me aseguré de que los Za'lek no te culparan personalmente "
"por lo ocurrido. Ahora deberían aceptarte en su espacio.\"\n"
"  El comandante empieza a marcharse, pero luego vuelve \"Oh, casi me olvido "
"de pagarte. Jeje. Aquí tienes {credits}.\""

msgid ""
"You helped the Dvaered High Command to liberate Mr. Danftang, public "
"relations executive at Goddard, who was imprisoned by the Za'lek for obscure "
"reasons. This executive is likely to help House Dvaered from a diplomatic "
"angle. Many unexpected events happened during this operation, but you "
"managed to survive somehow."
msgstr ""
"Has ayudado al Alto Mando Dvaered a liberar al Sr. Danftang, ejecutivo de "
"relaciones públicas de Goddard, que fue encarcelado por los Za'lek por "
"razones oscuras. Es probable que este ejecutivo ayude a la Casa Dvaered "
"desde el punto de vista diplomático. Durante esta operación se produjeron "
"muchos imprevistos, pero lograsteis sobrevivir de alguna manera."

msgid ""
"\"Hello, {player}! You remember us?\" asks the captain, apparently unaware "
"of the fact that his appearance is hard to forget. \"We are ready to embark "
"whenever you want, pilot! You'll just have to make space for {tonnes} of "
"cargo (we have some equipment). Oh yes, and there is apparently a small "
"change in the plan regarding Captain Leblanc. She won't be able to join us. "
"Talk to the Lieutenant, he can explain it further.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Hola, {player}! ¿Te acuerdas de nosotros?\", pregunta el capitán, "
"aparentemente inconsciente de que su aspecto es difícil de olvidar. "
"\"¡Estamos listos para embarcar cuando quieras, piloto! Sólo tendrás que "
"hacer espacio para {tonnes} de carga (tenemos algo de equipo). Ah, sí, y al "
"parecer hay un pequeño cambio en el plan con respecto al capitán Leblanc. No "
"podrá unirse a nosotros. Habla con el Teniente, él puede explicarlo mejor.\""

msgid ""
"\"Hello, citizen. I guess you want to discuss the plan with the officers. "
"But first, can you explain to my why there are many so people in this room, "
"but none of them want to sit at the tables next to ours? Do you know what is "
"wrong with this part of the room?\" You answer that the people probably feel "
"unsafe sitting next to a group of dangerous-looking cyborgs, and she "
"answers: \"Meh, I don't think you're right. When I am in the Space Infantry "
"refectory, there are dangerous-looking cyborgs all around and nobody feels "
"unsafe. It must be something else...\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hola, ciudadano. Supongo que quieres discutir el plan con los oficiales. "
"Pero antes, ¿puedes explicarme por qué hay tanta gente en esta sala, pero "
"ninguno quiere sentarse en las mesas contiguas a la nuestra? ¿Sabe qué es lo "
"que pasa en esta parte de la sala?\". Tú respondes que probablemente la "
"gente se siente insegura al sentarse junto a un grupo de cyborgs de aspecto "
"peligroso, y ella responde \"No creo que tengas razón. Cuando estoy en el "
"comedor de la Infantería Espacial, hay cyborgs de aspecto peligroso por "
"todas partes y nadie se siente inseguro. Debe ser otra cosa...\""

msgid ""
"\"I ordered water and the waiter gave me this glass which is full of "
"bubbles. It does not look safe. Do you know what it is? I hope it's not "
"alcohol...\" As you tell him that it is simply sparkling water, and that it "
"doesn't contain alcohol nor anything toxic, he gratefully answers: \"Whoa, "
"you're quite the expert about drinks! You know, I asked because we cyborgs "
"of class gamma can't drink alcohol. Each morning we have to take special "
"medication, the Spacemarine's Cocktail, to ensure that our bodies continue "
"to support our biological and cybernetic implants. This cocktail is "
"incompatible with any alcohol.\n"
"   \"My brother drank a beer once by mistake, and he had to spend two months "
"in hospital. But he is doing better now, and is back with his unit.\" You "
"ask him if everyone in his family is as strong as he is and he answers: \"Oh "
"no, my little sister is much stronger. She fights on Totoran in the one-on-"
"one bare-hand championship. She won 6 matches in a row, last season. But I "
"am afraid she won't be able to take part in this cycle's championship as she "
"hasn't yet fully recovered from her decapitation during her last fight.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Pedí agua y el camarero me dio este vaso que está lleno de burbujas. No "
"parece seguro. ¿Sabe qué es? Espero que no sea alcohol...\" Mientras le "
"dices que es simplemente agua con gas, y que no contiene alcohol ni nada "
"tóxico, te responde agradecido: \"¡Vaya, eres todo un experto en bebidas! Lo "
"he preguntado porque los ciborgs de la clase gamma no podemos beber alcohol. "
"Todas las mañanas tenemos que tomar una medicación especial, el Cóctel de la "
"Marina Espacial, para que nuestros cuerpos sigan soportando nuestros "
"implantes biológicos y cibernéticos. Este cóctel es incompatible con "
"cualquier tipo de alcohol.\n"
"   \"Mi hermano bebió una vez una cerveza por error y tuvo que pasar dos "
"meses en el hospital. Pero ahora está mejor y ha vuelto a su unidad\". Le "
"preguntas si todos los miembros de su familia son tan fuertes como él y te "
"responde: \"Oh no, mi hermana pequeña es mucho más fuerte. Ella lucha en "
"Totoran en el campeonato de mano desnuda uno a uno. Ganó 6 combates "
"seguidos, la temporada pasada. Pero me temo que no podrá participar en el "
"campeonato de este ciclo, ya que aún no se ha recuperado del todo de su "
"decapitación durante su último combate.\""

msgid ""
"\"Hi, citizen. Are you ready to transport us once more? Have you spoken to "
"the Captain? And to the pilot? I don't really know the details of the "
"operation, so you'll have to ask them.\"\n"
"   The corporal seems to hesitate, and then continues: \"Today, the "
"Lieutenant asked me a riddle: let's say Major Tam is running after a turtle. "
"When Major Tam arrives at the point where the turtle was when he started to "
"run, the turtle has moved forward a bit in the same time, right? Then, he "
"arrives at the point where the turtle was when he reached the previous "
"point, but the turtle has again moved forward. And so on. Conclusion: Major "
"Tam is quicker than the turtle, but he never catches up. How is that "
"possible?\"\n"
"   Strafer then arrives: \"Yep, I was at the museum of Theras one day, and "
"this riddle was written in a book from before the space age. The name of the "
"author was: 'Senior High School Philosophy Class'. That's a strange name, "
"actually. I remembered that riddle while we were hiking on {pnt} a while "
"ago, and we saw a turtle.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hola, ciudadano. ¿Estás listo para transportarnos una vez más? ¿Has "
"hablado con el capitán? ¿Y con el piloto? No conozco los detalles de la "
"operación, así que tendrás que preguntarles a ellos\".\n"
"   El cabo parece dudar, y luego continúa: \"Hoy, el Teniente me ha "
"planteado un acertijo: supongamos que el Mayor Tam corre detrás de una "
"tortuga. Cuando el comandante Tam llega al punto donde estaba la tortuga "
"cuando empezó a correr, la tortuga ha avanzado un poco en el mismo tiempo, "
"¿no? Luego, llega al punto donde estaba la tortuga cuando llegó al punto "
"anterior, pero la tortuga ha vuelto a avanzar. Y así sucesivamente. "
"Conclusión: El mayor Tam es más rápido que la tortuga, pero nunca la "
"alcanza. ¿Cómo es posible?\"\n"
"   Entonces llega Strafer: \"Sí, un día estuve en el museo de Theras, y este "
"acertijo estaba escrito en un libro de antes de la era espacial. El nombre "
"del autor era: 'Clase de filosofía del instituto'. Es un nombre extraño, en "
"realidad. Me acordé de ese acertijo mientras estábamos de excursión en {pnt} "
"hace un tiempo, y vimos una tortuga.\""

msgid ""
"You look at the lieutenant, surprised not to see Captain Leblanc, as "
"expected. \"Unexpected circumstance have arisen. The general was attacked in "
"Doranthex by mercenary pilots and our squadron had to rescue him. The second "
"in command got killed, so Leblanc can not delegate her command any more. We "
"need her to lead the squadron, and she sent me instead. Do not worry, I "
"might be slightly less gifted than her, but I am still a dogfight ace. I "
"have 15 confirmed dogfight victories so far, you know, and that does not "
"take into account the secret operations I have taken part in.\n"
"   \"So, on the way in, I will follow you with my civilian Vendetta and you "
"will just have to hail me if you want me to do anything special. During the "
"extraction, I'll focus on the drones so that you can take on the main ship. "
"On the way back, we will take separate ways. We'll take off when you decide."
"\""
msgstr ""
"Mira al teniente, sorprendido de no ver al capitán Leblanc, como se "
"esperaba. \"Han surgido circunstancias inesperadas. El general fue atacado "
"en Doranthex por pilotos mercenarios y nuestro escuadrón tuvo que "
"rescatarlo. El segundo al mando fue asesinado, así que Leblanc ya no puede "
"delegar su mando. La necesitamos para dirigir el escuadrón y me envió a mí "
"en su lugar. No te preocupes, puede que esté un poco menos dotado que ella, "
"pero sigo siendo un as de los combates aéreos. Tengo 15 victorias "
"confirmadas en combates aéreos hasta ahora, y eso sin tener en cuenta las "
"operaciones secretas en las que he participado.\n"
"   \"Así que, de camino, te seguiré con mi Vendetta civil y sólo tendrás que "
"llamarme si quieres que haga algo especial. Durante la extracción, me "
"centraré en los drones para que puedas enfrentarte a la nave principal. En "
"el camino de vuelta, tomaremos caminos separados. Despegaremos cuando tú lo "
"decidas.\""

msgid "Ready for action?"
msgstr "¿Preparado para la acción?"

msgid ""
"Are you ready to start \"Operation Drugstore Thunder\"? (Hamfresser named "
"it.)"
msgstr ""
"¿Estás listo para comenzar la \"Operación Trueno de Farmacia\"? (Hamfresser "
"la nombró.)"

msgid "At the hospital"
msgstr "Al hospital"

msgid ""
"After giving the signal to Hamfresser, you enter the cockpit of your ship "
"and start the engines in anticipation of an escape. A heavy explosion coming "
"from the distance shakes your ship, followed by detonations that seem to "
"grow closer. After a while, you see the commandos running in your direction, "
"pursued by Za'lek police androids. When the last member of the team enters "
"the ship, you take off in a hurry, closely followed by a few drones. \"We "
"made a mess, out there!\" Says Hamfresser \"But at least we've got the "
"device!\""
msgstr ""
"Tras dar la señal a Hamfresser, entras en la cabina de tu nave y enciendes "
"los motores en previsión de una huida. Una fuerte explosión procedente de la "
"distancia sacude tu nave, seguida de detonaciones que parecen acercarse. Al "
"cabo de un rato, ves a los comandos corriendo en tu dirección, perseguidos "
"por los androides de la policía Za'lek. Cuando el último miembro del equipo "
"entra en la nave, despegas a toda prisa, seguido de cerca por unos cuantos "
"drones. \"¡Hemos hecho un lío, ahí fuera!\" Dice Hamfresser \"¡Pero al menos "
"tenemos el dispositivo!\""

msgid ""
"Escape to {pnt} in {sys}. Do NOT destroy any occupied Za'lek ship (only "
"drones are allowed)"
msgstr ""
"Escapa a {pnt} en {sys}. NO destruir ninguna nave Za'lek ocupada (sólo se "
"permiten los drones)"

#. Test to see if the player killed a zlk inhabited ship
msgid "The mission failed"
msgstr "La misión falló"

msgid "The rule was not to kill anybody, did you forget?"
msgstr "La regla era no matar a nadie, ¿lo has olvidado?"

#. Intercept the ship
#. At first jump, it gets announced that you've got to land
msgid "Journey to the other side"
msgstr "Viaje al otro lado"

msgid ""
"After outrunning your enemies, you start asking how the operation went at "
"the hospital. A quick look in your living quarters gives you an answer. You "
"see the VIP, still unconscious, his body covered by electrodes connected to "
"the medical device. However, he is no longer blue. Next to him, the "
"commandos look like they've had better days. Hamfresser, his face as pale as "
"death, sits on the ground, leaning on a pillar, busy changing a ragged, "
"blood-soaked bandage on his left arm. Sergeant Nikolov stares at a huge hole "
"in her foot with a vacant eye and the medic, Therus, limps from one soldier "
"to another leaving a trail of bloody handprints on the walls.\n"
"   Lying in the centre of the room, covered with bandages, is private Tronk. "
"His battle armour, pierced with multiple holes, has been tossed a few metres "
"away in a puddle of blood. With a sad smile, the soldier gazes at the two "
"remaining fingers of his less damaged arm that are slowly walking on the "
"ground. \"Leopold, you remember when you were a kid? Did you play with your "
"fingers like that?\" Hamfresser answers: \"Tronky-boy, don't use my first "
"name, only dying people have used my first name before...\" \"Don't be "
"afraid, this won't change, Leopold.\"\n"
"   Suddenly, the soldier opens his eyes wide and calls the medic: \"Therus! "
"I know why Major Tam can catch the turtle! Each time, when he reaches the "
"point where the turtle previously was, the time he needs for that is "
"smaller. And at some point, it becomes so infinitely small that even if you "
"have an infinity of steps to go, the total time is finite.\" The medic looks "
"at the dying man: \"Tronky, how did you? Tronky?\" She then stops and takes "
"the pulse at Tronk's neck \"It's over, captain.\" Hamfresser answers: "
"\"Damn! He's the fifth kid to die under my command and it still hurts as "
"much. I just can't get used to that.\""
msgstr ""
"Tras dejar atrás a tus enemigos, empiezas a preguntar cómo ha ido la "
"operación en el hospital. Un rápido vistazo a tu vivienda te da la "
"respuesta. Ves al VIP, todavía inconsciente, con el cuerpo cubierto de "
"electrodos conectados al aparato médico. Sin embargo, ya no está azul. A su "
"lado, los comandos parecen haber tenido días mejores. Hamfresser, con el "
"rostro pálido como la muerte, está sentado en el suelo, apoyado en un pilar, "
"ocupado en cambiar un vendaje harapiento y empapado de sangre en su brazo "
"izquierdo. La Sargento Nikolov mira un enorme agujero en su pie con los ojos "
"vacíos y el médico, Therus, cojea de un soldado a otro dejando un rastro de "
"huellas de manos ensangrentadas en las paredes.\n"
"   En el centro de la sala, cubierto de vendas, se encuentra el soldado "
"Tronk. Su armadura de combate, perforada con múltiples agujeros, ha sido "
"arrojada a unos metros de distancia en un charco de sangre. Con una sonrisa "
"triste, el soldado mira los dos dedos que le quedan de su brazo menos dañado "
"y que caminan lentamente por el suelo. \"Leopold, ¿recuerdas cuando eras un "
"niño? ¿Jugabas así con los dedos?\". responde Hamfresser: \"Tronky-boy, no "
"uses mi nombre de pila, sólo los moribundos han usado mi nombre de pila "
"antes...\" \"No tengas miedo, esto no va a cambiar, Leopold\".\n"
"   De repente, el soldado abre mucho los ojos y llama al médico: \"¡Therus! "
"¡Ya sé por qué el Mayor Tam puede atrapar la tortuga! Cada vez, cuando llega "
"al punto donde antes estaba la tortuga, el tiempo que necesita para ello es "
"menor. Y en un momento dado, se hace tan infinitamente pequeño que, aunque "
"tenga una infinidad de pasos que dar, el tiempo total es finito\". El médico "
"mira al moribundo: \"Tronky, ¿cómo lo has hecho? ¿Tronky?\" Luego se detiene "
"y toma el pulso en el cuello de Tronk \"Se acabó, capitán\". Hamfresser "
"responde: \"¡Maldición! Es el quinto chico que muere bajo mi mando y sigue "
"doliendo igual. No puedo acostumbrarme a eso.\""

#. give him top equipment
#. TODO switch to equipopt
#. Behaviour
#. /!\ We did not claim this system /!#. In the case the player successfully lands or uses an hypergate.
#. Taking off is already managed by the enter hook.
#. Empire Blocus:
#. /!\ We did not claim this system /!#. Special case: jump from dealsys to dealjump
#. Functions for the escort
msgid "Mission Failed: escort destroyed"
msgstr "Misión Fallida: escolta destruida"

msgid "Your escort died. You have to abort the mission"
msgstr "Tu escolta ha muerto. Tienes que abortar la misión"

msgid "A new passenger"
msgstr "Un nuevo pasajero"

msgid ""
"The commandos gather near the airlock. This time, four combat androids are "
"in the front. Hamfresser gives his orders and the first android smashes the "
"enemy ship's airlock with its fist. After that, the team rushes into the "
"ship and explosions start to thunder. Before long, the team returns. Nikolov "
"enters first, carrying an immobile and blue man in prison garb, followed by "
"Hamfresser, followed by the medic, Therus, who is busily applying compresses "
"on a large bloody wound on the captain's side, and by Tronk, who seems to be "
"busy trying to explain himself. After that come the androids, which seem to "
"have received heavy damage. You jump into the cockpit and start the engines."
msgstr ""
"Los comandos se reúnen cerca de la esclusa. Esta vez, cuatro androides de "
"combate están al frente. Hamfresser da sus órdenes y el primer androide "
"destroza la esclusa de la nave enemiga con su puño. Después de eso, el "
"equipo se precipita hacia la nave y las explosiones comienzan a retumbar. Al "
"poco tiempo, el equipo regresa. Primero entra Nikolov, que lleva a un hombre "
"inmóvil y azul con vestimenta de presidiario, seguido de Hamfresser, seguido "
"del médico, Therus, que se afana en aplicar compresas en una gran herida "
"sangrienta en el costado del capitán, y de Tronk, que parece estar ocupado "
"tratando de explicarse. Después vienen los androides, que parecen haber "
"recibido grandes daños. Saltas a la cabina y enciendes los motores."

msgid ""
"You were supposed to disable that ship, not destroy it. How are you supposed "
"to free anyone now?"
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías incapacitar esa nave, no destruirla. ¿Cómo se supone "
"que vas a liberar a alguien ahora?"

msgid ""
"You were supposed to disable that ship, not let it escape. How are you "
"supposed to free anyone now?"
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías incapacitar esa nave, no dejarla escapar. ¿Cómo se "
"supone que vas a liberar a alguien ahora?"

#. Hamfresser explains that we need to land at an hospital
msgid "We are in trouble"
msgstr "Tenemos problemas"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"When you finally jump out, Hamfresser reports: \"We hit an unexpected "
"situation back there. After we destroyed the androids and got to the jail "
"cell, we saw that there were three other prisoners along with the target, "
"and far more human guards than expected. They blew up our first assault bot, "
"and we had to take them down with the paralysers, but one of the prisoners "
"grabbed a weapon and, for some reason, started to fire on us. Fortunately "
"for me, he just pierced my lung. That is a replaceable part.\n"
"   \"Then, Tronk paralysed all the prisoners, and we identified and "
"recovered the target. That's why the guy is blue, actually. But in his "
"hurry, Tronk used the extra-strength dose. According to the medic, it is "
"worse that we first thought. Apparently, she can keep the guy alive for a "
"few periods, but she needs a special medical device to save him. So at our "
"next stop, I'm afraid we will have to steal the device at the spaceport's "
"hospital. It really annoys me as that's the kind of operation that can get "
"ugly very quickly, especially since we're still wanted by the Za'leks, but "
"we have no choice. I'll just be waiting for your signal at the bar next time "
"we land.\n"
"   \"If I may, I'd advise you to land somewhere within a quarter of a "
"period, otherwise the VIP is likely to die. Choose a place with a shipyard "
"and an outfitter so that you'll be able to prepare your ship in case we need "
"to escape quickly.\""
msgstr ""
"Cuando finalmente saltas, Hamfresser informa: \"Nos encontramos con una "
"situación inesperada allí. Después de destruir a los androides y llegar a la "
"celda de la cárcel, vimos que había otros tres prisioneros junto con el "
"objetivo, y muchos más guardias humanos de lo esperado. Volaron nuestro "
"primer robot de asalto y tuvimos que derribarlos con los paralizadores, pero "
"uno de los prisioneros cogió un arma y, por alguna razón, empezó a "
"dispararnos. Afortunadamente para mí, sólo me perforó el pulmón. Esa es una "
"parte reemplazable.\n"
"   \"Entonces, Tronk paralizó a todos los prisioneros y nosotros "
"identificamos y recuperamos el objetivo. Por eso el tipo es azul, en "
"realidad. Pero en su prisa, Tronk usó la dosis extra fuerte. Según el "
"médico, es peor de lo que pensábamos al principio. Aparentemente, puede "
"mantener al tipo con vida durante unos períodos, pero necesita un "
"dispositivo médico especial para salvarlo. Así que en nuestra próxima "
"parada, me temo que tendremos que robar el dispositivo en el hospital del "
"puerto espacial. Me molesta mucho, ya que es el tipo de operación que puede "
"ponerse fea muy rápidamente, sobre todo porque todavía nos buscan los "
"Za'leks, pero no tenemos otra opción. Esperaré tu señal en el bar la próxima "
"vez que aterricemos.\n"
"   \"Si me lo permites, te aconsejo que aterrices en algún lugar dentro de "
"los 3 periodos, de lo contrario es probable que el VIP muera. Elige un lugar "
"con un astillero y un armador para que puedas preparar tu nave en caso de "
"que necesitemos escapar rápidamente.\""

msgid ""
"Land anywhere to let Hamfresser steal a medical device. Time left: {time}"
msgstr ""
"Aterriza en cualquier lugar para que Hamfresser robe un dispositivo médico. "
"Tiempo restante: {time}"

msgid ""
"Hamfresser rushes to the bridge. \"All is lost, {player}! The guy died. Our "
"mission failed!\""
msgstr ""
"Hamfresser corre hacia el puente. \"¡Todo está perdido, {player}! El tipo ha "
"muerto. ¡Nuestra misión ha fracasado!\""

#. Player takes off from planet after attacking the hospital
#. Clear all Zlk pilots in a given radius of the player to avoid being insta-killed at takeoff
#. Drones are after the player after the hospital attack
#. This says that at next jump, Tronk will die
#. Spawns a group of civilian ships whose role is to discover a stealth player
#. Spawn blockade ships
#. 0 disables the stuff so it's unusable
#. 0 disables the stuff so it's unusable
#. The player sees the blocus fleet
#. avoid having that happening twice in systems where there are 2 blocus
msgid "Troubles straight ahead!"
msgstr "¡Problemas de frente!"

msgid ""
"As you approach the jump point, your sensors pick up a squadron of military "
"ships in a tight formation near the jump point. No doubt those ships are "
"waiting for you, and it seems foolhardy to try to run the blockade."
msgstr ""
"Cuando te acercas al punto de salto, tus sensores detectan un escuadrón de "
"naves militares en formación cerrada cerca del punto de salto. Sin duda, "
"esas naves te están esperando, y parece imprudente tratar de burlar el "
"bloqueo."

#. TODO if possible: choose the right squad
#. Strafer enters the system
msgid "Trader Gawain"
msgstr "Comerciante Gawain"

#. Why do some ship still attack him ?
#. Don't know. Workaround:
#. The player discuss with Strafer
msgid "A friend in the dark"
msgstr "Un amigo en la oscuridad"

msgid ""
"The Gawain hails you. When you respond, you hear a familiar voice. \"Strafer "
"here. I was wondering what was taking you so long. It looks like you had "
"trouble with the Za'lek after all. There are blockades in {1}, {2}, {3} and "
"{4}. They scan all ships. You have no chance to cross these systems alive. "
"What did you to them to upset them like that? Anyway, I did not come empty-"
"handed. I've got as much fuel as you want. Unfortunately, I can't board you "
"as they would chase me as well, so I have jettisoned a few tanks at "
"coordinates I will give to you. Just go there and scoop them. Good luck!\""
msgstr ""
"El Gawain te llama. Cuando respondes, oyes una voz familiar. \"Aquí Strafer. "
"Me preguntaba por qué tardabas tanto. Parece que has tenido problemas con "
"los Za'lek después de todo. Hay bloqueos en {1}, {2}, {3} y {4}. Escanean "
"todas las naves. No tienes ninguna posibilidad de cruzar estos sistemas con "
"vida. ¿Qué les has hecho para molestarlos así? De todos modos, no vine con "
"las manos vacías. Tengo todo el combustible que quieras. Desgraciadamente, "
"no puedo abordarte ya que me perseguirían también, así que he lanzado unos "
"cuantos tanques en unas coordenadas que te daré. Sólo tienes que ir allí y "
"recogerlos. ¡Buena suerte!\""

msgid "Tanks of usable fuel."
msgstr "Tanques de combustible utilizables."

#. Lasts for an houer
msgid "FUEL"
msgstr "COMBUSTIBLE"

#. Player gathers fuel
#. Only care about fuel
msgid "You filled your fuel tanks."
msgstr "Has llenado los depósitos de combustible."

#. Remove scan hooks
#. Put Agents at the bar when landing/loading
msgid "Fake transponder dealer"
msgstr "Distribuidor de falsos transpondedores"

msgid ""
"This shifty person is for sure one of the pirates that wants to sell you a "
"fake transponder."
msgstr ""
"Esta persona sospechosa es seguramente uno de los piratas que quiere "
"venderte un falso transpondedor."

msgid "Feather-hat agent"
msgstr "Agente del sombrero de pluma"

msgid ""
"The Imperial agent looks like a nondescript trader, as there are so many in "
"Imperial space."
msgstr ""
"El agente imperial parece un comerciante indescriptible, como hay muchos en "
"el espacio Imperial."

#. Spawns the odd imperial pilot
msgid "Strange Pilot"
msgstr "Piloto Extraño"

#. Don't wreck my Captain HewHew
msgid "Help offer"
msgstr "Oferta de ayuda"

msgid ""
"The pilot of the ship addresses you with a strange and disturbing "
"familiarity: \"Doing well, folks? Ya just walked into those Za'lek freaks' "
"space, wrecked a squadron, helped a prisoner escape, and demolished a "
"hospital. You're worse than the Incident, mates!\" You wonder how this pilot "
"could know so much about your operation, but his spiel continues: "
"\"Hewhewhew! People usually think I'm some sort of useless pirates scum. I "
"know you thought that, too! Neh, don't lie to me!\"\n"
"   The pilot's voice suddenly becomes harsh: \"In reality, I am a faithful "
"subject of his Imperial Majesty, as should you be, {player}! But instead "
"you've chosen to aid and abet those criminals, the Dvaereds. For that you "
"should be severely punished. Don't forget, {player}: The Empire is watching "
"you. Anywhere. Anytime. Anyhow.\n"
"   \"Hewhewhew! And what was the other one already? Oh yeah: The Emperor "
"sees all! But ya're all lucky, 'cause the Empire is in a merciful mood "
"today. So at your next stop, you will kindly go and talk to the agent with a "
"feather hat, and the two of you will reach an agreement, and hopefully we "
"won't have to kill you!\""
msgstr ""
"El piloto de la nave se dirige a ti con una extraña e inquietante "
"familiaridad: \"¿Os va bien, amigos? Acabáis de entrar en el espacio de esos "
"monstruos Za'lek, habéis destrozado un escuadrón, habéis ayudado a escapar a "
"un prisionero y habéis demolido un hospital. Sois peores que el Incidente, "
"compañeros\". Te preguntas cómo este piloto puede saber tanto sobre tu "
"operación, pero su discurso continúa: \"¡Hewhewhew! La gente suele pensar "
"que soy una especie de escoria pirata inútil. ¡Sé que tú también pensabas "
"eso! Neh, ¡no me mientas!\"\n"
"   La voz del piloto se vuelve repentinamente áspera: \"¡En realidad, soy un "
"fiel súbdito de su Majestad Imperial, como deberías serlo tú, {player}! Pero "
"en lugar de eso has elegido ayudar e instigar a esos criminales, los "
"Dvaereds. Por eso deberías ser severamente castigado. No lo olvides, "
"{player}: El Imperio te está observando. En cualquier lugar. En cualquier "
"momento. En cualquier caso.\n"
"   \"¡Hewhewhew! ¿Y cuál era ya la otra? Oh sí: ¡El Emperador lo ve todo! "
"Pero tenéis suerte, porque el Imperio está hoy de un humor misericordioso. "
"Así que en vuestra próxima parada, tendréis la amabilidad de ir a hablar con "
"el agente con sombrero de pluma, y los dos llegaréis a un acuerdo y, con "
"suerte, ¡no tendremos que mataros!\""

msgid ""
"Do you accept the deal with the pirates? It costs {price}, and you'll be "
"able to skirt any Imperial blockades."
msgstr ""
"¿Aceptas el trato con los piratas? Cuesta {price}, y podrás eludir cualquier "
"bloqueo Imperial."

msgid "Accept, immediate payment"
msgstr "Aceptar, pago inmediato"

msgid "Accept, deferred payment"
msgstr "Aceptar, pago aplazado"

msgid "Immediate payment"
msgstr "Pago inmediato"

msgid ""
"When you hand over the credit chips, the pirate looks surprised: \"Whow, "
"mate, I didn't know I was talking to a millionaire. Well then thanks, here "
"is your transponder.\""
msgstr ""
"Cuando le entregas las fichas de crédito, el pirata parece sorprendido: "
"\"Vaya, amigo, no sabía que estaba hablando con un millonario. Pues gracias, "
"aquí tienes tu transpondedor.\""

msgid ""
"Escape to {pnt} in {sys}. Thanks to your new, fake transponder, the "
"squadrons should not stop you any more"
msgstr ""
"Escapa a {pnt} en {sys}. Gracias a tu nuevo y falso transpondedor, los "
"escuadrones ya no deberían detenerte"

msgid "Not enough money"
msgstr "No hay suficiente dinero"

msgid ""
"\"Don't try to trick me, crook! I can see from here that you don't have "
"enough money!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡No intentes engañarme, sinvergüenza! ¡Puedo ver desde aquí que no tienes "
"suficiente dinero!\""

msgid "Pirate debt"
msgstr "Deuda pirata"

msgid ""
"\"Here is your transponder,\" the pirate says. \"Don't forget to pay once "
"you can, otherwise...\""
msgstr ""
"\"Aquí está tu transpondedor\", dice el pirata. \"No te olvides de pagar "
"cuando puedas, si no...\""

msgid "You're way too expensive"
msgstr "Es demasiado caro"

msgid ""
"\"As you wish,\" says the pirate. \"Come back when you realize that I'm your "
"only chance!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Como quieras\", dice el pirata. \"¡Vuelve cuando te des cuenta de que soy "
"tu única oportunidad!\""

msgid "Deal with the Empire"
msgstr "Trato con el Imperio"

msgid ""
"As you approach, the agent seems to recognize you immediately. \"Hello, "
"{player}. I guess they told you that I may have a solution to your little... "
"problem.\" You look suspiciously at the agent and ask: \"What do you want in "
"exchange?\" The agent smiles: \"Simple. I want to speak with the Dvaered "
"captain. Give me 10 hectostu on the spacedock alone with him, not more, and "
"the commander of the fleet in {dealsys} will forget to scan your ship when "
"you jump to {dealjump}.\"\n"
"   This is certainly an unusual request. You think of all the state secrets "
"a wounded Hamfresser is able to give to the Empire in 10 hectostu. But, "
"Hamfresser is a professional after all, trained avoid revealing any valuable "
"information. But, probably the Imperial agent is a professional as well, "
"trained to recover valuable information. And the pirate proposition still "
"holds. So you answer:"
msgstr ""

msgid "You made the only good choice"
msgstr "Has hecho la única buena elección"

msgid ""
"After accepting, you invite the agent to follow you to the dock. You enter "
"your ship, where the commandos are waiting for you, and inform Hamfresser "
"about the situation. He anxiously looks at the two other remaining members "
"of his team. Nikolov grimaces and Therus nervously hits the wall. \"If you "
"think we have no other choice...\" says the captain. After removing his "
"uniform jacket (where his name and rank are written), Hamfresser takes a "
"deep breath and joins the Imperial agent outside, in front of the ship. From "
"a window, you see them having what looks like a peaceful conversation.\n"
"   After a while, Hamfresser returns to the ship and the agent waves to "
"indicate that you're allowed to take off. Nikolov asks her captain: \"And?\" "
"\"Who knows what these Imperial weirdos wanted to know? I tried to dodge all "
"the questions, but... well... You never know.\""
msgstr ""
"Tras aceptar, invitas al agente a que te siga hasta el muelle. Entra en tu "
"nave, donde te esperan los comandos, e informa a Hamfresser de la situación. "
"Éste mira con ansiedad a los otros dos miembros restantes de tu equipo. "
"Nikolov hace una mueca y Therus golpea nerviosamente la pared. \"Si crees "
"que no tenemos otra opción...\", dice el capitán. Tras quitarse la chaqueta "
"del uniforme (donde están escritos su nombre y su rango), Hamfresser respira "
"profundamente y se une al agente imperial en el exterior, frente a la nave. "
"Desde una ventana, se les ve manteniendo lo que parece una conversación "
"tranquila.\n"
"   Al cabo de un rato, Hamfresser vuelve a la nave y el agente le hace un "
"gesto para indicarle que puede despegar. Nikolov pregunta a su capitán: \"¿Y?"
"\" \"¿Quién sabe qué querían saber esos raros imperiales? Intenté esquivar "
"todas las preguntas, pero... bueno... Nunca se sabe.\""

msgid ""
"Escape to {pnt} in {sys}. Thanks to your deal with the Empire, the squadron "
"in {dealsys} won't prevent you from jumping to {dealjump}"
msgstr ""
"Escapa a {pnt} en {sys}. Gracias a tu acuerdo con el Imperio, el escuadrón "
"en {dealsys} no te impedirá saltar a {dealjump}"

msgid "That was the wrong answer"
msgstr "Esa fue la respuesta equivocada"

msgid ""
"\"Mwell.\" Says the agent. \"I guess you need to see for yourself that this "
"is the only solution. If you're still alive when you're done, come back, we "
"will be waiting for you.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Bien\". Dice el agente. \"Supongo que tienes que ver por ti mismo que esta "
"es la única solución. Si sigues vivo cuando termines, vuelve, te estaremos "
"esperando.\""

msgid "Shock of two worlds"
msgstr "Choque de dos mundos"

msgid ""
"You hear an unusual and agitated voice coming from the living quarters. When "
"you get there, you see that the VIP is back on his feet. \"To sum up, a "
"Dvaered general, whose name you won't disclose, sent you to free me from the "
"Za'lek, for reasons you won't explain, right?\" Hamfresser answers: "
"\"Totally correct, sir.\"\n"
"   The executive moans and shakes his head \"You Dvaered are foolish! Do you "
"think that violence is the solution to any problem?\" Hamfresser seems "
"surprised \"Is there any other way to solve a problem?\" The VIP then looks "
"at you: \"Hey, you seem a bit less brutish than the others... You're not a "
"Dvaered, right? You know what? My grandma was always saying that the Dvaered "
"and the Za'lek were the worst in the universe. And she was right. First, the "
"Za'lek imprisoned me under the bogus charge of 'scientific embezzlement', "
"and now, you Dvaered storm your way to my cell and kidnap me.\"\n"
"   Hamfresser defends himself: \"But sir, if the operation succeeds, you'll "
"be back to business very soon. Isn't that wonderful?\" \"... and if the "
"operation fails, we all die! No, strong-arm! Patience, negotiation, bribing, "
"and craftiness can achieve much more than violence and destruction. I had "
"hired the best lawyers in Za'lek space and my assistants negotiated with the "
"authorities -- I was sure to get out in about half a cycle.\" Hamfresser "
"simply raises his shoulders: \"Dvaered warriors don't use deception, nor "
"patience, nor craftiness. Dvaered warriors use respectable methods instead, "
"like violence and destruction.\""
msgstr ""
"Oyes una voz inusual y agitada procedente de la sala de estar. Cuando llegas "
"allí, ves que el VIP está de nuevo en pie. \"Resumiendo, un general Dvaered, "
"cuyo nombre no quieres revelar, te ha enviado para que me liberes del "
"Za'lek, por razones que no quieres explicar, ¿verdad?\". Responde "
"Hamfresser: \"Totalmente correcto, señor\".\n"
"   El ejecutivo gime y sacude la cabeza \"¡Ustedes los Dvaered son unos "
"tontos! ¿Crees que la violencia es la solución a cualquier problema?\" "
"Hamfresser parece sorprendido \"¿Hay alguna otra forma de resolver un "
"problema?\" El VIP te mira entonces: \"Oye, pareces un poco menos bruto que "
"los demás... No eres un Dvaered, ¿verdad? ¿Sabes qué? Mi abuela siempre "
"decía que los Dvaered y los Za'lek eran los peores del universo. Y tenía "
"razón. Primero, los Za'lek me encarcelaron bajo la falsa acusación de "
"'malversación científica', y ahora, vosotros los Dvaered irrumpís en mi "
"celda y me secuestráis\".\n"
"   Hamfresser se defiende: \"Pero señor, si la operación tiene éxito, usted "
"volverá a los negocios muy pronto. ¿No es maravilloso?\" \"... y si la "
"operación falla, ¡todos moriremos! ¡No, mano dura! La paciencia, la "
"negociación, el soborno y la astucia pueden lograr mucho más que la "
"violencia y la destrucción. Contraté a los mejores abogados del espacio "
"Za'lek y mis ayudantes negociaron con las autoridades: estaba seguro de "
"salir en medio ciclo\". Hamfresser simplemente levanta los hombros: \"Los "
"guerreros Dvaered no utilizan el engaño, ni la paciencia, ni la astucia. Los "
"guerreros Dvaered utilizan en cambio métodos respetables, como la violencia "
"y la destrucción.\""

#. Aborting if mem.stage >= 4: reset zlk reputation
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Dvaered Diplomacy">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>2</priority>
#. <chance>30</chance>
#. <done>Dvaered Escape</done>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <faction>Dvaered</faction>
#. <cond>var.peek("dv_pirate_debt") == false</cond>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Frontier Invasion</campaign>
#. <done_evt name="Repay General Klank"/>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Dvaered Diplomacy
#. -- It does not go together well, does it?
#. -- This is the 4th mission of the Frontier War Dvaered campaign.
#. -- The player has to trap and kill a group of assassins who are after Major Tam
#.
#. Stages :
#. 0) On the way (can leave the system)
#. 1) Looking for hostiles (cannot leave the system)
#. 2) Land to get rewarded
#. 3) Pursuit: cleaning the first system before jumping
#. 4) Pursuit: you may jump after the target
#. 5) Pursuit: cleaning the first system before landing
#. 6) Pursuit: you may land after the target
#. --
#. Non-persistent state
#. Forward-declared functions
#. common hooks
#. Mission constants
msgid ""
"\"Good question, citizen! It is likely the intelligence services of the "
"other nations know that General Klank and I are involved in the invasion "
"project. Though, they probably don't know how imminent it is. It's likely "
"they hired henchmen to hound or outright stop us. We have identified some of "
"the henchmen, actually. They are the kind of independent mercenaries we find "
"in any kind of shady operations... A bit like you in fact.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Buena pregunta, ciudadano! Es probable que los servicios de inteligencia "
"de las otras naciones sepan que el general Klank y yo estamos involucrados "
"en el proyecto de invasión. Aunque es probable que no sepan lo inminente que "
"es. Es probable que hayan contratado esbirros para acosar o directamente "
"detenernos. Hemos identificado a algunos de los secuaces en realidad. Son el "
"tipo de mercenarios independientes que encontramos en cualquier tipo de "
"operaciones turbias... Un poco como tú, de hecho.\""

msgid ""
"\"Aha! You're worrying about the soldiers of the warlord we killed last "
"time? Don't worry too much about them, most of them did not stay unemployed "
"for long. When a warlord dies, his surviving followers are sent to the "
"Dvaered Military Reserve, and they apply for positions in other warlords' "
"armies, or in the DHC. The only one I'm worried about is Colonel Hamelsen: "
"it will be very difficult for her to find a position with a warlord since "
"they prefer to have people they know at higher ranks, and the DHC only "
"rarely recruits new colonels.\n"
"   \"That's a pity actually because she is probably the most talented "
"officer of her generation. Do you know that she was the first one since the "
"Independence War who managed to become an ace before the end of her training?"
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Ahá! ¿Te preocupas por los soldados del señor de la guerra que matamos la "
"última vez? No te preocupes demasiado por ellos, la mayoría no permaneció "
"mucho tiempo en el paro. Cuando un señor de la guerra muere, sus seguidores "
"supervivientes son enviados a la Reserva Militar Dvaered, y solicitan "
"puestos en los ejércitos de otros señores de la guerra, o en el AMD. La "
"única que me preocupa es la coronel Hamelsen: le resultará muy difícil "
"encontrar un puesto con un señor de la guerra, ya que prefieren tener a "
"gente conocida en los rangos superiores, y el AMD rara vez recluta nuevos "
"coroneles.\n"
"   \"Es una pena, porque probablemente sea la oficial con más talento de su "
"generación. ¿Sabes que fue la primera desde la Guerra de la Independencia "
"que consiguió convertirse en un as antes de terminar su formación?\""

msgid ""
"You ask Major Tam to continue his story about when he used to be a fighter "
"pilot at the DHC base on Rhaana. A small smile appears on his face, and he "
"turns his eyes to the ceiling.\n"
"   \"Do you want me to tell you how I became an ace? Oh yes, you do. So. To "
"become a Dvaered ace, one has to score four confirmed fighter victories. A "
"confirmed victory is recorded when you, alone, destroy any kind of enemy "
"warship. As we tend to work in squads, we pretty often destroy ships without "
"scoring any confirmed victories. My first victory was a Pirate Hyena. The "
"pilot was probably drunk or something. They headed right towards my "
"Vendetta, broadcasting stupid taunts. My sergeant was nice and left the "
"Hyena all to me. My second victory was against a freak... I mean a local "
"warlord's pilot who claimed she could kill any DHC pilot in fair fight. "
"Apparently, it was not true.\n"
"   \"But the two others... Actually those are a much longer story. I'll tell "
"you another time, maybe.\""
msgstr ""
"Le pides al Mayor Tam que continúe su historia sobre cuando era piloto de "
"caza en la base de AMD en Rhaana. Una pequeña sonrisa aparece en su rostro y "
"vuelve los ojos hacia el cielo.\n"
"   \"¿Quiere que le cuente cómo me convertí en un as? Ah, sí, quieres. Así "
"que... Para llegar a ser un as Dvaered, uno tiene que conseguir cuatro "
"victorias confirmadas en el combate. Una victoria confirmada se registra "
"cuando uno, solo, destruye cualquier tipo de nave de guerra enemiga. Como "
"solemos trabajar en escuadrones, a menudo destruimos naves sin anotar "
"ninguna victoria confirmada. Mi primera victoria fue un Hiena Pirata. El "
"piloto estaba probablemente borracho o algo así. Se dirigió directamente "
"hacia mi Vendetta, emitiendo estúpidas burlas. Mi sargento fue amable y me "
"dejó a la Hiena toda para mí. Mi segunda victoria fue contra un monstruo... "
"Me refiero a una piloto de un señor de la guerra local que afirmaba que "
"podía matar a cualquier piloto del AMD en una lucha justa. Aparentemente, no "
"era cierto.\n"
"   \"Pero las otras dos... En realidad esas son una historia mucho más "
"larga. Te la contaré en otro momento quizás.\""

msgid ""
"\"Oh, the captain is doing well. He spent a few periods at the hospital, but "
"it was not so serious. The rest of his squad, I'm not too sure. I don't know "
"them very well, actually. They are more like statistics to me. I know it's "
"bad, but hey, I have so many things to think about right now.\n"
"   \"Oh, and we went to the funeral of private Amadeus Tronk, officially "
"killed in training, of course. It was nice. Leblanc's squadron made an "
"aerial display with a mace rocket concerto for the occasion, and we "
"organized a fight to death between a convicted criminal and a gladiator in "
"General Klank's private arena. Not only to honour the memory of the dead "
"warrior, but also to have some fun.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oh, el capitán está bien. Pasó algunos períodos en el hospital, pero no "
"fue tan grave. El resto de su escuadrón, no estoy muy seguro. En realidad no "
"los conozco muy bien. Son más bien estadísticas para mí. Sé que es malo, "
"pero oye, tengo muchas cosas en las que pensar ahora mismo.\n"
"   \"Ah, y fuimos al funeral del soldado Amadeus Tronk, oficialmente muerto "
"en el entrenamiento, por supuesto. Fue bonito. El escuadrón de Leblanc hizo "
"una exhibición aérea con un concierto de cohetes de mazas para la ocasión, y "
"organizamos una lucha a muerte entre un criminal convicto y un gladiador en "
"la arena privada del general Klank. No sólo para honrar la memoria del "
"guerrero muerto, sino también para divertirnos un poco.\""

msgid ""
"You were supposed to wait for Strafer to scan the system, and then if "
"needed, kill the hostiles."
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías esperar a que Strafer escaneara el sistema, y luego, "
"si era necesario, matar a los hostiles."

msgid ""
"Two of your targets went away. If there was only one, it could be "
"salvageable, but now, the mission has failed."
msgstr ""
"Dos de sus objetivos han desaparecido. Si sólo hubiera uno, podría ser "
"salvable, pero ahora, la misión ha fracasado."

msgid "The major seems to be waiting for you."
msgstr "El mayor parece estar esperándote."

msgid "Ready for some diplomacy?"
msgstr "¿Preparado para la diplomacia?"

msgid ""
"Major Tam seems to be in a very good mood: \"Hello, citizen {player}! Have "
"you got plans for tonight?\" You fear he might invite you to a brawl-party, "
"or some other kind of event Dvaered usually organize when they want to have "
"good time, but he continues: \"Because I've got a very important mission for "
"you.\n"
"   \"Let me explain: I am currently in the middle of a secret diplomatic "
"campaign with the Imperials, House Goddard, and the Sirii. But a group of "
"assassins is constantly harassing me as I travel. This is very annoying, and "
"we have already lost two pilots of Leblanc's squadron in these ambushes, "
"including the second in command. The attackers use a mix of fighters "
"supported by medium ships. They even have a Kestrel!\n"
"   \"So we have decided to deal with them before we proceed with the "
"diplomatic meetings. Are you in?\""
msgstr ""
"El Mayor Tam parece estar de muy buen humor: \"¡Hola, ciudadano {player}! "
"¿Tienes planes para esta noche?\" Temes que te invite a una pelea-fiesta, o "
"a algún otro tipo de evento que Dvaered suele organizar cuando quiere pasar "
"un buen rato, pero continúa: \"Porque tengo una misión muy importante para "
"ti.\n"
"\" Déjame que te lo explique: Actualmente estoy en medio de una campaña "
"diplomática secreta con los Imperiales, la Casa Goddard y los Sirios. Pero "
"un grupo de asesinos me acosa constantemente mientras viajo. Esto es muy "
"molesto y ya hemos perdido a dos pilotos del escuadrón de Leblanc en estas "
"emboscadas, incluido el segundo al mando. Los atacantes utilizan una mezcla "
"de cazas apoyados por naves medianas. ¡Incluso tienen un cernícalo!\n"
"   \"Así que hemos decidido enfrentarnos a ellos antes de proceder a las "
"reuniones diplomáticas. ¿Te apuntas?\""

msgid "Another time maybe"
msgstr "En otra ocasión quizás"

msgid "Major Tam really seems disappointed. \"As you wish, citizen...\""
msgstr ""
"El Mayor Tam parece realmente decepcionado. \"Como quieras, ciudadano...\""

msgid "This is how we deal with our problems"
msgstr "Así es como tratamos nuestros problemas"

msgid ""
"\"You won't regret it!\" Tam says... \"Unless you're killed in the process I "
"guess... Anyway, I will go to {pnt} in {sys} in my Vigilance. No doubt the "
"assassins will set up an ambush somewhere on the way. You and a few pilots "
"from the Special Operations Force (SOF) will locate them and wait for me to "
"jump in. When they spring the ambush, the assassins will be caught in our "
"crossfire, and we will annihilate them to the last ship. Actually, that "
"sounds much more enticing than a three-period-long meeting with rogue Sirian "
"diplomats, doesn't it?\n"
"   \"Our side will not have much firepower, so I'm counting on you to arrive "
"with a lot of armour and guns (but you should still be able to outrun mid-"
"range destroyers). Because you two worked so well in the past, you'll again "
"team up with Lieutenant Strafer, and two other pilots. But the SOF does not "
"have an endless supply of pilots, so your reward will depend on how many of "
"them come back. Strafer will fly a scout with high performance sensors. He "
"will be our eyes, so his death would mean the end of the mission.\n"
"   \"If you have any additional questions, I'll stay at the bar until we "
"take off.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡No te arrepentirás!\" Tam dice... \"A menos que te maten en el proceso, "
"supongo... De todos modos, iré a {pnt} en {sys} en mi Vigilancia. Sin duda "
"los asesinos prepararán una emboscada en algún lugar del camino. Tú y unos "
"cuantos pilotos de la Fuerza de Operaciones Especiales (FOE) los "
"localizaréis y esperaréis a que yo salte. Cuando lancen la emboscada, los "
"asesinos quedarán atrapados en nuestro fuego cruzado y los aniquilaremos "
"hasta la última nave. En realidad, eso suena mucho más tentador que una "
"reunión de tres días con diplomáticos sirios renegados, ¿no es así?\n"
"   \"Nuestro bando no tendrá mucha potencia de fuego, así que cuento con que "
"lleguéis con mucho blindaje y cañones (pero deberíais ser capaces de dejar "
"atrás a los destructores de medio alcance). Como ustedes dos trabajaron tan "
"bien en el pasado, volverán a formar equipo con el teniente Strafer y otros "
"dos pilotos. Pero el FOE no tiene un suministro infinito de pilotos, así que "
"tu recompensa dependerá de cuántos de ellos vuelvan. Strafer pilotará un "
"explorador con sensores de alto rendimiento. Él será nuestros ojos, por lo "
"que su muerte significaría el fin de la misión.\n"
"   \"Si tienen alguna pregunta adicional, me quedaré en el bar hasta que "
"despeguemos.\""

#. TODO: ensure the cleaning doesn't take too long
msgid "Dvaered Diplomacy"
msgstr "Diplomacia Dvaered"

msgid "Go to next system"
msgstr "Ve al siguiente sistema"

msgid "Wait until Strafer has scanned the system"
msgstr "Espera hasta que Strafer haya escaneado el sistema"

msgid "Wait for Tam and destroy the highlighted hostile ships"
msgstr "Espera por Tam y destruye las naves hostiles resaltadas"

msgid "Land anywhere to collect your pay"
msgstr "Aterrice en cualquier lugar para cobrar tu paga"

msgid ""
"You take part in an operation to trap and destroy a group of well armed "
"henchmen who are after Major Tam."
msgstr ""
"Participas en una operación para atrapar y destruir a un grupo de secuaces "
"bien armados que persiguen al Mayor Tam."

msgid "It depends on how many of your wingmen come back."
msgstr "Depende de cuántos de tus compañeros vuelvan."

#. Discussions with Major Tam at the bar
msgid "Ask Major Tam some questions"
msgstr "Hazle algunas preguntas al Mayor Tam"

#. Instructions
msgid "What do you want to ask Major Tam?"
msgstr "¿Qué quieres preguntarle al Mayor Tam?"

msgid "Ask about the assassins"
msgstr "Pregunta por los asesinos"

msgid "Ask about Battleaddict's soldiers"
msgstr "Pregunta por los soldados de AdictoABatalla"

msgid "Ask about his deeds as fighter pilot"
msgstr "Pregunta por sus hazañas como piloto de caza"

msgid "Ask for news about Hamfresser"
msgstr "Pregunte por noticias de Hamfresser"

msgid "Goodbye, we meet in space."
msgstr "Adiós, nos encontramos en el espacio."

msgid ""
"Hey, do you think I'm some kind of amnesic? You literally asked this "
"question 10 seconds ago!"
msgstr ""
"Oye, ¿crees que soy una especie de amnésico? ¡Literalmente hiciste esta "
"pregunta hace 10 segundos!"

msgid "You were supposed to clear the system before pursuing the fleeing ship."
msgstr ""
"Se suponía que debías despejar el sistema antes de perseguir a la nave que "
"huía."

msgid "You were supposed to land on {pnt}."
msgstr "Se suponía que debías aterrizar en {pnt}."

msgid "You were supposed to jump to {sys}."
msgstr "Se supone que debes saltar a {sys}."

#. Land for reward
#. Arrived in system
#. The Gawain
#. Choose a random point in the system for him to stay around
#. The Kestrel
#. The Kestrel
#. The Goddard
#. Faction's ships come with upgraded weaponry
#. the Gawain is flying around a random point
#. the Gawain is going away
#. Are there still other pirates to kill ?
msgid "Mission accomplished"
msgstr "Misión Completada"

msgid ""
"Your mission is a success, except for the escape of the enemy leader, "
"Colonel Hamelsen. You can now collect your {credits} reward."
msgstr ""
"Tu misión ha sido un éxito, excepto por la huida del líder enemigo, el "
"Coronel Hamelsen. Ahora puedes recoger tu recompensa de {credits}."

#. Landing after an enemy (victory as well)
#. it's Hamelsen and she escapes
#. No pity for non-Hamelsen henchmen
msgid "End of the hunt"
msgstr "Fin de la caza"

msgid ""
"You land and walk around the spacedock, in search of your target's ship. You "
"finally see it. A mighty {ship}, covered in the score marks of the battle "
"that just occurred. You hide yourself behind some crates near the ship and "
"wait for the pilot to come back and take off in order to finish your job in "
"space.\n"
"   When looking closer at the ship, you see both ancient and recent marks on "
"the hull, caused by all kinds of weapons during the lifetime of the ship. "
"Among the ship's scars, you see a twisted welding around the ship's nose, "
"filled with bubbles and think: \"Damn! They had to deal with the same old "
"deficient welding android that fixed my airlock on Alteris last time!\"\n"
"   Suddenly, you realize someone whispers behind you \"Hey, {player}, you're "
"blocking my firing line!\" You turn around and see nothing but a deformed "
"crate that continues to speak: \"It's me, Sergeant Nikolov. In the box. Hide "
"yourself better or you will ruin our mission.\" You then remember that she "
"is a member of the space infantry commandos, and Hamfresser's second in "
"command. Tam probably sent her to execute the enemy pilot."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas y recorres el muelle espacial en busca de la nave de tu objetivo. "
"Finalmente la ves. Una poderosa {ship}, cubierta con las marcas de la "
"batalla que acaba de ocurrir. Te escondes detrás de unas cajas cerca de la "
"nave y esperas a que el piloto vuelva y despegue para terminar tu trabajo en "
"el espacio.\n"
"   Al mirar más de cerca la nave, ves marcas tanto antiguas como recientes "
"en el casco, causadas por todo tipo de armas durante la vida de la nave. "
"Entre las cicatrices de la nave, ves una soldadura retorcida alrededor del "
"morro de la nave, llena de burbujas y piensas: \"¡Maldita sea! Han tenido "
"que lidiar con el mismo androide soldador deficiente que arregló mi esclusa "
"en Alteris la última vez\".\n"
"   De repente, te das cuenta de que alguien susurra detrás de ti \"¡Oye, "
"{player}, estás bloqueando mi línea de tiro!\". Te das la vuelta y no ves "
"más que un cajón deformado que sigue hablando: \"Soy yo, el Sargento "
"Nikolov. En la caja. Escóndete mejor o arruinarás nuestra misión\". Entonces "
"recuerdas que ella es miembro de los comandos de infantería espacial, y la "
"segunda al mando de Hamfresser. Probablemente Tam la envió a ejecutar al "
"piloto enemigo."

msgid ""
"A few moments later, you hear a message from Nikolov's radio: \"Tam here. "
"The target escaped and won't come back to the ship. Clear the spacedock.\" "
"The spacemarines emerge from the crates and disappear in a flash, while you "
"start heading to the bar. On the way, you meet Strafer who explains the "
"situation: \"We identified the hostile pilot: it was Colonel Hamelsen, "
"Battleaddict's former second in command, but she got away using one of her "
"other ships and we lost her track.\n"
"   \"Poor woman. It's hard to get a new post when you're the second in "
"command of a dead warlord, you know. So I guess someone managed to hire her "
"to assassinate the major. Anyway, I guess you should have received your "
"payment of {credits} by now.\""
msgstr ""
"Unos momentos después, se escucha un mensaje de la radio de Nikolov: \"Aquí "
"Tam. El objetivo se ha escapado y no va a volver a la nave. Despeja el "
"muelle espacial\". Los marines espaciales salen de las cajas y desaparecen "
"en un instante, mientras tú te diriges al bar. Por el camino, os encontráis "
"con Strafer que os explica la situación: \"Hemos identificado a la piloto "
"hostil: era la coronel Hamelsen, antigua segunda al mando de AdictoABatalla, "
"pero se escapó utilizando otra de sus naves y le perdimos la pista.\n"
"   \"Pobre mujer. Es difícil conseguir un nuevo puesto cuando eres la "
"segunda al mando de un señor de la guerra muerto, ya sabes. Supongo que "
"alguien se las arregló para contratarla para asesinar al Mayor. De todos "
"modos, supongo que ya debes haber recibido tu pago de {credits}.\""

msgid ""
"A bit later, you see a woman coming from the empty corridor, anxiously "
"looking behind her and pulling a key out of her pocket. While still "
"approaching the ship, she presses the key's button and the ship beeps. At "
"that very moment, a sudden and loud fracas erupts from all around you shakes "
"your stomach. The pilot falls without a word. Nikolov and two other soldiers "
"emerge from the crates. The sergeant approaches the pilot, kneels and takes "
"her pulse. She thoughtfully looks at her face \"Damn! She looked like a nice "
"person...\" And then addresses the soldiers: \"All right, folks we pack up!"
"\" and the unit enters the ship with the body and takes off.\n"
"   You stay alone, on the empty dock, with nothing but your thoughts. Even "
"the broken crates have been picked up by the commandos. You think about all "
"the causes that pilot must have served in her life. The just causes, the "
"evil ones... and all the others. \"Meh,\" you think \"killing people in "
"space is definitely much better for morale.\""
msgstr ""
"Un poco más tarde, ves a una mujer que viene del pasillo vacío, mirando "
"ansiosamente detrás de ella y sacando una llave de su bolsillo. Mientras se "
"acerca a la nave, pulsa el botón de la llave y la nave emite un pitido. En "
"ese mismo momento, una súbita y ruidosa refriega a tu alrededor te sacude el "
"estómago. El piloto cae sin mediar palabra. Nikolov y otros dos soldados "
"salen de las cajas. El sargento se acerca al piloto, se arrodilla y le toma "
"el pulso. Se queda pensativo mirando su cara \"¡Maldita sea! Parecía una "
"buena persona...\" Y luego se dirige a los soldados: \"¡Muy bien, amigos, "
"recogemos!\" y la unidad entra en la nave con el cuerpo y despega.\n"
"   Tú te quedas solo, en el muelle vacío, sin nada más que tus pensamientos. "
"Incluso las cajas rotas han sido recogidas por los comandos. Piensas en "
"todas las causas a las que esa piloto debió servir en su vida. Las causas "
"justas, las malvadas... y todas las demás. \"Meh\", piensas \"matar gente en "
"el espacio es definitivamente mucho mejor para la moral.\""

msgid ""
"When you finally go to the bar to think about something else, you get "
"notified on your holowatch that {credits} have been transferred to your "
"account. The leader of the ambushers has been identified: it's Colonel "
"Hamelsen, who used to work for Battleaddict before his death. Unfortunately, "
"the Colonel has escaped."
msgstr ""
"Cuando por fin vas al bar a pensar en otra cosa, recibes una notificación en "
"tu holovisor de que se han transferido {credits} a tu cuenta. El líder de "
"los emboscados ha sido identificado: es la coronel Hamelsen, que trabajaba "
"para AdictoABatalla antes de su muerte. Por desgracia, la Coronel ha "
"escapado."

#. Give him nice outfits
#. TODO switch to equipopt
#. TODO: see if we want that for Strafer
#. Spawn the bad guys
#. They're mercenaries to avoid getting too high outfits
#. I love wedge formation
#. Targets
#. This variable ensure the enemies only runaway once
#. Spawn Tam and his crew
#. Strafer sees the bountyhunters
msgid "Hostiles spotted!"
msgstr "¡Hostiles detectados!"

#. Remove all the markers.
#. Strafer doesn't see anybody and returns
msgid "No hostiles here. We can proceed to next system."
msgstr "No hay hostiles aquí. Podemos proceder al siguiente sistema."

#. Baddies are in position: start the battle after a small delay
msgid "All right, let's wait for Tam"
msgstr "Muy bien, esperemos a Tam"

msgid "There will be roasted Tam for lunch today!"
msgstr "¡Habrá Tam asado para el almuerzo de hoy!"

msgid "Tam is in place, folks! Don't miss him, this time!"
msgstr "¡Tam está en su sitio, amigos! ¡No fallen, esta vez!"

#. Death hooks
#. It's Hamelsen: she escapes with a Schroedinger
#. It's the first one who escapes
#. Store target values
#. You won't follow several enemies
#. Actually, after checking, this is very unlikely to happen...
#. It's the first one who escapes
#. You won't follow several enemies
msgid "This is not good"
msgstr "Esto no es bueno"

msgid ""
"You suddenly realize that your radar no longer displays Strafer's sensor "
"data. This means the Lieutenant got killed. As a result, the fleet is flying "
"blind and the mission has failed."
msgstr ""
"De repente te das cuenta de que tu radar ya no muestra los datos del sensor "
"de Strafer. Esto significa que el Teniente ha muerto. Como resultado, la "
"flota está volando a ciegas y la misión ha fracasado."

msgid ""
"The blinking cross marked \"Major Tam\" on your radar screen suddenly turns "
"off. At first, you think your screen is buggy and hit it with your open "
"hand, but soon, you realize that the radar works perfectly well. This means "
"that the major's ship was annihilated by the ambushers, and therefore your "
"mission is a miserable failure."
msgstr ""
"La cruz parpadeante marcada como \" Mayor Tam \" en la pantalla de tu radar "
"se apaga de repente. Al principio crees que tu pantalla está estropeada y la "
"golpeas con la mano abierta, pero pronto te das cuenta de que el radar "
"funciona perfectamente. Esto significa que la nave del Mayor ha sido "
"aniquilada por los emboscados, y por tanto has fallado miserablemente tu "
"misión."

#. Start the battle
msgid "What about I cook you to death?"
msgstr "¿Qué tal si te cocino hasta la muerte?"

#. Baddie death
#. See if it's one of the 3 targets
msgid "One of the targets was destroyed!"
msgstr "¡Uno de los objetivos fue destruido!"

msgid "All targets eliminated"
msgstr "Todos los objetivos eliminados"

msgid ""
"All three primary targets have been eliminated. The remaining ones are no "
"longer a threat. You can land to get your reward."
msgstr ""
"Los tres objetivos principales han sido eliminados. Los restantes ya no son "
"una amenaza. Puedes aterrizar para obtener tu recompensa."

#. Killed the last enemy after the pursuit
msgid "The last target was destroyed! You can now land."
msgstr "¡El último objetivo fue destruido! Ya puedes aterrizar."

msgid ""
"While your sensors lose track of the target you were supposed to kill, you "
"expect to receive a mission failure message, but instead, you hear Tam's "
"ship communication: \"One of them escaped. Continue destroying the others. "
"Afterwards, {player}, you will jump to {sys} and destroy that ship.\""
msgstr ""
"Mientras tus sensores pierden el rastro del objetivo que debías matar, "
"esperas recibir un mensaje de fallo de la misión, pero en su lugar, escuchas "
"la comunicación de la nave de Tam: \"Uno de ellos ha escapado. Continúa "
"destruyendo a los demás. Después, {player}, saltarás a {sys} y destruirás "
"esa nave.\""

msgid "Clear the current system"
msgstr "Limpiar el sistema actual"

msgid "Jump to {sys} to follow your target"
msgstr "Salta a {sys} para seguir a tu objetivo"

msgid ""
"While your sensors lose track of the target you were supposed to kill, you "
"expect to receive a mission failure message, but instead, you hear Tam's "
"ship communication: \"One of them escaped. Continue destroying the others. "
"Afterwards, {player}, you will land on {pnt} to keep track on the pilot.\""
msgstr ""
"Mientras tus sensores pierden el rastro del objetivo que debías matar, "
"esperas recibir un mensaje de fallo de misión, pero en su lugar, escuchas la "
"comunicación de la nave de Tam: \"Uno de ellos ha escapado. Continúa "
"destruyendo a los demás. Después, {player}, aterrizarás en {pnt} para seguir "
"el rastro del piloto.\""

msgid "Land on {pnt} to follow your target"
msgstr "Aterriza en {pnt} para seguir a tu objetivo"

#. That's not very elegant...
#. escort[1]:setNoDisable()
#. Strafer is attacked: he runs away around the system
#. time for stampede
msgid "Hostiles are running away. Don't let them escape!"
msgstr "Los hostiles están huyendo. ¡No les dejes escapar!"

#. System cleaned
msgid "Hostiles eliminated."
msgstr "Hostiles eliminados."

#. Pursued enemy jumped out (this is actually kind of unlikely, but...)
#. Pursued enemy landed (this is actually kind of unlikely, but...)
msgid "The target ran away again: continue the pursuit."
msgstr "El objetivo huyó de nuevo: continúe la persecución."

msgid "You won't take me alive! Never!"
msgstr "¡Nunca me cogerás con vida! ¡Nunca!"

msgid ""
"A group of assassins, who were after Major Tam, have been trapped and "
"killed. For now, we don't know who paid them, but they were led by Colonel "
"Hamelsen, who managed to escape."
msgstr ""
"Un grupo de asesinos, que iban tras el Mayor Tam, han sido atrapados y "
"asesinados. Por ahora, no sabemos quién les pagó, pero estaban dirigidos por "
"la Coronel Hamelsen, que logró escapar."

#. Test if an element is in a list of destinations
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Dvaered Meeting">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>2</priority>
#. <chance>25</chance>
#. <done>Dvaered Diplomacy</done>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <faction>Dvaered</faction>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Frontier Invasion</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Dvaered Meeting
#. -- This is the 5th mission of the Frontier War Dvaered campaign.
#. -- The player has to secure a Dvaered Warlord Meeting.
#. -- Hamelsen lures out the player, while Strafer gets killed by a spy who runs away.
#. -- There are two parts in the mission : part 1 is mainly contemplative, and part 2 is tricky, with fights and so.
#.
#. Stages :
#. 0) Way to Dvaer Prime
#. 1) Briefing at Dvaer Prime and patrol around DHC
#. 2) Following Hamelsen towards Laars (main purpose of this is to let the player save the game because second part is tricky)
#. 3) Taking off from Laars
#. 4) Land on Laars and get rewarded
#. --
#. luacheck: globals toocloseControl1 toocloseControl2 toocloseControl3 toocloseControl4 toocloseControl5 incomingControl1 incomingControl2 incomingControl3 incomingControl4 incomingControl5
#. Non-persistent state
#. Forward-declared functions
#. common hooks
#. TODO: hooks to penalize attacking people
#. Mission constants
msgid ""
"\"Both squadrons of the DHC station's space security force will be deployed "
"with a full range ships from Vendettas to Goddards. Those squadrons are the "
"'Beta-Storks' and the 'Beta-Hammer' and their mission will be to control "
"medium and heavy ships and to provide heavy firepower in case of need. Our "
"squadron, named 'Alpha-NightClaws', is in charge of fast ships (Yachts and "
"Fighters). We will be flying Hyenas.\n"
"   \"The plan is the following: any ship approaching the station will be "
"assigned to a squad by the fleet leader, and then to a pilot by the squad "
"leader (Captain Leblanc). When a ship is assigned to you, you will have to "
"approach the ship within 1000 km. Their security clearance code will be "
"automatically requested and processed by the system we'll install in your "
"core unit. Afterwards, the ship will be allowed to land, or ordered to fly "
"away. The same thing happens for ships that leave the station.\n"
"   \"Finally, in case something unexpected happens, you will, of course, "
"have to obey orders. Watch your messages closely. A few pilots will be kept "
"in reserve close to the station.\n"
"   \"Oh, and there is another thing I must warn you about: it's the "
"warlord's odd sense of humour. When they see a small ship close to their "
"Goddard, they may get the idea to shoot a small railgun-volley in your "
"direction. Some of them tend to enjoy seeing pilots fend for their lives. "
"Dvaered law allows warlords to do so provided they can assure the High "
"Command that there was no hostile intention. That can be a bit annoying, "
"sometimes.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Los dos escuadrones de la fuerza de seguridad espacial de la estación AMD "
"se desplegarán con una gama completa de naves, desde Vendettas hasta "
"Goddards. Esos escuadrones son el 'Beta-Cigueñas' y el 'Beta-Martillo' y su "
"misión será controlar las naves medianas y pesadas y proporcionar potencia "
"de fuego pesada en caso de necesidad. Nuestro escuadrón, llamado 'Alpha-"
"GarrasNocturnas', está a cargo de las naves rápidas (Yates y Cazas). "
"Volaremos con Hienas.\n"
"   \"El plan es el siguiente: cualquier nave que se acerque a la estación "
"será asignada a un escuadrón por el jefe de la flota, y luego a un piloto "
"por el jefe del escuadrón (el capitán Leblanc). Cuando se le asigne una "
"nave, tendrá que acercarse a ella a menos de 1000 km. Su código de "
"autorización de seguridad será solicitado y procesado automáticamente por el "
"sistema que instalaremos en tu unidad central. Después, se permitirá que la "
"nave aterrice o se le ordenará que se aleje. Lo mismo ocurre con las naves "
"que abandonan la estación.\n"
"   \"Por último, en caso de que ocurra algo inesperado, tendrás, por "
"supuesto, que obedecer las órdenes. Vigila tus mensajes con atención. Unos "
"cuantos pilotos se mantendrán en reserva cerca de la estación.\n"
"   \"Ah, y hay otra cosa sobre la que debo advertirles: es el extraño "
"sentido del humor del señor de la guerra. Cuando vean una nave pequeña cerca "
"de su Goddard, puede que se les ocurra disparar una pequeña ráfaga de "
"cañones de riel en tu dirección. Algunos de ellos suelen disfrutar viendo a "
"los pilotos defenderse. La ley Dvaered permite hacerlo siempre que puedan "
"asegurar al Alto Mando que no hubo intención hostil. Eso puede ser un poco "
"molesto, a veces.\""

msgid ""
"When you mention Colonel Hamelsen, Strafer cuts you off: \"Ex-Colonel "
"Hamelsen! She is a traitor and has lost all her commendations. Now she is "
"nothing to the Dvaered, and things are better like that.\" You ask him if "
"things may have turned differently for her and he answers:\n"
"   \"Watch out, citizen: these kinds of questions lead to compassion. "
"Compassion leads to weakness and weakness leads to death. Death for yourself "
"and for those who trusted you. Death for your leaders and for your "
"subordinates. Death for people you love and people you respect. Remember: if "
"you want to be strong, don't listen to compassion. Don't even give "
"compassion a chance to reach your heart.\""
msgstr ""
"Cuando mencionas al Coronel Hamelsen, Strafer te corta: \"¡Ex-coronel "
"Hamelsen! Es una traidora y ha perdido todos sus reconocimientos. Ahora no "
"es nada para los Dvaered, y las cosas están mejor así\". Le preguntas si las "
"cosas podrían haber sido diferentes para ella y te responde:\n"
"   \"Cuidado, ciudadano: este tipo de preguntas llevan a la compasión. La "
"compasión lleva a la debilidad y la debilidad lleva a la muerte. Muerte para "
"ti y para los que confiaron en ti. Muerte para tus líderes y para tus "
"subordinados. Muerte para las personas que amas y para las que respetas. "
"Recuerda: si quieres ser fuerte, no escuches a la compasión. Ni siquiera le "
"des a la compasión la oportunidad de llegar a tu corazón.\""

msgid ""
"You ask Strafer why Major Tam requested you for the mission. \"Actually, we "
"did not need a private pilot. I just managed to convince Captain Leblanc to "
"hire you.\" As you wonder why he did that, Strafer thinks a bit and smiles: "
"\"Well, I get the feeling that together we do a good job. Don't we?\""
msgstr ""
"Le preguntas a Strafer por qué el Mayor Tam te solicitó para la misión. \"En "
"realidad, no necesitábamos un piloto privado. Sólo conseguí convencer al "
"capitán Leblanc para que te contratara\". Mientras te preguntas por qué lo "
"hizo, Strafer piensa un poco y sonríe: \"Bueno, tengo la sensación de que "
"juntos hacemos un buen trabajo. ¿No es así?\""

msgid ""
"\"You wish to become one of them?\" Before you have a chance to deny, he "
"continues: \"Anybody can become a warlord. One just has to have achieved the "
"'9th grade commendation', and to conquer a planet (or a station). In the "
"army, every rank gives you a commendation grade, for example, I have the 3rd "
"grade. Civilians also obtain commendation for their high deeds; you obtained "
"the 1st grade commendation for your involvement in the FLF destruction, if I "
"am right. The 9th grade commendation, that is associated to the rank of "
"first-class General in the army, gives the right to own a military base, and "
"by extension, to be granted regal power over a region.\n"
"   \"In the Dvaered army, everybody starts as a raw soldier, no matter if "
"you're an infantryman, a pilot, a medic, or even a General's child. And only "
"Valor decides how quick you rise in the hierarchy. Warlord is the ultimate "
"rank for the military and for private combat pilots, like yourself)\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Deseas convertirte en uno de ellos?\" Antes de que tengas la oportunidad "
"de negar, continúa: \"Cualquiera puede convertirse en un señor de la guerra. "
"Sólo hay que haber alcanzado el '9º grado de recomendación', y conquistar un "
"planeta (o una estación). En el ejército, cada rango te da un grado de "
"recomendación, por ejemplo, yo tengo el 3er grado. Los civiles también "
"obtienen elogios por sus altas acciones; tú obtuviste el 1er grado de elogio "
"por tu participación en la destrucción del FLF, si no me equivoco. La "
"encomienda de 9º grado, que está asociada al rango de general de primera "
"clase en el ejército, da derecho a poseer una base militar y, por extensión, "
"a que se te conceda el poder real sobre una región.\n"
"   \"En el ejército Dvaered, todo el mundo empieza como un soldado en bruto, "
"no importa si eres un soldado de infantería, un piloto, un médico o incluso "
"el hijo de un general. Y sólo el Valor decide lo rápido que se asciende en "
"la jerarquía. El Señor de la guerra es el último rango para los militares y "
"para los pilotos de combate privados, como tú)\""

msgid "Ahoy, suckers! Here comes the master!"
msgstr "¡Ahoy, tontos! ¡Aquí viene el maestro!"

msgid "Look down, you weaklings."
msgstr "Mirad hacia abajo, debiluchos."

msgid "Only submission will save you from my anger!"
msgstr "¡Sólo la sumisión te salvará de mi ira!"

msgid "Kneel, for I am destined to rule you all!"
msgstr "¡Arrodillaos, pues estoy destinado a gobernaros a todos!"

msgid "Worship my strength, or burn by my railguns."
msgstr "Adorad mi fuerza, o arded por mis cañones de riel."

msgid "Here comes Daddy!"
msgstr "¡Aquí viene Papaito!"

msgid ""
"I am an artist of Pain and Destruction. Who wants to be part of my next "
"masterpiece?"
msgstr ""
"Soy un artista del Dolor y la Destrucción. ¿Quién quiere formar parte de mi "
"próxima obra maestra?"

msgid "Make way for the supplier of Hell!"
msgstr "¡Abrid paso al proveedor del Infierno!"

msgid ""
"Death is everyone's ultimate destination. Pissing me off means taking a "
"shortcut."
msgstr ""
"La muerte es el destino final de todos. Enojarme significa tomar un atajo."

#. This might be hard to translate, but that is not a problem IMHO as it is actually supposed to be an automatically generated message.
msgid "caterer"
msgstr "proveedor de comida"

msgid "butcher"
msgstr "carnicero"

msgid "brewer"
msgstr "cervecero"

msgid "waiter"
msgstr "camarero"

msgid "vigil"
msgstr "vigía"

msgid "gladiator"
msgstr "gladiador"

msgid "rat exterminator"
msgstr "exterminador de ratas"

msgid "emergency doctor"
msgstr "doctor de emergencias"

msgid "weapons dealer"
msgstr "vendedor de armas"

msgid "drug dealer"
msgstr "vendedor de drogas"

msgid "torturer"
msgstr "torturador"

msgid ""
"Judging by how he looks at you, Strafer needs you for another mission along "
"with the Dvaered Space Force."
msgstr ""
"A juzgar por cómo te mira, Strafer te necesita para otra misión junto con la "
"Fuerza Espacial Dvaered."

msgid "We need you once more"
msgstr "Te necesitamos de nuevo"

msgid ""
"As you sit at his table, the clearly anxious Dvaered pilot stops biting his "
"nails and explains why he is here.\n"
"   \"The High Command summoned, under request of General Klank, a special "
"meeting of the high council of Warlords, and all of them have agreed to "
"come...\" You frown, and before you have a chance to ask why that's a "
"problem, he continues: \"... but we received an intelligence report "
"according to which the ex-Colonel Hamelsen, who has already tried to murder "
"Major Tam several times, is going to take advantage of this meeting to take "
"action against us.\"\n"
"   \"Do you want to help us against this threat?\""
msgstr ""
"Mientras te sientas en su mesa, el piloto Dvaered, claramente ansioso, deja "
"de morderse las uñas y te explica por qué está aquí.\n"
"   \"El Alto Mando ha convocado, a petición del general Klank, una reunión "
"especial del alto consejo de Señores de la Guerra, y todos ellos han "
"accedido a venir...\" Frunces el ceño, y antes de que tengas la oportunidad "
"de preguntar por qué eso es un problema, continúa: \"... pero hemos recibido "
"un informe de inteligencia según el cual el ex Coronel Hamelsen, que ya ha "
"intentado asesinar al Mayor Tam varias veces, va a aprovechar esta reunión "
"para actuar contra nosotros\".\n"
"   \"¿Quiere ayudarnos contra esta amenaza?\""

msgid ""
"Mm. I see. You probably have much more interesting things to do than being "
"loyal to the Dvaered Nation..."
msgstr ""
"Mm. Ya veo. Probablemente tienes cosas mucho más interesantes que hacer que "
"ser leal a la Nación Dvaered..."

msgid "Here is the situation"
msgstr "Esta es la situación"

msgid ""
"\"General Klank has summoned the Warlords in order to present them with the "
"Frontier invasion plan. When a meeting of the high council of Warlords "
"occurs, a short truce takes place, and they all come to the DHC station with "
"their Goddards. This fact alone is already enough to put the station's "
"security service under pressure, as the warlords constantly provoke each "
"other and start brawls. But this time, we believe that Hamelsen will try to "
"either assassinate warlords, or record our invasion plan in order to sell it "
"to hostile foreign powers.\n"
"   \"This is why Major Tam wants our squadron from the Special Operations "
"Forces to support the regular units of the station. Fly to Dvaer Prime and "
"meet me in the bar there.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El General Klank ha convocado a los Señores de la Guerra para presentarles "
"el plan de invasión de Frontera. Cuando se produce una reunión del alto "
"consejo de los Señores de la Guerra, se produce una breve tregua y todos "
"ellos acuden a la estación AMD con sus Goddards. Este hecho, por sí solo, ya "
"es suficiente para poner en apuros al servicio de seguridad de la estación, "
"ya que los señores de la guerra se provocan constantemente entre sí e "
"inician reyertas. Pero esta vez, creemos que Hamelsen intentará asesinar a "
"los señores de la guerra, o grabar nuestro plan de invasión para venderlo a "
"potencias extranjeras hostiles.\n"
"   \"Por eso el Mayor Tam quiere que nuestro escuadrón de las Fuerzas de "
"Operaciones Especiales apoye a las unidades regulares de la estación. Vuela "
"a Dvaer Prime y reúnete conmigo en el bar de allí.\""

