#. 1) Way to any Dvaered Spob to get paid
#. --
#. Mission details
msgid "Monitoring of Warlords activity in {sys}"
msgstr "Seguimiento de la Actividad de los Señores de la Guerra en {sys}"

msgid ""
"Dvaered High Command requires a pilot to go to {sys} and detect {nb} Dvaered "
"ships."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dvaered Census"
msgstr "Censo Dvaered"

#. Enters in the mission's system
#. Note: there is no test on the player leaving the system before having scanned enough ships.
#. This behaviour is totally allowed.
#. Pay the player
msgid "Mission Complete"
msgstr "Misión Completada"

msgid ""
"You land and transmit a datapad to the local Dvaered liaison officer.\n"
"{reward}"
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas y transmites un datapad al oficial de enlace local Dvaered.\n"
"{reward}"

#. Manage counting of missions
#. Test pilots in range.
#. Wrong system: abort
#. Test if mission is complete
#. Not so big reputation growth (Dvaered kill cap is high)
#. Test pilots in range.
#. Wrong system: abort
#. Test if mission is complete
msgid "You have acquired data on enough Dvaered ships"
msgstr "Has adquirido datos sobre suficientes naves Dvaered"

#. Recursivity 1 s
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Dvaered Census 0">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>30</chance>
#. <cond>
#. --return require("misn_test").reweight_active() -- Don't reweight as this is important
#. return true
#. </cond>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <faction>Dvaered</faction>
#. <notes>
#. <tier>1</tier>
#. <campaign>Dvaered Recruitment</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Dvaered Census 0
#. -- This is the first mission of the Dvaered Recruitment arc
#. -- (facultative missions that make the player close to the Dvaered
#. -- and end up allowing them to purchase heavy weapons and ships licences).
#. -- The player has to get in range of a given amount of Dvaered Ships in a given system.
#.
#. Stages :
#. 0) Way to system and in-system traffic
#. 1) Way to any Dvaered Spob to get paid
#. --
msgid ""
"Nelly has noticed you. Wait? Is she trying to infuse a sausage in her Vodka?"
msgstr ""
"Nelly se ha fijado en ti. ¿Espera? ¿Estás tratando de infusionar una "
"salchicha en su Vodka?"

msgid "Wait? Is this woman trying to infuse a sausage in her Vodka?"
msgstr ""
"¿Espera? ¿Esta mujer está tratando de tener una salchicha infundida en su "
"Vodka?"

msgid ""
"\"Hi, {player}! How do you do? How long have you been here in Dvaered space? "
"Not so long, eh?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Hola, {player}! ¿Cómo estás? ¿Cuánto tiempo llevas aquí en el espacio "
"Dvaered? No mucho, ¿eh?\""

msgid "\"Hi, I'm Nelly! Oh! I guess you are new to Dvaered space, right?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Hola, soy Nelly! ¡Oh! Supongo que eres nueva en el espacio Dvaered, "
"¿verdad?\""

msgid ""
"Nelly puts her hands on the table and lifts herself up.\n"
"\"Do you want a good tip from an old skipper who has been sailing among the "
"stars for cycles?\""
msgstr ""
"Nelly pone las manos sobre la mesa y se levanta.\n"
"\"¿Quieres un buen consejo de un viejo patrón que ha estado navegando entre "
"las estrellas durante ciclos?\""

msgid ""
"A smile appears on her face and she sits down again.\n"
"\"Okay, just kidding. I'm not an old skipper. However, I still have found a "
"good way to make money by doing missions for the Dvaered.\n"
"It's not dangerous, the pay is decent, and it does not put you in trouble "
"with any other faction. Do you want me to explain?\""
msgstr ""
"Una sonrisa aparece en su rostro y vuelve a sentarse.\n"
"\"Vale, es una broma. No soy un viejo patrón. Sin embargo, he encontrado una "
"buena forma de ganar dinero haciendo misiones para los Dvaered.\n"
"\"No es peligroso, la paga es decente y no te pone en problemas con ninguna "
"otra facción. ¿Quieres que te lo explique?\""

msgid "\"As you wish.\""
msgstr "\"Como quieras.\""

#. Just in case
msgid ""
"\"I will tell you what I have understood.\n"
"Most of the Dvaered warships you see out there do belong to private armies, "
"that obey to generals, called the 'Warlords'. Those Warlords have many "
"privileges, but they also have some obligations. One of those obligations is "
"to patrol routes around the worlds they own.\n"
"But as the Dvaered are a bit… primitive, their administration is not able to "
"control that they actually protect the trade lanes. That is why they need "
"private pilots, like us, to count Dvaered ships.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Te diré lo que he entendido.\n"
"\"La mayoría de las naves de guerra Dvaered que ves ahí fuera pertenecen a "
"ejércitos privados, que obedecen a generales, llamados 'Señores de la "
"Guerra'. Esos Señores de la Guerra tienen muchos privilegios, pero también "
"tienen algunas obligaciones. Una de esas obligaciones es la de patrullar las "
"rutas alrededor de los mundos que poseen.\n"
"Pero como los Dvaered son un poco... primitivos, su administración no es "
"capaz de controlar que realmente protejan las rutas comerciales. Por eso "
"necesitan pilotos privados, como nosotros, para contar las naves Dvaered.\""

msgid ""
"\"Here is how it works: You simply have to browse a given stellar system, "
"and to get in sensor range of a given number of Dvaered ships. The data is "
"automatically acquired and processed.\n"
"The Dvaered authorities can then deduce from the transponder IDs what ship "
"belongs to which warlord.\n"
"Once you have seen enough ships, you can land on any Dvaered-controlled "
"planet to transmit your data and collect your pay.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Así es como funciona: Simplemente hay que navegar por un sistema estelar "
"determinado, y ponerse en el rango de sensores de un número determinado de "
"naves Dvaered. Los datos se adquieren y procesan automáticamente.\n"
"Las autoridades Dvaered pueden deducir a partir de los identificadores de "
"los transpondedores qué nave pertenece a qué señor de la guerra.\n"
"Una vez que hayas visto suficientes naves, puedes aterrizar en cualquier "
"planeta controlado por Dvaered para transmitir tus datos y cobrar tu paga.\""

msgid ""
"\"The last one I chose happened in {system}, you have to get in range of "
"{nb} ships, and the pay is {credits}. Those missions appear at the mission "
"computer to pilots who have required so to the authorities. But, you know "
"what? I can transfer mine to you. I needed to abort it anyways because this "
"freaking sausage has not finished infusing yet!\""
msgstr ""
"\"La última que elegí ocurrió en {system}, tienes que ponerte al alcance de "
"{nb} naves, y la paga es de {credits}. Esas misiones aparecen en el "
"ordenador de misiones a los pilotos que lo han requerido a las autoridades. "
"Pero, ¿sabes qué? Puedo transferirte la mía. ¡Tenía que abortarla de todos "
"modos porque esta maldita salchicha no ha terminado de infundirse todavía!\""

msgid "Accept the mission"
msgstr "Aceptar la misión"

msgid "Refuse the mission"
msgstr "Rechazar la misión"

msgid "\"Good luck with that mission, then!\""
msgstr "\"¡Buena suerte con esa misión, entonces!\""

#. Check to see if truly accepted
#. Create NPC for casual chatting
msgid "Nelly is still there."
msgstr "Nelly todavía está ahí."

#. Enters in the mission's system
#. Note: there is no test on the player leaving the system before having scanned enough ships.
#. This behaviour is totally allowed.
#. Pay the player
#. That's not realistic the player doesn't get killed, but that's not realistic either anyone would land here anyways...
#. Pay the player
msgid "Reward"
msgstr "Recompensa"

msgid ""
"You land and transmit a datapad to the local Dvaered liaison officer. They "
"unlock for you the Dvaered Census missions, that you can now find at the "
"mission computer under the label {label}."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas y transmites un datapad al oficial de enlace local Dvaered. Ellos "
"desbloquean para ti las misiones del Censo Dvaered, que ahora puedes "
"encontrar en el ordenador de misiones bajo la etiqueta {label}."

msgid ""
"You accomplished a patrol census mission for the Dvaered. They seem disposed "
"to entrust you with more missions of that kind in the future."
msgstr ""
"Has realizado una misión de censo de patrulla para los Dvaered. Parecen "
"dispuestos a confiarte más misiones de ese tipo en el futuro."

#. Recursivity 1 s
#. Facultative talk to Nelly
msgid "How did you end up in Dvaered Space?"
msgstr "¿Cómo acabaste en el Espacio Dvaered?"

msgid "Isn't it a bit odd, how the Dvaered society works, with those Warlords?"
msgstr ""
"¿No es un poco extraño cómo funciona la sociedad Dvaered, con esos Señores "
"de la Guerra?"

msgid "Suggest Nelly to prick the sausage with a fork to infuse it quicker"
msgstr ""
"Sugieres a Nelly que pinche la salchicha con un tenedor para infundirla más "
"rápido"

msgid "Leave Nelly"
msgstr "Dejar a Nelly"

msgid "\"How do you do?\""
msgstr "\"¿Cómo estás?\""

msgid ""
"\"Ah. Long story.\"\n"
"Nelly raises her eyes and lets her gaze wander on the filthy ceiling.\n"
"\"I had just landed on Brooks, in Arcturus, you know? For some reason, there "
"are often children playing soccer on the spaceport, there. While workers "
"were unloading goods from my ship, I was wondering why there had never been "
"an accident with those children. And suddenly, an accident occurred!\n"
"A kid shot the ball in the wrong direction, and it crashed into the side of "
"my poor Llama, breaking through the plating!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ah. Una larga historia\".\n"
"Nelly levanta los ojos y deja que su mirada se pierda en el mugriento "
"techo.\n"
"\"Acababa de aterrizar en Brooks, en Arcturus, ¿sabes? Por alguna razón, "
"suele haber niños jugando al fútbol en el puerto espacial, allí. Mientras "
"los trabajadores descargaban las mercancías de mi nave, me preguntaba por "
"qué nunca había habido un accidente con esos niños. Y de repente, ¡ocurrió "
"un accidente!\n"
"\"¡Un niño disparó la pelota en la dirección equivocada, y se estrelló "
"contra el costado de mi pobre Llama, rompiendo la chapa!\""

msgid ""
"If a soccer ball can break through your ship, what will happen with a "
"blaster?"
msgstr ""
"Si un balón de fútbol puede atravesar tu nave, ¿qué pasará con un blaster?"

msgid "Was it easy to repair?"
msgstr "¿Fue fácil de reparar?"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Nelly looks at you, surprised.\n"
"\"That's exactly what that cyber-grandpa told me. And then, he said the "
"problem was that my ship's absorption was not high enough. He spoke about a "
"coating that is only used by Dvaered pilots, the 'Impacto-Plastic Coating', "
"that can make your ship's armour much more resilient.\n"
"So, after the reparations were completed, I went to Dvaered space. But I "
"didn't find anybody who could install this coating on my ship yet. And what "
"is more, I suspect this will cost much more that I can afford. So I do "
"missions for the Dvaered in order to make money and explore a bit.\""
msgstr ""
"Nelly te mira, sorprendido.\n"
"\"Eso es exactamente lo que me dijo ese ciberabuelo. Y luego, dijo que el "
"problema era que la absorción de mi nave no era lo suficientemente alta. "
"Habló de un revestimiento que sólo utilizan los pilotos de Dvaered, el "
"'Revestimiento Impacto-Plástico', que puede hacer que el blindaje de tu nave "
"sea mucho más resistente.\n"
"\"Así que, después de las reparaciones, fui al espacio Dvaered. Pero todavía "
"no he encontrado a nadie que pueda instalar ese revestimiento en mi nave. Y "
"lo que es más, sospecho que esto costará mucho más de lo que puedo pagar. "
"Así que hago misiones para los Dvaered para ganar dinero y explorar un poco."
"\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"Well. The problem is that my hull's architecture is a bit… uncommon. Front "
"and back are from the original Llama Mk IV-BM version from UST-599, but on "
"the sides, I have adapted parts of the Llama Mk II-O version (from the batch "
"of UST-567, not the more mainstream batch of UST-568). As they cannot be "
"adapted together by default, I got a friend on Em5 to machine a special "
"adaptor.\n"
"\"Anyway, so the repairman on Brooks didn't have the needed parts to repair "
"my hull and I had to get someone to transport me to Darkshed. You know, it's "
"the best place to find spare parts for older models of ships as nebula "
"scavengers often sell their findings there. But once there, I met Robin. Do "
"you know Robin?\n"
"She is small, wants to kill me, has curly brunette hair and a smiling round "
"head. You are sure you don't know her? She talked a lot about killing me "
"lately. Anyway, I managed to hide in a rubbish bin, but unfortunately, I got "
"loaded by mistake on a garbage ship heading to that stinky planet in Soromid "
"space, you know? I got lucky I was in a pressurized compartment, and I "
"managed to get out in Father's Pride.\n"
"And after that I got an inter-system call from the repairman in Brooks who "
"actually found the needed set of parts (it was in a crate he was using to "
"wedge his desk). So I returned, had a bath and got my repaired ship!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Bueno. El problema es que la arquitectura de mi casco es un poco... poco "
"común. La parte delantera y trasera son de la versión original Llama Mk IV-"
"BM de UST-599, pero en los laterales he adaptado partes de la versión Llama "
"Mk II-O (del lote de UST-567, no del lote más corriente de UST-568). Como no "
"se pueden adaptar juntas por defecto, conseguí que un amigo de Em5 "
"mecanizara un adaptador especial.\n"
"\"De todos modos, el reparador de Brooks no tenía las piezas necesarias para "
"reparar mi casco y tuve que conseguir que alguien me transportara a Hangar "
"Oscuro. Ya sabes, es el mejor lugar para encontrar piezas de repuesto para "
"modelos antiguos de naves, ya que los carroñeros de la nebulosa suelen "
"vender allí sus hallazgos. Pero una vez allí, conocí a Robin. ¿Conoces a "
"Robin?\n"
"Es pequeña, quiere matarme, tiene el pelo moreno rizado y la cabeza redonda "
"y sonriente. ¿Seguro que no la conoces? Últimamente hablaba mucho de "
"matarme. En fin, conseguí esconderme en un cubo de basura, pero por "
"desgracia me embarcaron por error en una nave de basura que se dirigía a ese "
"apestoso planeta del espacio Soromida, ¿sabes? Tuve suerte de estar en un "
"compartimento presurizado, y conseguí salir en Orgullo de Padre.\n"
"Y después recibí una llamada entre sistemas del reparador de Brooks, que "
"encontró el juego de piezas que necesitaba (estaba en una caja que usaba "
"para calzar su escritorio). Así que volví, me di un baño y ¡recibí mi nave "
"reparada!\""

msgid ""
"\"Of course it is. But you know, they are not as advanced administratively "
"as we at the core Empire are.\n"
"The Dvaered don't have an administrative procedure to follow in every "
"situation of life, as we do in the core Imperial systems. So instead they "
"obey the strongest of them, the Warlords. They exist because the "
"administration here is not advanced enough to prevent violence in the "
"society.\n"
"It is actually sad, but I guess it is like that. They chose independence "
"after all…\""
msgstr ""
"\"Por supuesto que sí. Pero ya sabes, no están tan avanzados "
"administrativamente como nosotros en el núcleo del Imperio.\n"
"Los Dvaered no tienen un procedimiento administrativo que seguir en cada "
"situación de la vida, como nosotros en los sistemas imperiales centrales. "
"Así que en su lugar obedecen al más fuerte de ellos, los Señores de la "
"Guerra. Existen porque la administración aquí no es lo suficientemente "
"avanzada como para evitar la violencia en la sociedad.\n"
"Es realmente triste, pero supongo que es así. Después de todo, eligieron la "
"independencia...\""

msgid ""
"\"What? But of course not! It is the worst mistake possible. Haven't you "
"read any book on sausage infusion in your life? Everyone knows that you must "
"never, NEVER prick the sausage with a fork. At any cost!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué? ¡Pero claro que no! Es el peor error posible. ¿No has leído ningún "
"libro sobre infusión de salchichas en tu vida? Todo el mundo sabe que nunca, "
"NUNCA hay que pinchar la salchicha con un tenedor. ¡A cualquier precio!\""

