#. Non-persistent state
#. Forward-declared functions
msgid "Maikki wants you to help her find out what happened to her father."
msgstr "Maikki quiere que la ayudes a averiguar qué le pasó a su padre."

#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
#. Set up mission stuff
#. Re-add Maikki if accepted
msgid "Investigate the Za'lek"
msgstr "Investiga a los Za'lek"

msgid "\tGo to {pnt} in {sys}"
msgstr "\tVe a {pnt} en {sys}"

msgid ""
"\"The three Za'lek researchers you should seek out are:\n"
"{name1} in the {sys1} system,\n"
"{name2} in the {sys2} system,\n"
"and {name3} in the {sys3} system.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Los tres investigadores Za'lek que debes buscar son:\n"
"{name1} en el sistema {sys1},\n"
"{name2} en el sistema {sys2},\n"
"y {name3} en el sistema {sys3}.\""

msgid ""
"You approach Maikki who seems to have a fierce determination in her eyes."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas a Maikki que parece tener una feroz determinación en sus ojos."

msgid ""
"She looks encouraged by your findings in the nebula.\n"
"\"From what you told me, I think I have a good idea for our next lead. Would "
"you be interested in helping again?\""
msgstr ""
"Parece animada por tus hallazgos en la nebulosa.\n"
"\"Por lo que me has contado, creo que tengo una buena idea para nuestra "
"próxima pista. ¿Estarías interesado en ayudar de nuevo?\""

msgid "Help Maikki again"
msgstr "Ayuda a Maikki otra vez"

msgid ""
"You agreed to continue helping Maikki find her father. She told you to try "
"to find hints from three Za'lek researchers."
msgstr ""
"Aceptas seguir ayudando a Maikki a encontrar a su padre. Te dijo que "
"intentaras encontrar pistas de tres investigadores Za'lek."

msgid ""
"\"I think we should be able to find out what happened to my father's ship in "
"the nebula. It seems like someone is very interested on stuff that is being "
"found in the nebula and is behind the scavengers you met. Whoever is behind "
"them could also be related to whatever happened to the ship in the first "
"place.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Creo que deberíamos ser capaces de averiguar qué pasó con la nave de mi "
"padre en la nebulosa. Parece que alguien está muy interesado en las cosas "
"que se encuentran en la nebulosa y está detrás de los carroñeros que "
"conociste. Quienquiera que esté detrás de ellos también podría estar "
"relacionado con lo que le ocurrió a la nave en primer lugar.\""

msgid ""
"\"I ran a check on Za'lek researchers that would likely be interested in "
"stuff taken from the nebula and there seems to be fewer than I imagined. I "
"was able to get a list of three researchers. I'll give you the details on "
"them and you should pay them a visit to see if they know anything.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hice una comprobación de los investigadores Za'lek que probablemente "
"estarían interesados en las cosas tomadas de la nebulosa y parece que hay "
"menos de lo que imaginaba. Pude conseguir una lista de tres investigadores. "
"Te daré los detalles sobre ellos y deberías hacerles una visita para ver si "
"saben algo.\""

msgid ""
"She leans in close to you and looks into your eyes with fierce "
"determination.\n"
"\"You will do whatever it takes to find him right?\""
msgstr ""
"Se inclina hacia ti y te mira a los ojos con feroz determinación.\n"
"\"Harás lo que sea necesario para encontrarlo, ¿verdad?\""

msgid "\"Maybe…\""
msgstr "\" Quizás... \""

msgid ""
"\"You know the Za'lek can be very stubborn at times and may need some "
"convincing.\"\n"
"She winks at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Sabes que el Za'lek puede ser muy terco a veces y puede necesitar algo de "
"convencimiento.\"\n"
"Te guiña un ojo."

msgid ""
"\"I thought that after your experience in the nebula you would understand "
"how dangerous this can get.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Pensé que después de tu experiencia en la nebulosa entenderías lo "
"peligroso que puede llegar a ser esto.\""

msgid ""
"She glares at you.\n"
"\"I hope you're joking. This is very important to me and I hope you don't "
"lose this lead…\""
msgstr ""
"Ella te mira fijamente.\n"
"\"Espero que estés bromeando. Esto es muy importante para mí y espero que no "
"pierdas esta pista...\""

msgid ""
"\"Apparently the three researchers used to work together in some project "
"about the nebula's origins, but never really made anything public. I totally "
"think that they must know something about this; the disappearance of my "
"father was big news!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Al parecer, los tres investigadores solían trabajar juntos en algún "
"proyecto sobre los orígenes de la nebulosa, pero nunca hicieron nada "
"público. Creo totalmente que deben saber algo sobre esto; ¡la desaparición "
"de mi padre fue una gran noticia!\""

msgid ""
"She looks at you expectantly.\n"
"\"I will stay here and continue to search for him. Please pay those creepy "
"Za'lek researchers a visit and see if you can find out what happened to my "
"father!\""
msgstr ""
"Te mira expectante.\n"
"\"Me quedaré aquí y seguiré buscándolo. ¡Por favor, haz una visita a esos "
"espeluznantes investigadores Za'lek y ve si puedes averiguar qué le pasó a "
"mi padre!\""

msgid "Ask about the researchers"
msgstr "Pregunta por los investigadores"

msgid "Ask about her father (Kex)"
msgstr "Pregunta por su padre (Kex)"

#. TODO more options as more researchers are found
msgid "Tell her what you found"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"The researchers I told you about were involved in some sort of project "
"trying to find out the origins of the Incident by analysing artefacts taken "
"from the nebula. Most of it is classified so I wasn't able to get much "
"information.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Los investigadores de los que te hablé estaban involucrados en una especie "
"de proyecto que intentaba averiguar los orígenes del Incidente analizando "
"artefactos extraídos de la nebulosa. La mayor parte está clasificada, así "
"que no pude obtener mucha información.\""

msgid ""
"\"Apparently the project was disbanded for some reason or other, and some "
"members went missing. However, I was able to track down a few of them, but "
"it wasn't too easy. They have some weird system called tenure that nobody "
"understands and makes them move constantly from research laboratory to "
"research laboratory. So droll!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Al parecer, el proyecto se disolvió por una u otra razón, y algunos "
"miembros desaparecieron. Sin embargo, pude localizar a algunos de ellos, "
"aunque no fue demasiado fácil. Tienen un extraño sistema llamado titularidad "
"que nadie entiende y que les hace pasar constantemente de un laboratorio de "
"investigación a otro. ¡Tan gracioso!\""

msgid ""
"\"I don't think it will be easy for you to get information from the Za'lek. "
"They never give a straight answer and it's all \"that is illogical\" and "
"\"ma'am that beaker of acid is not a toy\". So boring!\"\n"
"She frowns and shakes her head."
msgstr ""
"\"No creo que te sea fácil obtener información de los Za'lek. Nunca dan una "
"respuesta directa y todo es \"eso es ilógico\" y \"señora ese vaso de ácido "
"no es un juguete\". ¡Qué aburrido!\"\n"
"Frunce el ceño y sacude la cabeza."

#. TODO messages regarding each of the researchers
msgid ""
"\"I don't remember much about my father, most of what I know about him are "
"from stories from my late mother and pilots who knew him.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No recuerdo mucho de mi padre, la mayor parte de lo que sé de él son "
"historias de mi difunta madre y de los pilotos que le conocieron.\""

msgid ""
"Her eyes light up.\n"
"\"Did you know that while scavenging near the Incident, an asteroid hit his "
"thrusters making them point the wrong way and he had to fly backwards "
"through five systems in the nebula while chased by pirates? Sounds crazy!\""
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos se iluminan.\n"
"\"¿Sabías que mientras buscaba en la basura cerca del Incidente, un "
"asteroide golpeó sus propulsores haciéndolos apuntar en la dirección "
"equivocada y tuvo que volar hacia atrás a través de cinco sistemas en la "
"nebulosa mientras era perseguido por piratas? ¡Parece una locura!\""

msgid ""
"\"They say he was also the first pilot to chart all the systems in the "
"Nebula after the Incident. Not even getting his leg crushed while recovering "
"parts of the last emperor's flagship stopped him from going back and back to "
"the nebula.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Dicen que también fue el primer piloto en cartografiar todos los sistemas "
"de la nebulosa después del Incidente. Ni siquiera el hecho de que le "
"aplastaran una pierna mientras recuperaba partes de la última nave insignia "
"del emperador le impidió volver y regresar a la nebulosa.\""

msgid ""
"Her eyes darken a little and her voice softens.\n"
"\"His obsession with finding the truth meant he was away from home most of "
"the time and my mother was probably very lonely. She told me he never came "
"to any of my birthdays…\""
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos se oscurecen un poco y su voz se suaviza.\n"
"\"Su obsesión por encontrar la verdad significaba que estaba fuera de casa "
"la mayor parte del tiempo y mi madre probablemente se sentía muy sola. Me "
"dijo que nunca vino a ninguno de mis cumpleaños...\""

msgid ""
"Her eyes light up again.\n"
"\"However, those were exceptional times. Most of the universe and our "
"history as humans was lost! I would love to be able to meet him again and be "
"able to ask him all sorts of things.\""
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos se iluminan de nuevo.\n"
"\"Sin embargo, aquellos eran tiempos excepcionales. La mayor parte del "
"universo y de nuestra historia como humanos se perdió. Me encantaría poder "
"volver a encontrarme con él y poder preguntarle todo tipo de cosas.\""

msgid ""
"\"Since you found his ship in the nebula we have to get to the bottom of "
"what happened! There is no way this was an accident, and I'm sure the Za'lek "
"are involved in this. Since you didn't find a body, he has to be alive! We "
"have to find out what happened and set things right!\"\n"
"Her eyes sparkle with determination."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Ya que encontraste su nave en la nebulosa tenemos que llegar al fondo de "
"lo que pasó! No hay manera de que esto haya sido un accidente, y estoy "
"seguro de que los Za'lek están involucrados en esto. Ya que no encontraron "
"un cuerpo, ¡tiene que estar vivo! ¡Tenemos que averiguar lo que pasó y "
"arreglar las cosas!\"\n"
"Sus ojos brillan con determinación."

msgid ""
"You tell her about your plight with the Za'lek researchers, and Dr. "
"Strangelove, in particular. This includes the good news that Kex should be "
"at Minerva Station, taken into custody by some thugs."
msgstr ""
"Le cuentas tu situación con los investigadores Za'lek, y el Dr. Strangelove, "
"en particular. Esto incluye la buena noticia de que Kex debería estar en la "
"estación Minerva, detenido por unos matones."

msgid ""
"\"The Za'leks were assholes as expected, but I'm glad you found out what I "
"thought: that he's somewhere here being held captive or something… This is "
"still all very weird though.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Los Za'leks fueron unos gilipollas, como era de esperar, pero me alegro de "
"que hayas averiguado lo que yo pensaba: que está en algún lugar de aquí "
"cautivo o algo así... Aunque todo esto sigue siendo muy raro.\""

msgid ""
"\"I'm a bit worried about that Dr. Strangelove. What exactly did he mean? Is "
"he even a real doctor? We still don't even know what happened in the nebula "
"nor what they want with my father. Instead of answering questions we keep on "
"finding new questions. I suppose that this is progress?…\""
msgstr ""
"\"Estoy un poco preocupado por ese Dr. Strangelove. ¿Qué quiso decir "
"exactamente? ¿Es siquiera un médico de verdad? Todavía no sabemos qué pasó "
"en la nebulosa ni qué quieren con mi padre. En lugar de responder a las "
"preguntas, seguimos encontrando nuevas preguntas. Supongo que esto es un "
"progreso...\""

msgid ""
"\"Anyway, if we can believe Dr. Strangelove, my father is alive and "
"somewhere here! I don't think we have any reason to doubt him. Za'leks don't "
"tend to lie, they only bend the truth. All we have to do is find my father "
"now and everything should fall in place.\""
msgstr ""
"\"De todos modos, si podemos creer al Dr. Strangelove, ¡mi padre está vivo y "
"en algún lugar de aquí! No creo que tengamos ninguna razón para dudar de él. "
"Los Za'leks no tienden a mentir, sólo falsean la verdad. Todo lo que tenemos "
"que hacer es encontrar a mi padre ahora y todo debería encajar.\""

msgid ""
"She is visibly excited.\n"
"\"It is all coming together! I will finally be able to meet him again! This "
"is so great! I don't know what to tell him first. Do you think he'll "
"recognize me?\""
msgstr ""
"Está visiblemente emocionada.\n"
"\"¡Todo se va a concretar! ¡Por fin podré volver a verle! ¡Esto es genial! "
"No sé qué decirle primero. ¿Crees que me reconocerá?\""

msgid ""
"\"I don't have a lead at the moment, but it can't be far. Keep your eyes "
"open and if you find anything that looks suspicious, please get in touch "
"with me! I'll also be keeping my eyes open.\""
msgstr ""
"\"De momento no tengo ninguna pista, pero no puede estar lejos. Mantén los "
"ojos abiertos y si encuentras algo que parezca sospechoso, por favor ponte "
"en contacto conmigo. Yo también mantendré los ojos abiertos.\""

msgid ""
"\"Oh, I almost forgot. I got lucky with a Pachinko machine and won a lot of "
"Minerva Tokens and a lifetime supply of parfaits! Since I don't need the "
"tokens to buy anything anymore, here, you can take them.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oh, casi lo olvido. He tenido suerte con una máquina de Pachinko y he "
"ganado un montón de Fichas de Minerva y un suministro de por vida de "
"parfaits. Como ya no necesito las fichas para comprar nada, toma, puedes "
"cogerlas.\""

#. no reward, yet...
#. roughly 1M if you consider winning rates
msgid ""
"You reported to Maikki what Dr. Strangelove told you about her father. She "
"doesn't have any leads at the moment, but it does seem like he is at Minerva "
"Station."
msgstr ""
"Informaste a Maikki de lo que el Dr. Strangelove te dijo sobre tu padre. De "
"momento no tienes ninguna pista, pero parece que está en la estación Minerva."

msgid "\"I'll be around here if you find anything.\""
msgstr "\"Estaré por aquí si encuentras algo.\""

msgid ""
"You take your leave. Without any leads, it might prove hard to find where "
"Kex is. You wonder what your next steps should be…"
msgstr ""
"Te vas. Sin ninguna pista, podría resultar difícil encontrar dónde está Kex. "
"Te preguntas cuáles deberían ser tus próximos pasos…"

#. Can't run it in the VN or it causes an error
msgid ""
"You see a person in a fancy lab coat. It seems like they are enjoying their "
"time off."
msgstr ""
"Ves a una persona con una elegante bata de laboratorio. Parece que está "
"disfrutando de su tiempo libre."

msgid ""
"You see a young fellow intently reading a book. There seems to be a shrimp "
"floating in a nearby aquarium bowl."
msgstr ""
"Ves a un joven que lee atentamente un libro. Parece que hay una gamba "
"flotando en la pecera de un acuario cercano."

msgid "Hologram Projector"
msgstr "Proyector de Hologramas"

msgid ""
"An old decrepit hologram projector sits in the corner. It looks like you "
"could use this to communicate with the owner of the station."
msgstr ""
"Un viejo y decrépito proyector de hologramas se encuentra en una esquina. "
"Parece que puedes usarlo para comunicarte con el dueño de la estación."

msgid ""
"You met the three researchers that Maikki told you about and found out a "
"lead about another researcher."
msgstr ""
"Has conocido a los tres investigadores de los que te habló Maikki y has "
"descubierto una pista sobre otro investigador."

msgid ""
"\"Oh, I suddenly remembered. There was also a post-doctoral research "
"candidate working on the project by the name of Cayne. I think he was last "
"working at {pnt} in the {sys} system.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oh, de repente me acordé. También había un candidato a investigador "
"postdoctoral trabajando en el proyecto con el nombre de Cayne. Creo que "
"estuvo trabajando por última vez en {pnt} en el sistema {sys}.\""

#. The mission state will be updated afterwards
msgid "You approach the professor."
msgstr "Te acercas al profesor."

msgid "\"Hello, how can I help you?\""
msgstr "\"Hola, ¿En qué puedo ayudarte?\""

msgid ""
"You inquire about whether or not they are interested in artefacts from the "
"nebula."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"Very interesting, but I stopped working on that line of research several "
"cycles ago. It was really a mess of a project. The project leader was "
"pushing us very hard due to the other competition.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Muy interesado, pero dejé de trabajar en esa línea de investigación hace "
"varios ciclos. Era un verdadero desastre de proyecto. El jefe del proyecto "
"nos presionaba mucho debido a la otra competencia.\""

msgid ""
"\"In the end, some papers' results were falsified and the project leader was "
"barred from doing research. That was too much for them and they took their "
"own life. How illogical!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Al final, los resultados de algunos trabajos fueron falsificados y al "
"director del proyecto se le prohibió investigar. Eso fue demasiado para "
"ellos y se quitaron la vida.¡Qué ilógico!\""

msgid ""
"\"If you are interested in nebula research, you should go visit the museum "
"of nebula artefacts. Although due to administrative changes, I don't think "
"it'll open again for a few cycles.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Si te interesa la investigación de la nebulosa, deberías ir a visitar el "
"museo de artefactos de las nebulosas. Aunque debido a los cambios "
"administrativos, no creo que vuelva a abrir hasta dentro de unos ciclos.\""

msgid ""
"\"Oh, you might have good luck talking to other members of the project. "
"However, most of us have moved on from that traumatic experience and are now "
"researching new topics.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Puede que tengas buena suerte hablando con otros miembros del proyecto. "
"Sin embargo, la mayoría de nosotros hemos superado esa experiencia "
"traumática y ahora estamos investigando nuevos temas.\""

msgid ""
"\"Did I mention I have started working with infinitely meta-recursive hyper-"
"tables? They are a fascinating type of data structure based on self-"
"referencing Grassman manifold quasi-projections. They even implicitly handle "
"non-convex elliptic reflections without any meta-heuristics!\"\n"
"They are getting excited."
msgstr ""
"\"¿He mencionado que he empezado a trabajar con hipertablas infinitamente "
"meta-recursivas? Son un tipo fascinante de estructura de datos basada en "
"cuasi-proyecciones de colectores de Grassman autorreferenciados. ¡Incluso "
"manejan implícitamente reflexiones elípticas no convexas sin ninguna meta-"
"heurística!\"\n"
"Se está entusiasmando."

msgid ""
"\"Although my grant has been rejected five times, the damn review board is "
"still pushing the obsolete Riemann algebroid universal approximator theory "
"and won't listen to anything else. They are definitely the future! I think "
"they may even have a practical application!\"\n"
"Their excitement grows."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"They don't seem like they will stop talking anytime soon… You take your "
"leave as they start rambling in a trance-like state."
msgstr ""
"No parece que vaya a dejar de hablar en breve... Te despides mientras "
"empiezan a divagar en estado de trance."

msgid "\"What can I do for you?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué puedo hacer por ti?\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"They rub their temples.\n"
"\"Ah, the nebula artefacts… Not very good experiences with those, no, not "
"really interested in them any more.\""
msgstr ""
"Se frota las sienes.\n"
"\"Ah, los artefactos de la nebulosa... No hay muy buenas experiencias con "
"ellos, no, ya no me interesan.\""

msgid ""
"\"I was part of a really ambitious project to try to track down the origin "
"of the Incident, which just ended up being a bureaucratic nightmare.\""
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"You see, the bigger the research project, the more the project leader and "
"co-leaders want to have meetings and goals and work packages.\"\n"
"They shudder when they say the word \"work packages\"."
msgstr ""
"\" Verás, cuanto más grande es el proyecto de investigación, más quiere el "
"director y los codirectores del proyecto tener reuniones y objetivos y "
"paquetes de trabajo.\"\n"
"Se estremece cuando dice la palabra \"paquetes de trabajo\"."

msgid ""
"\"At the end, we were just chaining meetings and answering e-mails and not "
"getting anything done. We ended up handing in a 5-page report written by an "
"intern for the mid-project evaluation and almost lost all the funding. The "
"project leader panicked and it all went to hell from there.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Al final, no hacíamos más que encadenar reuniones y contestar correos "
"electrónicos sin conseguir nada. Acabamos entregando un informe de 5 páginas "
"escrito por un becario para la evaluación de mitad de proyecto y casi "
"perdimos toda la financiación. El jefe del proyecto entró en pánico y a "
"partir de ahí todo se fue al garete.\""

msgid ""
"\"All nebula research is doomed to end that way. I haven't seen a project "
"succeed yet, despite all the proposal calls attempting to address the issue."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"Toda la investigación sobre las nebulosas está condenada a terminar de "
"esta manera. Todavía no he visto ningún proyecto que tenga éxito, a pesar de "
"todas las convocatorias de propuestas que intentan abordar el tema.\""

msgid "You inquire about other project members."
msgstr "Pregunta por otros miembros del proyecto."

msgid ""
"\"The only logical step after that traumatic experience is to get as far "
"away as possible from nebula research. As far as I know all the project "
"members moved to new topics, although none as exciting as mine.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El único paso lógico después de esa experiencia traumática es alejarse lo "
"más posible de la investigación de la nebulosa. Por lo que sé, todos los "
"miembros del proyecto se pasaron a nuevos temas, aunque ninguno tan "
"apasionante como el mío.\""

msgid ""
"\"Have you heard of graphene infused hydro nano lattices? By taking sheets "
"of graphene and creating strong lateral strain under the effect of intense "
"Coriolis electro-magnetic induction fields, it is possible to obtain a "
"behaviour similar to turbulent hydrofoils. And what's even better is that "
"they naturally form octahedral quasi-lattices that allow absorbing most low-"
"spectrum frequencies!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Ha oído hablar de las hidro-redes infundidas de grafeno? Tomando láminas "
"de grafeno y creando una fuerte tensión lateral bajo el efecto de intensos "
"campos de inducción electromagnética de Coriolis, es posible obtener un "
"comportamiento similar al de los hidroplanos turbulentos. Y lo que es aún "
"mejor, ¡forman naturalmente cuasilátices octaédricos que permiten absorber "
"la mayoría de las frecuencias de bajo espectro!\""

msgid ""
"\"They could change material science as we know it! Imagine being able to "
"create materials with almost any property you desire! We do still have to "
"solve the problem of the subatomic crystallite implosion, but once I finish "
"recovering the notes from the crater left at my last laboratory, I should be "
"able to solve it in no time. By the way, since the accident with my last "
"assistant, I'm looking for a new one. Would you be interested?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Podrían cambiar la ciencia de los materiales tal y como la conocemos! "
"¡Imagina poder crear materiales con casi cualquier propiedad que desees! "
"Todavía tenemos que resolver el problema de la implosión de los cristalitos "
"subatómicos, pero una vez que termine de recuperar las notas del cráter que "
"dejó mi último laboratorio, debería poder resolverlo en poco tiempo. Por "
"cierto, desde el accidente de mi último ayudante, estoy buscando uno nuevo. "
"¿Te interesaría?\""

msgid "You get away as fast as you can from them as they keep on rambling."
msgstr "Te alejas tan rápido como puedes mientras sigue divagando."

msgid ""
"\"Ah, such fond memories. I have never been interested in the artefacts from "
"the nebula themselves, but I was part of a large project dealing with them "
"as part of the philosophical and ethical committee.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ah, qué buenos recuerdos. Nunca me han interesado los artefactos de la "
"nebulosa en sí, pero formé parte de un gran proyecto relacionado con ellos "
"como parte del comité filosófico y ético.\""

msgid ""
"\"It is a very fascinating topic. Since there is no way to prove the "
"existence of an absolute reality, from a practical point of view, there are "
"infinite relative realities, where everyone has their own. Everything else "
"is an illusion derived from us projecting our understanding and reality onto "
"the reality of others, deforming them to a way we can interpret them with "
"our imperfect minds.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Es un tema muy fascinante. Como no hay forma de demostrar la existencia de "
"una realidad absoluta, desde un punto de vista práctico, hay infinitas "
"realidades relativas, donde cada uno tiene la suya. Todo lo demás es una "
"ilusión derivada de que proyectamos nuestra comprensión y nuestra realidad "
"sobre la de los demás, deformándolas de manera que podamos interpretarlas "
"con nuestras mentes imperfectas.\""

msgid ""
"\"Recently, due to the illogical imbalance between science and humanities, "
"all large Za'lek projects are required to have at least a 10% of humanities "
"members. This has given me lots of opportunities to work on many interesting "
"projects.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Recientemente, debido al ilógico desequilibrio entre las ciencias y las "
"humanidades, todos los grandes proyectos de Za'lek están obligados a tener "
"al menos un 10% de miembros de humanidades. Esto me ha dado muchas "
"oportunidades de trabajar en muchos proyectos interesantes.\""

msgid ""
"\"Oh yes, on the nebula artefacts. I remember having fun conversations with "
"our colleagues about whether or not the artefacts from the nebula actually "
"do exist or not given that we are using imperfect sensory organs to see, "
"touch, and feel them. You see, given that we only perceive reality through "
"our imperfect organs, can we actually know whether or not there is an "
"absolute objective reality?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ah, sí, sobre los artefactos de la nebulosa. Recuerdo haber tenido "
"divertidas conversaciones con nuestros colegas sobre si los artefactos de la "
"nebulosa existen realmente o no, dado que estamos utilizando órganos "
"sensoriales imperfectos para verlos, tocarlos y sentirlos. Verás, dado que "
"sólo percibimos la realidad a través de nuestros órganos imperfectos, "
"¿podemos saber realmente si existe o no una realidad objetiva absoluta?\""

msgid "You inquire about the other members of the project."
msgstr "Preguntas por los demás miembros del proyecto."

msgid ""
"\"Other members? I recall a few, but they liked me so much, they promoted me "
"and gave me a windowless room in the basement. What an honour! Anyway, back "
"to what I was saying.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Otros miembros? Recuerdo algunos, pero les gusté tanto que me ascendieron "
"y me dieron una habitación sin ventanas en el sótano. ¡Qué honor! En fin, "
"volviendo a lo que decía.\""

msgid ""
"\"We must also further question not only our sensory organs, and the "
"existence of nebula artefacts, but our own existence. We apparently are able "
"to think and some would argue that by this, the only thing we can prove, "
"given imperfect sensory data, is our own existence. However, I argue that "
"this too is an illusion, and that our existence itself is something we can't "
"prove.\""
msgstr ""
"\"También debemos cuestionar aún más no sólo nuestros órganos sensoriales, y "
"la existencia de artefactos de la nebulosa, sino nuestra propia existencia. "
"Aparentemente somos capaces de pensar y algunos argumentarían que con esto, "
"lo único que podemos probar, dados los datos sensoriales imperfectos, es "
"nuestra propia existencia. Sin embargo, yo sostengo que esto también es una "
"ilusión, y que nuestra propia existencia es algo que no podemos probar.\""

msgid ""
"\"Every instant, what we perceive as ourselves is ceasing to exist and a new "
"existence, which, while very close to the \"ourselves\" from the previous "
"instance, is, arguably, a completely new existence. This fluidity makes it "
"not only impossible to perceive nor understand our self as it is, but also "
"makes it impossible to draw a line between different individuals…\""
msgstr ""
"\"A cada instante, lo que percibimos como nosotros mismos está dejando de "
"existir y una nueva existencia, que, aunque muy cercana al \"nosotros\" de "
"la instancia anterior, es, posiblemente, una existencia completamente nueva. "
"Esta fluidez hace que no sólo sea imposible percibir ni comprender nuestro "
"yo tal y como es, sino que también hace imposible trazar una línea entre los "
"distintos individuos...\""

#, fuzzy
msgid "You thank them and run away while they keep on talking to themselves."
msgstr "Le das las gracias y sales corriendo mientras sigue hablando."

msgid "Dr. Shrimp"
msgstr "Dr. Gamba"

msgid "Floating Shrimp"
msgstr "Gamba Flotante"

msgid ""
"You approach the young man who has POST-DOCTORAL RESEARCHER written on his "
"lab coat. He seems to be really into a book titled 'SHRIMP: Anatomical "
"studies of the Neo-neo-neocaridina species'."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas al joven que lleva escrito en su bata de laboratorio "
"\"INVESTIGADOR POST-DOCTORAL\". Parece estar metido de lleno en un libro "
"titulado \"GAMBA: Estudios anatómicos de la especie Neo-neo-neocaridina\"."

msgid ""
"You wait to see if they notice your presence. While the young man reading "
"the book hasn't, it does seem like the strange shrimp-like creature floating "
"in an aquarium near them has. You feel like it's staring into your soul."
msgstr ""
"Espera a ver si se da cuenta de tu presencia. Aunque el joven que lee el "
"libro no lo ha hecho, parece que la extraña criatura parecida a un camarón "
"que flota en un acuario cerca de ellos sí lo ha hecho. Sientes que te está "
"mirando el alma."

msgid ""
"After what seems to be an eternity of a staring contest between you and the "
"shrimp, you hear a loud beep and the shrimp's speaker begins to make a "
"noise.\n"
"\"PERSON. PERSON.\""
msgstr ""
"Después de lo que parece ser una eternidad de un concurso de miradas entre "
"tú y la gamba, oyes un fuerte pitido y el altavoz de la gamba empieza a "
"hacer ruido.\n"
"\"PERSONA. PERSONA.\""

msgid ""
"The young man grumbles.\n"
"\"I told you I already submitted my temporal research proposal clarification "
"application yesterday.\""
msgstr ""
"El joven refunfuña.\n"
"\"Ya te dije que ayer presenté mi solicitud de aclaración de la propuesta de "
"investigación temporal.\""

msgid ""
"The young man suddenly breaks out of his reading stupor and looks at you as "
"if you had appeared out of thin air.\n"
"\"Wait, what? Who are you?\""
msgstr ""
"El joven sale de repente de su estupor de lectura y te mira como si hubieras "
"aparecido de la nada.\n"
"\"Espera, ¿qué? ¿Quién es usted?\""

msgid "\"PERSON. PERSON. PERSON.\""
msgstr "\"PERSONA. PERSONA. PERSONA.\""

msgid "\"C'mon Calliope, I already know that. Here, have a pellet.\""
msgstr "\"Vamos Calíope, ya lo sé. Toma, ten una bolita.\""

msgid "Calliope"
msgstr "Calíope"

msgid ""
"A pellet of shrimp food is released into the floating aquarium. The shrimp "
"wastes no time in scarfing it down.\n"
"   \"HAPPY. GOOD.\""
msgstr ""
"Se suelta un gránulo de comida para gambas en el acuario flotante. El "
"camarón no pierde tiempo en devorarlo.\n"
"   \"FELIZ. BUENO.\""

msgctxt "Dr. Shrimp"
msgid "\"What do you want?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué quieres?\""

msgid ""
"You explain to him that you are looking for information related to nebula "
"artefacts."
msgstr ""
"Le explicas que estás buscando información relacionada con los artefactos de "
"la nebulosa."

msgid ""
"\"Ah, that hellish project. Was doomed from the start, you know. The full-"
"time professors and researchers let their egos get to their heads and it "
"derailed spectacularly. I'm glad it ended as it did, or I would be still "
"stuck in that purgatory.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ah, ese proyecto infernal. Estaba condenado desde el principio. Los "
"profesores e investigadores a tiempo completo dejaron que sus egos se les "
"subieran a la cabeza y se descarriló espectacularmente. Me alegro de que "
"terminara como lo hizo, o todavía estaría atrapado en ese purgatorio.\""

msgid ""
"\"I don't think most of the people remember me, but I was the one stuck "
"doing most of the work. If you can call it that.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No creo que la mayoría de la gente se acuerde de mí, pero fui el que se "
"quedó haciendo la mayor parte del trabajo. Si se puede llamar así.\""

msgid ""
"\"My name is Cayne, but you can call me Dr. Shrimp. What would you like to "
"know?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Mi nombre es Cayne, pero puedes llamarme Dr. Gamba. ¿Qué te gustaría saber?"
"\""

msgid ""
"The young man suddenly breaks out of his reading stupor and looks at you as "
"if you had appeared out of thin air.\n"
"\"Ah, it is you again. Is there anything else you would want to know about?\""
msgstr ""
"El joven sale de repente de su estupor de lectura y te mira como si hubieras "
"aparecido de la nada.\n"
"\"Ah, es usted de nuevo. ¿Hay algo más que quieras saber?\""

msgid "\"Dr. Shrimp?\""
msgstr "\"¿Dr. Gamba?\""

msgid "Ask about nebula artefacts"
msgstr "Pregunta por los artefactos de la nebulosa"

msgid "Ask about other members."
msgstr "Pregunta por otros miembros."

msgid "Ask about Calliope"
msgstr "Pregunta sobre Calíope"

msgid "Ask about Dr. Strangelove"
msgstr "Pregunta por el Dr. Strangelove"

msgid "Anything else?…"
msgstr "¿Algo más?…"

msgid ""
"\"After the nebula project, like most other researchers on the team, I got "
"the hell away from nebula research. One day while visiting {pnt} I found out "
"about fresh-water shrimp breeding and became enthralled. One thing led to "
"another, and now I'm doing shrimp research.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Después del proyecto de la nebulosa, como la mayoría de los investigadores "
"del equipo, me alejé de la investigación de la nebulosa. Un día, mientras "
"visitaba {pnt} me enteré de la cría de gambas de agua dulce y me entusiasmé. "
"Una cosa llevó a la otra, y ahora me dedico a la investigación de la gamba.\""

msgid ""
"\"You see, shrimp are fascinating creatures. They have a really fast "
"reproduction cycle, and reproduce in large numbers, allowing for simple "
"genetic manipulation. While most are bred for colours and physical traits, "
"some have also been trained for mental traits. Calliope here is an example "
"of an extremely mentally capable shrimp.\"\n"
"He taps the tank of the floating shrimp next to him."
msgstr ""
"\"Verás, las gambas son criaturas fascinantes. Tienen un ciclo de "
"reproducción muy rápido y se reproducen en grandes cantidades, lo que "
"permite una manipulación genética sencilla. Aunque la mayoría se crían por "
"sus colores y rasgos físicos, algunos también han sido entrenados para "
"obtener rasgos mentales. Calíope es un ejemplo de una gamba con gran "
"capacidad mental.\"\n"
"Golpea el tanque de la gamba flotante que tiene al lado."

msgid ""
"\"The capabilities of these shrimp are endless, and they are helping us "
"understand much more about genetic modification than the brute-force "
"approaches of the Soromid, although our technology is still lagging behind.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Las capacidades de estas gambas son infinitas, y nos están ayudando a "
"entender mucho más sobre la modificación genética que los enfoques de fuerza "
"bruta Soromida, aunque nuestra tecnología todavía se está quedando atrás.\""

msgid ""
"\"And what's best, look how cute they are!\"\n"
"He enthusiastically points towards Calliope.\n"
"\"Isn't she the cutest?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Y lo que es mejor, ¡mira qué bonitas son!\"\n"
"Señala con entusiasmo a Calíope.\n"
"\"¿No es ella la más linda?\""

msgid ""
"\"After focusing on shrimp for a few cycles, people started calling me Dr. "
"Shrimp and the name stuck. Honestly, it's the best nickname they could give "
"me. Makes me feel like getting my PhD was finally worth it!\""
msgstr ""
"\" Calíope fue criada por sus facultades mentales. Con su acuario flotante "
"especial es capaz de articular hasta 20 palabras únicas. ¡Es increíble! Y no "
"sólo eso, sino que hemos conservado su buen aspecto. ¡Además, como neo-neo-"
"neocaridina, es mucho más grande que las neo-neocaridinas!\""

msgid ""
"\"Calliope was bred for her mental faculties. With her special floating "
"aquarium she is able to articulate up to 20 unique words! It's incredible! "
"Not only that, but we kept her good looks! Plus as a neo-neo-neocaridina, "
"she is much larger than neo-neocaridinas.\""
msgstr ""
"\" Calíope fue criada por sus facultades mentales. Con su acuario flotante "
"especial es capaz de articular hasta 20 palabras únicas. ¡Es increíble! Y no "
"sólo eso, sino que hemos conservado su buen aspecto. Además, como neo-neo-"
"neocaridina, es mucho más grande que las neo-neocaridinas.\""

msgid "\"FOOD. FOOD. FOOD.\""
msgstr "\"COMIDA. COMIDA. COMIDA.\""

msgid ""
"\"What would I do without her?\"\n"
"He activates her feeding system and a food pellet drops out."
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué haría sin ella?\"\n"
"Activa su sistema de alimentación y cae una bolita de comida."

msgid "\"HAPPY. HAPPY.\""
msgstr "\"FELIZ. FELIZ.\""

msgid ""
"\"She's the best shrimp we've been able to produce so far. She isn't capable "
"of self-awareness yet, and tends to forget words if she isn't properly "
"trained, but it is a start. By expanding their neural functionality we "
"expect them to be compatible with neuro-implants eventually. This will open "
"up a whole set of new functionality, given that their reaction speed and "
"neuro-motor ability is superb.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Es la mejor gamba que hemos podido producir hasta ahora. Todavía no es "
"capaz de tener conciencia de sí misma y tiende a olvidar las palabras si no "
"se la entrena adecuadamente, pero es un comienzo. Al ampliar su "
"funcionalidad neural, esperamos que con el tiempo sea compatible con los "
"neuroimplantes. Esto abrirá toda una serie de nuevas funcionalidades, dado "
"que su velocidad de reacción y su capacidad neuromotora son magníficas.\""

msgid ""
"\"I named her after a muse from some archaic religion I found while "
"researching. She is the only thing that keeps me going during my 17th post "
"doctoral fellowship.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Le puse el nombre de una musa de una religión arcaica que encontré "
"mientras investigaba. Ella es lo único que me hace seguir adelante durante "
"mi 17ª beca postdoctoral.\""

msgid ""
"\"What sort of artefacts we were dealing with? All sorts. Pretty much "
"anything we could get our hands on. We were trying to get a hold of stuff "
"closer to the origin, near Sol, but, most of the time, scavengers brought us "
"stuff from the outer areas. Many times they were even trying to sell us "
"random debris as nebula artefacts, but that's really easy to detect.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Con qué tipo de artefactos estábamos tratando? De todo tipo. "
"Prácticamente cualquier cosa que pudiéramos conseguir. Intentábamos hacernos "
"con cosas más cercanas al origen, cerca de Sol, pero, la mayoría de las "
"veces, los carroñeros nos traían cosas de las zonas exteriores. Muchas veces "
"incluso intentaban vendernos restos aleatorios como artefactos de la "
"nebulosa, pero eso es muy fácil de detectar.\""

msgid ""
"\"You see, the nebula emits a specific type of radiation. We aren't too "
"familiar with it, but it does alter the subatomic particles of space debris "
"in nearly imperceptible ways. Our tools could detect the alterations easily."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"Verá, la nebulosa emite un tipo específico de radiación. No estamos muy "
"familiarizados con ella, pero altera las partículas subatómicas de la basura "
"espacial de forma casi imperceptible. Nuestras herramientas podrían detectar "
"las alteraciones fácilmente.\""

msgid ""
"\"When the project failed, most of the artefacts were confiscated to who "
"knows where, but I managed to keep a nut from what I think is a space "
"station, although not entirely sure. It's a bit damaged beyond recognition "
"you see.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Cuando el proyecto fracasó, la mayoría de los artefactos fueron "
"confiscados a quién sabe dónde, pero me las arreglé para conservar una "
"tuerca de lo que creo que es una estación espacial, aunque no estoy del todo "
"seguro. Está un poco dañada hasta el punto de que no se puede reconocer.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"With the failure of most nebula projects, I don't think there is anybody "
"buying nebula artefacts any more. Not much of a market for them, and most "
"easy to access debris has all been scavenged anyway. Some collectors are "
"still interested in that, but that's about it. Furthermore, it's not "
"entirely legal if you catch my drift.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Con el fracaso de la mayoría de los proyectos de nebulosa, no creo que "
"haya ya nadie que compre artefactos de nebulosa. No hay mucho mercado para "
"ellos, y la mayoría de los restos de fácil acceso han sido recogidos de "
"todos modos. Algunos coleccionistas siguen interesados en ello, pero eso es "
"todo. Además, no es del todo legal, si me entiendes.\""

msgid ""
"\"Most of the project members were full professors, which is probably why it "
"failed. Us post-doctoral researchers do all the work and get none of the "
"credit.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La mayoría de los miembros del proyecto eran profesores titulares, y "
"probablemente por eso fracasó. Los investigadores posdoctorales hacemos todo "
"el trabajo y no recibimos ningún crédito.\""

msgid ""
"\"After it went to hell, many of the researchers lost their posts or went "
"into hiding. The few I know that still are active are Prof. Stova, Prof. "
"Sato, and Prof. Hsu. I think they even got some stupid promotion, while the "
"other post docs and I lost our jobs.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Después de que se fuera al infierno, muchos de los investigadores "
"perdieron sus puestos o se escondieron. Los pocos que conozco que siguen en "
"activo son el profesor Stova, el profesor Sato y el profesor Hsu. Creo que "
"incluso consiguieron algún estúpido ascenso, mientras que los otros post "
"docs y yo perdimos nuestros trabajos.\""

msgid ""
"\"It's pretty incredible to think that there were originally 100ish people "
"on the project. Yet even with all the people fired for falsification of "
"results, not a single tenured post opened! It's ridiculous! If industry "
"wasn't so horrible, I would quit academia in an instant!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Es bastante increíble pensar que originalmente había unas 100 personas en "
"el proyecto. Sin embargo, incluso con toda la gente despedida por "
"falsificación de resultados, ¡no se abrió ni un solo puesto de titular! Es "
"ridículo. Si la industria no fuera tan horrible, dejaría el mundo académico "
"en un instante.\""

msgid ""
"\"Now that I think of it, there was another guy. What was his name? I "
"totally forget. Oh well.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ahora que lo pienso, había otro tipo. ¿Cómo se llamaba? Lo he olvidado por "
"completo. Ah, bueno.\""

msgid ""
"\"Now I remember! There was a another post-doctoral researcher who worked "
"with me. He was a bit weird and kept obsessing over the nebula artefacts. "
"Quite a few went missing during the project and I think it was probably him "
"who was taking them.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Ahora me acuerdo! Había otro investigador posdoctoral que trabajaba "
"conmigo. Era un poco raro y se obsesionaba con los artefactos de la "
"nebulosa. Desaparecieron bastantes durante el proyecto y creo que "
"probablemente era él quien se los llevaba.\""

msgid ""
"\"He was really upset when the project got cancelled, threw a big tantrum "
"and all. He was locked in his office for days until they managed to coax him "
"out. Nobody really did much as we were all busy dealing with all the "
"paperwork of the project cancellation.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Se enfadó mucho cuando se canceló el proyecto, hizo un gran berrinche y "
"todo. Estuvo encerrado en su despacho durante días hasta que consiguieron "
"sacarlo. Nadie hizo gran cosa porque todos estábamos ocupados con todo el "
"papeleo de la cancelación del proyecto.\""

msgid ""
"\"Eventually he sort of disappeared. Last I heard, he said he was going to "
"{sys}, which is a bit strange, because not only is there not a research "
"centre there, but there isn't even an inhabited planet nor station!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Al final desapareció. Lo último que supe es que iba a {sys}, lo cual es un "
"poco extraño, porque no sólo no hay un centro de investigación allí, ¡sino "
"que ni siquiera hay un planeta habitado ni una estación!\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"It's really weird but if you are really interested, I suppose you could "
"try to take a look around there. The whole thing gives me the creeps though."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"Es realmente extraño, pero si estás realmente interesado, supongo que "
"podrías intentar echar un vistazo por allí. Aunque todo esto me da "
"escalofríos.\""

msgid "\tGo to {sys}"
msgstr "Ve a {sys}"

msgid ""
"You found about a strange researcher who appears to be in Westhaven and is "
"related to the nebula research."
msgstr ""
"Descubriste a un extraño investigador que parece estar en Refugio Oeste y "
"está relacionado con la investigación de la nebulosa."

msgid "Feral Drone"
msgstr "Dron Salvaje"

#. Spawn the drones
msgid "Feral Alpha Drone"
msgstr "Dron Salvaje Alfa"

msgid "Security Drone"
msgstr "Dron de Seguridad"

#. Easier to spot
#. Around j1
#. Around j2
#. Fuzzes a position a bit
#. We are nice and make the drones easier to see for this mission
msgid "Hostiles detected!"
msgstr "¡Hostiles detectados!"

msgid "UNAUTHORIZED VESSEL DETECTED. ELIMINATING."
msgstr "NAVEGACIÓN NO AUTORIZADA DETECTADA. ELIMINANDO."

#. All dead
msgid "Your ship detects that one of the asteroids isn't what it seems…"
msgstr "Tu nave detecta que uno de los asteroides no es lo que parece…"

msgid ""
"You were attacked by a Za'lek security system and found a laboratory "
"disguised as an asteroid in Westhaven."
msgstr ""
"Has sido atacado por un sistema de seguridad Za'lek y has encontrado un "
"laboratorio disfrazado de asteroide en Refugio Oeste."

msgid "Unknown Voice"
msgstr "Voz Desconocida"

#. Really slow fade in so the player stops mashing keys due to combat (keypresses aren't processed in animations)
msgid ""
"While the drone is blowing up, you receive a faint, audio-only transmission."
msgstr "Mientras el dron explota, recibes una débil transmisión de audio."

msgid "\"Thank you for setting me free…\""
msgstr "\"Gracias por liberarme...\""

msgid ""
"You wonder what that was about as you watch the drone thrash as it blows up. "
"Westhaven is a really weird place."
msgstr ""
"Te preguntas de qué se trata mientras ves cómo el dron se estrella al "
"explotar. Refugio Oeste es un lugar realmente extraño."

msgid ""
"From the ship scraps you are able to find a very damaged… thing… You guess "
"this is what Dr. Strangelove was referring to as a nebula artefact. "
"Strangely, your ship sensors identify it as mainly biological material…"
msgstr ""
"De los restos de la nave consigues encontrar una cosa... muy dañada... "
"Supones que es lo que el Dr. Strangelove denominaba artefacto de la "
"nebulosa. Extrañamente, los sensores de tu nave lo identifican como material "
"principalmente biológico…"

msgid "Nebula Artefact?"
msgstr "¿Artefacto de Nebulosa?"

msgid ""
"A very damaged thing that seems to be mainly biological. I guess this is the "
"nebula artefact?"
msgstr ""
"Una cosa muy dañada que parece ser principalmente biológica. ¿Supongo que "
"esto es el artefacto de la nebulosa?"

msgid "Go back to Dr. Strangelove"
msgstr "Vuelve a ver al Dr. Strangelove"

msgid ""
"You recovered a nebula artefact that Dr. Strangelove wanted from feral "
"drones."
msgstr ""
"Has recuperado un artefacto de la nebulosa que el Dr. Strangelove quería de "
"los drones salvajes."

msgid "Just destroy me and put me out of my misery."
msgstr "Sólo destrúyeme y sácame de mi miseria."

msgid "Why am I still alive?"
msgstr "¿Por qué estoy todavía vivo?"

#, fuzzy
msgid "I can't deal with this any more."
msgstr "No puedo seguir lidiando con esto."

msgid "Please end me!"
msgstr "¡Por favor, acaba conmigo!"

msgid "Living is suffering."
msgstr "Vivir es sufrir."

msgid "It all hurts."
msgstr "Todo duele."

msgid "Please kill me!"
msgstr "¡Por favor, mátame!"

#. We go with nebula music
msgid ""
"The hologram projector flickers and what appears to be a grumpy old man "
"appears into view. He doesn't look very pleased to be disturbed."
msgstr ""
"El proyector de hologramas parpadea y aparece lo que parece ser un viejo "
"gruñón. No parece muy contento de ser molestado."

msgid "\"How did you get in there? Who are you!\""
msgstr "\"¿Cómo has entrado ahí? ¿Quién eres tú?\""

msgid ""
"You explain to him that you are looking for information about nebula "
"artefacts."
msgstr ""
"Le explicas que estás buscando información sobre artefactos de la nebulosa."

msgid ""
"\"Who sent you here? Was it Dr. Bob? That weasel was always after my "
"precious artefacts. Well, he can't have them! I got all this with my hard "
"work, sweat, and tears! They're all mine!\"\n"
"He cackles manically."
msgstr ""
"\"¿Quién te envió aquí? ¿Fue el Dr. Bob? Esa comadreja siempre estaba detrás "
"de mis preciosos artefactos. ¡Bueno, no puede tenerlos! ¡Tengo todo esto con "
"mi trabajo duro, sudor y lágrimas! Son todos míos\".\n"
"Se ríe maníacamente."

msgid ""
"\"I have hidden them very well. Even though you somehow got past my security "
"system and made it into my laboratory, you'll never find them!\"\n"
"You glance at a crate labelled 'NEBULA ARTEFACTS #082' in the corner of the "
"room."
msgstr ""
"\"Los he escondido muy bien. Aunque de alguna manera hayas burlado mi "
"sistema de seguridad y hayas conseguido entrar en mi laboratorio, ¡nunca los "
"encontrarás!\"\n"
"Miras una caja etiquetada como \"ARTEFACTOS DE NEBULOSA #082\" en la esquina "
"de la habitación."

msgid ""
"\"Anyway, I am very busy now, yes? All this science won't do itself. Almost "
"have a new specimen ready and it will be better than ever! The old ones were "
"fairly inadequate.\""
msgstr ""
"\"De todos modos, estoy muy ocupado ahora, ¿sí? Toda esta ciencia no se hará "
"sola. Casi tengo un nuevo espécimen listo y será mejor que nunca. Los "
"antiguos eran bastante inadecuados.\""

msgid "You met an eccentric researcher named Dr. Strangelove in Westhaven."
msgstr ""
"Conociste a un excéntrico investigador llamado Dr. Strangelove en Refugio "
"Oeste."

msgid ""
"The hologram projector flickers and Dr. Strangelove comes into view. He "
"doesn't look very happy to see you again."
msgstr ""
"El proyector de hologramas parpadea y el Dr. Strangelove aparece. No parece "
"muy contento de volver a verte."

msgctxt "Dr. Strangelove"
msgid "\"What do you want?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué quieres?\""

msgid "Ask about the nebula"
msgstr "Pregunta por la nebulosa"

msgid "Ask about this place"
msgstr "Pregunta por este lugar"

msgid "Hand over the artefact"
msgstr "Entrega el artefacto"

msgid "Ask about job"
msgstr "Pregunta por el trabajo"

msgid ""
"\"Ah yes, the nebula. The pinnacle of human creation! Isn't it just "
"mesmerizing and beautiful to look at? I've always been attracted to it ever "
"since the Incident destroyed my university. Destruction is so pretty, is it "
"not?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ah sí, la nebulosa. La cúspide de la creación humana. ¿No es simplemente "
"hipnotizante y hermoso de ver? Siempre me ha atraído desde que el Incidente "
"destruyó mi universidad. La destrucción es tan bonita, ¿no?\""

msgid ""
"\"I recently had the great opportunity to work directly on nebula research. "
"It was a fabulous project with hundreds of the brightest Za'lek minds "
"working in tandem! Not as brilliant as me, but the numbers were what "
"mattered.\"\n"
"He grins as nostalgia takes him over."
msgstr ""
"\"Hace poco tuve la gran oportunidad de trabajar directamente en la "
"investigación de las nebulosas. Fue un proyecto fabuloso con cientos de las "
"mentes más brillantes de los Za'lek trabajando en conjunto. No tan "
"brillantes como yo, pero los números eran lo que importaba.\"\n"
"Sonríe mientras la nostalgia se apodera de él."

msgid ""
"\"We were able to have dedicated teams recovering all sorts of incredible "
"items! We even found the remains of a Proteron replicator! It was only able "
"to replicate cheese fondue, but it was incredible. I integrated it with a "
"drone platform and that has kept me healthy and in shape since! It should be "
"in the bar if you want to try it.\"\n"
"You see a greasy robot in the corner that is boiling some sort of brown "
"liquid. Is that… cheese?"
msgstr ""
"\"¡Pudimos tener equipos dedicados a recuperar todo tipo de objetos "
"increíbles! ¡Incluso encontramos los restos de un replicador Proteron! Sólo "
"era capaz de replicar fondue de queso, pero era increíble. Lo integré con "
"una plataforma de drones y ¡eso me ha mantenido sano y en forma desde "
"entonces! Debería estar en el bar si quieres probarlo.\"\n"
"Ves un robot grasiento en la esquina que está hirviendo una especie de "
"líquido marrón. ¿Es eso... queso?"

msgid ""
"\"Anyway, it is a real shame that the bureaucrats in central station killed "
"the project in its prime. At least I was able to bring most of the devices "
"here and keep acquiring more artefacts afterwards. Haven't found anything as "
"fancy as the replicator yet, but the bodies have been very interesting.\"\n"
"He coughs, wracking his body."
msgstr ""
"\"De todos modos, es una verdadera lástima que los burócratas de la estación "
"central hayan matado el proyecto en su mejor momento. Al menos pude traer la "
"mayoría de los dispositivos aquí y seguir adquiriendo más artefactos "
"después. Todavía no he encontrado nada tan elegante como el replicador, pero "
"los cuerpos han sido muy interesantes.\"\n"
"Tose, sacudiendo su cuerpo."

msgid "\"Bodies…?\""
msgstr "\"¿Cuerpos...?\""

msgid "\"What devices?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué dispositivos?\""

msgid ""
"\"Ahaha. You are interested, no? That information won't come cheap. I have a "
"job that I would like you to do, and, in exchange, I might give you the "
"information you seek.\""
msgstr ""
"\" Jajaja. Estás interesado, ¿no? Esa información no será barata. Tengo un "
"trabajo que me gustaría que hicieras y, a cambio, podría darte la "
"información que buscas.\""

msgid "Refuse the job"
msgstr "Rechazas el trabajo"

msgid "\"You don't scratch my back and I don't scratch yours.\""
msgstr "\"Tú no me rascas la espalda y yo no te rasco la tuya.\""

msgid ""
"\"I see you are braver than you look. I have a bit of an issue. You see, I "
"was upgrading some of my drones with some nebula artefacts to test to see if "
"the functionality could be improved. Sadly, an incompatibility resulted in "
"the drones going… ahem… feral.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Veo que eres más valiente de lo que pareces. Tengo un pequeño problema. "
"Verás, estaba mejorando algunos de mis drones con algunos artefactos de la "
"nebulosa para probar si se podía mejorar la funcionalidad. Lamentablemente, "
"una incompatibilidad hizo que los drones se volvieran... ejem... salvajes.\""

msgid ""
"\"I was going to try to deal with them with my security drones, but as you "
"can guess, that is no longer an option since you smashed them to smithereens."
"\"\n"
"He glares at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Iba a intentar ocuparme de ellos con mis drones de seguridad, pero como "
"puedes adivinar, eso ya no es una opción desde que los hiciste añicos\".\n"
"Te mira fijamente."

msgid ""
"\"While the drones themselves are dispensable, I need you to recover the "
"nebula artefacts used in their upgrading. They should be roaming around the "
"asteroid field and should be fairly easy to find. Make sure to recover the "
"parts in one piece!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Mientras que los propios drones son prescindibles, necesito que recuperes "
"los artefactos de la nebulosa utilizados en su mejora. Deberían estar "
"vagando por el campo de asteroides y deberían ser bastante fáciles de "
"encontrar. ¡Asegúrate de recuperar las piezas en una sola pieza!\""

msgid "Recover nebula artefacts from the {sys} asteroid field"
msgstr ""
"Recupera los artefactos de la nebulosa del campo de asteroides en {sys}"

msgid ""
"You accepted Dr. Strangelove's request to recover nebula artefacts from "
"feral drones in Westhaven."
msgstr ""
"Has aceptado la petición del Dr. Strangelove de recuperar los artefactos de "
"la nebulosa de los drones salvajes en Refugio Oeste."

msgid ""
"\"It should be an easy job. All you have to do is recover the nebula "
"artefacts from the feral drones. They may put up a fight or not be easy to "
"catch, but I expect that a pilot who blasted through all my security drones "
"will have no problem with a few feral drones. Try to bring the artefacts in "
"one piece.\"\n"
"He glares at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Debería ser un trabajo fácil. Todo lo que tienes que hacer es recuperar "
"los artefactos de la nebulosa de los drones salvajes. Puede que se resistan "
"o que no sean fáciles de atrapar, pero espero que un piloto que se cargó "
"todos mis drones de seguridad no tenga problemas con unos cuantos drones "
"salvajes. Intenta traer los artefactos de una pieza.\"\n"
"Te mira fijamente."

msgid ""
"\"How do you like it? Cutting edge Za'lek research! I had to borrow a lot of "
"things from my past jobs, but they can't have it back. It's all mine now! I "
"made sure everything is covered in my scent so that they won't be able to "
"appropriate it!\"\n"
"He smiles mischievously."
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué te parece? ¡Investigación Za'lek de vanguardia! Tuve que tomar "
"prestadas muchas cosas de mis trabajos anteriores, pero no pueden "
"recuperarlas. ¡Ahora es todo mío! ¡Me aseguré de que todo estuviera cubierto "
"de mi olor para que no pudieran apropiarse de él!\"\n"
"Sonríe con picardía."

msgid ""
"\"My drones dug it out and it's the cosiest place I have ever lived in, but "
"I don't get many guests. In fact, you are my…\"\n"
"He starts counting on his fingers intently.\n"
"\"…first guest! Yes, that's it, the first true living biological being other "
"than me to visit!\"\n"
"You don't like how he puts emphasis on 'living biological'…"
msgstr ""
"\"Mis drones los desenterraron y es el lugar más acogedor en el que he "
"vivido, pero no tengo muchos invitados. De hecho, tú eres mi...\"\n"
"Empieza a contar con los dedos atentamente.\n"
"\"...¡el primer invitado! Sí, eso es, ¡el primer ser biológico vivo "
"verdadero que me visita!\"\n"
"No te gusta cómo pone el énfasis en \"biológico vivo\"…"

msgid ""
"\"Feel free to use the facilities as you please, but stay out of the "
"backroom.\"\n"
"Given the smell of the entire laboratory and especially the horrible scents "
"wafting from the backroom, you feel like it is best to heed his advice for "
"your own safety."
msgstr ""
"\"Siéntete libre de usar las instalaciones como quieras, pero mantente "
"alejado de la habitación trasera.\"\n"
"Teniendo en cuenta el olor de todo el laboratorio y, sobre todo, los "
"horribles olores que emanan de la sala trasera, crees que es mejor seguir su "
"consejo por tu propia seguridad."

msgid ""
"You show him the nebula artefact and suddenly a couple of small drones whirl "
"into the room and start to perform a deeper inspection."
msgstr ""
"Le muestras el artefacto de la nebulosa y, de repente, un par de pequeños "
"drones entran en la sala y comienzan a realizar una inspección más profunda."

msgid ""
"\"Energy levels 7%… I see, I see… minor flux instability… not that bad…\n"
"no vitals… not very good… mmmm… nebula radiation at minimum… can't be helped "
"I guess…\""
msgstr ""
"\"Niveles de energía 7%... ya veo, ya veo... inestabilidad de flujo menor... "
"no es tan malo...\n"
"no hay signos vitales... no es muy bueno... mmmm... la radiación de la "
"nebulosa al mínimo... no se puede evitar, supongo...\""

msgid ""
"He goes on for what seems like an eternity before finally remembering that "
"you are there.\n"
"\"Why are you still here? Go back to wherever the hell you came from!\""
msgstr ""
"Continúa durante lo que parece una eternidad antes de recordar finalmente "
"que estás ahí.\n"
"\"¿Por qué sigues aquí? ¡Vuelve al infierno de donde has venido!\""

msgid "\"What about my information?\""
msgstr "\"¿Y mi información?\""

msgid "\"What the hell is this thing?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué demonios es esta cosa?\""

msgid ""
"\"I see… You don't grasp the importance of this artefact. I guess it can't "
"be helped with such an inferior intellect as yours.\"\n"
"He sneers."
msgstr ""
"\"Ya veo... No comprendes la importancia de este artefacto. Supongo que no "
"se puede evitar con un intelecto tan inferior como el tuyo.\"\n"
"Se burla."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"This is my latest creation, amalgamate of ancient nebula technology and "
"life. Think of this as something that not only surpasses any of the Soromid "
"biotechnology, but also Za'lek cybertechnology. It is the peak of "
"technological advancement!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Esta es mi última creación, una amalgama de tecnología y vida de la "
"nebulosa antigua. Piensa en esto como algo que no sólo supera cualquier "
"biotecnología Soromida, sino también la cibertecnología Za'lek. ¡Es la cima "
"del avance tecnológico!\""

msgid ""
"\"While it has an incredible potential, there are… some complications still. "
"The mental faculties tend to lack stability. While this one is a very "
"interesting failure, it is still a failure at heart. Most of my other "
"creations have had much more success.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Aunque tiene un potencial increíble, hay... algunas complicaciones "
"todavía. Las faculteaes mentales tienden a carecer de estabilidad. Aunque "
"este es un fracaso muy interesante, sigue siendo un fracaso en el fondo. La "
"mayoría de mis otras creaciones han tenido mucho más éxito.\""

msgid "\"What was it you wanted?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué era lo que querías?\""

msgid "You ask him if he knows anything about Kex's ship in the nebula."
msgstr "Le preguntas si sabe algo de la nave de Kex en la nebulosa."

msgid ""
"\"Ah yes! I remember that wreck. A very, very curious one indeed. At that "
"time I was exploring the nebula myself, and we came upon this most curious "
"wreck that had clear signs of fighting. While it is not uncommon for "
"scavengers to squabble among themselves, this one had most of the damage on "
"the inside. The damage on the outside was clearly done later to confuse "
"people who were investigating like us.\"\n"
"He coughs."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Ah, sí! Recuerdo ese naufragio. Uno muy, muy curioso. Por aquel entonces "
"yo mismo estaba explorando la nebulosa, y nos topamos con este pecio tan "
"curioso que tenía claros signos de lucha. Aunque no es raro que los "
"carroñeros se peleen entre ellos, éste tenía la mayor parte de los daños en "
"el interior. El daño en el exterior fue claramente hecho después para "
"confundir a la gente que estaba investigando como nosotros.\"\n"
"Tose."

msgid ""
"\"While it was not a pre-incident ship nor had any interesting "
"characteristics, what was inside was surprising. There were two bodies still "
"warm to the touch, it seems like time passes differently in such deep "
"nebula. Normally I would ignore such things. However, they had been infused "
"with so much nebula radiation that they seemed to have potential!\"\n"
"He starts to get excited."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"That's when I realized it, humankind and the nebula are one and the same. "
"Our futures are intertwined! By absorbing the nebula into the body, one can "
"transcend humanity and live forever among the stars! There is no limit to "
"the potential infused in the nebula! Now I get it! All my research had led "
"up to this!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Fue entonces cuando me di cuenta, la humanidad y la nebulosa son una misma "
"cosa. ¡Nuestros futuros están entrelazados! ¡Al absorber la nebulosa en el "
"cuerpo, uno puede trascender la humanidad y vivir para siempre entre las "
"estrellas! ¡No hay límite para el potencial infundido en la nebulosa! ¡Ahora "
"lo entiendo! ¡Toda mi investigación me había llevado a esto!\""

msgid ""
"\"And that's when it hit me, by amalgamating nebula and flesh, we can "
"transcend ourselves! I had to do it; it had to be done! And it worked, oh "
"boy did it work. There were some difficulties with flesh incompatibility, "
"but with suitable replacements I was able to solve it.\"\n"
"He laughs manically."
msgstr ""
"\"Y fue entonces cuando me di cuenta de que, amalgamando la nebulosa y la "
"carne, ¡podemos trascender a nosotros mismos! Tenía que hacerlo; ¡había que "
"hacerlo! Y funcionó, vaya si funcionó. Hubo algunas dificultades con la "
"incompatibilidad de la carne, pero con los reemplazos adecuados pude "
"resolverlo.\"\n"
"Se ríe maníacamente."

msgid ""
"\"They were oh so perfect, like Adam and Eve, ready to create a new perfect "
"humanity. However, it isn't as simple as that. The man, an ungrateful fool, "
"had too much attachment to his previous life. How weak… That's when I "
"realized it. You need a perfect mind and perfect flesh to become the perfect "
"being. With the nebula, the perfect flesh can be done, but the mind must "
"also be perfect. It was so simple!\"\n"
"He seems delirious."
msgstr ""
"\"Eran tan perfectos, como Adán y Eva, dispuestos a crear una nueva "
"humanidad perfecta. Sin embargo, no es tan sencillo. El hombre, un tonto "
"desagradecido, tenía demasiado apego a su vida anterior. Qué débil... Fue "
"entonces cuando me di cuenta. Se necesita una mente perfecta y una carne "
"perfecta para convertirse en el ser perfecto. Con la nebulosa, la carne "
"perfecta puede hacerse, pero la mente también debe ser perfecta. Era tan "
"sencillo\".\n"
"Parece desvariar."

msgid ""
"\"So I did it. I tried to upgrade myself. But it isn't so simple, you see, "
"it's the near-death experience that is necessary. On healthy flesh it just "
"deteriorates the body.\"\n"
"He coughs, convulsing."
msgstr ""
"\"Así que lo hice. Intenté actualizarme. Pero no es tan sencillo, verás, es "
"la experiencia cercana a la muerte lo que es necesario. En la carne sana "
"sólo deteriora el cuerpo.\"\n"
"Tose, convulsionando."

msgid ""
"\"The mind was good enough, but not my body. No, and I don't have much time. "
"I'm wasting away. So close and here wasting away. What uselessness.\"\n"
"He lowers his gaze."
msgstr ""
"\"La mente era lo suficientemente buena, pero no mi cuerpo. No, y no tengo "
"mucho tiempo. Me estoy consumiendo. Tan cerca y aquí consumiéndose. Qué "
"inutilidad.\"\n"
"Baja la mirada."

msgid "You ask what happened to the 'individuals' in the experiments."
msgstr "Preguntas qué pasó con los \"individuos\" de los experimentos."

msgid ""
"\"I did try to track him down, last I checked he got caught by thugs at "
"Minerva Station. Nasty place in the Limbo system. No nebula and very stale "
"space. Not beautiful at all.\"\n"
"He coughs softly."
msgstr ""
"\"Intenté localizarlo, la última vez que lo comprobé fue atrapado por unos "
"matones en la estación Minerva. Un lugar desagradable en el sistema Limbo. "
"No hay nebulosas y el espacio es muy rancio. No es nada bonito\".\n"
"Tose suavemente."

msgid ""
"\"She tried to help me, but she too was weak of mind, and one day left for "
"the stars. I couldn't stop her, but I thought I was close enough. I just "
"need more time. One more cycle…\"\n"
"His voice gets softer and softer as he keeps on mumbling."
msgstr ""
"\"Intentó ayudarme, pero ella también estaba débil de mente, y un día partió "
"hacia las estrellas. No pude detenerla, pero pensé que estaba lo "
"suficientemente cerca. Sólo necesito más tiempo. Un ciclo más...\"\n"
"Su voz se vuelve cada vez más suave mientras sigue murmurando."

msgid ""
"You try to get his attention again, but it doesn't seem to work. He seems to "
"have fallen into a stupor. You feel you have enough information to report to "
"Maikki again."
msgstr ""
"Intentas llamar su atención de nuevo, pero no parece funcionar. Parece haber "
"caído en un estado de estupor. Crees que tienes suficiente información para "
"informar a Maikki de nuevo."

msgid "Report back to Maikki in the Limbo system"
msgstr "Informa a Maikki en el sistema Limbo"

msgid ""
"You learned that Dr. Strangelove saved what appears to be Kex and another "
"individual from a wreck in the nebula. Kex appears to have run away and is "
"likely held by thugs at Minerva station."
msgstr ""
"Te has enterado de que el Dr. Strangelove ha salvado a lo que parece ser Kex "
"y a otro individuo de un naufragio en la nebulosa. Kex parece haber huido y "
"es probable que esté retenido por matones en la estación Minerva."

msgid ""
"You leave behind the hologram projection and hope you won't have to deal "
"with Dr. Strangelove in the future."
msgstr ""
"Dejas atrás la proyección del holograma y esperas no tener que lidiar con el "
"Dr. Strangelove en el futuro."

msgid ""
"You turn off the hologram projector and Dr. Strangelove's image flickers and "
"disappears."
msgstr ""
"Apagas el proyector de hologramas y la imagen del Dr. Strangelove parpadea y "
"desaparece."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 1">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <cond>var.peek("minerva_altercation_probability")~=nil</cond>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. <requires name="Minerva Altercation 1" />
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Beat up Dvaered thugs making them think the za'leks did it
#. --
#. Mission constants:
#. in seconds
#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 0: Go pick up Drone
#. 1: Trigger Thugs
#. 2: Survive
#. 3: Run away
#. 4: Get back to Minerva STation
#. Non-persistent state
msgid "Someone wants you to mess around with Dvaered thugs."
msgstr "Alguien quiere que te metas con los matones Dvaered."

msgid "Cold hard credits"
msgstr "Créditos duros y fríos"

msgid "Dvaered Thugs"
msgstr "Matones Dvaered"

msgid ""
"You approach the sketchy individual who seems to be calling your attention."
msgstr "Te acercas a la individua sospechosa que parece llamar tu atención."

msgid ""
"\"What do you think about them Za'leks and Dvaereds? Quite a work, eh? "
"Always getting into fights with each other and creating trouble for those "
"who just want to enjoy life. Such a bother.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué piensas de los Za'leks y los Dvaereds? Todo un trabajo, ¿eh? Siempre "
"metiéndose en peleas entre ellos y creando problemas a los que sólo quieren "
"disfrutar de la vida. Una molestia.\""

msgid ""
"\"Say what, I know you're a pretty decent pilot. Would you be interested in "
"a somewhat non-standard job? Nothing very out of the ordinary, just want to "
"ruffle some feathers.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Dime qué, sé que eres un piloto bastante decente. ¿Estarías interesado en "
"un trabajo un tanto atípico? Nada muy fuera de lo común, sólo quiero "
"alborotar algunas plumas.\""

msgid "Kindly decline"
msgstr "Rechazar amablemente"

msgid "You decline their offer and take your leave."
msgstr "Rechazas su oferta y te vas."

msgid ""
"\"Excellent. As you probably know, the Za'lek and Dvaered want to take "
"control of this station, hence the large amount of military crawling all "
"over the station. This leads to inevitable disagreements, quarrels, brawls, "
"altercations, fights, you name it. Instead of trying to take care of it "
"directly, we can sort of encourage them to take care of each other and "
"problem solved, no?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Excelente. Como probablemente sabes, los Za'lek y los Dvaered quieren "
"tomar el control de esta estación, de ahí la gran cantidad de militares que "
"se arrastran por toda la estación. Esto conduce a inevitables desacuerdos, "
"riñas, peleas, altercados, peleas, lo que sea. En lugar de intentar "
"ocuparnos directamente, podemos animarles a que se ocupen unos de otros y "
"problema resuelto, ¿no?\""

msgid ""
"\"I know what you're thinking, that's a great idea right? So it's very "
"simple. Some Dvaered thugs are stationed around the system, they are not the "
"cleverest of folks, so I want you to provoke them. You know, just rough them "
"up a little and get out of there.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Sé lo que estás pensando, es una gran idea, ¿verdad? Pues es muy sencillo. "
"Algunos matones Dvaered están apostados por el sistema, no son los más "
"listos, así que quiero que los provoques. Ya sabes, dales un poco de caña y "
"sal de ahí.\""

msgid ""
"\"Sounds naïve, yes? Might be. So, I've managed to get a Za'lek drone shell, "
"all it has is the engine and some basic following software, but no weapons "
"or gear. If you were to drag it along while harassing the thugs, they "
"probably would think that there is some kind of Za'lek involvement. They're "
"not the smartest fellows in the world if you catch my drift.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Suena ingenuo, ¿no? Puede ser. Así que me las he arreglado para conseguir "
"un caparazón de dron Za'lek, todo lo que tiene es el motor y algún software "
"básico de seguimiento, pero no hay armas ni equipo. Si lo arrastras mientras "
"acosas a los matones, probablemente pensarán que hay algún tipo de "
"participación Za'lek. No son los tipos más inteligentes del mundo, si me "
"entiendes.\""

msgid ""
"\"To make sure they are all riled up, I want you to spend 15 seconds "
"harassing them near their original location. Make sure to harass them, but "
"don't kill them! We want them to tell the other Dvaereds about this. Once "
"the time is up, get the hell away from there, in one piece if possible.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Para asegurarte de que están todos irritados, quiero que pases 15 segundos "
"acosándolos cerca de su ubicación original. Asegúrate de acosarlos, pero no "
"los mates. Queremos que le cuenten esto a los otros Dvaereds. Una vez que el "
"tiempo se acabe, aléjate de allí, en una pieza si es posible.\""

msgid ""
"\"I've sent you the coordinates of both the Za'lek drone and the Dvaered "
"thugs. I'll pay you well if you manage to pull this off. Oh and one more "
"thing, when getting away, make sure to jump to the {sys} system to make it "
"look even more like the Za'lek did it.\"\n"
"They beam a smile at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Te he enviado las coordenadas tanto del dron Za'lek como de los matones "
"Dvaered. Te pagaré bien si consigues llevar a cabo esto. Ah, y una cosa más, "
"cuando te alejes, asegúrate de saltar al sistema {sys} para que parezca aún "
"más que lo hizo los Za'lek.\"\n"
"Te sonríen."

#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
msgid ""
"You accepted a job from a sketchy individual to harass Dvaered thugs in the "
"Limbo system and make it seem like the Za'lek were involved."
msgstr ""
"Aceptaste un trabajo de un individuo sospechoso para acosar a los matones "
"Dvaered en el sistema Limbo y hacer parecer que los Za'lek estaban "
"involucrados."

msgid "Thug Decoy"
msgstr "Señuelo de Matones"

msgid "Get the drone to follow you"
msgstr "Haz que el dron te siga"

msgid "Harass the thugs"
msgstr "Acosa a los matones"

msgid "Jump to {sys}"
msgstr "Salta a {sys}"

msgid "Go back to Minerva Station"
msgstr "Vuelve a la Estación Minerva"

msgid ""
"After you land on Minerva Station you are once again greeted by the sketchy "
"character that gave you the job dealing with the Dvaered thugs."
msgstr ""
"Después de aterrizar en la Estación Minerva, te vuelve a saludar el "
"personaje sospechoso que te dio el trabajo de lidiar con los matones Dvaered."

msgid ""
"\"I hear it went rather well. This should cause more tension between the "
"Za'lek and the Dvaered so we can get them off this station. However, this is "
"only the beginning.\""
msgstr ""
"\"He oído que ha ido bastante bien. Esto debería causar más tensión entre "
"los Za'lek y los Dvaered para que podamos sacarlos de esta estación. Sin "
"embargo, esto es sólo el comienzo.\""

msgid ""
"\"If you are interested, I may have another job for you which I believe you "
"are more than capable of handling. Meet me up at the bar if you want more "
"information. I have also transferred a sum of credits to your account as a "
"reward for your services.\"\n"
"She winks at you and walks way."
msgstr ""
"\"Si estás interesado, puedo tener otro trabajo para ti que creo que eres "
"más que capaz de manejar. Reúnete conmigo en el bar si quieres más "
"información. También he transferido una suma de créditos a tu cuenta como "
"recompensa por tus servicios.\"\n"
"Te guiña un ojo y se marcha."

msgid ""
"You succeeded in making the Dvaered think that the Za'lek were harassing "
"their thugs near Minerva station."
msgstr ""
"Has conseguido hacer creer a los Dvaered que los Za'lek estaban acosando a "
"sus matones cerca de la estación de Minerva."

msgid "You were supposed to harass the thugs with the drone."
msgstr "Se suponía que ibas a acosar a los matones con el dron."

msgid "You were supposed to jump to the {sys} system!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que ibas a saltar al sistema {sys}!"

msgid "Za'lek Drone"
msgstr "Dron Za'lek"

msgid "#gThe drone begins to follow you."
msgstr "#gEl dron comienza a seguirte."

#. Make enemies
msgid "I'm going to wash my ship's hull with your blood, Za'lek Scum!"
msgstr "¡Voy a lavar el casco de mi nave con tu sangre, Escoria Za'lek!"

msgid "You were supposed to harass the thugs, not kill them!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que tenías que acosar a los matones, no matarlos!"

msgid "#rYou are moving too far away from the harassment point!"
msgstr "#r¡Te estás alejando demasiado del punto de acoso!"

msgid "You moved too far away from the harassment location!"
msgstr "¡Te has alejado demasiado del lugar de acoso!"

msgid "#gThe thugs seem to be sufficiently riled up."
msgstr "#gLos matones parecen estar suficientemente irritados."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 2">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <done>Minerva Pirates 1</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Destroy a suspicious Za'lek drone.
#. --
#. Mission constants:
#. HERE should be rather close to jumpin pos.
#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 0: Go kill drone
#. 1: Get back to Minerva Station
#. Non-persistent state
msgid ""
"Someone wants you to incapacitate a suspicious Za'lek drone with only "
"Dvaered weapons. Usable weapons are:"
msgstr ""
"Alguien quiere que incapacites a un dron Za'lek sospechoso sólo con armas "
"Dvaered. Las armas utilizables son:"

msgid ""
"\n"
"* "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"* "

msgid ""
"You approach the sketchy individual who seems to be calling your attention "
"once again."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas a la individua sospechosa que parece llamar tu atención una vez "
"más."

msgid ""
"\"It seems like our last job worked better than we thought. The Dvaered are "
"all riled up, just as planned. However, there is still a lot left to do.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Parece que nuestro último trabajo funcionó mejor de lo que pensábamos. Los "
"Dvaered están alborotados, tal y como estaba previsto. Sin embargo, aún "
"queda mucho por hacer.\""

msgid ""
"\"I have another job if you are interested. It should be simpler than last "
"time, only this time we target the Za'lek instead of the Dvaered to try to… "
"improve the situation.\"\n"
"She smiles at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Tengo otro trabajo si estás interesado. Debería ser más sencillo que la "
"última vez, sólo que esta vez nos dirigimos a los Za'lek en vez de a los "
"Dvaered para intentar... mejorar la situación.\"\n"
"Te sonríe."

msgid "You decline her offer and take your leave."
msgstr "Rechazas su oferta y te marchas."

msgid ""
"\"Glad to have you onboard again! So the idea is very simple, we've seen "
"that the Za'lek are setting up some reconnaissance stuff around the system. "
"Nothing very conspicuous, but there are some scout drones here and there. I "
"want you to take them out.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Me alegro de tenerte a bordo de nuevo! Así que la idea es muy simple, "
"hemos visto que los Za'lek están estableciendo algunas cosas de "
"reconocimiento alrededor del sistema. Nada muy llamativo, pero hay algunos "
"drones exploradores aquí y allá. Quiero que los elimines.\""

msgid ""
"\"Just destroying them won't cut it though. We need to make it look like the "
"Dvaered did it this time. However, that should be simple. Make sure to use "
"Dvaered weapons to take the drones out. You know, Mace Launchers, Vulcan "
"Guns, Shredders, Mass Drivers, Railguns and such. Make sure to not use any "
"non-Dvaered weapons!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Sin embargo, destruirlos no será suficiente. Tenemos que hacer que parezca "
"que los Dvaered lo hicieron esta vez. Sin embargo, eso debería ser sencillo. "
"Asegúrate de usar las armas de los Dvaered para eliminar los drones. Ya "
"sabes, Lanzadores Maza, Cañones Vulcano, Trituradores, Impulsores de Masa, "
"Cañones de Riel y demás. ¡Asegúrate de no usar ningún arma que no sea "
"Dvaered!\""

msgid ""
"\"There should be two drones out there. I have given you the locations where "
"they were last seen. Try to take out the drones as fast as possible and get "
"back here in one piece.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Debería haber dos drones ahí fuera. Os he dado las localizaciones donde "
"fueron vistos por última vez. Intenta acabar con los drones lo más rápido "
"posible y vuelve aquí de una pieza.\""

#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
msgctxt "OSD Title"
msgid "Za'lek Scout Drone"
msgstr "Dron Explorador Za'lek"

msgid "Destroy the scout drone with Dvaered weapons"
msgstr "Destruye el dron explorador con armas Dvaered"

msgid ""
"You accept another job from the sketchy individual to destroy some Za'lek "
"scout drones around Minerva Station with Dvaered weapons only to make it "
"seem like the Dvaered are targeting Za'lek drones."
msgstr ""
"Aceptas otro trabajo de un individuo sospechoso para destruir algunos drones "
"exploradores Za'lek alrededor de la Estación Minerva con armas Dvaered sólo "
"para hacer creer que los Dvaered están atacando a los drones Za'lek."

msgid ""
"After you land on Minerva Station you are once again greeted by the sketchy "
"character that gave you the job to clear the Za'lek drones."
msgstr ""
"Después de aterrizar en la Estación Minerva, vuelves a ser recibido por el "
"personaje sospechoso que te encargó la tarea de eliminar los drones Za'lek."

msgid ""
"\"Excellent piloting there. We didn't think that the Za'lek would catch on "
"so fast and send in reinforcements, however, it all worked out in the end.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Excelente pilotaje. No pensamos que los Za'lek se dieran cuenta tan rápido "
"y enviaran refuerzos, sin embargo, al final todo salió bien.\""

msgid ""
"\"This should bring suspicions to a new high between Dvaered and Za'lek. "
"There have already been 20 casualties from fighting this period! At this "
"rate they will basically solve themselves. However, that might be a bit "
"slow, so let us try to accelerate the process a bit more.\"\n"
"She winks at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Esto debería llevar las sospechas a un nuevo nivel entre Dvaered y Za'lek. "
"¡Ya ha habido 20 bajas en los combates de este periodo! A este ritmo, "
"básicamente se resolverán por sí solas. Sin embargo, eso podría ser un poco "
"lento, así que tratemos de acelerar el proceso un poco más\".\n"
"Te guiña un ojo."

msgid ""
"\"I've wired you some credits for your efforts. Meet me up at the bar for "
"another potential job.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Te he transferido algunos créditos por tus esfuerzos. Reúnete conmigo en "
"el bar para otro posible trabajo.\""

msgid ""
"You succeeded in destroying Za'lek drones and making it seem like the "
"Dvaered were involved."
msgstr ""
"Lograste destruir drones Za'lek y hacer parecer que los Dvaered estaban "
"involucrados."

msgid " ({ship})"
msgstr " ({ship})"

msgid "Non-Dvaered equipped weapons detected: {list}"
msgstr "Detectadas armas equipadas no Dvaered: {list}"

msgid "You were supposed to kill the drones with Dvaered-only weapons!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que debías matar a los drones con armas Dvaered!"

msgid "You detected another Za'lek drone in the system!"
msgstr "¡Has detectado otro dron Za'lek en el sistema!"

msgid "You let a drone get away!"
msgstr "¡Has dejado escapar un dron!"

msgid "Your sensors are detecting a Za'lek fleet inbound!"
msgstr "¡Tus sensores detectan una flota Za'lek en camino!"

msgid "#oZa'lek reinforcements have arrived!"
msgstr "#o¡Los refuerzos de Za'lek han llegado!"

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 3">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <done>Minerva Pirates 2</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. <provides name="Spa Propaganda" />
#. <provides name="Chicken Rendezvous">Kidnapped Winner</provides>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Find the Dvaered spy
#. --
#. TODO unique?
msgid ""
"Present your winning ticket at the terminal to enter the Minerva Station Spa."
msgstr ""
"Presenta tu billete ganador en la terminal para entrar en el Balneario de la "
"Estación Minerva."

#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 0: try to find out how to plant listening device
#. 1. hear about chicken spa event
#. 2. enter chicken spa event
#. 3. obtain spa event ticket from harper
#. 4. do chicken spa event
#. 5. planted listening device
#. These two will be done in another mission
#. 6. kidnap spy and take to torture ship
#. 7. defend torture ship
#. Non-persistent state
msgid ""
"Someone wants you to find a Dvaered spy that appears to be located at "
"Minerva Station."
msgstr ""
"Alguien quiere que encuentres a un espía Dvaered que parece estar ubicado en "
"la Estación Minerva."

msgid "Finding the Dvaered Spy"
msgstr "Encontrar Al Espía Dvaered"

#. Clear variable just in case
#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
msgid "Minerva Station Spa"
msgstr "Balneario de la Estación Minerva"

#. A reminder in case the player starts Kex's branch and forgets this was pending.
msgid "Minerva Moles"
msgstr "Topos Minerva"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Report back to {pir}."
msgstr "Informe en {pnt}"

#. Not accepted
msgid ""
"You approach the sketchy individual who seems to be calling your attention "
"yet once again."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas a la individua sospechosa que parece llamar tu atención una vez "
"más."

msgid ""
"\"Hello again, we have another job for you. Our previous actions have led us "
"to believe that there are several Dvaered and Za'lek spies deeply "
"infiltrated into the station infrastructure. Would you be up to the "
"challenge of helping us get rid of them?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hola de nuevo, tenemos otro trabajo para ti. Nuestras acciones anteriores "
"nos han llevado a creer que hay varios espías Dvaered y Za'lek profundamente "
"infiltrados en la infraestructura de la estación. ¿Estarías dispuesto a "
"ayudarnos a deshacernos de ellos?\""

msgid "Plant a listening device in a VIP room."
msgstr "Coloca un dispositivo de escucha en una sala VIP."

msgid ""
"You accepted another job from the sketchy individual to uncover moles at "
"Minerva Station."
msgstr ""
"Aceptaste otro trabajo del individuo sospechoso para descubrir topos en la "
"Estación Minerva."

msgid ""
"\"Glad to have you onboard again. From the few intercepted Dvaered and "
"Za'lek communications we were able to decode, it seems like we might have "
"some moles at Minerva Station. They are probably really deep so it won't be "
"an easy task to drive them out.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Me alegro de tenerte a bordo de nuevo. A partir de las pocas "
"comunicaciones interceptadas Dvaered y Za'lek que pudimos decodificar, "
"parece que podríamos tener algunos topos en la estación Minerva. "
"Probablemente estén muy profundos, así que no será una tarea fácil "
"expulsarlos.\""

msgid ""
"\"That's where this comes in to place.\"\n"
"She takes out a metallic object from her pocket and show it to you. You "
"don't know what to make of it.\n"
"\"Ain't she a beauty?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ahí es donde entra esto.\"\n"
"Saca un objeto metálico de su bolsillo y te lo muestra. No sabes qué pensar "
"de él.\n"
"\"¿No es una belleza?\""

msgid ""
"\"This is some high-tech shit that we got from some geeks. It's a latest gen "
"signal capturing device, and should be able to bypass most jammers. However, "
"we're going to need you to plant it in a VIP room or some place where we "
"might catch the mole.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Esta es una mierda de alta tecnología que conseguimos de algunos genios. "
"Es un dispositivo de captura de señales de última generación, y debería ser "
"capaz de eludir la mayoría de los inhibidores. Sin embargo, vamos a "
"necesitar que lo coloques en una sala VIP o en algún lugar donde podamos "
"atrapar al topo.\""

msgid ""
"\"The main issue we have right now is that VIP rooms and such are not easy "
"to access, so we're going to have to keep our eyes open and see if we can "
"spot an opportunity to plant the device.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El principal problema que tenemos ahora mismo es que las salas VIP y demás "
"no son de fácil acceso, así que vamos a tener que mantener los ojos abiertos "
"y ver si podemos detectar una oportunidad para plantar el dispositivo.\""

msgid ""
"She hands you the signal capturing device and briefly explains how it "
"works.\n"
"\"Take the device and see if you can find a chance to place it. I'll be at "
"the spaceport bar if you figure anything out.\""
msgstr ""
"Te entrega el dispositivo de captación de señales y te explica brevemente "
"cómo funciona.\n"
"\"Coge el dispositivo y mira a ver si puedes encontrar una oportunidad para "
"colocarlo. Estaré en el bar del puerto espacial por si averiguas algo.\""

#. Accepted.
msgid "You approach the sketchy character you have become familiarized with."
msgstr "Te acercas al personaje sospechoso con el que te has familiarizado."

msgid ""
"You explain to them that you were able to successfully plant the device in "
"the Minerva Spa."
msgstr ""
"Les explicas que has podido colocar con éxito el dispositivo en el Balneario "
"de Minerva."

msgid ""
"\"Great job! I knew you had it in you. Catching the mole now should be just "
"a matter of time. After we collect some data and process them, we can see "
"how to catch the asshole. Meet me again at the bar in a bit, I have a "
"feeling we will catch them soon.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Gran trabajo! Sabía que lo llevabas dentro. Atrapar al topo ahora debería "
"ser sólo cuestión de tiempo. Después de recoger algunos datos y procesarlos, "
"podremos ver cómo atrapar al gilipollas. Reúnete conmigo en el bar dentro de "
"un rato, tengo el presentimiento de que los atraparemos pronto.\""

msgid ""
"You planted a listening device in the Minerva Spa to catch a mole and were "
"rewarded for your actions."
msgstr ""
"Has colocado un dispositivo de escucha en el Balneario de Minerva para "
"atrapar a un topo y has sido recompensado por tus acciones."

msgid "\"Is there anything you would like to know?\""
msgstr "\"¿Hay algo que te gustaría saber?\""

msgid "Ask them about the spa"
msgstr "Pregunta por el balneario"

msgid "Show them the spa ticket"
msgstr "Muéstrales el billete del balneario"

msgid "Show them the winning ticket"
msgstr "Muéstrales el billete ganador"

msgid ""
"\"From the few intercepted Dvaered and Za'lek communications we were able to "
"decode, it seems like we might have some moles at Minerva Station. They are "
"probably really deep so it won't be an easy task to drive them out.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Por las pocas comunicaciones interceptadas Dvaered y Za'lek que pudimos "
"decodificar, parece que podríamos tener algunos topos en la Estación "
"Minerva. Probablemente están muy profundos, así que no será una tarea fácil "
"expulsarlos.\""

msgid ""
"\"The high-tech latest gen signal capturing device I gave should be able to "
"bypass most jammers. However, you're going to have to plant it in a VIP room "
"or in some place where we might be able to catch the mole.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El dispositivo de captación de señales de última generación de alta "
"tecnología que te di debería ser capaz de eludir la mayoría de los "
"inhibidores. Sin embargo, vas a tener que colocarlo en una sala VIP o en "
"algún lugar donde podamos atrapar al topo.\""

msgid ""
"\"You never know when we'll get a chance, just take your time doing stuff "
"near Minerva station and I'm sure you'll find an opening.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Nunca se sabe cuándo tendremos una oportunidad, tómate tu tiempo haciendo "
"cosas cerca de la estación Minerva y seguro que encuentras un hueco.\""

msgid ""
"\"The Spa sounds like a perfect place to set up the signal capturing device. "
"Nobody will suspect a thing! You should buy a ticket to the Spa and see if "
"we can get lucky. If not, we may have to take other measures to ensure "
"success.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El Balneario parece un lugar perfecto para instalar el dispositivo de "
"captación de señales. Nadie sospechará nada. Deberías comprar una entrada "
"para el Balneario y ver si tenemos suerte. Si no, puede que tengamos que "
"tomar otras medidas para asegurar el éxito.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"I can't believe we didn't win a ticket to the Spa. However, it seems like "
"this guy called Harper Bowdoin managed to get it instead.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No puedo creer que nos hayamos ganado una entrada para el Balneario. Sin "
"embargo, parece que este tipo llamado Harper Bowdown se las arregló para "
"conseguirlo en su lugar.\""

msgid ""
"\"I need you to go pay this guy a visit. See if you can 'encourage' them to "
"give the ticket to you. Everyone has a price at Minerva Station.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Necesito que vayas a visitar a este tipo. A ver si puedes 'animarle' a que "
"te dé el billete. Todo el mundo tiene un precio en la Estación de Minerva.\""

msgid ""
"\"You got the ticket to the Minerva Spa, so all you have to do now is go in, "
"plant the listening device, and enjoy the thermal waters.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tienes la entrada al Balneario de Minerva, así que lo único que tienes que "
"hacer ahora es entrar, colocar el dispositivo de escucha y disfrutar de las "
"aguas termales.\""

msgid ""
"\"Isn't this place great? They managed to set up an incredibly successful "
"business model here. The way the Empire basically turns a blind eye to "
"everything that goes on here is just incredible! Makes you want to root for "
"their success you know?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿No es genial este lugar? Han conseguido establecer un modelo de negocio "
"increíblemente exitoso aquí. La forma en que el Imperio básicamente hace la "
"vista gorda a todo lo que sucede aquí es simplemente increíble. Hace que "
"quieras alentar su éxito, ¿sabes?\""

msgid ""
"\"The issue is that even though the set-up is great, all the Dvaered and "
"Za'lek bickering is just messing it all up. It would be a real shame if "
"things went tits up and either the Dvaered or Za'lek were able to take over "
"this wonderful place.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El problema es que, aunque el montaje es genial, todas las discusiones "
"entre los Dvaered y los Za'lek lo están estropeando todo. Sería una "
"verdadera lástima que las cosas se fueran al garete y que los Dvaered o los "
"Za'lek pudieran hacerse con este maravilloso lugar.\""

msgid ""
"\"So me and my investors thought to ourselves, what could we do to ensure "
"the success of such a wonderful place? This led to that and here we are.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Así que mis inversores y yo pensamos: ¿qué podríamos hacer para garantizar "
"el éxito de un lugar tan maravilloso? Esto nos llevó a ello y aquí estamos.\""

msgid ""
"\"Ah, so you heard the news too? The Spa sounds like a perfect place to set "
"up the signal capturing device. Nobody will suspect a thing! You should buy "
"a ticket and see if we can get lucky. If not, we may have to take other "
"measures to ensure success.\"\n"
"She winks at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Ah, ¿así que tú también has oído las noticias? El balneario parece un "
"lugar perfecto para instalar el dispositivo de captación de señales. Nadie "
"sospechará nada. Deberías comprar una entrada y ver si tenemos suerte. Si "
"no, puede que tengamos que tomar otras medidas para asegurar el éxito.\"\n"
"Te guiña un ojo."

msgid "Our chances of getting into the Spa can't be that bad, can they?"
msgstr ""
"Nuestras posibilidades de entrar en el Balneario no pueden ser tan malas, "
"¿verdad?"

msgid ""
"Suddenly, the terminals around you blast a fanfare and begin to talk on the "
"loudspeakers.\n"
"\"WE ARE HAPPY TO ANNOUNCE THE WINNER OF THE FABULOUS SPA WITH CYBORG "
"CHICKEN EVENT!\"\n"
"The terminal pauses for emphasis."
msgstr ""
"De repente, los terminales que te rodean lanzan una fanfarria y empiezan a "
"hablar por los altavoces.\n"
"\"¡NOS COMPLACE ANUNCIAR AL GANADOR DEL FABULOSO BALNEARIO CON EL EVENTO DEL "
"POLLO CYBORG!\"\n"
"El terminal hace una pausa para enfatizar."

msgid ""
"\"THE WINNER IS HARPER BOWDOIN! PLEASE COME TO YOUR NEAREST TERMINAL TO "
"COLLECT YOUR PRIZE.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡EL GANADOR ES HARPER BOWDOIN! POR FAVOR, ACUDA AL TERMINAL MÁS CERCANO "
"PARA RECOGER SU PREMIO.\""

msgid ""
"\"Shit! I thought we had that rigged. Damn it. Give me one second.\"\n"
"She starts frantically typing into her portable holo-deck. It makes weird "
"beeps and noises."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Mierda! Pensaba que lo teníamos amañado. Maldita sea. Dame un segundo.\"\n"
"Empieza a teclear frenéticamente en su holocubierta portátil. Hace pitidos y "
"ruidos extraños."

msgid ""
"\"OK, so we aren't so bad off. It seems like the winner was doing some space "
"tourism around the system. Not like there is anything to see here.\""
msgstr ""
"\"OK, así que no estamos tan mal. Parece que el ganador estaba haciendo "
"turismo espacial por el sistema. No hay nada que ver aquí.\""

msgid ""
"\"So change of plans, I need you to go pay this guy a visit. See if you can "
"'encourage' them to give the ticket to you. Everyone has a price at Minerva "
"Station.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Así que cambio de planes, necesito que vayas a visitar a este tipo. A ver "
"si puedes 'animarle' a que te de el billete. Todo el mundo tiene un precio "
"en la Estación Minerva.\""

msgid "Get Harper Bowdoin's ticket in Limbo."
msgstr "Consigue el billete de Harper Bowdoin en el Limbo."

msgid ""
"You did not obtain the winning ticket of the Minerva Spa event and were "
"tasked with obtaining it from a so called Harper Bowdoin."
msgstr ""
"No obtuviste la papeleta ganadora del evento del Balneario de Minerva y te "
"encargaron que la obtuvieras de un tal Harper Bowdoin."

msgid "You show them the winning ticket you took from Harper Bowdoin."
msgstr "Muéstrales el boleto ganador que tomaste de Harper Bowdoin."

msgid ""
"\"Great job out there. It's like taking candy from a baby.\"\n"
"She beams you a smile.\n"
"\"Now go enjoy yourself at the Spa and don't forget to plant the listening "
"device!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Gran trabajo ahí fuera. Es como quitarle un caramelo a un bebé\".\n"
"Te dedica una sonrisa.\n"
"\"¡Ahora ve a disfrutar en el Balneario y no te olvides de plantar el "
"dispositivo de escucha!\""

msgid "Plant a listening device in the Spa."
msgstr "Coloca un dispositivo de escucha en el Spa."

msgid "You obtained the winning ticket to enter the Minerva Spa."
msgstr ""
"Has obtenido el billete ganador para entrar en el Balneario de Minerva."

msgid ""
"You take your leave and ponder where you should start looking. The casino "
"seems to be your best bet."
msgstr ""
"Te despides y reflexionas sobre dónde deberías empezar a buscar. El casino "
"parece ser tu mejor opción."

#. Don't stop spawns, but claimed in case something else stops spawns
#. TODO maybe add Minerva patrols that aggro ta make it a bit harder?
#. Spawn Harper Bowdoin and stuff
msgid "Harper"
msgstr "Harper"

#. Should make them loiter forever
#. Don't distress or everyone aggros
#. Clear variables to be kind to the player
msgid "You were supposed to get the ticket, but you blew up Harper's ship!"
msgstr ""
"¡Se suponía que ibas a conseguir el billete, pero volaste la nave de Harper!"

#. Case harper lands with the ticket, i.e., ran away
msgid "You were supposed to get the ticket but Harper got away!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que conseguirías el billete pero Harper se escapó!"

msgid ""
"You violently enter Harper's ship and plunder the ticket which you were "
"after, while Harper spends his time cowering in the corner of the cockpit."
msgstr ""
"Entras violentamente en la nave de Harper y saqueas el billete que buscabas, "
"mientras Harper se pasa el tiempo encogido en un rincón de la cabina."

#. Run to land at the station
msgid "Stop shooting! Maybe we can reach an agreement!"
msgstr "¡Deja de disparar! ¡Tal vez podamos llegar a un acuerdo!"

msgid "Pay him {credits} (#rnot enough!#0)"
msgstr "Le pagas {credits} (#r¡no es suficiente!#0)"

msgid "Pay him {credits}"
msgstr "Le pagas {credits}"

msgid "Offer {credits} (#rnot enough!#0)"
msgstr "Ofreces {credits} (#r¡no es suficiente!#0)"

msgid "Offer {credits}"
msgstr "Ofreces {credits}"

#. He goes land now
msgid "You see Harper's hologram appear into view. He looks paler than usual."
msgstr ""
"Ves el holograma de Harper aparecer. Parece más pálido que de costumbre."

msgid ""
"\"I have had a change of mind.\"\n"
"He gulps.\n"
"\"How about I give you the ticket for a mere {credits}?"
msgstr ""
"\"He cambiado de opinión.\"\n"
"Traga saliva.\n"
"\"¿Qué tal si te doy el billete por unos pocos {credits}?"

msgid "Threaten him"
msgstr "Amenázale"

msgid ""
"\"Actually, swimming with a chicken sounds like a bit of a drag. I think I "
"might be allergic to them anyway.\"\n"
"He coughs nervously."
msgstr ""
"\"La verdad es que nadar con una gallina suena un poco a rollo. Creo que "
"podría ser alérgico a ellos de todos modos.\"\n"
"Tose nerviosamente."

#. Player can theoretically board to loot it back
msgid ""
"You wire him the money and he gives you the digital code that represents the "
"ticket. Looks like you are set."
msgstr ""
"Le envías el dinero y él te da el código digital que representa el billete. "
"Parece que estás listo."

msgid ""
"He laughs nervously.\n"
"\"You have to be kidding right? You wouldn't kill me in cold blood would "
"you? I have a family waiting for me back home."
msgstr ""
"Se ríe nerviosamente.\n"
"\"Tienes que estar bromeando, ¿verdad? No me matarías a sangre fría, "
"¿verdad? Tengo una familia que me espera en casa."

msgid "Aim your weapons at him"
msgstr "Apúntale con tus armas"

msgid ""
"\"I have a daughter! She is turning 5 soon. You wouldn't be so cold-hearted "
"to leave her an orphan would you?\"\n"
"He is sweating profusely."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Tengo una hija! Pronto cumplirá 5 años. No tendrías el corazón tan frío "
"de dejarla huérfana, ¿verdad?\"\n"
"Está sudando profusamente."

msgid "Prime your weapon systems"
msgstr "Prepara tus sistemas de armas"

msgid ""
"\"Ah, damn this! I've still got things worth living for. Here, just take the "
"damn thing.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Ah, maldita sea! Todavía tengo cosas por las que vale la pena vivir. "
"Toma, coge la maldita cosa.\""

msgid ""
"He gives you the digital code that represents the ticket. Looks like you are "
"set."
msgstr ""
"Te da el código digital que representa el billete. Parece que estás listo."

msgid ""
"\"Wait do you mean you don't have the money?\"\n"
"He looks around nervously.\n"
"\"Ah, damn this. I've still got things worth living for. Here, just take the "
"damn thing.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Espera, ¿quieres decir que no tienes el dinero?\"\n"
"Mira a su alrededor con nerviosismo.\n"
"\"Ah, maldita sea. Todavía tengo cosas por las que vale la pena vivir. Toma, "
"coge la maldita cosa.\""

msgid "Get away from me!"
msgstr "¡Aléjate de mí!"

msgid "An impatient man appears into view."
msgstr "Un hombre impaciente aparece a la vista."

msgid "\"You again? I don't have time to deal with you.\""
msgstr "\"¿Otra vez tú? No tengo tiempo para tratar contigo.\""

msgid "The comm goes silent…"
msgstr "La comunicación se enmudece…"

msgid "You hail Harper's vessel and you see him appear into view."
msgstr "Llamas a la nave de Harper y lo ves aparecer."

msgid "\"What do you want? Can't you see I'm celebrating my luck?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué quieres? ¿No ves que estoy celebrando mi suerte?\""

msgid "\"Luck?\""
msgstr "\"¿Suerte?\""

msgid "\"Celebrating?\""
msgstr "\"¿Celebrando?\""

msgid ""
"\"Yeah, you may have heard the news, but I'm the big winner of the Minerva "
"hot spring event! On my first time to Minerva Station too! Maybe this will "
"finally cure my back pains once and for all. The ticket is even made of pure "
"gold!\"\n"
"He looks triumphant as he boasts."
msgstr ""
"\"Sí, puede que hayas oído las noticias, ¡pero soy el gran ganador del "
"evento de aguas termales de Minerva! ¡En mi primera vez en la Estación "
"Minerva también! Quizá esto cure por fin mis dolores de espalda de una vez "
"por todas. ¡El billete es incluso de oro puro!\"\n"
"Parece triunfante mientras se jacta."

msgid "\"About the ticket…\""
msgstr "\"Sobre el billete...\""

msgid "End transmission"
msgstr "Fin de la transmisión"

msgid "\"What about it?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué pasa con eso?\""

msgid "\"Give it to me. Now.\""
msgstr "\"Dámelo. Ahora.\""

msgid "\"I would like to take it off your hands.\""
msgstr "\"Me gustaría quitártelo de las manos.\""

msgid ""
"\"What are you going to do? Shoot me?\"\n"
"He scoffs at you and closes the transmission."
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué vas a hacer? ¿Dispararme?\"\n"
"Se burla de ti y cierra la transmisión."

msgid ""
"\"I don't know. This is very valuable you know? What would you trade for it?"
"\""
msgstr "\"No sé. Esto es muy valioso, ¿sabes? ¿Qué cambiarías por él?\""

msgid "Offer {bribe} (have {tokens})"
msgstr "Ofrecer {bribe} (tienes {tokens})"

msgid ""
"\"Actually, swimming with a chicken sounds like a bit of a drag. I think I "
"might be allergic to them anyway.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La verdad es que nadar con una gallina suena un poco a rollo. Creo que "
"podría ser alérgico a ellos de todos modos.\""

msgid ""
"You wire him the tokens and he gives you the digital code that represents "
"the ticket. Looks like you are set."
msgstr ""
"Le transfieres las fichas y él te da el código digital que representa el "
"billete. Parece que estás listo."

msgid ""
"\"{credits} only? I spent more than that gambling just to get this ticket.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Sólo {credits}? He gastado más que eso apostando sólo para conseguir este "
"billete.\""

msgid ""
"\"You trying to pull my leg or something? You don't have enough credits. "
"Anyway, I'm busy now.\"\n"
"He cuts the transmission."
msgstr ""
"\"¿Intentas tomarme el pelo o algo así? No tienes suficientes créditos. De "
"todos modos, ahora estoy ocupado.\"\n"
"Corta la transmisión."

msgid "You close the transmission channel."
msgstr "Cierras el canal de transmisión."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 4">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <done>Minerva Pirates 3</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. <done_evt name="Chicken Rendezvous" />
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. -- Torture the Dvaered Spy
#. --
#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 0. have to find spy
#. 1. kidnap spy and take to torture ship
#. 2. defend torture ship
#. Non-persistent state
msgid ""
"Someone wants you to deal with a Dvaered spy that appears to be located at "
"Minerva Station."
msgstr ""
"Alguien quiere que te encargues de un espía Dvaered que parece estar ubicado "
"en la Estación Minerva."

#. In the case the player failed/crashed the mission ,we want to clear the
#. change so they can repeat it without modifying their save
#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
#. Signal they were caught
#. On to next state
#. Set up stuff
#. Should fight back a bit
#. Update OSD
msgid "Minerva Mole"
msgstr "Topo de Minerva"

msgid "Find out who the mole is"
msgstr "Averigua quién es el topo"

msgid ""
"You accepted another job from the sketchy individual to deal with a mole at "
"Minerva Station."
msgstr ""
"Aceptaste otro trabajo del individuo sospechoso para ocuparte de un topo en "
"la Estación Minerva."

#. Not accepted
msgid "You approach the sketchy individual who seems to be somewhat excited."
msgstr "Te acercas a la individua sospechosa que parece estar algo excitado."

msgid ""
"\"It seems like we have finally started to get the fruits of our labour. We "
"believe we have found the mole, and would like you to help us deal with "
"them. Are you up to the task? Things might get a little… messy though.\"\n"
"They beam you a smile."
msgstr ""
"\"Parece que por fin hemos empezado a obtener los frutos de nuestro trabajo. "
"Creemos que hemos encontrado al topo, y nos gustaría que nos ayudaras a "
"enfrentarnos a ellos. ¿Estás a la altura de la tarea? Aunque las cosas "
"podrían ponerse un poco... desordenadas\".\n"
"Te dirigen una sonrisa."

msgid ""
"\"Glad to have you onboard again! So we have tracked down the mole and know "
"from intercepted messages that they are most likely working at the station. "
"Now, there are not many places to work at the station, so it is likely that "
"they are involved in the gambling facility.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Me alegro de tenerte de nuevo a bordo! Así que hemos rastreado el topo y "
"sabemos por los mensajes interceptados que lo más probable es que estén "
"trabajando en la estación. Ahora, no hay muchos lugares para trabajar en la "
"estación, por lo que es probable que estén involucrados en la instalación de "
"juegos de azar.\""

msgid ""
"\"The bad news is we don't exactly know who the mole is. However, the good "
"news is we were able to intercept a messenger. It was after a delivery so we "
"weren't able to capture anything very interesting. But there was a small "
"memo we found that could be a hint.\"\n"
"The individual produces a crumpled up dirty piece of paper that has '10k¤ "
"5-6-3-1' on it and hands it to you."
msgstr ""
"\"La mala noticia es que no sabemos exactamente quién es el topo. Sin "
"embargo, la buena noticia es que pudimos interceptar a un mensajero. Fue "
"después de una entrega, así que no pudimos captar nada muy interesante. Pero "
"encontramos un pequeño memorándum que podría ser una pista.\"\n"
"El individuo saca un trozo de papel sucio y arrugado que tiene \"10k¤ "
"5-6-3-1\" y te lo entrega."

msgid "Crumpled Up Note"
msgstr "Nota Arrugada"

msgid ""
"This is a crumpled up note that says '10k¤ 5-6-3-1' on it. How could this be "
"related to the Dvaered spy on Minerva Station?"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una nota arrugada que dice '10k¤ 5-6-3-1' en ella. ¿Cómo podría "
"estar relacionado con el espía Dvaered en la Estación Minerva?"

msgid ""
"\"We're still trying to figure exactly who they are, but that note is our "
"best hint. Maybe it can be of use to you when looking for them. Once we get "
"them we'll kindly escort them to an interrogation ship we have and we can "
"try to get them to spill the beans.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Todavía estamos tratando de averiguar exactamente quiénes son, pero esa "
"nota es nuestra mejor pista. Quizá pueda serte útil a la hora de buscarlos. "
"Una vez que los tengamos, los escoltaremos amablemente a una nave de "
"interrogación que tenemos y podremos intentar que suelten la lengua.\""

msgid ""
"\"How is the search going? We haven't been able to find any new leads on the "
"mole. Our best bet is still the note I gave you that says '10k¤ 5-6-3-1' on "
"it. Maybe it's some sort of code for something?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Cómo va la búsqueda? No hemos podido encontrar ninguna pista nueva sobre "
"el topo. Nuestra mejor apuesta sigue siendo la nota que te di que dice '10k¤ "
"5-6-3-1' en ella. ¿Tal vez sea algún tipo de código para algo?\""

msgid ""
"After the chuck-a-luck dealer's shift you follow him to a back alley in the "
"station."
msgstr ""
"Tras el cambio del repartidor del chuck-a-luck, lo sigues hasta un callejón "
"de la estación."

msgid ""
"\"I don't recognize you, are you the new messenger? Last guy got sliced up."
"\"\n"
"They make a cutting gesture from their belly up to their neck.\n"
"\"Poor kid, not the best way to leave this world.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No te reconozco, ¿eres el nuevo mensajero? El último fue troceado.\"\n"
"Hace un gesto de corte desde el vientre hasta el cuello.\n"
"\"Pobre chico, no es la mejor manera de dejar este mundo.\""

msgid "\"Hey, wait a moment. Haven't I seen you around?\""
msgstr "\"Oye, espera un momento. ¿No te he visto por aquí?\""

msgid ""
"While they furrow their brows, you suddenly hear a soft thud and the sound "
"of strong electric current. You see their eyes glaze over and muscles "
"stiffen. They quickly drop to the ground and a familiar face appears into "
"view."
msgstr ""
"Mientras frunce el ceño, oyes de repente un suave golpe y el sonido de una "
"fuerte corriente eléctrica. Ves que sus ojos se ponen vidriosos y sus "
"músculos se agarrotan. Rápidamente caen al suelo y aparece una cara conocida."

msgid ""
"\"Great job! It seems like you found our mole. However, our job is not done "
"here. We have to get all the information we can out of him. This is not "
"something we can do here at Minerva Station. Here, take him on your ship and "
"bring him to the {sys} system. There should be a ship waiting for him in the "
"middle of the asteroid field, it might be a bit hard to spot at first.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Gran trabajo! Parece que has encontrado a nuestro topo. Sin embargo, "
"nuestro trabajo no ha terminado aquí. Tenemos que sacarle toda la "
"información que podamos. Esto no es algo que podamos hacer aquí en la "
"Estación Minerva. Toma, llévatelo en tu nave y llévalo al sistema {sys}. "
"Debería haber una nave esperándote en medio del campo de asteroides, puede "
"ser un poco difícil de ver al principio.\""

msgid ""
"\"I'll be waiting on the ship with my crew. Make sure to bring him over, "
"however, watch out for any Dvaered patrols. We don't want them to know we "
"have taken him. We're not expecting much trouble, but bring a strong ship "
"just in case.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Estaré esperando en la nave con mi tripulación. Asegúrate de traerlo, sin "
"embargo, ten cuidado con las patrullas Dvaered. No queremos que sepan que "
"nos lo hemos llevado. No esperamos muchos problemas, pero trae una nave "
"fuerte por si acaso.\""

#. Add illegal cargo
msgid "Dvaered Mole"
msgstr "Topo Dvaered"

msgid ""
"An unconscious and restrained Dvaered mole. You better not let Dvaered ships "
"find out you are carrying this individual."
msgstr ""
"Un topo Dvaered inconsciente y retenido. Será mejor que no dejes que las "
"naves Dvaered se enteren de que llevas a este individuo."

msgid "Take the mole to the interrogation facility at {sys}"
msgstr "Lleva al topo a la instalación de interrogación en {sys}"

msgid "You were supposed to protect the interrogation ship!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que debías proteger la nave de interrogatorios!"

#. Clear system
#. TODO maybe don't clear everything, leave some dvaered and stuff around as an obstacle
#. take the last (should only be one)
#. Main ship player has to protect
msgid "Interrogation Ship"
msgstr "Nave de Interrogación"

#. only fight back
#. Stay around origin
#. Some hooks
#. Increase state
#. We exploit the 'guard' AI to get the Dvaered to go on top of the
#. interrogation ship and destroy it
#. Go to mainship
#. don't actually want to guard
#. Set leader stuff
#. "Dvaered Vendetta",
#. "Dvaered Ancestor",
#. Still left
#. Add a delay for the followup
#. Mission should be done
msgid "Strangely Familiar Voice"
msgstr "Voz Extrañamente Familiar"

msgid ""
"You board the ship and are once again greeting by the sketchy figure you are "
"getting used to."
msgstr ""
"Abordas la nave y vuelves a ser recibido por la figura sospechosa a la que "
"te estás acostumbrando."

msgid ""
"\"I was worried. Glad you made it here in one piece!\"\n"
"Some crew members escort the Dvaered mole towards the inner part of the "
"ship. They have fairly rough and burly complexions."
msgstr ""
"\"Estaba preocupado. ¡Me alegro de que hayas llegado de una pieza!\"\n"
"Algunos miembros de la tripulación escoltan al topo Dvaered hacia el "
"interior de la nave. Tienen una complexión bastante ruda y corpulenta."

msgid ""
"\"Don't worry about the mole, we'll take care of them from now on.\"\n"
"She beams you a smile.\n"
"\"If all goes well, we'll get the information we were looking for in the "
"next few periods and we can all go celebrate with drinks back at the bar.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You faintly hear an angry voice that sounds strangely familiar.\n"
"\"What the hell are you guys doing loafing around? We have work to do! I "
"don't pay you to sit on your bums all day!\""
msgstr ""
"Oyes débilmente una voz enfadada que te resulta extrañamente familiar.\n"
"\"¿Qué demonios hacéis holgazaneando? ¡Tenemos trabajo que hacer! ¡No os "
"pago para que estéis todo el día sentados sobre vuestros culos!\""

#. codespell:ignore loafing
msgid ""
"They visibly wince when they hear the angry voice.\n"
"\"Let us talk about your payment.\""
msgstr ""
"Se estremece visiblemente al escuchar la voz enfadada.\n"
"\"Hablemos de tu pago.\""

#. blaring alarm
msgid "Suddenly an alarm starts blaring throughout the ship."
msgstr "De repente, una alarma empieza a sonar en toda la nave."

#. Using boars as slang for Dvaered
msgid ""
"The familiar and angry voice bellows in the distance.\n"
"\"Zuri! We've got incoming boars closing in on our position! Take care of it!"
"\""
msgstr ""
"La voz familiar y furiosa brama en la distancia.\n"
"\"¡Zuri! ¡Tenemos jabalíes acercándose a nuestra posición! Encárgate de ello!"
"\""

msgid ""
"\"Shit, it looks like we have Dvaered company. Make sure they don't find our "
"ship! I dunno, just shoot them or something! I'll be manning the turrets "
"here.\"\n"
"She rushes off into the depths of the ship."
msgstr ""
"\"Mierda, parece que tenemos compañía Dvaered. ¡Asegúrate de que no "
"encuentren nuestra nave! No sé, ¡dispárales o algo! Estaré manejando las "
"torretas aquí.\"\n"
"Ella se apresura a las profundidades de la nave."

msgid "You race to get back to your ship before the Dvaereds jump in."
msgstr "Corres para volver a tu nave antes de que los Dvaereds salten."

msgid "Defend the {ship}!"
msgstr ""

#. Dvaered jump in hooks
msgid "Sensors detecting Dvaered patrol incoming from {sys}!"
msgstr "¡Sensores detectando patrulla Dvaered entrando desde {sys}!"

#. Unboard
msgid "We are under attack!"
msgstr "¡Estamos bajo ataque!"

msgid "We have been discovered!"
msgstr "¡Hemos sido descubiertos!"

msgid "The interrogation ship was destroyed!"
msgstr "¡La nave de interrogación fue destruida!"

#. Get ready!
msgid "Reinforcements are coming!"
msgstr "¡Vienen refuerzos!"

#. Reinforcement spawners
#. Try to guard the Rhino
#. Reinforcements!
#. Message stuff
msgid "Support incoming! Hurrah!"
msgstr "¡Apoyos en camino! ¡Hurra!"

msgid "Clean up the Dvaered patrols"
msgstr "Limpia las patrullas Dvaered"

#. Detect all Dvaered deaths
msgid "Try to buy us time! We have reinforcements coming!"
msgstr "¡Intenta ganar tiempo! ¡Vienen refuerzos!"

msgid "They keep on coming! Keep them distracted!"
msgstr "¡Siguen llegando! ¡Mantenlos distraídos!"

msgid "Just a bit more and reinforcements should arrive!"
msgstr "¡Sólo un poco más y deberían llegar los refuerzos!"

msgid "Shit, is that a Dvaered Goddard?"
msgstr "Mierda, ¿es un Goddard Dvaered?"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As everything settles down you receive an incoming transmission from the "
"interrogation ship, and the individual apparently known as 'Zuri' appears on-"
"screen."
msgstr ""
"Cuando todo se calma, recibes una transmisión entrante desde la nave de "
"interrogación, y el individuo aparentemente conocido como \"Zuri\" aparece "
"en pantalla."

msgid ""
"\"Damn that was close. I never thought the Dvaered would be tricky enough to "
"trail us over here. Pretty sure the damn mole had some sort of tracking "
"device we must have missed.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Maldición, eso estuvo cerca. Nunca pensé que los Dvaered serían lo "
"suficientemente astutos como para seguirnos hasta aquí. Estoy seguro de que "
"el maldito topo tenía algún tipo de dispositivo de rastreo que no "
"encontramos.\""

msgid ""
"\"I'm sure you have a lot of questions, however, now is not the time for "
"answers. We can't linger here long, the Dvaered are bound to be back, and "
"this time in larger numbers.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Estoy seguro de que tienes muchas preguntas, sin embargo, ahora no es el "
"momento de dar respuestas. No podemos quedarnos aquí mucho tiempo, los "
"Dvaered van a volver, y esta vez en mayor número.\""

msgid ""
"The still familiar voice butts in.\n"
"\"Zuri! Get your ass back to navigation! Wait until I tell you how that "
"Dvaered squealed like a pig!\""
msgstr ""
"La voz, todavía familiar, irrumpe.\n"
"\"¡Zuri! ¡Vuelve a la navegación! ¡Espera hasta que te cuente cómo ese "
"Dvaered chilló como un cerdo!\""

msgid ""
"Zuri makes a somewhat complicated face at the unwanted interruption.\n"
"\"I have some business to attend to.\"\n"
"She gives you a tired grin.\n"
"\"Anyway, I'll wire you a reward. Meet me back at Minerva Station.\""
msgstr ""
"Zuri pone una cara algo complicada ante la indeseada interrupción.\n"
"\"Tengo algunos asuntos que atender.\"\n"
"Te dedica una sonrisa cansada.\n"
"\"De todos modos, te enviaré una recompensa. Reúnete conmigo en la Estación "
"Minerva.\""

#. Rewards
msgid "You helped defend an interrogation ship from Dvaered vessels."
msgstr "Has ayudado a defender una nave de interrogación de las naves Dvaered."

#. Pirates go away
#. Guard AI is bad for stuff other than guarding
#. We done here
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 5">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <done>Minerva Pirates 4</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Destroy Za'lek hacking station
#.
#. TODO probably should be changed from Gammacron to Fried system
#.
#. This mission has two ways of being done:
#. 1. Using brute force and killing everything.
#. 2. Using stealth if the player boards the drone controllers or hacking centre, they can disable drones.
#.
#. There are drones patrolling the hacking centre, it requires disabling two drone controllers to get there.
#. There are also drones wandering around that are independent / depend on the hacking centre.
#. --
#. Forward-declared functions
#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 1. fly to mainsys
#. 2. mission time!
#. 3. hacking centre disabled
#. Non-persistent state
msgid ""
"Zuri wants you to disable a Za'lek hacking centre located near Minerva "
"Station."
msgstr ""
"Zuri quiere que desactives un centro de hackeo Za'lek situado cerca de la "
"Estación Minerva."

#. If not accepted, mem.misn_state will still be nil
msgid "Za'lek Hacking Centre"
msgstr "Centro de Hackeo Za'lek"

msgid "Destroy the hacking centre"
msgstr "Destruye el centro de hackeo"

msgid "Return to Minerva Station"
msgstr "Regresa a la Estación Minerva"

msgid ""
"You accepted a job from Zuri to take out a Za'lek hacking centre at the "
"{sys} system"
msgstr ""
"Aceptaste un trabajo de Zuri para eliminar un centro de hackeo Za'lek en el "
"sistema {sys}"

msgid "High-Density Explosives"
msgstr "Explosivos de Alta Densidad"

msgid ""
"Explosives that can be used to detonate all sorts of critical infrastructure."
msgstr ""
"Explosivos que pueden utilizarse para detonar todo tipo de infraestructuras "
"críticas."

msgid ""
"You approach Zuri to report your success. She listens to you intently as you "
"explain how things went down when you took out the hacking centre."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas a Zuri para informarle de tu éxito. Te escucha atentamente "
"mientras le explicas cómo fueron las cosas cuando eliminaste el centro de "
"hackeo."

msgid ""
"\"Great work out there. This will definitely set the Za'lek scheme back a "
"few decaperiods. Must have been satisfying see the show of fireworks as the "
"hacking station went down. I just wish I was able to see it, but I haven't "
"been able to properly pilot a ship in ages. Boss just never cuts me any "
"slack.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Gran trabajo ahí fuera. Esto definitivamente hará retroceder el esquema "
"Za'lek unos cuantos decaperiodos. Debe haber sido satisfactorio ver el "
"espectáculo de fuegos artificiales cuando la estación de hackeo cayó. Me "
"gustaría poder verlo, pero no he sido capaz de pilotar correctamente una "
"nave en años. El jefe nunca me da tregua.\""

msgid ""
"\"I've wired you your reward as always.\"\n"
"She grins at you.\n"
"\"That said, our work is still far from done. We won't stop until Minerva "
"Station is free from Za'lek and Dvaered inference. Meet me up in the bar in "
"a bit if you want to help.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Te he enviado tu recompensa como siempre.\"\n"
"Te sonríe.\n"
"\"Dicho esto, nuestro trabajo aún está lejos de terminar. No nos detendremos "
"hasta que la Estación Minerva esté libre de inferencia Za'lek y Dvaered. "
"Encuéntrame en el bar dentro de un rato si quieres ayudar.\""

#. Rewards
msgid ""
"You took down an advanced Za'lek hacking centre and got rewarded for your "
"efforts."
msgstr ""
"Has derribado un centro de hackeo Za'lek avanzado y has sido recompensado "
"por tus esfuerzos."

#. Not accepted
msgid ""
"You approach Zuri who seems to be motioning to you. She seems faintly tired."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas a Zuri, que parece hacerte un gesto. Parece ligeramente cansada."

msgid ""
"\"I suppose you have a lot of questions, but first things first. Remember "
"the suspicious Za'lek drones? Well, we were able to look into that some "
"more, and it seems like they were part of the scouts of an advanced hacking "
"attack on Minerva Station.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Supongo que tienes muchas preguntas, pero lo primero es lo primero. "
"¿Recuerdas los sospechosos drones Za'lek? Bueno, hemos podido investigar un "
"poco más, y parece que formaban parte de los exploradores de un ataque de "
"hackeo avanzado en la Estación Minerva.\""

msgid ""
"\"Those Za'lek are always pretending to talk about science and research, and "
"the moment you turn your back on them, they start prodding and stealing "
"everything they can find.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Esos Za'lek siempre pretenden hablar de ciencia e investigación, y en el "
"momento en que les das la espalda, empiezan a pinchar y robar todo lo que "
"encuentran.\""

msgid ""
"\"Long story short, we need you to take out their hacking centre nearby. "
"This time we won't be able to use much brute force, you'll have to use more "
"finesse. Will you help us again?\"\n"
"She smiles at you."
msgstr ""
"\"Resumiendo, necesitamos que destruyas su centro de hackeo cercano. Esta "
"vez no podremos usar mucha fuerza bruta, tendrás que usar más delicadeza. "
"¿Nos ayudarás de nuevo?\"\n"
"Te sonríe."

msgid ""
"\"Great! We can always count on you.\n"
"So, as I was saying, it seems like the Za'lek have set up some pretty "
"serious surveillance and hacking infrastructure in the nearby {sys} system. "
"We sent a scout to look at it quickly and it looks like they have set up "
"several drone controllers besides the hacking centre. The main objective is "
"taking out the hacking centre, but it looks like it won't be possible "
"without taking out the drone controllers too.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Genial! Siempre podemos contar contigo.\n"
"Así que, como iba diciendo, parece que los Za'lek han montado una "
"infraestructura de vigilancia y hackeo bastante seria en el sistema {sys} "
"cercano. Enviamos un explorador a echar un vistazo rápidamente y parece que "
"han instalado varios controladores de drones además del centro de hackeo. El "
"objetivo principal es acabar con el centro de hackeo, pero parece que no "
"será posible sin acabar también con los controladores de los drones.\""

msgid ""
"\"The main issue is that the system is infested with Za'lek drones. Heavies, "
"bombers, lights, you name it. While usually not a real challenge to a great "
"pilot like you, their sheer numbers make it so that a frontal attack will "
"only end up getting you killed. However, controlling so many drones requires "
"infrastructure, and the Za'lek, being the lazy bums they are, are not "
"commanding them from ships, but using the drone controllers. If you could "
"take them out, that should incapacitate most of the drones and make taking "
"out the hacking centre a piece of cake.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El problema principal es que el sistema está infestado de drones Za'lek. "
"Pesados, bombarderos, luces, lo que sea. Aunque normalmente no son un "
"verdadero desafío para un gran piloto como tú, su gran número hace que un "
"ataque frontal sólo acabe matándote. Sin embargo, controlar tantos drones "
"requiere infraestructura, y los Za'lek, siendo los vagos que son, no los "
"comandan desde las naves, sino que utilizan los controladores de los drones. "
"Si pudieras eliminarlos, eso debería incapacitar a la mayoría de los drones "
"y hacer que eliminar el centro de hackeo sea pan comido.\""

msgid ""
"\"My recommendation to you is to jump into {sys} and stay low. We've got "
"some really good explosives we'll hook you up with that should let you take "
"out the drone controllers or hacking stations if you can get close enough. "
"So try to sneak past all the drones, plant the bombs on the drone "
"controllers, and once they are out, do the same with the hacking centre. Of "
"course, if you prefer to be old fashioned, you can take the hacking centre "
"down with missiles, railguns, or whatever you have on hand. Probably easier "
"said than done, but I know you can do it.\"\n"
"She grins at you."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"That said, given the amount of drones, you should probably take a stealthy "
"ship that is also able to take some out if you get found. They are really "
"fast, so it's unlikely you will be able to outrun them while planting the "
"explosives.\"\n"
"\"Oh and about the explosives, they've already been loaded onto your ship so "
"you don't have to worry about them.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Dicho esto, dada la cantidad de drones, probablemente deberías llevar una "
"nave sigilosa que también sea capaz de eliminar a algunos si te encuentran. "
"Son muy rápidos, así que es poco probable que puedas dejarlos atrás mientras "
"colocas los explosivos.\"\n"
"\"Ah, y sobre los explosivos, ya han sido cargados en tu nave, así que no "
"tienes que preocuparte por ellos.\""

#. Accepted.
msgid "You approach Zuri."
msgstr "Te acercas a Zuri."

msgid "\"Are you pirates?\""
msgstr "\"¿Sois piratas?\""

msgid ""
"\"The job is a bit trickier than what we've done up until now, but you "
"should be able to handle it. The main objective is to take out the Za'lek "
"hacking centre in the {sys} system; everything else can be ignored. That "
"said, the system is infested with drones that are being controlled by "
"several drone controllers. You should probably take them out first if you "
"want to have a shot at the hacking centre.\""
msgstr ""
"\"El trabajo es un poco más complicado que lo que hemos hecho hasta ahora, "
"pero deberías ser capaz de manejarlo. El objetivo principal es acabar con el "
"centro de pirateo de Za'lek en el sistema {sys}; todo lo demás puede ser "
"ignorado. Dicho esto, el sistema está infestado de drones que están siendo "
"controlados por varios controladores de drones. Probablemente deberías "
"eliminarlos primero si quieres tener una oportunidad con el centro de "
"pirateo.\""

msgid ""
"\"We've loaded explosives onto your ship, so if you are able to avoid the "
"drones and board the drone controllers or even the hacking centre, you "
"should be able to detonate them easily. However, they should also be able to "
"be taken down by conventional weapons. Whatever is easier for you.\"\n"
"She beams you a smile.\n"
"\"Make sure you take a stealthy ship that can take down a couple of drones "
"if things go wrong, and you get caught.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hemos cargado explosivos en tu nave, así que si eres capaz de evitar los "
"drones y abordar los controladores de los drones o incluso el centro de "
"hackeo, deberías ser capaz de detonarlos fácilmente. Sin embargo, también "
"deberían poder ser derribados con armas convencionales. Lo que te resulte "
"más fácil\".\n"
"Te dedica una sonrisa.\n"
"\"Asegúrate de llevar una nave sigilosa que pueda derribar un par de drones "
"si las cosas van mal y te atrapan.\""

msgid ""
"\"Pirates?\"\n"
"She chuckles.\n"
"\"Let me ask you one thing, do you think the decrepit Empire is good? "
"Overtaxing and overworking the citizens to feed the ostentatious bureaucracy "
"and aristocracy, all the while starving and exploiting the workers all over. "
"Is this what we want?\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Piratas?\"\n"
"Se ríe.\n"
"\"Déjame preguntarte una cosa, ¿crees que el decrépito Imperio es bueno? "
"Sobrecargar de impuestos y de trabajo a los ciudadanos para alimentar a la "
"ostentosa burocracia y a la aristocracia, mientras se mata de hambre y se "
"explota a los trabajadores por doquier. ¿Es esto lo que queremos?\""

msgid "\"Yes, it brings stability.\""
msgstr "\"Sí, trae estabilidad.\""

msgid "\"No, it hampers human development.\""
msgstr "\"No, dificulta el desarrollo humano.\""

msgid "\"How is this related to my question?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué relación tiene esto con mi pregunta?\""

msgid ""
"\"We represent those who want to stand up to this tyranny and oppression, "
"and believe that a better universe is possible. Sure, there are those who "
"dismissively label us as pirates or scoundrels, but that is because they "
"represent the status quo. They do not want anyone to challenge their reign "
"and want to continue their life of luxury.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Representamos a quienes quieren enfrentarse a esta tiranía y opresión, y "
"creemos que es posible un universo mejor. Seguro que hay quienes nos tachan "
"con desprecio de piratas o sinvergüenzas, pero eso es porque representan el "
"statu quo. No quieren que nadie desafíe su reinado y quieren seguir con su "
"vida de lujo.\""

msgid ""
"\"Of course, it is not that easy, as many people are complicit even against "
"their own interests. They believe they can become part of the elite if they "
"work hard enough, you know, the Imperial dream. However, that never happens, "
"and they die a sad, depressed life filled with delusions of grandeur. This "
"is not the universe we wish for humankind.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Por supuesto, no es tan fácil, ya que muchas personas son cómplices "
"incluso en contra de sus propios intereses. Creen que pueden formar parte de "
"la élite si se esfuerzan lo suficiente, ya sabes, el sueño Imperial. Sin "
"embargo, eso nunca sucede, y mueren en una vida triste y deprimida, llena de "
"delirios de grandeza. Este no es el universo que deseamos para la humanidad."
"\""

msgid ""
"\"It is not easy to go toe-to-toe with such a large establishment, which is "
"why we have to work from the shadows and focus on small objectives, like "
"Minerva Station. The Station has such potential, yet it is wasted on Za'lek "
"and Dvaered squabbles. We wish to free the people of Minerva Station to live "
"their full potential, even though we have to ruffle some feathers here and "
"there.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No es fácil enfrentarse a un estamento tan grande, por eso tenemos que "
"trabajar desde la sombra y centrarnos en objetivos pequeños, como la "
"Estación Minerva. La Estación tiene un gran potencial, pero se desperdicia "
"en las disputas entre Za'lek y Dvaered. Queremos liberar a los habitantes de "
"la Estación Minerva para que vivan todo su potencial, aunque tengamos que "
"erizar algunas plumas aquí y allá.\""

msgid ""
"\"So yes, maybe we are pirates. Pirates who dream of a better universe for "
"you and me.\"\n"
"Her eyes blaze with hard determination."
msgstr ""
"\"Así que sí, tal vez seamos piratas. Piratas que sueñan con un universo "
"mejor para ti y para mí.\"\n"
"Sus ojos brillan con una dura determinación."

#. Controller spawning functions
msgid "Drone Controller"
msgstr "Controlador Dron"

#. Controllers can't detect anything
#. Much more bulky than normal
#. Can board them to blow them up
#. Groups of controlled drones
#. Fuzzes a position a bit
#. We are nice and make the drones easier to see for this mission
#. Spawn the main controllers
msgid "Hacking Centre"
msgstr "Centro de Hackeo"

#. Main boss, isn't necessary to kill
#. Be nice and give only close-range weapons
#. ["Launcher"]      = { max=0 },
#. Should be enough to go far out for torpedo type weapons
#. Now add the different patrol groups
#. local tiny_group = {
#. "Za'lek Light Drone",
#. "Za'lek Light Drone",
#. }
#. add_guard_group( pos_drone_control1, tiny_group, drone_group1 )
#. add_guard_group( pos_drone_control2, tiny_group, drone_group2 )
#. Tell the player to f off
msgid ""
"Due to military exercises, {sys} is under lockdown. Please evacuate the area "
"immediately."
msgstr ""
"Debido a los ejercicios militares, {sys} está bajo bloqueo. Por favor, "
"evacue la zona inmediatamente."

msgid "Unwelcome ships will be terminated. You have been warned."
msgstr "Las naves no deseadas serán eliminadas. Están advertidos."

#. Drone controllers disable their respective drones
msgid "You plant explosives on the ship."
msgstr "Colocas explosivos en la nave."

#. Move the boss a bit away
msgid "The hacking centre has been destroyed!"
msgstr "¡El centro de hackeo ha sido destruido!"

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Minerva Pirates 6">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Minerva Station</spob>
#. <done>Minerva Pirates 5</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Minerva</campaign>
#. <done_misn name="Kex's Freedom 5" />
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Assassinate a Dvaered Warlord and Za'lek General.
#. --
msgid "Limbo Mayhem"
msgstr "Caos Limbo"

msgid "Eisen"
msgstr "Eisen"

msgid "Lord Battlebloke"
msgstr "Señor BloqueDeBatalla"

#. Mission states:
#. nil: mission not accepted yet
#. 1. fly to position
#. 2. mayhem starts
#. 3. both targets down
msgid ""
"Zuri wants you to help a Za'lek General and Dvaered Warlord finish each "
"other off."
msgstr ""
"Zuri quiere que ayudes a un General Za'lek y a un Señor de la Guerra Dvaered "
"a acabar el uno con el otro."

#. If not accepted, mem.state will still be nil
msgid "Get to the position"
msgstr "Llegar a la posición"

msgid "Wait for the targets"
msgstr "Espera a los objetivos"

msgid "Eliminate the targets"
msgstr "Elimina los objetivos"

msgid ""
"You accepted a job from Zuri to assassinate both a Za'lek General and "
"Dvaered Warlord at the same time in the {sys} system."
msgstr ""
"Has aceptado un encargo de Zuri para asesinar a un general Za'lek y a un "
"Señor de la Guerra Dvaered al mismo tiempo en el sistema {sys}."

#. Must be goal system
msgid "You were supposed to take out the targets!"
msgstr "¡Se suponía que tenías que eliminar a los objetivos!"

#. Mission completed
msgid ""
"You quickly land after the chaos, take a deep breath and get off your ship "
"to find Zuri waiting for you."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas rápidamente tras el caos, respiras hondo y bajas de tu nave para "
"encontrarte a Zuri esperándote."

msgid "You give her a brief overview of the situation, with both targets down."
msgstr ""
"Le haces un breve resumen de la situación, con los dos objetivos abatidos."

msgid ""
"\"Seems like you got the job done. I expected nothing less from such an ace "
"pilot! If only me colleagues were half as reliable.\"\n"
"She lets out a short sigh."
msgstr ""
"\"Parece que has hecho el trabajo. No esperaba menos de un piloto tan bueno. "
"Ojalá mis colegas fueran la mitad de fiables.\"\n"
"Suelta un pequeño suspiro."

msgid ""
"\"House Dvaered and House Za'lek must be seething now. I wouldn't be "
"surprised if they bust out the main forces now and give us nicer fireworks "
"to illuminate the sky. It's going to be messy, but where there's mayhem, "
"there is opportunity!\""
msgstr ""
"\"La Casa Dvaered y la Casa Za'lek deben estar furiosas ahora. No me "
"extrañaría que sacaran las fuerzas principales ahora y nos regalaran fuegos "
"artificiales más bonitos para iluminar el cielo. Va a ser un desastre, pero "
"donde hay caos, ¡hay oportunidad!\""

msgid "\"For our next step, we should... Wait, what is that?\""
msgstr "\"Para nuestro siguiente paso, deberíamos... Espera, ¿qué es eso?\""

msgid "Empire Combat Bureaucrat"
msgstr "Burócrata de Combate del Imperio"

#. TODO add sound?
msgid ""
"Suddenly a siren indicating a station-wide announcement echoes throughout "
"the station, and an Empire Combat Bureaucrat materializes in the middle of "
"the spaceport bar."
msgstr ""
"De repente, una sirena que indica un anuncio en toda la estación resuena a "
"través de la estación, y un Burócrata de Combate del Imperio se materializa "
"en medio del bar del puerto espacial."

msgid ""
"\"Ahem.\"\n"
"They clear their throat.\n"
"\"Attention Citizens of {spb}!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ejem.\"\n"
"Se aclaran la garganta.\n"
"\"¡Atención Ciudadanos de {spb}!\""

msgid ""
"\"It has been brought to the attention of the Empire, that the {sys} system "
"has fallen into lawlessness. There have been reports of heavy pirate "
"activity, scuffles between Great Houses, kidnappings, assassinations, and "
"the likes.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ha llegado a oídos del Imperio que el sistema {sys} ha caído en la "
"anarquía. Ha habido informes de una fuerte actividad pirata, refriegas entre "
"Grandes Casas, secuestros, asesinatos y cosas por el estilo.\""

msgid ""
"They hit their fist on a table in front of them.\n"
"\"The Empire will not stand for such displays of brazen debauchery, and thus "
"invokes EL2897 regarding the sovereignty of the {sys} system.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"All interested parties should proceed to the Jade Court in the {sys} "
"system. Deliberations will begin once quorum is reached.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Todas las partes interesadas deben dirigirse a la Corte de Jade en el "
"sistema {sys}. Las deliberaciones comenzarán una vez que se alcance el "
"quórum.\""

msgid "\"The Empire is watching you.\""
msgstr "\"El Imperio te está vigilando.\""

msgid ""
"Without any fanfare, the Empire Combat Bureaucrat dematerializes and the bar "
"breaks into chaos. Hey, is that the Minerva CEO running around?"
msgstr ""
"Sin ninguna fanfarria, el Burócrata de Combate del Imperio se desmaterializa "
"y el bar se sume en el caos. Eh, ¿es el Director General de Minerva el que "
"anda por ahí?"

msgid ""
"You turn back to Zuri who is seems to be thinking profously.\n"
"\"That was faster than expected. Never seen the Empire react so fast... but "
"if we play our cards right... we could win big!\""
msgstr ""
"Te vuelves hacia Zuri, que parece estar pensando profusamente.\n"
"\"Eso fue más rápido de lo esperado. Nunca he visto al Imperio reaccionar "
"tan rápido... pero si jugamos bien nuestras cartas... ¡podríamos ganar a lo "
"grande!\""

msgid ""
"\"Here, take this reward.\"\n"
"She shoves a credit chip into your hand.\n"
"\"I'm going to have to make some calls and move some strings. Meet me up at "
"the bar in a bit!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Toma, coge esta recompensa.\"\n"
"Te pone una ficha de crédito en la mano.\n"
"\"Voy a tener que hacer algunas llamadas y mover algunos hilos. ¡Nos vemos "
"en el bar en un rato!\""

#. Rewards
msgid ""
"You took out a Za'lek General and Dvaered Warlord in the {sys} system. Upon "
"informing Zuri of your accomplishment, an announcement that deliberations "
"regarding the sovereignty of {spb} will be held at {trialspb} in the "
"{trialsys} system. Zuri told you to meet up with her afterwards at bar at "
"{spb}."
msgstr ""
"Has eliminado a un General Za'lek y a un Señor de la Guerra Dvaered en el "
"sistema {sys}. Tras informar a Zuri de tu logro, se anuncia que las "
"deliberaciones sobre la soberanía de {spb} se celebrarán en {trialspb}, en "
"el sistema {trialsys}. Zuri te ha dicho que te reúnas con ella después en el "
"bar de {spb}."

msgid ""
"She joins the chaos of people running around the station and fades into the "
"shadows."
msgstr ""
"Se une al caos de gente que corre por la estación y se desvanece en las "
"sombras."

msgid "You approach Zuri who seems a bit preoccupied."
msgstr "Te acercas a Zuri, que parece un poco preocupada."

msgid ""
"\"Hey, {playername}. I'm still preparing our next steps. Maybe you can clean "
"up other jobs you have left at the station?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hola, {playername}. Todavía estoy preparando nuestros próximos pasos. "
"¿Quizás puedas terminar otros trabajos que has dejado en la estación?\""

#. Not accepted
msgid "You approach a strangely giddy Zuri calling you to her table."
msgstr "Te acercas a una Zuri extrañamente mareada que te llama a su mesa."

msgid ""
"\"It looks like we finally have a nice window of opportunity! My sources "
"indicate that a Za'lek General and Dvaered Warlord are going to be passing "
"through the system at roughly the same time. You know what this means.\"\n"
"She winks at you."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Parece que por fin tenemos una buena oportunidad! Mis fuentes indican que "
"un General Za'lek y un Señor de la Guerra Dvaered van a pasar por el sistema "
"más o menos al mismo tiempo. Ya sabes lo que eso significa.\"\n"
"Te guiña un ojo."

msgid "\"Get them to fight each other?\""
msgstr "\"¿Hacer que se peleen entre ellos?\""

msgid "\"Invite them for tea and settle this peacefully?\""
msgstr "\"¿Invitarlos a tomar el té y resolver esto pacíficamente?\""

msgid "\"No idea.\""
msgstr "\"Ni idea.\""

msgid "\"Exactly! Two birds with... zero stones I guess? It's perfect!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Exactamente! ¿Dos pájaros con... cero piedras supongo? ¡Es perfecto!\""

msgid ""
"\"Exactly! Wait, no!\"\n"
"She shakes her head.\n"
"\"We get them to fight each other! I thought we were on the same wavelength!"
"\""
msgstr ""
"\" ¡Exactamente! Espera, ¡no!\"\n"
"Ella sacude la cabeza.\n"
"\"¡Hacemos que se peleen entre ellos! ¡Pensaba que estábamos en la misma "
"onda!\""

msgid ""
"\"We get them to fight each other! I thought we were on the same wavelength!"
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Hacemos que se peleen entre ellos! ¡Creía que estábamos en la misma onda!"
"\""

msgid ""
"\"Tensions at Minerva Station are at an all high, if not only a Za'lek "
"General goes down, but a Dvaered Warlord does too, it's going to really "
"ruffle a lot of feathers! Pretty sure the Empire will have to get involved, "
"and if we play our cards right, the Great Houses get kicked out "
"unceremoniously!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Las tensiones en la Estación Minerva están en su punto más alto, si no "
"sólo cae un General Za'lek, sino también un Señor de la Guerra Dvaered, ¡se "
"van a alborotar muchas plumas! ¡Seguro que el Imperio tendrá que "
"involucrarse, y si jugamos bien nuestras cartas, las Grandes Casas serán "
"expulsadas sin contemplaciones!\""

msgid ""
"\"You game for pulling the plug on the Dvaered and Za'lek oppressors? Should "
"be a cinch!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Te apuntas a desenchufar a los opresores Dvaered y Za'lek? ¡Debería ser "
"pan comido!\""

msgid ""
"\"Great! Let me get you up to date with the plan. The Za'lek General {zlk} "
"is set to do a rendezvous of the system soon as part of an inspection of the "
"Za'lek border systems. Coincidently, the Dvaered Warlord {dv} is also going "
"to be in the system after some training in a nearby system. We've pulled a "
"few strings to make sure their timing in the {sys} system matches. Setting "
"us up for a perfect operation.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Genial! Déjame ponerte al día con el plan. El General Za'lek {zlk} va a "
"hacer una visita al sistema en breve como parte de una inspección de los "
"sistemas fronterizos Za'lek. Coincidentemente, el Señor de la Guerra Dvaered "
"{dv} también va a estar en el sistema después de un entrenamiento en un "
"sistema cercano. Hemos movido algunos hilos para asegurarnos de que su "
"tiempo en el sistema {sys} coincide. Preparándonos para una operación "
"perfecta.\""

msgid ""
"\"For this mission, I've enlisted the aid of a few helping hands. They "
"should make sure that the mayhem gets started by launching a Za'lek drone to "
"attack the Warlord, while simultaneously using mace rockets to draw the "
"attention of the General. If all goes well we'll have a great nice firework "
"display visible from Minerva Station!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Para esta misión, he reclutado la ayuda de algunos ayudantes. Deben "
"asegurarse de que el caos comience lanzando un dron Za'lek para atacar al "
"Señor de la Guerra, mientras simultáneamente usas cohetes maza para llamar "
"la atención del General. ¡Si todo va bien, tendremos un gran espectáculo de "
"fuegos artificiales visible desde la estación Minerva!\""

msgid ""
"\"However, the thing is, we have to make sure both the General and the "
"Warlord go down, and that is where you come in! You have to make sure both "
"the General and Warlord ships are destroyed. Do not let them get away, in "
"particular, I would guess the Za'lek General will try to make a break for "
"it, so make sure to break them before they can jump out of the system.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Sin embargo, la cosa es que tenemos que asegurarnos de que tanto el "
"General como el Señor de la Guerra caen, ¡y ahí es donde entras tú! Tienes "
"que asegurarte de que tanto la nave del General como la del Señor de la "
"Guerra son destruidas. No dejéis que se escapen, en particular, supongo que "
"el General Za'lek intentará huir, así que aseguraos de romperlas antes de "
"que puedan saltar fuera del sistema.\""

msgid ""
"\"With both the targets down, this will force the Houses to react, and the "
"Empire will be forced to intervene. The ineptitude of both House Za'lek and "
"House Dvaered, should make it unlikely that they will get a good resolution "
"in their favour, and if we play our cards right, we can kick them out of the "
"system.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Con ambos objetivos derribados, esto obligará a las Casas a reaccionar, y "
"el Imperio se verá forzado a intervenir. La ineptitud tanto de la Casa "
"Za'lek como de la Casa Dvaered, debería hacer improbable que consigan una "
"buena resolución a su favor, y si jugamos bien nuestras cartas, podremos "
"echarlos del sistema.\""

msgid ""
"\"Remember, our helper will wait for you at the rendezvous location. Once "
"you get in position, make sure to take out the targets! If all goes well, "
"you should be able to make use of the chaos to achieve our goals! Return "
"here so we can discuss what to do next.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Recuerda, nuestro ayudante te esperará en el punto de encuentro. Una vez "
"en posición, ¡asegúrate de eliminar a los objetivos! Si todo va bien, "
"¡podrás aprovechar el caos para lograr nuestros objetivos! Vuelve aquí para "
"que podamos discutir qué hacer a continuación.\""

msgid ""
"\"You have to take out the Za'lek General and Dvaered Warlord that will be "
"visiting the {sys} system. We've made sure that they should be in the system "
"at roughly the same time. A helping hand will be there to start the mayhem, "
"making them fight each other and you have to take advantage of the chaos to "
"take out the priority targets.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tienes que eliminar al General Za'lek y al Señor de la Guerra Dvaered que "
"visitarán el sistema {sys}. Nos hemos asegurado de que estén en el sistema "
"más o menos al mismo tiempo. Una mano amiga estará allí para iniciar el "
"caos, haciendo que luchen entre ellos y tú tienes que aprovechar el caos "
"para acabar con los objetivos prioritarios.\""

msgid "Zuri's Helper"
msgstr "El Ayudante de Zuri"

msgid "\"Let's get this operation over with.\""
msgstr "\"Acabemos con esta operación.\""

msgid "Hello there. Come here and we can start the operation."
msgstr "Hola. Ven aquí y podemos empezar la operación."

#. Player meets up near Limbo IIA
#. Get rid of all pilots
#. Have the helper talk to the player
msgid "The targets have entered the system!"
msgstr "¡Los objetivos han entrado en el sistema!"

#. General goes from Provectus Nova to Sollav
msgid "General {zl}"
msgstr "General {zl}"

#. Warlord goes from Sollav to Provectus Nova
msgid "Warlord {dv}"
msgstr "Señor de la Guerra {dv}"

#. NPC will chatter with the player
msgid "Wait here, I'll start the strike when they get close."
msgstr "Espera aquí, empezaré el golpe cuando se acerquen."

msgid "Haven't done this in ages."
msgstr "Hace años que no hago esto."

msgid "Any time now."
msgstr "En cualquier momento."

msgid "Say, since we've got some time to kill..."
msgstr "Oye, ya que tenemos algo de tiempo para matar..."

msgid "Want to hear about the time I met a space iguana?"
msgstr "¿Quieres que te cuente la vez que conocí a una iguana espacial?"

msgid "So I was returning to Haven, when I saw a derelict."
msgstr "Así que volvía a Refugio, cuando vi un derrelicto."

msgid "Being the fellow I am, I boarded it."
msgstr "Siendo como soy, lo abordé."

msgid "Ship was all covered in blood and bodies."
msgstr "La nave estaba cubierto de sangre y cadáveres."

msgid "Fresh bodies means fresh goods, great I thought."
msgstr "Cuerpos frescos significa mercancías frescas, genial pensé."

msgid "Until I got to the command room."
msgstr "Hasta que llegué a la sala de mando."

msgid "Bloody Iguana chomping on the captain's leg!"
msgstr "¡La Maldita Iguana mordisqueando la pierna del capitán!"

msgid "Almost crapped my trousers!"
msgstr "¡Casi me cago en los pantalones!"

msgid "It gave me one look, and blam, I was outta there."
msgstr "Me dio una mirada, y blam, me fui de allí."

msgid "Now I never board without my Iguana repellent!"
msgstr "¡Ahora nunca abordo sin mi repelente de Iguanas!"

msgid "Seriously though, you should get some too."
msgstr "En serio, tú también deberías comprarte algo."

msgid "It could really come in handy..."
msgstr "Podría ser realmente útil..."

msgid "No! No! No! I'm out of here!"
msgstr "¡No! ¡No! ¡No! ¡Me voy de aquí!"

#. Must both be alive
#. See if they will start to get further away in 10 seconds as criteria for attack
msgid "Go! Go! Go!"
msgstr "¡Vamos! ¡Vamos! ¡Vamos!"

msgid "TARGET ACQUIRED."
msgstr "OBJETIVO ADQUIRIDO."

#. At least npc tries to get away
#. Have them duke it out
#. Make the factions enemies
#. Say something
msgid "Dvaered fire? The Za'lek fear no Dvaered!"
msgstr "¿Fuego Dvaered? ¡Los Za'lek no temen a los Dvaered!"

msgid "Petty Za'leks. Time to coat my hull in blood!"
msgstr "Za'leks Mezquinos. ¡Es hora de cubrir mi casco de sangre!"

#. Have some nasty Imperials jump in
#. Go to where the action is
#. They'll eventually overpower the player, although I doubt they'll every try to take them down
#. Main objective is done
msgid "Targets eliminated! Return to {spb}."
msgstr "¡Objetivos eliminados! Regresa a {spb}."

msgid "In the name of the Emperor, cease fighting or perish!"
msgstr "¡En nombre del Emperador, dejad de luchar o pereced!"

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Adblocker">
#. <unique />
#. <chance>10</chance>
#. <cond>
#. local mtest = require("misn_test")
#. if not mtest.cargo(true) or not mtest.reweight_active() then
#. return false
#. end
#. return true
#. </cond>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Adblocker
#. Author: Lemuria
#.
#. Player has to kill a ship that's been spamming the local comms with
#. excessive advertisements.
#.
#. I was bored and had nothing better to do, so I made this Naev mission,
#. my first.
#. --
msgid "Adblocker"
msgstr "Adblocker"

msgid ""
"Destroy a ship spamming the {sys} system with excessive advertising "
"transmissions"
msgstr ""
"Destruir una nave enviando spam al sistema {sys} con transmisiones excesivas "
"de publicidad"

msgid "Desperate captain"
msgstr "Capitán Desesperado"

msgid "You see a desperate looking captain."
msgstr "Ves a un capitán de aspecto desesperado."

msgid ""
"\"Look, I don't have much time! There's this annoying ship that's been "
"spamming the local comms with tons of advertisements! I can't take it any "
"more! Please, you've got to stop it! I'll give you {creds} if you stop it!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Mira, no tengo mucho tiempo! Hay una nave molesta que ha estado "
"bombardeando las comunicaciones locales con montones de anuncios. No puedo "
"soportarlo más. ¡Por favor, tienes que pararlo! ¡Te daré {creds} si lo "
"detienes!\""

msgid "You walk away, ignoring him."
msgstr "Te alejas, ignorándolo."

msgid "\"Thank you! Again, just stop that thing! Do what you have to!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Gracias! De nuevo, ¡sólo detén esa cosa! ¡Haz lo que tengas que hacer!\""

msgid ""
"A ship is currently spamming {sys} with tons of unwanted advertisements. A "
"desperate captain has asked you to destroy, or disable it."
msgstr ""
"Una nave está bombardeando {sys} con toneladas de publicidad no deseada. Un "
"capitán desesperado te ha pedido que la destruyas o la desactives."

msgid "Return to {spob} ({sys} system)"
msgstr "Vuelve a {spob} (sistema {sys})"

msgid "Advertiser 108CK"
msgstr "Anuncio 108CK"

#. Generate ads if not available
#. Only spam if not disabled
msgid ""
"The man runs towards you. \"Thank you so much for destroying that ship! The "
"advertisements were about to drive me crazy! Man they're so annoying!\""
msgstr ""
"El hombre corre hacia ti. \"¡Muchas gracias por destruir esa nave! ¡Los "
"anuncios estaban a punto de volverme loco! ¡Tío, son tan molestos!\""

msgid "You destroyed a ship spamming advertisements."
msgstr "Has destruido una nave haciendo spam."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Animal transport">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>10</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <faction>Sirius</faction>
#. <cond>
#. if spob.cur():tags().station then
#. return false
#. end
#. return require("misn_test").reweight_active()
#. </cond>
#. <notes>
#. <tier>1</tier>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#.
#. MISSION: Animal transport
#. DESCRIPTION: A man asks you to transport a crate of specially bred creatures for
#. his in-law's exotic pet store on another planet. It's a standard fare A-to-B mission,
#. but doing this mission infests the player's current ship with the creatures.
#.
#. --
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Sirian Bounty">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>3</priority>
#. <spob>The Wringer</spob>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <cond>
#. return require("misn_test").reweight_active()
#. </cond>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Academy Hack</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. This is the first mission in the Academy Hack minor campaign.
#. --
#. Mission constants
#. displayed reward
#. real reward
#. This mission ONLY spawns if the system it's in is not claimed by another mission. Special hack to mutex with Dark Shadow.
msgid "A Fyrra civilian"
msgstr "Un civil Fyrra"

#. Get an M-class Sirius planet at least 2 and at most 4 jumps away. If not found, don't spawn the mission.
msgid ""
"There's a civilian here, from the Fyrra echelon by the looks of him. He's "
"got some kind of crate with him."
msgstr ""
"Hay un civil aquí, del escalón de Fyrra por lo que parece. Tiene una especie "
"de caja con él."

msgid ""
"\"Good day to you, captain. I'm looking for someone with a ship who can take "
"this crate here to planet {pnt} in the {sys} system. The crate contains a "
"colony of rodents I've bred myself. My in-law has a pet shop on {pnt} where "
"I hope to sell them. Upon delivery, you will be paid {credits}. Are you "
"interested in the job?\""
msgstr ""
"\" Buenos días, capitán. Busco a alguien con una nave que pueda llevar esta "
"caja al planeta {pnt} en el sistema {sys}. La caja contiene una colonia de "
"roedores que yo mismo he criado. Mi suegro tiene una tienda de mascotas en "
"{pnt} donde espero venderlos. A la entrega, se te pagará {credits}. ¿Estás "
"interesado en el trabajo?\""

msgid ""
"\"Excellent! My in-law will send someone to meet you at the spaceport to "
"take the crate off your hands, and you'll be paid immediately on delivery. "
"Thanks again!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Excelente! Mi suegro enviará a alguien a buscarte al puerto espacial para "
"quitarte la caja de las manos, y se te pagará inmediatamente a la entrega. "
"¡Gracias de nuevo!\""

msgid ""
"You've been hired to transport a crate of specially engineered rodents to "
"{pnt} ({sys} system)."
msgstr ""
"Has sido contratado para transportar una caja de roedores especialmente "
"diseñados a {pnt} (sistema {sys})."

msgid "You will be paid {credits} on arrival."
msgstr "Se te pagará con {credits} a tu llegada."

msgid "Animal transport"
msgstr "Transporte de Animales"

msgid ""
"As promised, there's someone at the spaceport who accepts the crate. In "
"return, you receive a number of credit chips worth {credits}, as per the "
"arrangement. You go back into your ship to put the chips away before heading "
"off to check in with the local authorities. But did you just hear something "
"squeak…?"
msgstr ""
"Como se te prometió, hay alguien en el puerto espacial que acepta la caja. A "
"cambio, recibes un número de fichas de crédito por valor de {credits}, según "
"el acuerdo. Vuelves a tu nave para guardar las fichas antes de dirigirte a "
"registrarte con las autoridades locales. Pero, ¿escuchas un chillido...?"

msgid ""
"You successfully transported a crate of rodents for a Fyrra civilian. You "
"could have sworn you heard something squeak."
msgstr ""
"Has transportado con éxito una caja de roedores para un civil Fyrra. Podrías "
"jurar que has oído un chillido."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Antivirus">
#. <unique />
#. <chance>10</chance>
#. <done>Adblocker</done>
#. <chapter>[^0]</chapter>
#. <cond>
#. local scur = spob.cur()
#. if system.get("Straight Row"):jumpDist( system.cur() ) &gt; 8 then
#. return false
#. elseif not scur:faction():tags().generic then
#. return false
#. end
#. local maxsize = player.pilot():ship():size()
#. for k,s in ipairs(player.ships()) do
#. maxsize = math.max( maxsize, s.ship:size() )
#. end
#. if maxsize &lt; 6 then
#. return false
#. end
#. local misn_test = require "misn_test"
#. return misn_test.mercenary() and misn_test.reweight_active()
#. </cond>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Sequel to/edit of Adblocker; player has to fight the 4DV3RT1Z3R capship.
#. - Zivi (hsza)
#. --
msgid "Antivirus"
msgstr ""

msgid "Take down the advertising bandit in {sys}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You see a representative of local law enforcement, considering you with a "
"thoughtful expression."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"On behalf of the {spob} government, I have been investigating some of the "
"advertiser ships in this sector of space. You see, sometimes they behave all "
"too erratically, sending hundreds of advertisements a hectostu, and when we "
"board one of them, the captain is none the wiser!\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"Someone has been planting malware on those ships to fulfil dozens of "
"advertising contracts simultaneously and funnel all of the profits to "
"themselves. Too bad for them - we have managed to track the head of the "
"operation down to the {sys} system. Several of our own agent barely got out "
"of there alive, so we need a more than capable pilot to take the bandit "
"down. Pay is {creds}. Willing to give it a go?\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Ah, too bad. Might have been wise of you to pass on this job, though."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"Again, the target should be somewhere in {sys} at the moment. Come "
"prepared.\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Battle the orchestrator of advertising spam in {sys}."
msgstr ""

msgid "4DV3RT1Z3R >:)"
msgstr ""

#. boss:intrinsicSet('fbay_capacity', 20)
#. Generate ads if not available
#. Only spam if not disabled
#. Rename all the drones too for the fun of it
#. Good opportunity to check if we want to summon reinforcements yet
msgid "The advertisements are overloading your ship!"
msgstr ""

#. local loc = vec2.newP(rnd.rnd() * 0.4 * system.cur():radius(), rnd.angle()) + location
msgid "Advertiser {n}DK"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you move in to board the ship, it seems as there's no way inside. Docking "
"at all is quite a challenge, and the airlock is completely sealed up. "
"However, with some effort, and at a cost to the ship's hull, you are able to "
"force your way in."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You rush to investigate the interior. The first thing you see is a few "
"partway-decomposed bodies scattered by the airlock. Was this the original "
"crew of the ship? It seems as the airlock and life support systems have been "
"nonfunctional for a considerable amount of time."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"I suppose you would be curious about this ship's logs, but I'm wary of "
"connecting to the systems - most likely, it's under complete control of the "
"malware that investigator was talking about, and who knows what it can do?\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Try to connect"
msgstr ""

msgid "Do not"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you're about to make a decision, the screens in the cockpit flash a "
"warning - \"SECURITY SELF-DESTRUCT INITIATED\". Welp, that's your cue to get "
"out of here. Better luck next time?"
msgstr ""

#. codespell:ignore welp
msgid ""
"Rushing out the compromised ship, you spot a strange device connected to one "
"of the terminals, and curiosity gets the better of you. This must contain "
"the malicious payload - could it be worth studying? You grab it as you run "
"back to your ship."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"You're back? The target is eliminated? What a relief! You won't believe "
"just how irritating that scheme has been. It will take me a while to write "
"my report, but you're due your reward.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You defeated a malware vendor and advert defrauder to the great relief of ad-"
"loathing captains around the universe."
msgstr ""

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Terraforming Antlejos 1">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>4</priority>
#. <chance>5</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <cond>
#. -- Must be "nearby" Antlejos
#. local d = system.jumpDist("Antlejos")
#. if d &lt; 4 or d &gt; 12 then
#. return false
#. end
#. return require("misn_test").reweight_active()
#. </cond>
#. <notes>
#. <tier>1</tier>
#. <campaign>Terraforming Antlejos</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Campaign to Terraform Antlejos V
#.
#. Just take Verner to see Antlejos V and set up camp.
#. --
#. Amount in mass
#. Tell the player to land
#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Terraforming Antlejos 6">
#. <unique />
#. <priority>3</priority>
#. <chance>100</chance>
#. <location>Bar</location>
#. <spob>Antlejos V</spob>
#. <cond>require('common.antlejos').unidiffLevel() &gt;= 6</cond>
