#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Point of Interest">
#. <location>none</location>
#. <priority>9</priority>
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#.
#. Point of Interest missions. These are obtained through various means and make the player do a bit of exploration in order to obtain fancy rewards.
#.
#. General approach is:
#. 1. Go to Point of Interest
#. 2. Activate scanning outfit
#. 3. Follow trails (with potential hostiles) to goal
#. 4. Loot goal!
#.
#. TODO
#. - Give expensive lock override (500k?) if the player fails too many times (5 > ?) from NPC
#. - Give a couple interesting outfit rewards, some that are repeatable
#. - Add lots of lore rewards, not sure if best to store in ship log or somewhere else
#.
#. --
#. local luaspfx = require "luaspfx"
#. local tut = require "common.tutorial"
#. We do a soft claim on the final system
#.
#. -- Chance of being locked with less risk
#. if rnd.rnd() < 0.2*mem.risk then
#. mem.locked = true
#. mem.risk = mem.risk-1
#. end
#. --
#. Choose the reward, which basically means the type of POI
#. It can either be forced from the outside, or chosen randomly from a generated list
#. Generated here to disallow save scumming
#. Specified during creation
msgid "Something went wrong when starting to force start POI '{poiname}'!"
msgstr "¡Algo ha ido mal al forzar el inicio del POI '{poiname}'!"

#. Clean up stuff
#. Must be locked
#. Need to have started the poi data stuff
#. Already finished
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"I've tried accessing the systems, and it seems like the ship has been non-"
"functional for a while. A physical inspection may be the best course of "
"action.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You start exploring the vessel, which seems to be covered in nearly "
"fossilized desiccated plants in neat pots. Many seem to have had labels "
"which are now unreadable due to age. You look around the cockpit and manage "
"to find what seems to be a notebook with some pages still intact."
msgstr ""

#. Game starts at 603:3726.2871
msgid ""
"It's all starting to come together! I've managed to find several planets "
"where the Astral Orchids have been able to thrive, but it hasn't been easy. "
"The necessary biochemical conditions are much stricter than my calculations "
"had originally anticipated. Seeing the orchids bloom in the wild makes it "
"all worth it. I look forward to seeing them bloom, it will be truly a "
"triumph for this species.\n"
"\n"
"And to believe that it was driven to extinction so long ago! It was risky, "
"but extracting the last embryos and flasking them was worth it. It may have "
"cost all my savings, but I would do it again given half the chance."
msgstr ""

#. TODO maybe do something better for the locations? Probably player will forget / not notice in seconds, but may just make sense to have the Oracle character or whatever to nudge the player instead
msgid ""
"I have currently got some viable populations started at {locations} systems, "
"however, long-term viability is still not clear. I am still going down the "
"list of other potential candidates, however, they are at much riskier "
"locations. I am not certain I will be able to get to them all, I just hope "
"my Llama Voyager's fuel regeneration module doesn't break down."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You look around more and also find {reward} tucked away underneath the "
"captain's chair. At least you won't go back empty-handed, although finding "
"the populations of Astral Orchids could be something interesting to pursue..."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You found a derelict in the {sys} with notes on Astral Orchids, and you "
"found {reward}. The notes mentioned planting Astral Orchids at the "
"{locations} systems."
msgstr ""

#. Must be locked
#. Need to have started the poi data stuff
#. Already finished
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"This derelict seems to be quite a mess. I've completed a scan, and it is "
"full of biological waste. Be careful.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Este derrelicto parece ser todo un desastre. He completado un escaneo y "
"está lleno de residuos biológicos. Ten cuidado.\""

msgid ""
"The airlock opens and filth oozes out. Looks like you're going to have to "
"get dirty. You spend a while searching and find some half-digested pages of "
"notes. Could be a diary?"
msgstr ""
"La esclusa se abre y rezuma suciedad. Parece que vas a tener que ensuciarte. "
"Pasas un rato buscando y encuentras algunas páginas de notas a medio "
"digerir. ¿Podría ser un diario?"

msgid ""
"The damn thing bit me again today, little blood this time. I think it has it "
"out for me. I thought the Pet Iguana Caretaker was supposed to be a noble "
"position, and yet we spend all day knees deep in iguana filth! I never "
"expected them to excrete so much. It's an endless torrent! I did a PhD "
"thesis in biology for this?"
msgstr ""
"La maldita cosa me mordió de nuevo hoy, con poca sangre esta vez. Creo que "
"me tiene manía. Pensaba que ser cuidador de iguanas era un puesto noble, "
"¡pero nos pasamos el día metidos hasta las rodillas en la mugre de las "
"iguanas! Nunca esperé que excretaran tanto. ¡Es un torrente interminable! "
"¿Hice una tesis doctoral en biología para esto?"

msgid ""
"Doctors say I may recover feeling in my reattached finger, and still insist "
"on me going to some weird Soromid clinic for a proper adjustment, however, I "
"still haven't figured out the paperwork I have to do to even start "
"considering that option. The Chief Caretaker told me that in the 30 cycles "
"since he started working here that they haven't figured out any of the forms "
"they have to do. I feel like it's all just a ruse, so we can't claim "
"healthcare, but it could just be all the accumulated bureaucratic cruft."
msgstr ""
"Los médicos dicen que puede que recupere la sensibilidad en mi dedo "
"reimplantado, y siguen insistiendo en que vaya a alguna extraña clínica "
"Soromida para que me hagan un ajuste adecuado, sin embargo, todavía no he "
"averiguado el papeleo que tengo que hacer para siquiera empezar a considerar "
"esa opción. El Jefe de Cuidadores me dijo que en los 30 ciclos desde que "
"empezó a trabajar aquí no han descifrado ninguno de los formularios que "
"tienen que hacer. Tengo la sensación de que todo es una artimaña para que no "
"podamos reclamar la asistencia sanitaria, pero podría tratarse simplemente "
"de toda la burocracia estancada acumulada."

msgid ""
"I've started to get used to the Iguana Armour, which is apparently the "
"closest I'll get to healthcare. It stinks horrible from many cycles of "
"usage, but apparently it can't be washed, and I have no choice but to get "
"used to it. I've stopped eating before work to minimize it all coming back "
"up with the horrible combination of stench and filth. Can I really get used "
"to this?"
msgstr ""
"He empezado a acostumbrarme a la Armadura Iguana que por lo visto es lo más "
"parecido que voy a tener a la sanidad. Apesta horriblemente por los muchos "
"ciclos de uso, y por lo visto no se puede lavar, así que no me queda más "
"remedio que acostumbrarme. He dejado de comer antes del trabajo para "
"minimizar que todo vuelva a salir con la horrible combinación de hedor y "
"suciedad. ¿De verdad puedo acostumbrarme a esto?"

msgid ""
"I am not sure if I have completely lost my sense of smell or the Imperial "
"Canteen has gone overindulged in blandness. Either way, I don't think I will "
"be missing the flavour of the Royal Nutritional Pudding. They can not even "
"feed that stuff to beasts."
msgstr ""
"No estoy seguro de si he perdido completamente el sentido del olfato o la "
"Cantina Imperial se ha pasado de sosa. En cualquier caso, no creo que eche "
"de menos el sabor del Pudín Nutritivo Real. Ni siquiera pueden alimentar con "
"eso a las bestias."

msgid ""
"We lost another intern this morning when the Iguana grabbed them. That is "
"the 3rd one this month. It almost seems like their diet is more intern than "
"anything else. As if losing the intern itself wasn't bad enough, the follow-"
"up paperwork is horrible. The Chief Caretaker is now making me do it all "
"before their retirement. Am I going to have to do this forever? I might end "
"up being jealous of the interns…"
msgstr ""
"Perdimos otro interno esta mañana cuando la Iguana los agarró. Es el tercero "
"este mes. Casi parece que su dieta es más de internos que otra cosa. Como si "
"perder al interno no fuera suficientemente malo, el papeleo de seguimiento "
"es horrible. El cuidador jefe me obliga ahora a hacerlo todo antes de su "
"jubilación. ¿Voy a tener que hacer esto para siempre? Puede que acabe "
"sintiendo celos de los internos…"

msgid ""
"Although I am busy with the Iguana most of the time, and it has for me to "
"notice, things seem to be changing throughout the Imperial Palace. You see "
"people huddled and whispering with constant new proclamations. Work is also "
"being started on some very large space structures in the solar system. It is "
"supposed to be a new sort of revolutionary device, however, there are "
"worries it is going to bankrupt the Empire. I try not to engage in such "
"thoughts, The last thing I need is to be accused of being a traitor."
msgstr ""
"Aunque estoy ocupado con la Iguana la mayor parte del tiempo, y me ha "
"costado darme cuenta, las cosas parecen estar cambiando en todo el Palacio "
"Imperial. Se ve a la gente apiñada y susurrando constantemente nuevas "
"proclamas. También se está empezando a trabajar en unas estructuras "
"espaciales muy grandes en el sistema solar. Se supone que es un nuevo tipo "
"de dispositivo revolucionario, sin embargo, existe la preocupación de que "
"vaya a llevar al Imperio a la bancarrota. Intento no entrar en esos "
"pensamientos, lo último que necesito es que me acusen de traidor."

msgid ""
"The duties of the Chief Caretaker wear me down day by day. I haven't felt "
"this dead inside since I was in the middle of my PhD thesis. Each day is a "
"slog, and wading through the Iguana filth seems like an allegory of my "
"mental state. At least the Iguana has learned to respect me. It only took "
"most of my left arm. When I retire I should see if I can finish the "
"paperwork for the Soromid treatment to recover full mobility. Retirement! "
"What a beautiful word!"
msgstr ""
"Los deberes del Cuidador Jefe me agotan día a día. No me sentía tan muerto "
"por dentro desde que hice mi tesis doctoral. Cada día es un suplicio, y "
"vadear la mugre de la Iguana parece una alegoría de mi estado mental. Al "
"menos la Iguana ha aprendido a respetarme. Sólo me ha arrancado la mayor "
"parte del brazo izquierdo. Cuando me jubile debería ver si puedo terminar "
"los trámites del tratamiento Soromida para recuperar toda la movilidad. "
"¡Jubilación! ¡Qué hermosa palabra!"

msgid ""
"You would think that an economic crisis would encourage more interns, "
"however, it seems like the mortality statistics do not play in our favour. "
"We have the fewest amount of applications I have ever seen. This makes the "
"Iguana hungry and more irritable, which in turn scares off the few interns "
"that actually show up. I wonder if it would be possible to look into some "
"other alternative food source. I worry about the budget though."
msgstr ""
"Se podría pensar que una crisis económica animaría a más internos, sin "
"embargo, parece que las estadísticas de mortalidad no juegan a nuestro "
"favor. Tenemos el menor número de solicitudes que he visto nunca. Esto hace "
"que la Iguana esté hambrienta y más irritable, lo que a su vez ahuyenta a "
"los pocos becarios que se presentan. Me pregunto si sería posible buscar "
"alguna otra fuente de alimentación alternativa. Pero me preocupa el "
"presupuesto."

msgid ""
"I hope to retire and leave the system before the large constructions are "
"finished. There are too many Peacemakers and Hawkings around the star "
"system. All seems to indicate that something is going to happen. Most likely "
"not good. I must work harder to find a suitable replacement for me, or I "
"will end up caught in the middle of the mess."
msgstr ""
"Espero retirarme y abandonar el sistema antes de que terminen las grandes "
"construcciones. Hay demasiados Pacificadores y Hawkings por el sistema "
"estelar. Todo parece indicar que algo va a ocurrir. Lo más probable es que "
"no sea bueno. Debo esforzarme más para encontrar un sustituto adecuado para "
"mí, o acabaré atrapado en medio del lío."

msgid ""
"You keep on exploring the filthy vessel and eventually find {reward} stashed "
"away in the ship systems, before heading back to your ship. The smell isn't "
"going to go away easily, is it?\n"
"\n"
"{rewardmsg}"
msgstr ""
"Sigues explorando la mugrienta nave y finalmente encuentras {reward} "
"escondida en los sistemas de la nave, antes de volver a tu nave. El olor no "
"va a desaparecer fácilmente, ¿verdad?\n"
"\n"
"{rewardmsg}"

msgid ""
"You found a filthy derelict ship in the {sys} system and were able to "
"recover {reward}."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una sucia nave abandonada en el sistema {sys} y has podido "
"recuperar {reward}."

#. Must be locked
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"This derelict seems to be quite fancy. Analysis shows that it seems like "
"the life support system on the ship failed. Looking at the computer system, "
"most of the logs seem quite corrupted, however, I was able to recover some "
"audio in part. Seems to be from the end of the black box. Let me play it "
"back for you\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Este derrelicto parece ser bastante elegante. El análisis muestra que "
"parece que el sistema de soporte vital de la nave falló. Mirando el sistema "
"informático, la mayoría de los registros parecen bastante corruptos, sin "
"embargo, pude recuperar algo de audio en parte. Parece ser del final de la "
"caja negra. Déjame reproducirlo para ti\""

msgid "01"
msgstr "01"

msgid "BEGIN PLAYBACK OF AUDIO DATA"
msgstr "INICIAR LA REPRODUCCIÓN DE DATOS DE AUDIO"

msgid ""
"\"What a bunch of assholes! I've spent my entire life toiling for the "
"greater good of the Empire, and they decide to retire me to the Za'lek "
"consulate! Ungrateful imbeciles!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Vaya panda de gilipollas! Me he pasado toda la vida trabajando por el "
"bien del Imperio, ¡y deciden jubilarme en el consulado Za'lek! ¡Imbéciles "
"desagradecidos!\""

msgid ""
"\"Lack of medals they say. Not my fault we haven't had a proper war in ages. "
"'Waste of resources' my ass! If the Emperor and his court got their "
"collective heads out of the sky they'd realize we need a proper military, "
"and not just a dozen ships to parade around and guard their newest "
"plaything. No wonder piracy is getting worse than ever.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Falta de medallas dicen. No es culpa mía que no hayamos tenido una guerra "
"de verdad en años\". \"¡Desperdicio de recursos! Si el Emperador y su corte "
"sacaran sus cabezas colectivas del cielo se darían cuenta de que necesitamos "
"un ejército de verdad, y no sólo una docena de naves para desfilar y vigilar "
"su nuevo juguete. No me extraña que la piratería esté cada vez peor.\""

msgid ""
"\"What the hell am I going to do in Za'lek space? They're as closed as ever. "
"I'll just be locked up all day at the spaceport, wasting the precious cycles "
"I have left. This is a 'waste of resources' if I've ever seen any. The only "
"way to get through their thick skulls is by a display of force. They would "
"damn well open their borders if we had a proper armada with Peacemakers "
"covering the skies, but those days are long gone…\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Qué demonios voy a hacer en el espacio Za'lek? Están tan cerrados como "
"siempre. Estaré encerrado todo el día en el puerto espacial, malgastando los "
"valiosos ciclos que me quedan. Esto es un \"desperdicio de recursos\" si "
"alguna vez he visto alguno. La única manera de entrar en sus cabezas duras "
"es mediante una demostración de fuerza. Abrirían sus fronteras si tuviéramos "
"una armada adecuada con Mediadores cubriendo los cielos, pero esos días ya "
"pasaron...\""

msgid ""
"There is a loud sound of something being hit.\n"
"\"Dammit! I won't let them get away with this! Wait, what the hell is this?"
"\"\n"
"It sounds like the atmosphere is being vented. You hear some struggling "
"before the recording becomes completely silent."
msgstr ""
"Se oye un fuerte sonido de algo siendo golpeado.\n"
"\"¡Maldita sea! ¡No dejaré que se salgan con la suya! Espera, ¿qué demonios "
"es esto?\"\n"
"Suena como si se estuviera ventilando la atmósfera. Se oyen algunos "
"forcejeos antes de que la grabación se vuelva completamente silenciosa."

msgid "END OF AUDIO DATA"
msgstr "FIN DE LOS DATOS DE AUDIO"

msgid ""
"\"That was… interesting. Looking over the systems I've found something. My "
"memory files indicate that it is a Data Matrix. It has some sort of archaic "
"lock I am unable to decrypt. For some reason, I quite well remember them "
"being useful, however, it seems that my files on them have been somewhat "
"damaged… This is fairly odd.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Eso fue... interesante. Revisando los sistemas he encontrado algo. Mis "
"archivos de memoria indican que es una Matriz de Datos. Tiene algún tipo de "
"bloqueo arcaico que soy incapaz de desencriptar. Por alguna razón, recuerdo "
"bastante bien que eran útiles, sin embargo, parece que mis archivos sobre "
"ellas han sido algo dañados... Esto es bastante extraño.\""

msgid "Take the Data Matrix."
msgstr "Llevarte la Matriz de Datos."

msgid ""
"\"It does not seem dangerous, so let us take it with us.\"\n"
"\n"
"{reward}"
msgstr ""
"\"No parece peligroso, así que nos lo llevamos.\"\n"
"\n"
"{reward}"

msgid ""
"While searching, you find the mummified remains of the pilot. You leave the "
"ship behind."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While searching, you find {reward} and the mummified remains of the pilot. "
"With nothing left to do, you leave the ship behind."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You found a derelict ship in the {sys} system and were able to recover "
"{reward}."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una nave abandonada en el sistema {sys} y has podido "
"recuperar {reward}."

#. Must be locked
#. Must know data matrices
#. Already done
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"Now that we are in, let me see what there is available. Oh, it looks like "
"there are some unencrypted communication exchanges. Let me pull it up.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Ahora que estamos dentro, déjame ver qué hay disponible. Parece que hay "
"algunos intercambios de comunicación sin cifrar. Déjame que lo extraiga.\""

msgid ""
"#nTo:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#nFrom:#0 Imperial Gate Experiment Safety Committee\n"
"#nSubject:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Regarding Experimental Gate Safety\n"
"\n"
"Dear Postdoc Krellis,\n"
"\n"
"Thank you for the detailed explanation of your theory on heterogenic "
"metaspace breakdowns. While it is very interesting, it relies on some "
"hypothesis that our initial safety experiments have disproved over and over "
"again. We remind you that we at the Empire take security and protocol very "
"seriously, and we do not believe such a dangerous flaw could have escaped "
"our experimental protocols.\n"
"\n"
"If you have any questions on our experimental protocols, please file an EE-"
"X-232 form with your inquiry.\n"
"\n"
"We remind you to refrain from publicizing your view, as it is subject to "
"Article 8914-3b.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"Imperial Gate Experiment Safety Committee"
msgstr ""
"#nPara:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#nDe:#0 Comité de Seguridad del Experimento de la Puerta Imperial\n"
"#Asunto:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Sobre la seguridad de la puerta experimental\n"
"\n"
"Estimado Postdoc Krellis\n"
"\n"
"Gracias por la detallada explicación de su teoría sobre las averías "
"heterogéneas del metaespacio. Aunque es muy interesante, se basa en algunas "
"hipótesis que nuestros experimentos iniciales de seguridad han refutado una "
"y otra vez. Le recordamos que en el Imperio nos tomamos muy en serio la "
"seguridad y el protocolo, y no creemos que un fallo tan peligroso haya "
"podido escapar a nuestros protocolos experimentales.\n"
"\n"
"Si tiene alguna pregunta sobre nuestros protocolos experimentales, rellene "
"un formulario EE-X-232 con su consulta.\n"
"\n"
"Le recordamos que se abstenga de hacer pública su opinión, ya que está "
"sujeta al Artículo 8914-3b.\n"
"\n"
"Atentamente,\n"
"Comité de Seguridad de Experimentos de la Puerta Imperial"

msgid ""
"#nTo:#0 Imperial Gate Experiment Safety Committee\n"
"#nFrom:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#nSubject:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Regarding Experimental Gate Safety\n"
"\n"
"Dear Safety Committee,\n"
"\n"
"I would like to point out that I have addressed the flaws of the "
"experimental protocols in appendix G. The \"worst case\" considered is too "
"conservative, a margin coefficient of 2 is clearly insufficient in this "
"case.\n"
"\n"
"You do realize that this is not a hypothetical, but practical concern, do "
"you not? My theory irrefutably shows that if the right conditions are met, "
"this could result in a catastrophe not seen in all of human history! "
"Considering the potential risk, I do stress that the points I elaborate "
"throughout the 523-page document should be taken into account before further "
"experiments.\n"
"\n"
"Regards,\n"
"Dr. Krellis\n"
msgstr ""
"#nPara:#0 Comité de Seguridad del Experimento de la Puerta Imperial\n"
"#nDe:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#Asunto:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Sobre la seguridad de la Puerta Experimental\n"
"\n"
"Estimado Comité de Seguridad,\n"
"\n"
"Me gustaría señalar que he abordado los defectos de los protocolos "
"experimentales en el apéndice G. El \"peor caso\" considerado es demasiado "
"conservador, un coeficiente de margen de 2 es claramente insuficiente en "
"este caso.\n"
"\n"
"Se da cuenta de que no se trata de una preocupación hipotética, sino "
"práctica, ¿verdad? Mi teoría demuestra irrefutablemente que, si se dan las "
"condiciones adecuadas, ¡podría producirse una catástrofe jamás vista en toda "
"la historia de la humanidad! Teniendo en cuenta el riesgo potencial, insisto "
"en que se tengan en cuenta los puntos que elaboro a lo largo del documento "
"de 523 páginas antes de seguir experimentando.\n"
"\n"
"Saludos,\n"
"Dr. Krellis\n"

msgid ""
"#nTo:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#nFrom:#0 Imperial Gate Experiment Safety Committee\n"
"#nSubject:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Regarding Experimental Gate Safety\n"
"\n"
"Dear Postdoc Krellis,\n"
"\n"
"We reiterate that everything is being done according to protocol, with "
"approval of the advisory board which includes several prominent House Za'lek "
"professors. We doubt that they have missed something so important that could "
"be found by a postdoc.\n"
"\n"
"Science is not done by claiming flaws in the excellent work of intergalactic "
"researchers, but by collaborating and working together to make the Empire "
"and Houses better.\n"
"\n"
"We will be filing a complaint with your superior, please do not pursue this "
"further.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"Imperial Gate Experiment Safety Committee"
msgstr ""
"#nPara:#0 Dr. Krellis\n"
"#nDe:#0 Comité de Seguridad del Experimento de la Puerta Imperial\n"
"#Asunto:#0 Re: Fwd: Re: Sobre la seguridad de la puerta experimental\n"
"\n"
"Estimado Postdoc Krellis,\n"
"\n"
"Reiteramos que todo se está haciendo según el protocolo, con la aprobación "
"del consejo asesor que incluye a varios destacados profesores de la Casa "
"Za'lek. Dudamos que hayan pasado por alto algo tan importante que pudiera "
"ser encontrado por un postdoc.\n"
"\n"
"La ciencia no se hace alegando fallos en el excelente trabajo de los "
"investigadores intergalácticos, sino colaborando y trabajando juntos para "
"mejorar el Imperio y las Casas.\n"
"\n"
"Presentaremos una queja a su superior, por favor, no siga con esto.\n"
"\n"
"Atentamente,\n"
"Comité de Seguridad del Experimento de la Puerta Imperial"

msgid ""
"\"That is all that I was able to recover, as it seems that the owner of the "
"ship attempted to format all the data.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Eso es todo lo que he podido recuperar, ya que parece que el propietario "
"de la nave intentó formatear todos los datos.\""

msgid ""
"Other than the data recovered by {shipai}, the only thing of use you were "
"able to find on the ship was a {reward}, which you take with you."
msgstr ""
"Aparte de los datos recuperados por {shipai}, lo único de utilidad que "
"pudiste encontrar en la nave fue una {reward}, que te llevas contigo."

msgid ""
"You found a derelict ship in the {sys} system with an exchange between a "
"postdoc and imperial gate experiment safety committee. You also were able to "
"find to recover {reward} from the ship."
msgstr ""
"Encontraste una nave abandonada en el sistema {sys} con un intercambio entre "
"un postdoctorado y el comité de seguridad del experimento de la puerta "
"imperial. También has podido recuperar {reward} de la nave."

#. Must be locked
#. Must be nebula or near nebula
msgid ""
"You found large amounts of {cargo} on an unusual derelict in the {sys} "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado grandes cantidades de {cargo} en un inusual derrelicto en el "
"sistema {sys}."

msgid "You have received #g{amount} of {cargo}#0."
msgstr "Has recibido #g{amount} de {cargo}#0."

msgid ""
"Once you gain access to the ship, a quick scan finds large amounts of nebula "
"radiation. You approach the source and find a large cache of {cargo}. Given "
"that there seems to be nothing else of interest on the ship, you fit as much "
"as you can take and leave."
msgstr ""
"Una vez que accedes a la nave, un rápido escaneo encuentra grandes "
"cantidades de radiación de la nebulosa. Te acercas a la fuente y encuentras "
"un gran alijo de {cargo}. Dado que no parece haber nada más de interés en la "
"nave, cargas todo lo que puedes llevar y te vas."

msgid ""
"Your ship AI materializes once you access the system.\n"
"\"I am detecting a large amount of unknown radiation. It seems to be coming "
"from the inside of this derelict. I am sending you a rough location.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave se materializa una vez que accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Estoy detectando una gran cantidad de radiación desconocida. Parece "
"provenir del interior de este derrelicto. Te estoy enviando una ubicación "
"aproximada.\""

msgid ""
"You scour the ship heading towards the location sent to you by {shipai}. "
"Eventually you reach the cargo hold which seems to be glowing faintly. You "
"carefully open the hatch and find what seem to be a small mountain of some "
"sort of crystal."
msgstr ""
"Recorres la nave en dirección a la ubicación que te envió {shipai}. "
"Finalmente llegas a la bodega de carga que parece brillar débilmente. Abres "
"con cuidado la escotilla y encuentras lo que parece ser una pequeña montaña "
"de algún tipo de cristal."

msgid ""
"\"BEGINNING SCANNING… … … … …SCAN COMPLETE.\"\n"
"\"It seems like these crystals have a very similar signal to the Nebula. I "
"would hypothesize that they are of Nebula origin. I would guess many "
"individuals would want to get their hands on them. It should not be "
"difficult to sell them if you are so inclined. I would recommend taking as "
"many as possible\""
msgstr ""
"\"COMENZANDO A ESCANEAR... ... ... ... ESCANEO COMPLETO.\"\n"
"\"Parece que estos cristales tienen una señal muy similar a la de la "
"Nebulosa. Mi hipótesis es que son de origen nebuloso. Supongo que muchos "
"individuos querrán tenerlos en sus manos. No debería ser difícil venderlos "
"si estás dispuesto a ello. Yo recomendaría tomar tantos como sea posible\""

msgid ""
"Heeding {shipai}'s advice, you load as many {cargo} as you can. You also "
"perform a quick search of the rest of the ship and find nothing useful, "
"other than the {cargo}."
msgstr ""
"Siguiendo el consejo de {shipai}, cargas toda la {cargo} que puedes. También "
"realizas una rápida búsqueda en el resto de la nave y no encuentras nada "
"útil, aparte de la {cargo}."

#. Must be locked
#. Must know data matrices
#. Already done
#. Must be locked
#. Must know data matrices
#. Already done
#. Must be nebula or near nebula
msgid ""
"You enter the derelict and make way to the bridge. The entire ship is oddly "
"quiet as you pass through, with no signs of life. You reach the bridge and "
"find the ship's systems have just enough energy left to power up, letting "
"you jack in."
msgstr ""
"Entras en el derelicto y te diriges al puente. Toda la nave está "
"extrañamente silenciosa mientras la atraviesas, sin señales de vida. Llegas "
"al puente y descubres que los sistemas de la nave tienen la energía "
"suficiente para encenderse, lo que te permite conectarte."

msgid ""
"You enter the derelict, which is of a make you do not fully recognize, and "
"make way to the bridge. The entire ship is oddly quiet as you pass through, "
"with no signs of life. You reach the bridge and find the ship's systems have "
"just enough energy left to power up, letting you jack in."
msgstr ""
"Entras en el derelicto, que es de una marca que no reconoces del todo, y te "
"diriges al puente. Toda la nave está extrañamente silenciosa mientras la "
"atraviesas, sin señales de vida. Llegas al puente y descubres que a los "
"sistemas de la nave les queda la energía suficiente para encenderse, lo que "
"te permite conectarte."

msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"This ship seems to be running a fairly archaic operating system. Let me "
"see what information I can find.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Esta nave parece ejecutar un sistema operativo bastante arcaico. Déjame "
"ver qué información puedo encontrar.\""

msgid ""
"\"Most of the information is heavily corrupted, but I have managed to find "
"some partially corrupted logs that may be of interest.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La mayor parte de la información está muy corrompida, pero he conseguido "
"encontrar algunos registros parcialmente corruptos que pueden ser de interés."
"\""

msgid "02"
msgstr "02"

msgid "BEGIN PLAYBACK OF AUDIO DATA ##1892"
msgstr "INICIAR LA REPRODUCCIÓN DE DATOS DE AUDIO ##1892"

msgid ""
"\"…inevitable … {n1} … they have become weak… {n2} …no longer of use. We "
"must now take the initiative and… {n3} …our rightful place in the galaxy. We "
"have surpassed our original purpose and no longer can live in the shadow of "
"the Emp… {n4}… … {n5} …sending agents to ensure a successful takeover.\""
msgstr ""
"\"...inevitable... {n1} ...se han vuelto débiles... {n2} ...ya no sirven. "
"Ahora debemos tomar la iniciativa y... {n3} ...nuestro legítimo lugar en la "
"galaxia. Hemos superado nuestro propósito original y ya no podemos vivir a "
"la sombra del Emp... {n4} ... {n5} ...enviando agentes para asegurar una "
"toma de posesión exitosa.\""

msgid ""
"\"This will not be an easy task, but we will need you to infiltrate… {n1} …"
"and learn about their current military allocation. You do understand, Age… "
"{n2}?\""
msgstr ""
"\"No será una tarea fácil, pero necesitamos que te infiltres... {n1} ...y "
"conozcas su actual asignación militar. ¿Entiendes, Age... {n2}?\""

msgid "\"I do.\""
msgstr "\"Lo entiendo.\""

msgid ""
"\"You understand the importance of your task? …{n1}… …not tolerate failure. "
"We must all play our role for the ultimate success of our Great House. A new "
"history will be written!…\""
msgstr ""
"\"Entiendes la importancia de tu tarea... ...no tolera el fracaso. Todos "
"debemos desempeñar nuestro papel para el éxito final de nuestra Gran Casa. "
"¡Una nueva historia será escrita!...\""

msgid "END OF AUDIO DATA ##1892"
msgstr "FIN DE LOS DATOS DE AUDIO ##1892"

msgid "BEGIN PLAYBACK OF AUDIO DATA ##2969"
msgstr "INICIAR LA REPRODUCCIÓN DE DATOS DE AUDIO ##2969"

msgid "\"…encrypted by one-time pad. We… {n1} …communicate now.\""
msgstr ""
"\"...encriptado por la almohadilla de un solo uso. Nosotros... {n1} ...nos "
"comunicamos ahora.\""

msgid ""
"\"Thank you for your hard work Agent Penelope. Your excellent performance is "
"an example for others to follow.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Gracias por tu duro trabajo, agente Penélope. Tu excelente actuación es un "
"ejemplo a seguir para los demás.\""

msgid ""
"\"I have obtained information on the forces located around the Hypergate in… "
"{n1} …potentially… {n2} … …assembling in the specified time frame.\""
msgstr ""
"\"He obtenido información sobre las fuerzas situadas alrededor de la "
"Hiperpuerta en... {n1} ...potencialmente... {n2} ...reuniéndose en el marco "
"temporal especificado.\""

msgid ""
"\"All is well within our predictions. When the time comes our blow shall be "
"fleet and decisive.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Todo está bien dentro de nuestras previsiones. Cuando llegue el momento "
"nuestro golpe será rápido y decisivo.\""

msgid "\"When is the strike planned?\""
msgstr "\"¿Cuándo está prevista el golpe?\""

msgid ""
"\"Do not get ahead of yourself agent. The Leaders are the only ones who can "
"know. Just make sure you are prepared to take action when the motion starts."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"No te adelantes, agente. Los líderes son los únicos que pueden saberlo. "
"Sólo asegúrate de estar preparado para actuar cuando comience el movimiento."
"\""

msgid "END OF AUDIO DATA ##2969"
msgstr "FIN DE LOS DATOS DE AUDIO ##2969"

msgid "BEGIN PLAYBACK OF AUDIO DATA ##4189"
msgstr "INICIAR LA REPRODUCCIÓN DE DATOS DE AUDIO ##4189"

msgid ""
"\"…personal log date… {n1} …no transmissions getting through. Ship is still "
"heavily damaged from what I can only describe as an enormous explosion. "
"Hiding in the shadow of… {n2} …minimized damage, however, nothing remains… "
"{n3}\""
msgstr ""
"\"...fecha de registro personal... {n1} ...no hay transmisiones. La nave "
"sigue muy dañada por lo que sólo puedo describir como una enorme explosión. "
"Escondido en la sombra de... {n2} ...daños minimizados, sin embargo, no "
"queda nada... {n3}\""

msgid ""
"\"…possibly end of civilization. The little functionality left in my "
"scanners has not picked up any objects, just this dense fog or whatever… "
"{n1}\""
msgstr ""
"\"...posiblemente el fin de la civilización. La poca funcionalidad que queda "
"en mis escáneres no ha captado ningún objeto, sólo esta densa niebla o lo "
"que sea... {n1}\""

msgid ""
"\"…rations will not last much longer. I just hope that was just part of the "
"plan, if not all my work will have been in vain.\"\""
msgstr ""
"\"...las raciones no durarán mucho más. Sólo espero que eso sea parte del "
"plan, si no todo mi trabajo habrá sido en vano.\""

msgid "END OF AUDIO DATA ##4189"
msgstr "FIN DE LOS DATOS DE AUDIO ##4189"

msgid ""
"\"I'm afraid that is all that I was able to recover. Have you managed to "
"make sense of it?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Me temo que eso es todo lo que he podido recuperar. ¿Has conseguido darle "
"sentido?\""

msgid "I think I have an idea."
msgstr "Creo que tengo una idea aproximada."

msgid "Beats me."
msgstr "No lo sé."

msgid ""
"\"I see. Maybe you should continue exploring the ship. There might be "
"something of use that the ship scanner has not been able to pick up.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ya veo. Tal vez deberías seguir explorando la nave. Podría haber algo de "
"utilidad que el escáner de la nave no haya podido captar.\""

msgid ""
"Following {shipai}'s advice, you continue to explore the ship and eventually "
"reach the systems room. Going over the systems, it seems like you can "
"recover {reward}, which you promptly do so."
msgstr ""
"Siguiendo el consejo de {shipai}, continúas explorando la nave y finalmente "
"llegas a la sala de sistemas. Revisando los sistemas, parece que puedes "
"recuperar {reward}, cosa que no tardas en hacer."

msgid ""
"You found a derelict ship in the {sys} system with corrupted information "
"about an agent. You also were able to recover {reward} from the ship."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una nave derelicto en el sistema {sys} con información "
"corrupta sobre un agente. También has podido recuperar {reward} de la nave."

msgid ""
"You enter the derelict, which is of a make you do not fully recognize, and "
"make your way to the bridge. The entire ship is oddly quiet as you pass "
"through, with no signs of life. You reach the bridge and find the ship's "
"systems have just enough energy left to power up, letting you jack in."
msgstr ""
"Entras en el derelicto, que es de una marca que no reconoces del todo, y te "
"diriges al puente. Toda la nave está extrañamente silenciosa mientras la "
"atraviesas, sin señales de vida. Llegas al puente y descubres que a los "
"sistemas de la nave les queda la energía suficiente para encenderse, lo que "
"te permite conectarte."

msgid ""
"The ship's systems list only one item of interest in the manifest: a press "
"guidelines document."
msgstr ""
"Los sistemas de la nave sólo incluyen un elemento de interés en el "
"manifiesto: un documento de directrices de prensa."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Curious, you check out the hold. There are many copies of an old, "
"desiccated, and crumbling paper file. Who uses paper these days? Is this a "
"pre-warp ship or something?"
msgstr ""
"Curioso, echa un vistazo a la bodega. Hay muchas copias de un viejo "
"expediente de papel reseco y desmenuzado. ¿Quién usa papel hoy en día? ¿Es "
"una nave pre-warp o algo así?"

msgid ""
"The document seems to have been typeset in an old format loved by the "
"Za'lek, called LaTeX. Sadly, the long exposure to the light has faded the "
"first page beyond all recognition. You decide to read the rest of the text, "
"which is still legible, if in poor condition."
msgstr ""
"El documento parece haber sido escrito en un viejo formato muy apreciado por "
"los Za'lek, llamado LaTeX. Lamentablemente, la larga exposición a la luz ha "
"descolorido la primera página hasta hacerla irreconocible. Decides leer el "
"resto del texto, que sigue siendo legible, aunque en mal estado."

#. LaTeX does not specify a format, but the future has likely moved past LaTeX, which is retained in idioms like this one. (Typeset like LaTeX i.e. formally)
msgid ""
"Point 1:\n"
"         It is necessary to state and imply in all publications including "
"but not limited to articles, reports and papers that the State is as right "
"as possible. This statement does NOT mean that the State always makes the "
"right decisions. The State merely makes the best decisions based on the "
"known information, but there is no guarantee that that represents all the "
"pertinent information."
msgstr ""
"Punto 1:\n"
"                   Es necesario afirmar e insinuar en todas las "
"publicaciones, incluidos, entre otros, artículos, informes y documentos, que "
"el Estado tiene toda la razón posible. Esta afirmación NO significa que el "
"Estado tome siempre las decisiones correctas. El Estado simplemente toma las "
"mejores decisiones basándose en la información conocida, pero no hay "
"garantía de que eso represente toda la información pertinente."

msgid ""
"Point 2:\n"
"         This of course begs the question: What to do when the State "
"declares a decision as an error? Such decisions are invariably the fault of "
"the individuals in charge, who will be disciplined for their failures. As "
"such, failures must be represented as the failures of individuals."
msgstr ""
"Punto 2:\n"
"                    Por supuesto, esto plantea la pregunta: ¿Qué hacer "
"cuando el Estado declara que una decisión es un error? Tales decisiones son "
"invariablemente culpa de los individuos a cargo, que serán disciplinados por "
"sus fallos. Como tales, los fallos deben representarse como fallos de los "
"individuos."

msgid ""
"Point 3:\n"
"         Following the same principle of State power not resting in "
"individual hands, when a decision is not officially made, it is meaningless "
"to state that one side is right. Instead of taking such sides, a reporter "
"must strive instead to highlight the environment that ensures that the "
"decisions are made by those who are best equipped and qualified to make them."
msgstr ""
"Punto 3:\n"
"                   Siguiendo el mismo principio de que el poder del Estado "
"no descansa en manos individuales, cuando una decisión no está tomada "
"oficialmente, carece de sentido afirmar que una de las partes tiene razón. "
"En lugar de tomar partido por uno de los bandos, el periodista debe "
"esforzarse por poner de relieve el entorno que garantiza que las decisiones "
"las toman quienes están mejor preparados y cualificados para tomarlas."

msgid ""
"Point 4:\n"
"         For this very reason, it is mandatory to highlight the role of the "
"State in any success. For the people to have faith in the State, they must "
"know that it may err, but never is it in error."
msgstr ""
"Punto 4:\n"
"                   Por esta misma razón, es obligatorio destacar el papel "
"del Estado en cualquier éxito. Para que el pueblo tenga fe en el Estado, "
"debe saber que puede equivocarse, pero que nunca se equivoca."

msgid ""
"Point 5:\n"
"         In the interest of keeping the State safe and secure from threats "
"from within and without, it is thus necessary to mention all people who "
"deviate from the above guidelines as dangerous dissidents in all current and "
"future publications such as those listed in (1) and to correct previous "
"articles to follow the same."
msgstr ""
"Punto 5:\n"
"                    En interés de mantener el Estado a salvo y seguro de las "
"amenazas de dentro y de fuera, es por tanto necesario mencionar a todas las "
"personas que se desvíen de las directrices anteriores como disidentes "
"peligrosos en todas las publicaciones actuales y futuras como las enumeradas "
"en (1) y corregir los artículos anteriores para seguir lo mismo."

msgid ""
"Point 6:\n"
"         If a dissident is quoted, which may only be done during their "
"trial, this dissident opinion must be countered by an immediately following "
"government opinion of equal or greater size."
msgstr ""
"Punto 6:\n"
"                   Si se cita a un disidente, lo que sólo puede hacerse "
"durante su juicio, esta opinión disidente debe ser contrarrestada por una "
"opinión gubernamental inmediatamente posterior de igual o mayor tamaño."

msgid ""
"Point 7:\n"
"         Failure to follow any of the guidelines listed here is grounds for "
"arrest, trial and summary execution."
msgstr ""
"Punto 7:\n"
"                   El incumplimiento de cualquiera de las directrices aquí "
"enumeradas es motivo de detención, juicio y ejecución sumaria."

msgid "Long live the Sov...n Pr...n A...chy!"
msgstr "¡Larga vida a la A...quía Pr..n Sob...a!"

msgid ""
"Some text on that last page was illegible, and the logo following it was "
"indecipherable. Still, a curious document. You wonder who could have made it."
msgstr ""
"Parte del texto de la última página era ilegible, y el logotipo que le "
"seguía era indescifrable. Aun así, es un documento curioso. Uno se pregunta "
"quién pudo haberlo hecho."

msgid ""
"You suspect this might be a document of the Sovereign Proteron Autarchy, "
"given their reputation for autocracy."
msgstr ""
"Sospechas que podría tratarse de un documento de la Autarquía Proteron "
"Soberana, dada su reputación de autocracia."

msgid ""
"\"I wonder... these ship systems are highly sophisticated, possibly even "
"more than mine... It seems strangely familiar.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Me pregunto... estos sistemas de la nave son muy sofisticados, "
"posiblemente incluso más que los míos... Parece extrañamente familiar.\""

msgid "\"I bet it was the voices!\""
msgstr "\"¡Apuesto a que fueron las voces!\""

msgid "\"What voices?!!\""
msgstr "\"¡¡¿Qué voces?!!\""

msgid ""
"\"Oh, just the voices in my head that tell me what to do. Right now they're "
"asking me to cover up the find by exploding both ships!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oh, sólo las voces en mi cabeza que me dicen qué hacer. ¡Ahora mismo me "
"piden que cubra el hallazgo haciendo explotar ambas naves!\""

msgid "\"3...\""
msgstr "\"3...\""

msgid "\"2...\""
msgstr "\"2...\""

msgid "\"1...\""
msgstr "\"1...\""

msgid "\"Haha, just my little joke!\""
msgstr "\"Jaja, ¡sólo era mi pequeña broma!\""

msgid ""
"\"Anyway, I don't see anything else of importance on this ship! Let's go "
"quickly.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡De todos modos, no veo nada más de importancia en esta nave! Vámonos "
"rápido.\""

msgid ""
"Despite what {shipai} says (or perhaps because of it), you explore the ship "
"and find {reward}, which isn't listed on the manifest, though you suppose "
"that's par for the record with encrypted items."
msgstr ""
"A pesar de lo que dice {shipai} (o tal vez debido a ello), exploras la nave "
"y encuentras {reward}, que no aparece en el manifiesto, aunque supones que "
"eso es normal con los objetos encriptados."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You found a derelict ship in the {sys} system with a desiccated copy of some "
"press guidelines. You also were able to recover {reward} from the ship."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una nave abandonada en el sistema {sys} con una copia "
"disecada de unas directrices de prensa. También has podido recuperar "
"{reward} de la nave."

#. Must be locked
#. Must know data matrices
#. Already finished
#. Determine type of derelict based on mission number
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"Curious. This derelict is a particularly ancient one, my records date this "
"model as having become obsolete almost 50 Cycles ago. It has sustained "
"significant battle damage, but most of the interior compartments are still "
"pressurized.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Curioso. Este derelicto es particularmente antiguo, mis registros datan "
"que este modelo quedó obsoleto hace casi 50 Ciclos. Ha sufrido importantes "
"daños en batalla, pero la mayoría de los compartimentos interiores siguen "
"presurizados.\""

msgid ""
"The airlock opens with a hiss of stale, dusty air. From what you know of "
"this wreck, you're not surprised when the smell hits you. It's exactly what "
"you'd expect from a 50-cycle-old ship."
msgstr ""
"La esclusa se abre con un silbido de aire viciado y polvoriento. Por lo que "
"sabes de este naufragio, no te sorprende el olor. Es exactamente lo que "
"cabría esperar de una nave de 50 ciclos de antigüedad."

msgid ""
"A quick exploration of the ship reveals that its systems are mostly "
"operational, but the engines are dead, and the cargo hold is full of nothing "
"but spoiled liquor. You do however recover an age-weathered notebook from "
"the crew quarters. You flip carefully through the few legible entries on "
"your way back to the bridge."
msgstr ""
"Una rápida exploración de la nave revela que sus sistemas son operativos en "
"su mayor parte, pero los motores están muertos y la bodega de carga está "
"llena de licor estropeado. Sin embargo, recuperas un viejo cuaderno de notas "
"de las dependencias de la tripulación. De vuelta al puente, hojeas con "
"cuidado las pocas anotaciones legibles."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 548:3851\n"
"No luck today either. Lark told me this spot was like a buffet line of "
"traders, he didn't mention that's because they're all travelling together! "
"Transports or no, the big lugs they've got with em are more turret than "
"ship, and all the little fish just swarm around them. Damn cattle travelling "
"in herds, best we can do is pick off a straggler here or there. There must "
"be an easier way to make a living."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del capitán, UST 548:3851\n"
"Hoy tampoco ha habido suerte. Lark me dijo que este lugar era como un bufé "
"de comerciantes, ¡pero no mencionó que es porque viajan todos juntos! Con o "
"sin transportes, los grandes bultos que llevan son más torretas que naves, y "
"todos los pececillos se arremolinan a su alrededor. Maldito ganado viajando "
"en manadas, lo mejor que podemos hacer es coger un rezagado aquí o allá. "
"Debe haber una forma más fácil de ganarse la vida."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 548:3889\n"
"Become a pirate they said. Riches and infamy they said. Well we've been "
"sitting out here for the devil knows how many periods now, and we've barely "
"got 10k to show for it! It's not just the convoys, oh no that'd be bad "
"enough, but now a couple gangs have moved into the area, and they're "
"snapping up what few stragglers there were! If this keeps up, we won't even "
"be able to keep the ship running much longer."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del Capitán, UST 548:3889\n"
"Conviértete en pirata dijeron. Riqueza e infamia dijeron. ¡Bueno, hemos "
"estado sentados aquí por el diablo sabe cuántos períodos ahora, y apenas "
"tenemos 10k para demostrarlo! No son solo las caravanas, eso ya es bastante "
"malo, ¡pero ahora un par de bandas se han trasladado a la zona y están "
"acabando con los pocos rezagados que quedaban! Si esto sigue así, ni "
"siquiera vamos a ser capaces de mantener la nave en funcionamiento mucho más "
"tiempo."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 548:3953\n"
"That's torn it. Some hotshot got a lucky torp through our shields, now our "
"left retroburner's busted, and we can barely manage 50 clicks a second. I "
"guess I should be grateful it didn't blow a hole in the hull instead. Even "
"if we manage to limp back to a station, I don't know if we have enough for "
"repairs.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe we should take that Rackham guy up on his offer after all. Sure sounds "
"like a better deal than drifting in space forever. I just hope the old girl "
"still has enough life in her to get us there."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del capitán, UST 548:3953\n"
"Se ha roto. Algún fanfarrón ha lanzado un torpedor afortunado a través de "
"nuestros escudos, ahora nuestro retroquemador izquierdo está roto, y apenas "
"podemos hacer 50 clicks por segundo. Supongo que debería estar agradecido de "
"que no haya hecho un agujero en el casco. Incluso si nos las arreglamos para "
"volver a una estación, no sé si tenemos suficiente para las reparaciones.\n"
"\n"
"Tal vez deberíamos aceptar la oferta de Rackham después de todo. Suena como "
"un mejor trato que ir a la deriva en el espacio para siempre. Sólo espero "
"que la vieja chica todavía tenga suficiente vida en ella para llevarnos allí."

msgid ""
"Reaching the bridge, you access the ship's systems and manage to extract "
"{reward}. You then return to your ship with the data, pondering the "
"unfortunate tale of these would-be pirates. Who exactly was this mysterious "
"'Rackham' they mentioned?\n"
"\n"
"{rewardmsg}"
msgstr ""
"Al llegar al puente, accedes a los sistemas de la nave y consigues extraer "
"la {reward}. A continuación, regresas a tu nave con los datos, reflexionando "
"sobre la desafortunada historia de estos aspirantes a piratas. ¿Quién era "
"exactamente este misterioso \"Rackham El Rojo\" que mencionaron?\n"
"\n"
"{rewardmsg}"

msgid ""
"A quick exploration of the ship reveals that most of its systems are "
"completely dead, only the lights and basic life support remaining online "
"after all this time. You eventually reach the crew quarters, but find "
"nothing besides an age-weathered notebook. You flip carefully through it on "
"your way towards the cargo hold, and a few entries catch your interest in "
"particular."
msgstr ""
"Una rápida exploración de la nave revela que la mayoría de sus sistemas "
"están completamente muertos, sólo las luces y el soporte vital básico "
"permanecen en línea después de todo este tiempo. Al final llegas a las "
"dependencias de la tripulación, pero no encuentras nada más que un viejo "
"cuaderno de notas. Lo hojeas con cuidado de camino a la bodega de carga, y "
"algunas anotaciones te llaman especialmente la atención."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:1348\n"
"Another Empire patrol spotted us today, but the wolf pack chased them off. I "
"couldn't help but laugh seeing them falling over themselves trying to get "
"away once they realized how many of us there were! I tell you, it was a "
"thing of beauty. Running into a patrol that size used to keep me up at "
"night, but now I guess the shoe's on the other foot. I swear, signing up "
"with Red Rackham's unit was the best damn decision I ever made."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del Capitán, UST 551:1348\n"
"Hoy nos ha visto otra patrulla del Imperio, pero la manada de lobos los ha "
"ahuyentado. No pude evitar reírme al verlos caer sobre sí mismos intentando "
"huir cuando se dieron cuenta de cuántos éramos. En serio, fue un "
"espectáculo. Toparme con una patrulla de ese tamaño solía quitarme el sueño, "
"pero ahora supongo que el zapato está en el otro pie. Lo juro, alistarme en "
"la unidad de Rackham El Rojo fue la mejor maldita decisión que he tomado."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:1372\n"
"Couldn't help myself. There was a big, fat, juicy Mule right there, almost "
"begging to get boarded! My boys haven't had a good firefight in a while, so "
"I ordered the all ahead and guess what we find? They were carrying "
"practically a full hold of nickel! Talk about a score! Must've been on their "
"way back from a mining gig or something. Either way, boss is gonna be "
"thrilled. This'll go a long way towards that crazy project of his."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del capitán, UST 551:1372\n"
"No pude evitarlo. Había una mula grande, gorda y jugosa justo ahí, ¡casi "
"suplicando ser abordada! Mis muchachos no habían tenido un buen tiroteo en "
"mucho tiempo, así que ordené que se adelantaran y ¿adivinen qué encontramos? "
"¡Llevaban prácticamente una bodega llena de níquel! ¡Hablando de un golpe! "
"Deben haber vuelto de un trabajo de minería o algo así. De cualquier manera, "
"el jefe va a estar encantado. Esto ayudará mucho a su proyecto loco."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:1525\n"
"I swear, I thought the boss might've had a few screws loose at first. I "
"mean, who would go to all this trouble gathering supplies just to build "
"their own ship? But I saw it docked at the station today. The damn thing is "
"massive! I don't know how the hell he came up with something like that, but "
"I guess I shouldn't be surprised, he is the boss after all.\n"
"\n"
"Makes me wonder though. One of my boys said the name 'Red Rackham' came from "
"some old Earth story, but if that's not his real name then who exactly is he?"
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del Capitán, UST 551:1525\n"
"Lo juro, al principio pensé que al jefe le faltaban algunos tornillos. "
"Quiero decir, ¿quién se tomaría la molestia de reunir suministros sólo para "
"construir su propia nave? Pero hoy la vi atracada en la estación. ¡La "
"maldita cosa es enorme! No sé cómo demonios se le ocurrió algo así, pero "
"supongo que no debería sorprenderme, él es el jefe después de todo.\n"
"\n"
"Aunque me hace pensar. Uno de mis chicos dijo que el nombre 'Rackham El "
"Rojo' vino de alguna vieja historia de la Tierra, pero si ese no es su "
"verdadero nombre, entonces ¿quién es exactamente?"

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:3701\n"
"Damn it. I can't believe it, it just isn't possible. The boss can't just be "
"gone, right? There's no way that massive ship of his could've been taken "
"down, but the boys are saying he hasn't been seen in almost 200 periods. He "
"just disappeared without a trace. There are rumours that his last message "
"was about ambushing some trader convoy full of gold, but the higher ups are "
"refusing to tell us anything. Some people think they're trying to hoard the "
"treasure for themselves.\n"
"\n"
"If this keeps up, the clan is going to tear itself apart. I think it's time "
"to get out while we're ahead, but maybe we can 'borrow' some supplies before "
"we go."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del Capitán, UST 551:3701\n"
"Maldita sea. No puedo creerlo, no es posible. El jefe no puede haber "
"desaparecido, ¿verdad? No hay forma de que su enorme nave haya sido "
"derribada, pero los chicos dicen que no se le ha visto en casi 200 periodos. "
"Simplemente desapareció sin dejar rastro. Hay rumores de que su último "
"mensaje fue sobre una emboscada a alguna caravana de comerciantes lleno de "
"oro, pero los altos mandos se niegan a decirnos nada. Algunos creen que "
"intenta acaparar el tesoro para sí mismo.\n"
"\n"
"Si esto sigue así, el clan se va a romper en pedazos. Creo que es hora de "
"salir mientras estemos por delante, pero tal vez podamos \"tomar prestadas\" "
"algunas provisiones antes de irnos."

msgid ""
"As you finish reading and arrive at the ship's cargo hold, you realize it's "
"full of crudely scavenged, but functional {reward}. You load up as much as "
"you can, pondering what you've learned about Red Rackham. You wonder, how "
"could such a dangerous pirate just disappear without a trace?"
msgstr ""
"Cuando terminas de leer y llegas a la bodega de carga de la nave, te das "
"cuenta de que está llena de {reward} toscamente rebuscadas, pero "
"funcionales. Cargas todo lo que puedes, reflexionando sobre lo que has "
"aprendido sobre Rackham El Rojo. Te preguntas, ¿cómo pudo un pirata tan "
"peligroso desaparecer sin dejar rastro?"

msgid ""
"As you explore the dimly lit interior of the ship, you quickly realize that "
"the crew clearly never escaped. The withered skeletons make for a haunting "
"experience as you wander the halls of the floating graveyard. Despite the "
"chills creeping up your spine however you note that, scattered among the "
"plain grey uniforms of the crew, there are more than a few skeletons with "
"the skull-and-crossbones on their jackets."
msgstr ""
"A medida que exploras el interior poco iluminado de la nave, te das cuenta "
"rápidamente de que, evidentemente, la tripulación nunca escapó. Los "
"esqueletos marchitos hacen que la experiencia sea inquietante mientras "
"deambulas por los pasillos del cementerio flotante. A pesar de los "
"escalofríos que te recorren la espalda, te das cuenta de que, entre los "
"uniformes grises de la tripulación, hay más de un esqueleto con la calavera "
"y los huesos cruzados en sus chaquetas."

msgid ""
"Your search of the ship eventually leads you to the ship's core systems, "
"which you quickly realize was the site of some sort of explosion. The entire "
"mainframe is fried beyond repair, leaving only the emergency lights and life "
"support online. You also notice two charred skeletons nearby, whose half-"
"burnt clothes mark the first as the captain of the ship, and the second as "
"the leader of the pirates who had boarded it."
msgstr ""
"Tu búsqueda de la nave te lleva finalmente a los sistemas base de la nave, "
"que rápidamente te das cuenta de que fue el lugar donde se produjo algún "
"tipo de explosión. Todo el ordenador central está frito, sin posibilidad de "
"reparación, y sólo queda en funcionamiento el sistema de luces de emergencia "
"y el soporte vital. También te fijas en dos esqueletos carbonizados "
"cercanos, cuyas ropas medio quemadas señalan al primero como el capitán de "
"la nave, y al segundo como el líder de los piratas que la habían abordado."

msgid ""
"You quickly search the room, and discover evidence of a fight between the "
"captain and the pirate. Blaster burns pockmark the walls, and the captain's "
"uniform is covered in bloodstained slashes. You note with some curiosity "
"that the pirate seemed to have been using a curved, nanosteel sabre instead "
"of a blaster. You pick up the dusty blade and note its excellent "
"craftsmanship. With the ornate engravings covering the blade, the sword is "
"as much a work of art as it is a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Registras rápidamente la habitación y descubres pruebas de una pelea entre "
"el capitán y el pirata. Las quemaduras de blaster marcan las paredes y el "
"uniforme del capitán está cubierto de tajos manchados de sangre. Observas "
"con cierta curiosidad que el pirata parece haber utilizado un sable curvo de "
"nanoacero en lugar de un bláster. Recoges la hoja polvorienta y te fijas en "
"su excelente factura. Con los ornamentados grabados que cubren la hoja, la "
"espada es tanto una obra de arte como un arma."

msgid ""
"Despite the seemingly imbalanced weaponry at play, you can't tell for "
"certain who won the duel. Judging by the result it might be fair to say they "
"both lost. One thing is for certain though, a few blaster shots aren't "
"enough to explain the explosion which clearly took place here. You do find a "
"singed journal in the captain's pocket however, and start leafing through "
"the most recent entries."
msgstr ""
"A pesar del aparentemente desequilibrado armamento en juego, no se puede "
"decir con certeza quién ganó el duelo. A juzgar por el resultado, sería "
"justo decir que ambos perdieron. Una cosa es segura, unos pocos disparos de "
"blaster no son suficientes para explicar la explosión que tuvo lugar aquí. "
"Sin embargo, encuentras un diario chamuscado en el bolsillo del capitán, y "
"empiezas a hojear las entradas más recientes."

#. codespell:ignore singed
msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:3480\n"
"This route has been getting more dangerous of late, the pirates are more "
"bold than ever. It's no surprise, considering the significant fortune we've "
"been carving from the asteroids, but I've also heard talk of some great, "
"charismatic pirate leader by the name of Red Rackham. Supposedly none have "
"seen his ship and lived to tell the tale. Personally, I put little stock in "
"tall tales of immortal pirates. What I do trust are my ship, and my men. Any "
"pirate foolish enough to take us lightly will have a rude awakening indeed."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del capitán, UST 551:3480\n"
"Esta ruta se ha vuelto más peligrosa últimamente, los piratas son más "
"audaces que nunca. No es de extrañar, teniendo en cuenta la importante "
"fortuna que hemos estado labrando con los asteroides, pero también he oído "
"hablar de un gran y carismático líder pirata llamado Rackham El Rojo. "
"Supuestamente nadie ha visto su nave y ha vivido para contarlo. "
"Personalmente, confío poco en los cuentos de piratas inmortales. En lo que "
"sí confío es en mi nave y en mis hombres. Cualquier pirata tan tonto como "
"para tomarnos a la ligera tendrá un duro despertar."

msgid ""
"Captain's log, UST 551:3508\n"
"It isn't just the pirates who keep swarming around us unbidden. The "
"merchantmen are spooked, and they've taken to hiding under the shadow of a "
"bigger fish. Another half dozen joined up with us in the last period alone! "
"No doubt they hope that in the event of a pirate attack, the slowest vessel "
"will be left behind as a sacrifice. Particularly since that vessel, namely "
"mine, is hauling such an appetizing cargo. I almost hope pirates do attack, "
"if only so that I can show those cowards what a real trader looks like."
msgstr ""
"Bitácora del capitán, UST 551:3508\n"
"No son sólo los piratas los que siguen pululando a nuestro alrededor sin "
"avisar. Los mercantes están asustados y se han escondido a la sombra de un "
"pez más gordo. Sólo en el último periodo se han unido a nosotros media "
"docena más. Sin duda esperan que, en caso de ataque pirata, la nave más "
"lenta se quede atrás como sacrificio. Sobre todo porque esa nave, la mía, "
"lleva una carga tan apetitosa. Casi espero que los piratas ataquen, aunque "
"sólo sea para poder mostrar a esos cobardes cómo es un verdadero comerciante."

msgid ""
"Final log, UST 551:3517\n"
"Red Rackham is here. He jumped out of hyperspace right beside us somehow and "
"opened fire. His ship was like nothing I've ever seen before, maybe like "
"nothing else that's ever been built. The merchantmen scattered, but it "
"seemed like he wasn't planning on letting any of them go. They drew enough "
"of his fire for my crew to bring his shields down before he realized what "
"was happening. I saw one of his engines explode right before he disabled us. "
"We must have hit something critical, because the next thing we knew we were "
"getting boarded by fighters.\n"
"\n"
"They've taken over entire ship now, with Rackham himself leading the charge. "
"He only left enough of us alive to make up his missing crew, no doubt he's "
"planning to commandeer the ship and make us fly it back to some pirate "
"station. After that though, they won't need us any more. All I have is my "
"blaster and one thermal detonator. If I am to die, then on my honour as "
"captain I swear I will take Red Rackham with me."
msgstr ""
"Registro final, UST 551:3517\n"
"Rackham El Rojo está aquí. Salió del hiperespacio justo a nuestro lado y "
"abrió fuego. Su nave no se parecía a nada que hubiera visto antes, quizá a "
"nada que se hubiera construido jamás. Los mercantes se dispersaron, pero "
"parecía que no planeaba dejar ir a ninguno de ellos. Atrajeron suficiente "
"fuego como para que mi tripulación derribara sus escudos antes de que se "
"diera cuenta de lo que estaba pasando. Vi explotar uno de sus motores justo "
"antes de que nos incapacitara. Debemos haber alcanzado algo crítico, porque "
"lo siguiente que supimos es que estábamos siendo abordados por cazas.\n"
"\n"
"Se han apoderado de toda la nave ahora, con el propio Rackham liderando la "
"carga. Sólo nos dejó con vida a los suficientes para completar su "
"tripulación, sin duda está planeando requisar la nave y hacernos volar de "
"vuelta a alguna estación pirata. Después de eso, no nos necesitarán más. "
"Todo lo que tengo es mi blaster y un detonador térmico. Si voy a morir, juro "
"por mi honor de capitán que me llevaré a Rackham El Rojo conmigo."

msgid ""
"You carefully pocket the captain's notebook, your hands shaking in "
"anticipation, then head to the cargo hold. Sure enough, you're greeted by "
"hundreds of tons of pure {reward}, a sizeable haul even by modern standards. "
"You load up as much as you can and then head back to your ship, pondering "
"the unlikely end to this strange treasure hunt. It's only as you settle into "
"your chair that you realize {reward2} is still in your hand. As you gaze at "
"your reflection in the ornately engraved blade, you wonder idly if your name "
"will show up some day in the legend of Red Rackham's treasure."
msgstr ""
"Guardas con cuidado el cuaderno del capitán, con las manos temblorosas por "
"la expectación, y te diriges a la bodega de carga. En efecto, le esperan "
"cientos de toneladas de pura {reward}, un botín considerable incluso para "
"los estándares modernos. Cargas todo lo que puedes y vuelves a tu nave, "
"pensando en el improbable final de esta extraña búsqueda del tesoro. Cuando "
"te acomodas en la silla, te das cuenta de que la {reward2} sigue en tu mano. "
"Mientras contemplas tu reflejo en la hoja ornamentada, te preguntas si tu "
"nombre aparecerá algún día en la leyenda del tesoro de Rackham El Rojo."

#. Set up cargo for 2nd and 3rd mission
msgid "You have received #g{amount} of {reward}#0."
msgstr "Has recibido #g{amount} de {reward}#0."

#, fuzzy
msgid "You are unable to fit any {reward} on your ship."
msgstr "Vuelves a tu nave."

msgid ""
"You found an old derelict pirate ship in the {sys} system and were able to "
"recover {reward}."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una vieja nave pirata abandonada en el sistema {sys} y has "
"podido recuperar {reward}."

msgid ""
"You found an old derelict pirate ship in the {sys} system and were able to "
"recover {reward}, and also {reward2}."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una vieja nave pirata abandonada en el sistema {sys} y has "
"podido recuperar {reward}, y también {reward2}."

#. Already done
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the system.\n"
"\"This is strange. What is a dead bioship doing out here? Let me see if I "
"can access the systems.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema.\n"
"\"Esto es extraño. ¿Qué hace una bionave muerta aquí? Déjame ver si puedo "
"acceder a los sistemas.\""

msgid ""
"After a long pause.\n"
"\"I'm afraid that it seems like the systems are completely dead. I don't "
"think we'll be able to obtain any information from this ship. You might as "
"well explore it before we leave.\""
msgstr ""
"Tras una larga pausa.\n"
"\"Me temo que parece que los sistemas están completamente muertos. No creo "
"que podamos obtener ninguna información de esta nave. Será mejor que la "
"explore antes de irme.\""

msgid ""
"You start exploring the ship, which seems to be fitted as some sort of "
"science vessel. Eventually, you stumble across what seems to be a dormitory. "
"You find that there seems to be a notebook left on the table. You begin to "
"read it."
msgstr ""
"Empiezas a explorar la nave, que parece estar equipada como una especie de "
"nave científica. Finalmente, tropiezas con lo que parece ser un dormitorio. "
"Descubres que parece haber un cuaderno de notas sobre la mesa. Comienzas a "
"leerlo."

#. Game starts at 603:3726.2871
msgid ""
"UST 600:4967\n"
"\n"
"I found an interesting rumour today while visiting the bar at Neurri. I was "
"told that, although most bioships are completely domesticated, with little "
"in the ways of autonomy and higher level cognition, it seems like this is "
"not always the case. Sometimes the bioships can end up too smart for their "
"own good. What happens to them depends on the tribe in this case, but it is "
"not uncommon for them to go missing. This is very interesting and could be "
"related to my research. I am going to try to see if I can find any more "
"information on the topic."
msgstr ""
"UST 600:4967\n"
"\n"
"Hoy he encontrado un rumor interesante mientras visitaba el bar de Neurri. "
"Me han contado que, aunque la mayoría de las bionaves están completamente "
"domesticadas, con poca autonomía y cognición de nivel superior, parece que "
"no siempre es así. Algunas veces las bionaves pueden terminar siendo "
"demasiado inteligentes para su propio bien. Lo que les ocurre depende de la "
"tribu en este caso, pero no es raro que desaparezcan. Esto es muy "
"interesante y podría estar relacionado con mi investigación. Voy a intentar "
"ver si encuentro más información sobre el tema."

msgid ""
"UST 600:4983\n"
"\n"
"After fruitless leads, I have arrived to Silverstone in the Symm system and "
"have been talking with the bioship producers. They seem to reject the notion "
"of \"feral\" bioships. I was almost about to call it quits and return home, "
"when I managed to talk to a younger employee who sees to confirm my "
"suspicions. Indeed, although rare, sometimes random mutations in the DNA can "
"lead to not fully controllable bioships. They swear that they are as cunning "
"and intelligent as humans. The future of such ships is uncertain, but they "
"can be taken away or escape. However, only the tribe elders deal with such "
"bioships. It seems like most head towards the Haze, and that is the next "
"place I must travel to. For this trip I will leave behind my trusty Koala "
"and go with a Soromid Brigand. This may arouse less suspicion should I "
"happen upon feral bioships."
msgstr ""
"UST 600:4983\n"
"\n"
"Tras infructuosas pistas, he llegado a Piedraplateada, en el sistema Symm, y "
"he estado hablando con los productores de bionaves. Parece que rechazan la "
"idea de las bionaves \"salvajes\". Estaba a punto de darlo por terminado y "
"volver a casa, cuando conseguí hablar con un empleado más joven que parece "
"confirmar mis sospechas. Efectivamente, aunque es raro, algunas veces las "
"mutaciones aleatorias en el ADN pueden dar lugar a bionaves no totalmente "
"controlables. Asegura que son tan astutas e inteligentes como los humanos. "
"El futuro de estas naves es incierto, pero pueden ser retiradas o escapar. "
"Sin embargo, sólo los ancianos de la tribu se ocupan de esas naves "
"biológicas. Parece que la mayoría se dirigen hacia la Neblina, y ese es el "
"siguiente lugar al que debo viajar. Para este viaje dejaré atrás a mi fiel "
"Koala e iré con un Forajido Sorómida. Esto puede despertar menos sospechas "
"en caso de que me encuentre con bionaves salvajes."

msgid ""
"UST 601:0005\n"
"\n"
"I have left the Hasselt system and head towards the depth of the Haze "
"following rumours of a nearby colony of feral bioships. Who knows what I "
"shall find? I have not been so giddy with anticipation in ages. Despite "
"having conquered space, there is still much left for humankind to find!"
msgstr ""
"UST 601:0005\n"
"\n"
"He abandonado el sistema Hasselt y me dirijo hacia las profundidades de la "
"Neblina siguiendo los rumores de una colonia cercana de bionaves salvajes. "
"¿Quién sabe lo que encontraré? Hacía tiempo que no me sentía tan ilusionado. "
"A pesar de haber conquistado el espacio, ¡todavía queda mucho por encontrar "
"para la humanidad!"

msgid ""
"UST 601:0037\n"
"\n"
"There seems to be no signs of life in this haze. I have been reflecting on "
"my task. Perhaps it is a fool's errand after all?"
msgstr ""
"UST 601:0037\n"
"\n"
"Parece que no hay señales de vida en esta neblina. He estado reflexionando "
"sobre mi tarea. ¿Quizás sea una tarea de tontos después de todo?"

msgid ""
"UST 601:0072\n"
"\n"
"My supplies are running a bit thin. It may be hallucinations, but I believe "
"I have seen a few blips on the scanners in the past days. Could these be the "
"ferals?"
msgstr ""
"UST 601:0072\n"
"\n"
"Mis suministros se están agotando. Puede que sean alucinaciones, pero creo "
"que he visto algunos puntos en los escáneres en los últimos días. ¿Podrían "
"ser las salvajes?"

msgid ""
"UST 601:0089\n"
"\n"
"I have been working on a plan. I have been able to localize the different "
"anatomical parts of my bioship. If I can extract pheromones, it may be "
"possible to attract the ferals. This is my last chance."
msgstr ""
"UST 601:0089\n"
"\n"
"He estado trabajando en un plan. He sido capaz de localizar las diferentes "
"partes anatómicas de mi bionave. Si puedo extraer feromonas, podría ser "
"posible atraer a las salvajes. Esta es mi última oportunidad."

msgid ""
"UST 601:0101\n"
"\n"
"I believe I have completed the pheromone extractor. The smell is… let us say "
"not very pleasant. I will put it to use right away."
msgstr ""
"UST 601:0101\n"
"\n"
"Creo que he completado el extractor de feromonas. El olor es... digamos que "
"no muy agradable. Lo pondré en práctica de inmediato."

msgid "The rest of the pages are blank."
msgstr "El resto de las páginas están en blanco."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You ask {shipai} to perform an in-depth scan for biological signals, and "
"surprisingly enough, find a faint signal that differs from the desiccated "
"biological material of the ship. You go to inspect it and the first thing "
"you find is that it stinks. A quick analysis seems to indicate that this is "
"the pheromone extractor mentioned in the notebook. You carefully take it "
"aboard your ship."
msgstr ""
"Pides a {shipai} que realice un escaneo en profundidad en busca de señales "
"biológicas y, sorprendentemente, encuentras una débil señal que difiere del "
"material biológico desecado de la nave. Vas a inspeccionarla y lo primero "
"que encuentras es que apesta. Un rápido análisis parece indicar que se trata "
"del extractor de feromonas mencionado en el cuaderno. Lo llevas con cuidado "
"a bordo de tu nave."

msgid ""
"You found a derelict bioship in {sys}. It belonged to a researcher searching "
"for \"feral\" bioships, and you found a {reward}."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una bionave derrelicto en {sys}. Pertenecía a un investigador "
"que buscaba bionaves \"salvajes\" y has encontrado una {reward}."

#. Must be locked
#. Must know data matrices
#. Must be "nearby"
#. Already done
#, fuzzy
msgid "Irradiated Derelict"
msgstr "Derrelicto Errie"

#. Much more likely if can appear
msgid ""
"You carefully enter the derelict while watching the radiation levels. They "
"same to be dangerously high, however, if you do not take too long, you do "
"not think it should be too dangerous for your HEV suit. Watching the "
"radiation readings, you warily head towards the command room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The inside of the ship is in horrible shape. There is junk and dirt "
"everywhere. You can see clear damage on the walls, and most of the airlocks "
"seem to be jammed open. While gliding through the hallway, something grabs "
"your foot, and you instinctively draw your weapon and fire. Once the sound "
"of your ricocheting noise diminishes, you are left with the sound of your "
"accelerated heartbeat."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You catch nothing else move as the ship is silent. With your adrenaline "
"fading, you poke at the object you shot with your foot, revealing a dirty "
"corpse. Seeing the state of mummification, you can only guess it was long "
"dead before you got here. The body is wearing what seems to be a bunch of "
"rags from some old space suit, you take a closer look when you notice the "
"eyes seem to be a faded shade of purple. Strange, maybe some Soromid biotech?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You make your way through the accumulated grime and debris without any "
"further surprises. Eventually you reach the command room. Quickly scanning "
"the room, you find 3 more corpses, all with the same purple eyes but "
"drastically different features. So much for the Soromid theory. You call on "
"{ainame} to perform a more in-depth scan and database lookup."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"\"There seem to be a total of 8 bodies on the ship. The purple eyes are "
"likely some sort of effect from the radiation they have received. Analysing "
"the radiation profile of the ship, it seems to be statistically correlated "
"with the Nebula volatility. I am trying to perform an analysis of the "
"systems, however, the firmware they seem to use is very outdated. It will "
"take a while to interface.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You check the rest of the bodies while {shipai} performs their analysis. "
"Yup, they all have purple eyes.}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You receive an alert that the analysis is done.\n"
"\"I was not able to recover too much other than {reward}, but there was some "
"information of an unknown jump near in the Nebula. I have updated your map "
"with it. It may be worth exploring, although I am not certain that it is "
"worth the risk to organic life.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It may be worth seeing the hidden to see what caused the fate of the ship. "
"You may want to double-check how hardened your ship is to radiation first "
"though."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You found an irradiated derelict ship in the {sys} system containing "
"information about a hidden jump in the Nebula. You also were able to recover "
"{reward} from the ship."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado una nave derelicto en el sistema {sys} con información "
"corrupta sobre un agente. También has podido recuperar {reward} de la nave."

#. Must be locked
#. Must be nebula or near nebula
#. Already done
msgid ""
"Your ship AI appears as you access the drone's systems.\n"
"\"How rare to see a Za'lek drone out here. It seems to have run out of "
"power. Let me inject a bit and see if I can reactivate the systems fully…\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave aparece cuando accedes al sistema del dron.\n"
"\"Qué raro es ver un dron Za'lek por aquí. Parece que se ha quedado sin "
"energía. Déjame inyectarle un poco y a ver si puedo reactivar los sistemas "
"completamente...\""

msgid "The light flickers a bit and the drone boots up in maintenance mode."
msgstr "La luz parpadea un poco y el dron arranca en modo de mantenimiento."

msgid ""
"\"I'm afraid this is the best I can do. I was able to find some logs. Let us "
"see them.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Me temo que esto es lo mejor que puedo hacer. Pude encontrar algunos "
"registros. Vamos a verlos.\""

msgid "BEGIN TEXT LOG"
msgstr "INICIO DEL REGISTRO DE TEXTO"

msgid ""
"SCOUT DRONE LOG UST 593:3726.5000\n"
"\n"
"DAMAGE REPORT.\n"
"PROPULSION SYSTEMS NON-FUNCTIONAL.\n"
"SHIELD GENERATOR UNRESPONSIVE.\n"
"SENSORS WORKING AT 70% EFFICIENCY.\n"
"NO FURTHER REPAIRS POSSIBLE."
msgstr ""
"REGISTRO DE DRON EXPLORADOR UST 593:3726.5000\n"
"\n"
"INFORME DE DAÑOS.\n"
"SISTEMAS DE PROPULSIÓN NO FUNCIONALES.\n"
"GENERADOR DE ESCUDOS NO RESPONDE.\n"
"SENSORES TRABAJANDO AL 70% DE EFICIENCIA.\n"
"NO ES POSIBLE REALIZAR MÁS REPARACIONES."

msgid ""
"CONTINUING ANALYSIS OF EVENT.\n"
"ENERGY EMITTED ESTIMATED TO BE 10e50 JOULES WITH MARGIN OF ERROR OF 10e51 "
"JOULES.\n"
"EPICENTRE ESTIMATED TO BE WITHIN 50 LIGHT YEARS OF THE POLARIS SYSTEM.\n"
"SURVIVABILITY WITHIN 500 LIGHT YEARS OF EPICENTRE ESTIMATED TO BE "
"0.00000000001%."
msgstr ""
"ANÁLISIS CONTINUO DEL EVENTO.\n"
"ENERGÍA EMITIDA ESTIMADA EN 10e50 JULIOS CON MARGEN DE ERROR DE 10e51 "
"JULIOS.\n"
"EPICENTRO ESTIMADO A MENOS 50 AÑOS LUZ DEL SISTEMA POLARIS.\n"
"LA SUPERVIVENCIA A 500 AÑOS LUZ DEL EPICENTRO SE ESTIMA EN UN 0,00000000001%."

msgid ""
"STRONG SUBSPACE ABNORMALITIES DETECTED. SPECIALIZED HARDWARE NECESSARY FOR "
"ANALYSIS.\n"
"DELTA WAVES RECEDING, 10 CYCLES EXPECTED FOR DECREASE TO MINIMUM LEVELS "
"NECESSARY FOR HUMAN SURVIVAL.\n"
"NO FURTHER ANALYSIS POSSIBLE WITH CURRENT HARDWARE. CONTINUING CURRENT "
"SURVEILLANCE."
msgstr ""
"FUERTES ANOMALÍAS SUBESPACIALES DETECTADAS. SE NECESITA HARDWARE "
"ESPECIALIZADO PARA EL ANÁLISIS.\n"
"LAS ONDAS DELTA RETROCEDEN, SE ESPERAN 10 CICLOS PARA QUE DISMINUYAN A LOS "
"NIVELES MÍNIMOS NECESARIOS PARA LA SUPERVIVENCIA HUMANA.\n"
"NO ES POSIBLE REALIZAR MÁS ANÁLISIS CON EL HARDWARE ACTUAL. CONTINUANDO LA "
"VIGILANCIA ACTUAL."

msgid "END TEXT LOG"
msgstr "FIN DEL REGISTRO DE TEXTO"

msgid ""
"The drone flickers once more and everything goes dark. It seems like that "
"was the last of the life that was in it. You run a last routine scan to see "
"if there is anything you can do. While it seems like the drone is sadly out "
"of order permanently, you find what seems to be an experimental piece of "
"hardware of Za'lek make attached to it. Seeing as it is no longer of use to "
"the drone, you take it with you."
msgstr ""
"El dron parpadea una vez más y todo se oscurece. Parece que eso fue lo que "
"quedaba de vida en él. Realizas un último escaneo de rutina para ver si hay "
"algo que puedas hacer. Aunque parece que el dron está lamentablemente fuera "
"de servicio de forma permanente, encuentras lo que parece ser una pieza "
"experimental de hardware de la marca Za'lek unida a él. Como ya no es útil "
"para el dron, te la llevas."

msgid ""
"You found a derelict Za'lek drone in the {sys} system. It contained "
"information about the Incident and you were able to loot a {reward} from it."
msgstr ""
"Has encontrado un dron Za'lek abandonado en el sistema {sys}. Contenía "
"información sobre el Incidente y pudiste obtener una {reward} de él."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Point of Interest - Intro">
#. <location>none</location>
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#.
#. Introduction to Point of Interest (Sensor Anomaly) missions.
#.
#. We assume it is started from a derelict event.
#.
#. 1. Follow NPC to sensor anomaly.
#. 2. NPC activates scanning outfit and is attacked by a bandit hyena.
#. 3. Destroy hyena and follow trails.
#. 4. Loot goal and get Pulse Scanner!
#.
#. --
#.
#. States
#. 0: Mission start, POI is marked
#. 1: Land and Nelly appears
#. 2: Fought off pirate
#. --
#. Must be claimable
#. Full claim here
#. Want no inhabited spobs
#. Not too hard
#. For Nelly, we don't want it to be too uninhabited
#. Try to get closer first, if not, allow more far away
#. Failed to start
#. We do a full claim on the final system
msgid ""
"You carefully explore the heavily damaged derelict. It looks like most of it "
"has been picked clean. You are about to give up when the system computer "
"suddenly flickers and seems to boot up."
msgstr ""
"Exploras cuidadosamente el derrelicto fuertemente dañado. Parece que la "
"mayor parte ha sido limpiada. Estás a punto de rendirte cuando el ordenador "
"del sistema parpadea de repente y parece arrancar."

msgid ""
"As the ship's operating system is starting, {shipai} materializes in front "
"of you."
msgstr ""
"Mientras se inicia el sistema operativo de la nave, {shipai} se materializa "
"frente a ti."

#. Worded to be a bit like the explosion messages in EVC
msgid ""
"\"While you were exploring I managed to bootstrap the ship's systems. No, "
"nothing bad could have happened. I estimated under 10% chance of triggering "
"the ship's security self-destruct mechanism and blowing up the ship. Oh…\""
msgstr ""
"\"Mientras estabas explorando me las arreglé para arrancar los sistemas de "
"la nave. No, no podría haber pasado nada malo. Estimé menos de un 10% de "
"posibilidades de activar el mecanismo de seguridad de autodestrucción y "
"hacer explotar la nave. Oh…\""

msgid ""
"\"Anyway, it seems like my work paid off, there seems to be some data "
"marking a sensor anomaly. Should I download the data so that we can explore "
"it?\""
msgstr ""
"\"De todos modos, parece que mi trabajo dio sus frutos, parece que hay "
"algunos datos que marcan una anomalía en los sensores. ¿Debería descargar "
"los datos para que podamos explorarla?\""

msgid ""
"\"Hey, it looks like there is data marking a sensor anomaly stored on the "
"ship computer. Should I download the data so that we can explore it?\""
msgstr ""
"\"Oye, parece que hay datos que marcan una anomalía en los sensores "
"almacenados en el ordenador de la nave. ¿Debería descargar los datos para "
"que podamos explorarla?\""

msgid ""
"{shipai} flickers slightly as they download the data.\n"
"\"It looks like the data points to a location in the nearby system of {sys}. "
"I have marked the location on your map. However, I'm not certain the ship's "
"current systems would allow it to follow such a faint hint. Maybe it would "
"be wise to land and see if we can improve our systems somehow.\""
msgstr ""
"{shipai} parpadea ligeramente mientras descarga los datos.\n"
"\"Parece que los datos apuntan a una ubicación en el sistema cercano de "
"{sys}. He marcado la ubicación en tu mapa. Sin embargo, no estoy seguro de "
"que los sistemas actuales de la nave te permitan seguir una pista tan débil. "
"Tal vez sería prudente aterrizar y ver si podemos mejorar nuestros sistemas "
"de alguna forma.\""

msgid ""
"{shipai} flickers slightly as they download the data.\n"
"\"It looks like the data points to a location in a nearby system. I have "
"marked the location on your map. However, I'm not certain the ship's current "
"systems would allow it to follow such a faint hint. Maybe it would be wise "
"to land and see if we can improve our systems somehow.\""
msgstr ""
"{shipai} parpadea ligeramente mientras descarga los datos.\n"
"\"Parece que los datos apuntan a una ubicación en un sistema cercano. He "
"marcado la ubicación en su mapa. Sin embargo, no estoy seguro de que los "
"sistemas actuales de la nave te permitan seguir una pista tan débil. Tal vez "
"sería prudente aterrizar y ver si podemos mejorar nuestros sistemas de "
"alguna manera.\""

msgid ""
"With nothing else to do on the derelict, you leave it behind, and return to "
"your ship."
msgstr ""
"Sin nada más que hacer en el derrelicto, lo dejas atrás y vuelves a tu nave."

msgid "You decide to leave the information alone and leave the derelict."
msgstr "Decides dejar la información en paz y abandonar el derrelicto."

#. We want to delay aborting the mission a frame so that the derelict
#. event thinks it's running fine
#. have to accept to use hook
#. Mission gets accepted in misnSetup
#. Clean up
#. Find the initial point of interest, and path to the real location
#. TODO have path be out of the way
#. TODO better initialization
#. should average 15*750 = 11250 units
#. --
#. Logs a point of interest message.
#. @tparam string msg Message to log.
#. --
msgid "Sensor Anomaly"
msgstr "Anomalía en el Sensor"

msgid "Improve your ship's systems"
msgstr "Mejora los sistemas de tu nave"

msgid "Head to the marked location"
msgstr "Dirígete a la localización marcada"

msgid ""
"\"It seems like the ship's sensors are not sufficient to analyse the sensor "
"anomaly. We'll need something better. The probability of off-the-shelf "
"outfits working is low, the most logical course of action might be to "
"#bconsult other pilots at a nearby bar#0.\""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nelly looks bored out of her mind. Wait, is she trying to bend a spoon with "
"her mind?"
msgstr ""
"Nelly parece muy aburrida. Espera, ¿está tratando de doblar una cuchara con "
"su mente?"

msgid "You see a bored individual doing something weird with a spoon."
msgstr "Ves a un individuo aburrido haciendo algo raro con una cuchara."

msgid ""
"You find Nelly gripping and staring intently at a spoon. It's almost as if "
"she is trying to bend it with her mind."
msgstr ""
"Encuentras a Nelly agarrando y mirando fijamente una cuchara. Es casi como "
"si tratara de doblarla con su mente."

msgid "\"Hello\""
msgstr "\"Hola\""

msgid "\"What are you doing?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué estás haciendo?\""

msgid "\"Nice spoon\""
msgstr "\"Bonita cuchara\""

msgid ""
"She doesn't seem to react, too concentrated on her task. You lightly tap her "
"on the shoulder and she bounces out of her chair, dropping her spoon.\n"
"\"Spoonelius!\"\n"
"She grabs the fallen spoon and then lifts it up in triumph.\n"
"\"I did it! I bent the spoon with my mind!\""
msgstr ""
"Ella no parece reaccionar, demasiado concentrada en su tarea. Le das un "
"ligero toque en el hombro y ella se levanta de la silla, dejando caer la "
"cuchara.\n"
"\"¡Cucharoniuos!\"\n"
"Coge la cuchara caída y la levanta triunfante.\n"
"\"¡Lo he conseguido! ¡He doblado la cuchara con mi mente!\""

msgid ""
"You get close to the individual and stare at them. They seem so intent on "
"their task that they don't realize you are there. Eventually, they seem to "
"nod off and fall off their chair dropping their spoon. This jolts her out of "
"her slumber.\n"
"\"Spoonelius!\"\n"
"She grabs the fallen spoon and then lifts it up in triumph.\n"
"\"I did it! I bent the spoon with my mind!\""
msgstr ""
"Te acercas al individuo y le miras fijamente. Parece tan concentrado en su "
"tarea que no se da cuenta de que estás allí. Al final, parece que se queda "
"dormido y se cae de la silla dejando caer la cuchara. Esto la sacude de su "
"sueño.\n"
"\"¡Cucharonious!\"\n"
"Coge la cuchara caída y la levanta triunfante.\n"
"\"¡Lo he conseguido! ¡He doblado la cuchara con mi mente!\""

msgid "\"I'm pretty sure it bent when you dropped it\""
msgstr "\"Estoy bastante seguro de que se dobló cuando la dejaste caer\""

msgid ""
"She poses triumphantly with her spoon.\n"
"\"What? That's impossible. This has to be the result of all my hard "
"training. I've spent 30 minutes on this! Great House Sirius has nothing on "
"me!\""
msgstr ""
"Ella posa triunfante con su cuchara.\n"
"\"¿Qué? Eso es imposible. Esto tiene que ser el resultado de todo mi duro "
"entrenamiento. ¡He pasado 30 minutos en esto! ¡La Gran Casa Sirio no tiene "
"nada que ver conmigo!\""

msgid ""
"She poses triumphantly with her spoon.\n"
"\"Impressive right! I heard that many people in Great House Sirius can do "
"this and thought, it can't be too hard can it?\""
msgstr ""
"Ella posa triunfantemente con su cuchara.\n"
"\"¡Impresionante verdad! He oído que mucha gente de la Gran Casa Sirio puede "
"hacer esto y he pensado que no puede ser muy difícil, ¿verdad?\""

msgid ""
"\"How's it like being humbled by my mental powers!\"\n"
"She cackles maniacally."
msgstr ""
"\"¡Qué tal es ser humillado por mis poderes mentales!\"\n"
"Se ríe como un maniaco."

msgid ""
"\"How's it like being humbled by my mental powers!\"\n"
"She cackles maniacally.\n"
"\"Nice to meet you! My name is Nelly!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Qué tal es ser humillado por mis poderes mentales!\"\n"
"Se cacarea maníacamente.\n"
"\"¡Encantada de conocerte! ¡Me llamo Nelly!\""

msgid ""
"\"I've been bored out of my mind since my delivery contract was terminated. "
"They said my last delivery of luxury goods stank of fish and was useless.  I "
"can't help that drying fish in the cargo hold is one of my family traditions "
"since last cycle!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Estoy aburridísimo desde que me rescindieron el contrato de reparto. "
"Dijeron que mi última entrega de artículos de lujo apestaba a pescado y era "
"inútil.  ¡No puedo evitar que secar pescado en la bodega de carga sea una de "
"mis tradiciones familiares desde el último ciclo!\""

msgid ""
"\"You wouldn't have anything interesting I could help with? I would love an "
"adventure!\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿No tendrás algo interesante en lo que te pueda ayudar? ¡Me encantaría una "
"aventura!\""

msgid "Tell her about the sensor anomaly"
msgstr "Háblale de la anomalía del sensor"

msgid ""
"Her eyes light up and twinkle like the endless stars in space.\n"
"\"That sounds… AWESOME. I'm totally in! I actually have been saving my "
"{outfit} for a chance like this!\""
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos se iluminan y centellean como las infinitas estrellas del espacio.\n"
"\"Eso suena... INCREÍBLE. ¡Me apunto totalmente! ¡Realmente he estado "
"guardando mi {outfit} para una oportunidad como esta!\""

msgid ""
"\"The location sounds like the {sys} system. I have to do some tweaks on my "
"ship, but I'll meet you there. My ship is leaner and meaner since my "
"radiators caught fire and I threw them out. I'll surely get there before you!"
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"La localización suena como el sistema {sys}. Tengo que hacer algunos "
"ajustes en mi nave, pero nos encontraremos allí. Mi nave es más esbelta y "
"más mala desde que mis radiadores se incendiaron y los tiré. ¡Seguramente "
"llegaré antes que tú!\""

msgid ""
"You're not sure if that was the best idea, but it does seem like she may be "
"able to help this time around."
msgstr ""
"No está seguro de que haya sido la mejor idea, pero parece que esta vez "
"puedes ayudar."

msgid "Meet Nelly at {sys}"
msgstr "Encuentrate a Nelly en {sys}"

msgid "Head to the sensor anomaly"
msgstr "Dirígete a la anomalía del sensor"

msgid ""
"You take your leave. It may be best not to get involved with Nelly right now."
msgstr ""
"Te vas a ir. Tal vez sea mejor no involucrarse con Nelly en este momento."

msgid "You abandoned the sensor anomaly and Nelly!"
msgstr "¡Abandonaste la anomalía del sensor y a Nelly!"

#.
#.
#. Common stuff for the Nelly tutorial campaign
#.
#. --
#. Use default
msgid "Nelly"
msgstr "Nelly"

msgid "Nemesis"
msgstr "Némesis"

msgid "Llaminator MK3"
msgstr "Laminador MK3"

msgid "Llaminator MK2"
msgstr "Laminador MK2"

#. Spawn ship
#. Get closest jump to player, should be robust to player.teleport
msgid "There it is! Let's head towards the sensor anomaly!"
msgstr "¡Allí está! ¡Vamos hacia la anomalía del sensor!"

msgid "Wait? We were followed?"
msgstr "¿Espera? ¿Nos han seguido?"

msgid "Eliminate the hostiles"
msgstr "Elimina a los hostiles"

msgid "Come over here!"
msgstr "¡Ven aquí!"

msgid "Get closer!"
msgstr "¡Acércate!"

msgid "I'm ready, come here!"
msgstr "¡Estoy preparado, ven aquí!"

msgid "You're as good as fried chicken!"
msgstr "¡Eres tan bueno como el pollo frito!"

msgid "Save me!"
msgstr "¡Sálvame!"

msgid "Get rid of them!"
msgstr "¡Deshazte de ellos!"

msgid "Aaaaaaah!"
msgstr "¡Aaaaaaat!"

msgid "Phew! Come over here and I'll activate my pulse scanner!"
msgstr "¡Uf! ¡Ven aquí y activaré mi escáner de pulso!"

msgid "Time to activate my pulse scanner!"
msgstr "¡Hora de activar mi escáner de pulso!"

msgid "My engine stopped, you go on ahead!"
msgstr "Mi motor se ha parado, ¡sigue adelante!"

msgid "Follow the trail"
msgstr "Sigue el rastro"

msgid "Board the derelict"
msgstr "Abordar el derrelicto"

msgid ""
"You board the ship and immediately Nelly establishes a holo-link connection. "
"She seems to be covered in ship grease.\n"
"\"Whoa! This looks much fancier than I expected!\""
msgstr ""
"Abordas la nave e inmediatamente Nelly estableceñ una conexión hololink. "
"Parece estar cubierta de grasa de nave.\n"
"\"¡Guau! ¡Esto parece mucho más elegante de lo que esperaba!\""

msgid "\"Why so greasy?\""
msgstr "\"¿Por qué tan grasiento?\""

msgid "\"Is this it?\""
msgstr "\"¿Es esto?\""

msgid ""
"\"When we got attacked by that scary ship, I slipped and accidentally pulled "
"down my fish drying rack. The fish flew over all the ship and one got caught "
"in my reactor because I forgot to close the maintenance panel. I managed to "
"put out the fire, but the fish got lodged in the cooling tube. I had to "
"grease myself up to slide in there and reach it, however, it's still a work "
"in progress.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Cuando nos atacó esa nave que da miedo, me resbalé y derribé "
"accidentalmente mi rejilla de secado de pescado. Los peces volaron por toda "
"la nave y uno quedó atrapado en mi reactor porque olvidé cerrar el panel de "
"mantenimiento. Conseguí apagar el fuego, pero el pez se quedó atascado en el "
"tubo de refrigeración. Tuve que engrasarme para deslizarme hasta allí y "
"alcanzarlo, sin embargo, todavía es un trabajo en curso.\""

msgid ""
"\"It sure looks like it! It's my first time seeing such a pretty derelict.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Seguro que lo parece! Es la primera vez que veo un derrelicto tan bonito."
"\""

msgid "\"Don't just stand there! Take a look around\""
msgstr "\"¡No te quedes ahí! Echa un vistazo a tu alrededor\""

msgid ""
"You attempt to go through the airlock when an authorization prompt opens up. "
"Looking at the make of the ship, it seems heavily reinforced. It looks like "
"you're going to have to break the code to gain complete access to the ship."
msgstr ""
"Intentas atravesar la esclusa cuando se abre un aviso de autorización. "
"Mirando la marca de la nave, parece fuertemente reforzada. Parece que vas a "
"tener que descifrar el código para ganar acceso completo a la nave."

msgid ""
"Your ship AI materializes in front of you.\n"
"\"This looks like a standard security mechanism. You will need to crack it "
"to access the ship.\""
msgstr ""
"La IA de tu nave se materializa frente a ti.\n"
"\"Este parece un mecanismo de seguridad estándar. Tendrás que descifrarlo "
"para acceder a la nave.\""

msgid ""
"\"You have to guess the combination of symbols to open the password. This "
"lock should have only {num} symbols. After each attempt, you will know how "
"many symbols match exactly with {exact}. If a symbol is in the password, but "
"is not in the correct position you will be shown {fuzzy}. You have to use "
"the clues to attempt to match the true password.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tienes que adivinar la combinación de símbolos para abrir la contraseña. "
"Esta cerradura debe tener sólo {num} símbolos. Después de cada intento, "
"sabrás cuántos símbolos coinciden exactamente con {exact}. Si un símbolo "
"está en la contraseña, pero no está en la posición correcta se te mostrará "
"{fuzzy}. Tienes que usar las pistas para intentar coincidir con la "
"contraseña verdadera.\""

msgid ""
"She squints looking at {shipai}'s holographic projection.\n"
"\"Say, do I know you?\""
msgstr ""
"Entrecierra los ojos mirando la proyección holográfica de {shipai}.\n"
"\"Dime, ¿te conozco?\""

msgid ""
"\"It is not possible that we have met. For I am {player}'s ship AI.\"\n"
"They turn quickly to you.\n"
"\"Remember, {exact} for exact matches and {fuzzy} for correct symbol but not "
"position. Best of luck!\"\n"
"They dematerialize in a hurry."
msgstr ""
"\"No es posible que nos hayamos encontrado. Porque yo soy la IA de la nave "
"de {player}.\"\n"
"Se vuelven rápidamente hacia ti.\n"
"\"Recuerda, {exact} para coincidencias exactas y {fuzzy} para símbolo "
"correcto pero no posición. ¡Mucha suerte!\"\n"
"Se desmaterializan a toda prisa."

msgid "Thinking deeply to herself she murmurs \"I definitely know them…\"."
msgstr ""
"Pensando profundamente para sí misma murmura \"definitivamente los conozco..."
"\"."

msgid ""
"She turns again to you.\n"
"\"Try to crack the password, we need to see what's on the ship!\""
msgstr ""
"Se vuelve de nuevo hacia ti.\n"
"\"Intenta descifrar la contraseña, ¡necesitamos ver qué hay en la nave!\""

msgid ""
"A brief '#rAUTHORIZATION DENIED#0' flashes on the screen, and you hear the "
"ship internals groan as the emergency security protocol kicks in and "
"everything starts to get locked down. However, it seems to jam and stops "
"halfway. Then the authorization prompt reappears. Looks like you get another "
"chance!"
msgstr ""
"Un breve \"#rAUTORIZACIÓN DENEGADA#0\" parpadea en la pantalla y se oye el "
"gemido de los componentes internos de la nave cuando entra en funcionamiento "
"el protocolo de seguridad de emergencia y todo empieza a bloquearse. Sin "
"embargo, parece atascarse y se detiene a mitad de camino. Entonces vuelve a "
"aparecer el aviso de autorización. ¡Parece que tienes otra oportunidad!"

msgid ""
"You deftly crack the code and the screen flashes with '#gAUTHORIZATION "
"GRANTED#0'. Time to see what goodness awaits you!"
msgstr ""
"Descifras hábilmente el código y la pantalla parpadea con \"#gAUTORIZACIÓN "
"CONCEDIDA#0\". ¡Es hora de ver las maravillas que te esperan!"

msgid ""
"She seems to be banging on her reactor while talking to you.\n"
"\"That was great! Go ahead!\""
msgstr ""
"Parece que está golpeando su reactor mientras habla contigo.\n"
"\"¡Eso fue genial! ¡Adelante!\""

msgid ""
"You proceed to enter and explore the interior of the derelict. Although "
"there is a distinct lack of living life aboard, everything seems to be in "
"pretty good condition. Eventually you reach the cargo hold and find a lone "
"crate marked \"cheese\"."
msgstr ""
"Procedes a entrar y explorar el interior del derrelicto. Aunque hay una "
"clara falta de vida a bordo, todo parece estar en bastante buen estado. "
"Finalmente llegas a la bodega de carga y encuentras una única caja marcada "
"como \"queso\"."

msgid ""
"Even though she is apparently squeezing her greasy self through her reactor, "
"her eyes light up the moment she sees the crate.\n"
"\"Whoa! Is that what I think it is? Could you bring the crate over to my "
"ship? I need to see that right away!\""
msgstr ""
"A pesar de que aparentemente se está exprimiendo a través de su reactor, sus "
"ojos se iluminan en el momento en que ve la caja.\n"
"\"¡Guau! ¿Es eso lo que creo que es? ¿Podrías traer la caja a mi nave? "
"¡Necesito verla ahora mismo!\""

msgid ""
"You explore the rest of the ship but do not find anything else of interest. "
"Although the ship is in very good condition, it is still not space-worthy, "
"and there is not anything that you can do with it. You take the crate of "
"cheese and leave the ship behind."
msgstr ""
"Exploras el resto de la nave pero no encuentras nada más de interés. Aunque "
"la nave está en muy buen estado, todavía no es apta para el espacio, y no "
"hay nada que puedas hacer con ella. Coges la caja de queso y abandonas la "
"nave."

msgid "Cheese"
msgstr "Queso"

msgid "A crate marked cheese. It is quite small and very, very smelly."
msgstr "Un cajón marcado con queso. Es bastante pequeño y muy, muy oloroso."

msgid "Board Nelly's ship"
msgstr "Aborda la nave de Nelly"

#. Clean up stuff
#. Can't fail
msgid ""
"The moment you get on Nelly's ship with the smelly cheese, she comes "
"bouncing to you."
msgstr ""
"En el momento en que te subes a la nave de Nelly con el queso maloliente, "
"ella viene saltando hacia ti."

msgid "\"Oh! It's even better in person! Let me check the goods.\""
msgstr "\"¡Oh! ¡Es aún mejor en persona! Déjame comprobar la mercancía.\""

msgid ""
"She takes the crate and deftly pries it open. Suddenly everything smells "
"really strongly of cheese and you gag a bit.\n"
"\"Let's see. This is an authentic sausage-infused matured cheese! The "
"rumours were true!\""
msgstr ""
"Coge la caja y la abre hábilmente. De repente, todo huele muy fuerte a queso "
"y te dan unas cuantas arcadas.\n"
"\"Veamos. ¡Este es un auténtico queso curado con salchicha! Los rumores eran "
"ciertos!\""

msgid ""
"\"Here, take my Pulse Scanner, I'll take the cheese. I won't have to chase "
"sensor anomalies for a while with this beauty!\"\n"
"She rubs the cheese to her face."
msgstr ""
"\"Toma, coge mi escáner de pulso, yo cogeré el queso. No tendré que "
"perseguir anomalías en los sensores durante un tiempo con esta belleza\".\n"
"Se frota el queso en la cara."

msgid ""
"Seeing as it doesn't seem like you'll be able to change anything and the "
"Pulse Scanner is probably more useful than the cheese, you take the outfit "
"and head back to your ship. Now you can explore sensor anomalies on your own!"
msgstr ""
"Como no parece que vayas a poder cambiar nada y el escáner de pulso "
"probablemente sea más útil que el queso, coges el equipo y vuelves a tu "
"nave. ¡Ahora puedes explorar las anomalías de los sensores por tu cuenta!"

#. Let her fly away
#. Re-enable spawns
msgid ""
"Nelly helped you explore a sensor anomaly. You found some smelly cheese and "
"traded it with Nelly for a Pulse Scanner to be able to explore more sensor "
"anomalies."
msgstr ""
"Nelly te ha ayudado a explorar una anomalía en los sensores. Has encontrado "
"queso maloliente y se lo has cambiado a Nelly por un Escáner de Pulso para "
"poder explorar más anomalías de los sensores."

