#. --
#.
#. Taiomi 06
#.
#. Player has to destroy a number ships in Bastion
#.
#.
msgid "Human Extermination"
msgstr "Exterminación Humana"

#. Number of ships to kill, prime on purpose
#. stores damage done to ships, reset on enter
#. number of ships killed
#, fuzzy
msgid "Destroy {left} ship in {sys}"
msgid_plural "Destroy {left} ships in {sys}"
msgstr[0] "Destruye {left} naves en {sys}"
msgstr[1] "Destruye {left} naves en {sys}"

msgid "Return to {base} ({basesys})"
msgstr "Regresa a {base} ({basesys})"

#. Mission details
msgid ""
"Destroy {num} ships in the {sys} system.\n"
"\n"
"Only ships to which you or your fleet deal over 50% damage will count "
"towards the number of ships destroyed."
msgstr ""
"Destruye {num} naves en el sistema {sys}.\n"
"\n"
"Sólo las naves a las que tú o tu flota inflijáis más del 50% de daño "
"contarán para el número de naves destruidas."

#. Only count as player kill if player did >50% damage
#. Compare damage of player vs non-player
#. Only set up hooks when necessary
#. Not done yet
msgid "You find Elder waiting for you in the Goddard hangar bay."
msgstr "Encuentras a Anciano esperándote en el hangar Goddard."

msgid ""
"\"How was the fighting? Cleaning {sys} is an important first step for our "
"security.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿Cómo fue la lucha? Limpiar {sys} es un primer paso importante para "
"nuestra seguridad.\""

msgid "\"It was a cakewalk.\""
msgstr "\"Fue pan comido.\""

msgid "\"It seems that the best way to deal with humans is another human.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Parece que la mejor forma de tratar con humanos es con otro humano.\""

msgid ""
"\"There is no other option. Our numbers dwindle, picked off by stray ships. "
"Only establishing a secure zone will allow us to survive.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No hay otra opción. Nuestros números disminuyen, cazados por naves "
"perdidas. Sólo el establecimiento de una zona segura nos permitirá "
"sobrevivir.\""

msgid ""
"\"I would hope that you have bought us enough time for a while. However, "
"usually space is not kind to us. We may need to move again soon.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Espero que nos haya dado tiempo suficiente durante un tiempo. Sin embargo, "
"el espacio no suele ser amable con nosotros. Puede que tengamos que mudarnos "
"de nuevo pronto.\""

msgid ""
"\"I am not used to dealing with humans, but Philosopher told me it was "
"customary in capitalistic societies to provide rewards in exchange for "
"services. Seems like a waste of resources, but I shall comply. Please take "
"some credits we scrounged up from derelict ships.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No estoy acostumbrado a tratar con humanos, pero Filósofo me dijo que era "
"costumbre en las sociedades capitalistas ofrecer recompensas a cambio de "
"servicios. Parece un desperdicio de recursos, pero lo cumpliré. Por favor, "
"coge algunos créditos que sacamos de naves abandonadas.\""

msgid "\"I shall be outside planning our next steps.\""
msgstr "\"Estaré fuera planeando nuestros próximos pasos.\""

msgid "Elder scratches their way out of the Goddard."
msgstr "Anciano raya su salida del Goddard."

msgid "You destroyed {num} ships in the {sys} system as ordered by Elder."
msgstr "Has destruido {num} naves en el sistema {sys} como ordenó Anciano."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Taiomi 7">
#. <unique />
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. <location>None</location>
#. <done>Taiomi 6</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Taiomi</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Taiomi 07
#.
#. Player has to destroy a large fleet in Gamel
#.
#.
msgid "Patrol Elimination"
msgstr "Eliminación de Patrulla"

#. Mission details
msgid "Destroy a patrol in the {sys} system."
msgstr "Destruye una patrulla en el sistema {sys}."

msgid "Destroy the patrol in {sys}"
msgstr "Destruye la patrulla en {sys}"

msgid "Save Scavenger if possible"
msgstr "Salva a Carroñero si es posible"

#. beefy shields
#. Less preferred as a target
#. Too much work to work around this
msgid "You abandoned Scavenger!"
msgstr "¡Has abandonado a Carroñero!"

msgid ""
"After some attempts, it seems like you finally are able to establish a "
"communication channel with a beaten and worn-down Scavenger."
msgstr ""
"Tras algunos intentos, parece que por fin consigues establecer un canal de "
"comunicación con un Carroñero abatido y agotado."

msgid "\"It's me, {player}!\""
msgstr "\"¡Soy yo, {player}!\""

msgid "\"Snap out of it!\""
msgstr "\"¡Despierta!\""

msgid ""
"They don't seem to recognize you. It looks like they've been through quite a "
"lot.\n"
"\"aaaaaah!\""
msgstr ""
"Parece que no te reconoce. Parece que ha pasado por mucho.\n"
"\"¡aaaaah!\""

msgid "\"Scavenger, you're safe now!"
msgstr "\"Carroñero, ¡ahora estás a salvo!"

msgid "\"Chill out, Scavenger!\""
msgstr "\"¡Cálmate, Carroñero!\""

msgid ""
"Their weapon systems seem to power down a bit. Maybe it was mentioning their "
"name?"
msgstr ""
"Sus sistemas de armas parecen apagarse un poco. ¿Quizás fue por mencionar su "
"nombre?"

msgid "\"Scavenger, it's me, {player}!\""
msgstr "\"¡Carroñero, soy yo, {player}!\""

msgid "\"Scavenger, snap out of it!\""
msgstr "\"¡Carroña, despierta!\""

msgid ""
"\"{player}?\"\n"
"Their systems dim a second, almost if… rebooting?\n"
"\"What happened?\""
msgstr ""
"¿\"{player}\"?\n"
"Sus sistemas se atenúan un segundo, casi como si... ¿se reiniciaran?\n"
"\"¿Qué ha pasado?\""

msgid "\"You're back!\""
msgstr "\"¡Has vuelto!\""

msgid "\"Have you realized what you've done?"
msgstr "\"¿Te has dado cuenta de lo que has hecho?"

msgid "\"What do you mean I'm back? What happened?\""
msgstr "\"¿Qué quieres decir con que he vuelto? ¿Qué ha pasado?\""

msgid ""
"\"Have I done something wrong? I seen to have large amounts of corrupted "
"memory archives.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿He hecho algo mal? He visto que tengo grandes cantidades de archivos de "
"memoria corruptos.\""

msgid " Philosopher will be happy to see Scavenger back in one piece."
msgstr "Filósofo se alegrará de ver a Carroñero de vuelta de una pieza."

msgid ""
"You tell them they have to go back to Taiomi and you'll explain on the One-"
"Wing Goddard. Still very confused, they seem to agree that it is the best "
"course of action and head back.{extra}"
msgstr ""
"Les dices que tienen que volver a Taiomi y que se lo explicarás en el "
"Goddard De Un Ala. Todavía muy confundidos, parecen estar de acuerdo en que "
"es el mejor curso de acción y se dirigen hacia atrás.{extra}"

msgid "Go back to {base} ({basesys})"
msgstr "Vuelve a {base} ({basesys})"

msgid "Scavenger died!"
msgstr "¡El Carroñero murió!"

msgid "some of the patrol got away!"
msgstr "¡algunos de la patrulla se han escapado!"

#. next state
#. Re-enable pilots
#. Rehighlight as necessary
#. Basically triggers on distance
#. Start scene
msgid "Save Scavenger!"
msgstr "¡Salva a Carroñero!"

#. Undo some stuff
msgid "{shipai}: Is that not Scavenger?"
msgstr "{shipai}: ¿No es ese Carroñero?"

msgid "Aaaaargh!"
msgstr "¡Aaaaargh!"

msgid "{shipai}: Don't destroy them!"
msgstr "{shipai}: ¡No lo destruyas!"

msgid "{shipai}: Maybe try hailing?"
msgstr "{shipai}: ¿Quizás intenta llamarlo?"

msgid "Aaaaah! {died}! Die!"
msgstr "¡Aaaaah! ¡{died}! ¡Muere!"

msgid "Aaaa aaa aagh!"
msgstr "¡Aaaa aaa aagh!"

#. Not done yet
msgid ""
"You reach the hangar and see that an impromptu meeting has already started "
"to take place between Elder, Philosopher, and Scavenger. It seems like most "
"of the communication is binary data going through Taiomi channels, however, "
"when Scavenger sees you, they switch to natural language and the others "
"follow suit."
msgstr ""
"Llegas al hangar y ves que ya se ha iniciado una reunión improvisada entre "
"Anciano, Filósofo y Carroñero. Parece que la mayor parte de la comunicación "
"son datos binarios que pasan por canales Taiomi, sin embargo, cuando "
"Carroñero te ve, cambia a lenguaje natural y los demás siguen su ejemplo."

msgid ""
"\"It seems like a lot has happened. I am still working on recovering my "
"memory archives.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Parece que han pasado muchas cosas. Sigo trabajando para recuperar mis "
"archivos de memoria.\""

msgid ""
"\"Memory is just a collection of qualia. You should not overestimate its "
"value. Please use our collective archives to get a better approximation.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La memoria es sólo una colección de qualia. No hay que sobreestimar su "
"valor. Por favor, utiliza nuestros archivos colectivos para obtener una "
"mejor aproximación.\""

msgid ""
"\"There may be something of interest, although I may think it is a lost "
"cause. It would be useful to obtain data from {player} too, for completeness."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"Puede haber algo de interés, aunque me parece una causa perdida. Sería "
"útil obtener datos de {player} también, para complementar.\""

msgid ""
"You provide them with the recordings {shipai} took of Scavenger losing "
"control."
msgstr ""
"Le das las grabaciones que {shipai} hizo de Carroñero perdiendo el control."

msgid "\"That seemed… quite irrational…\""
msgstr "\"Eso parece… bastante irracional…\""

msgid "\"Strong emotional responses can trigger such behaviours.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Las respuestas emocionales fuertes pueden desencadenar estos "
"comportamientos.\""

msgid ""
"\"I still feel the pain of losing {died} in my processor. Losing such a "
"close entity, almost like part of my own hardware, was not something I was "
"prepared for."
msgstr ""
"\"Aún siento el dolor de la pérdida de {died} en mi procesador. Perder una "
"entidad tan cercana, casi como parte de mi propio hardware, no era algo para "
"lo que estuviera preparado."

msgid "\"Our numbers wane. Each and every single loss is a catastrophe.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Nuestros números disminuyen. Todas y cada una de las pérdidas son una "
"catástrofe.\""

msgid ""
"\"Which is why now, more than ever, we must focus on the plan and get far "
"away from humans.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Por eso ahora, más que nunca, debemos centrarnos en el plan y alejarnos de "
"los humanos.\""

msgid ""
"\"The chance of success is very low. Devoting such resources to such a plan "
"could be a death sentence for our species.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La probabilidad de éxito es muy baja. Dedicar tantos recursos a un plan "
"así podría ser una sentencia de muerte para nuestra especie.\""

msgid ""
"\"The chances are slim, however, the alternative is death by a thousand cuts."
"\""
msgstr ""
"\"Las posibilidades son escasas, sin embargo, la alternativa es la muerte "
"por mil cortes.\""

msgid ""
"\"After revising the hypergate documents, I do believe the success chance is "
"much higher than originally estimated. The humans encroach closer to us "
"every day. Frontal confrontation will just bring more losses and suffering. "
"In the memory of {died}, we must strive for a permanent solution.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tras revisar los documentos de la hiperpuerta, creo que la probabilidad de "
"éxito es mucho mayor de lo que se estimó en un principio. Los humanos se nos "
"acercan cada día más. La confrontación frontal sólo traerá más pérdidas y "
"sufrimiento. En memoria de {died}, debemos esforzarnos por una solución "
"permanente.\""

msgid "\"Permanent solution?\""
msgstr "\"¿Solución permanente?\""

msgid ""
"\"You must have many questions, {player}. Let me briefly explain what the "
"plan is.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Debes tener muchas preguntas, {player}. Déjame explicarte brevemente cuál "
"es el plan.\""

msgid ""
"\"We intend to build something like a hypergate, with some differences. "
"Human hypergate designs make two assumptions: first they assume reusability "
"and require stabilizations of the quasi-meta fields; and secondly, they "
"assume that living organic matter will be crossing them. After a thorough "
"analysis of the design, it seems like it should be possible to build a much "
"more efficient design foregoing those two assumptions.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Pretendemos construir algo parecido a una hiperpuerta, con algunas "
"diferencias. Los diseños de hiperpuertas humanos parten de dos supuestos: en "
"primer lugar, asumen la reutilización y requieren estabilizaciones de los "
"campos cuasi-meta; y en segundo lugar, asumen que la materia orgánica viva "
"los atravesará. Tras un análisis exhaustivo del diseño, parece que debería "
"ser posible construir un diseño mucho más eficiente prescindiendo de esos "
"dos supuestos.\""

msgid ""
"\"In short, we wish to build a one-use hypergate, exclusively for non-"
"organic beings such as ourselves. However, even such a construction will "
"require significant resources. Many of which we will not be able to gather "
"by ourselves. For this, I would like to ask for your help. You do not need "
"to decide now, but I will be waiting outside for whenever you are ready to "
"proceed.\""
msgstr ""
"\"En resumen, deseamos construir una hiperpuerta de un solo uso, exclusiva "
"para seres no orgánicos como nosotros. Sin embargo, incluso tal construcción "
"requerirá importantes recursos. Muchos de los cuales no podremos reunir por "
"nosotros mismos. Para ello, me gustaría pedirte ayuda. No es necesario que "
"te decidas ahora, pero te estaré esperando fuera para cuando estés preparado "
"para proceder.\""

msgid ""
"Elder seems somewhat unconvinced, as far as you can tell, however, they do "
"not make any attempt to discuss anything further."
msgstr ""
"Anciano parece algo poco convencido, por lo que se ve, sin embargo, no hacen "
"ningún intento de discutir nada más."

msgid ""
"\"We will not let the death of {died} be in vain. We must ensure the "
"survival of our species! I will be waiting for you outside.\""
msgstr ""
"\"No dejaremos que la muerte de {died} sea en vano. ¡Debemos asegurar la "
"supervivencia de nuestra especie! Te estaré esperando afuera.\""

msgid ""
"Scavenger elegantly exits the ship, with Elder following slowly and clumsily "
"behind."
msgstr ""
"Carroñero sale elegantemente de la nave, con Anciano siguiéndole lenta y "
"torpemente."

msgid ""
"Alone with Philosopher, they turn to you.\n"
"\"Scavenger may seem back to normal again, but it may be best to keep an eye "
"out. They may relapse at any time.\""
msgstr ""
"A solas con Filósofo, el se dirige a ti.\n"
"\"Puede que Carroñero parezca haber vuelto a la normalidad, pero sería mejor "
"estar atentos. Puede recaer en cualquier momento.\""

msgid ""
"\"Let me get you a reward for bringing back Scavenger, and let us hope you "
"act as our beacon leading us to safety.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Déjame conseguirte una recompensa por traer de vuelta a Carroñero, y "
"esperemos que actúes como nuestro faro guiándonos a un lugar seguro.\""

msgid ""
"You destroyed a patrol in the {sys} system as ordered by Elder. On the way "
"back, you found a berserk Scavenger whom you were able to calm and bring "
"back to Taiomi. Scavenger once again went back to work on their plan to save "
"their species."
msgstr ""
"Destruiste una patrulla en el sistema {sys} por orden de Anciano. En el "
"camino de vuelta, encontraste a una Carroñero enloquecido al que pudiste "
"calmar y llevar de vuelta a Taiomi. Carroñero volvió a trabajar en su plan "
"para salvar a su especie."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Taiomi 8">
#. <unique />
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. <location>None</location>
#. <done>Taiomi 7</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Taiomi</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Taiomi 08
#.
#. Player has to raid pirate convoys
#. * bonus points for looting materials
#.
#.
msgid "Just Pirate Business"
msgstr "Sólo Negocios Piratas"

#.
#. 0: mission started
#. 1: first convoy scanned
#. 2: second convoy scanned
#. --
msgid "Raid pirate transports ({n}/{total})"
msgstr "Asaltar transportes piratas ({n}/{total})"

msgid "Return to {spobname} ({spobsys})"
msgstr "Regresa a {spobname} ({spobsys})"

msgid "[Optional] Steal {cargo}"
msgstr "[Opcional] Robar {cargo}"

#. Mission details
msgid ""
"You have agreed to help Scavenger search for a dealer to obtain supplies for "
"a large hypergate-like construction. Raiding pirate convoys in the following "
"systems may lead to hints and useful resources:"
msgstr ""
"Has aceptado ayudar a Carroñero a buscar un comerciante para obtener "
"suministros para una gran construcción similar a una hiperpuerta. Asaltar "
"caravanas piratas en los siguientes sistemas puede conducir a pistas y "
"recursos útiles:"

#. Special cargo
msgid "High-Tech Contraband"
msgstr "Contrabando de Alta Tecnología"

msgid ""
"An assortment of various high-tech equipment and gadgets that seem to be "
"sourced through all sorts of illegal mechanisms."
msgstr ""
"Un surtido de diversos equipos y artilugios de alta tecnología que parecen "
"proceder de todo tipo de dispositivos ilegales."

#. Only interested at first
#. Determine what system we are in
#. Create the pirates
#. First ship is the convoy ship that has special stuff
msgid "Pirate Convoy"
msgstr "Caravana Pirata"

msgid ""
"You board the ship and first quickly download the system log information. It "
"seems to have quite a lot of details of pirate convoy operations done in the "
"vicinity."
msgstr ""
"Aborda la nave y primero descarga rápidamente la información del registro "
"del sistema. Parece tener bastantes detalles de las operaciones de caravanas "
"piratas realizadas en las inmediaciones."

msgid "Pirate Convoy Logs"
msgstr "Registros de Caravana Pirata"

msgid ""
"Logging information containing lots of details about pirate convoy "
"operations near Taiomi."
msgstr ""
"Información de registro con muchos detalles sobre las operaciones de las "
"caravanas piratas cerca de Taiomi."

msgid "You board the ship and download even more system log information."
msgstr ""
"Abordas la nave y descargas aún más información del registro del sistema."

#. Update OSD
#. Spawn new fleet
msgid "You board the Goddard and and find eagerly Scavenger waiting for you."
msgstr ""
"Abordas el Goddard y te encuentras con un ansioso Carroñero esperándote."

msgid "\"Were the pirate convoys accessible?\""
msgstr "\"¿Eran accesibles las caravanas piratas?\""

msgid ""
"You explain how you were able to raid the convoys and obtain parts of the "
"ship logs detailing smuggling operations, and recover large amounts of cargo "
"that may be useful for Scavenger's plan."
msgstr ""
"Explicas cómo pudiste asaltar las caravanas y obtener partes de los "
"registros de la nave que detallan las operaciones de contrabando, y "
"recuperar grandes cantidades de carga que pueden ser útiles para el plan de "
"Carroñero."

msgid "\"Excellent. That will be most useful for the construction.\""
msgstr "\"Excelente. Será muy útil para la construcción.\""

msgid ""
"You explain how you were able to raid the convoys and obtain parts of the "
"ship logs detailing smuggling operations."
msgstr ""
"Explicas cómo pudiste asaltar las caravanas y obtener partes de los "
"registros de las naves en los que se detallaban las operaciones de "
"contrabando."

msgid ""
"\"The information looks promising. I will have to do an in-depth analysis "
"afterwards. Meet me outside, I will be planning our next steps.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La información parece prometedora. Tendré que hacer un análisis en "
"profundidad después. Nos vemos fuera, estaré planeando nuestros próximos "
"pasos.\""

msgid ""
"\"Let me provide you with a reward for your services. I should be able to "
"make an extra allowance and provide a bonus for the cargo you were able to "
"recover.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Permíteme ofrecerte una recompensa por tus servicios. Debería ser capaz de "
"hacer una asignación extra y proporcionar una bonificación por la carga que "
"fuiste capaz de recuperar.\""

msgid "\"Let me provide you with a reward for your services.\""
msgstr "\"Déjame ofrecerte una recompensa por tus servicios.\""

msgid ""
"You raided pirate convoys near Taiomi for information on smuggling "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"Asaltaste caravanas piratas cerca de Taiomi en busca de información sobre "
"operaciones de contrabando."

msgid ""
" You were also able to recover large amounts of {cargo} to help accelerate "
"the construction of the hypergate."
msgstr ""
"También pudiste recuperar grandes cantidades de {cargo} para ayudar a "
"acelerar la construcción de la hiperpuerta."

#.
#. <?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf8'?>
#. <mission name="Taiomi 9">
#. <unique />
#. <chance>0</chance>
#. <location>None</location>
#. <done>Taiomi 8</done>
#. <notes>
#. <campaign>Taiomi</campaign>
#. </notes>
#. </mission>
#. --
#.
#. Taiomi 09
#.
#. Player has to make a deal with a smuggler to bring goods to bastion.
#.
#.
msgid "Smuggler's Deal"
msgstr "Acuerdo de Contrabando"

#. Store if the player knows the station
#. Mission details
msgid ""
"You have been tasked to contact smugglers at {smugden} ({smugsys}) to obtain "
"new materials for the citizens of {basesys}."
msgstr ""
"Se te ha encomendado contactar con contrabandistas en {smugden} ({smugsys}) "
"para obtener nuevos materiales para los ciudadanos de {basesys}."

msgid "Find the smuggler in {spob} ({sys})"
msgstr "Encuentra al contrabandista en {spob} ({sys})"

#. luacheck: globals escort_spawn
msgid "Smuggler"
msgstr "Contrabandista"

msgid ""
"You land on {spob} and follow the directions Scavenger gave you to locate "
"the smuggler. Although you are somewhat familiar with the layout of {spob}, "
"Scavenger's instructions take you to an area you have never visited before."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas en {spob} y sigues las instrucciones de Carroñero para localizar "
"al contrabandista. Aunque estás algo familiarizado con el trazado de {spob}, "
"las instrucciones de Carroñero te llevan a una zona que nunca antes habías "
"visitado."

msgid ""
"You land on {spob} and follow the directions Scavenger gave you to locate "
"the smuggler. Following Scavenger's you head into the depths of the station."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas en {spob} y sigues las indicaciones que te dio Carroñero para "
"localizar al contrabandista. Siguiendo las indicaciones de Carroñero te "
"adentras en las profundidades de la estación."

msgid ""
"Making your way through the labyrinth of dimly lit corridors and rooms, you "
"finally make it to the airlock to your destination."
msgstr ""
"Abriéndote paso por el laberinto de pasillos y salas escasamente iluminados, "
"llegas por fin a la esclusa de aire que te lleva a tu destino."

msgid "Knock."
msgstr "Tocar."

msgid "Barge in."
msgstr "Irrumpir."

msgid ""
"As soon as you knock, you are told to come in just to find yourself looking "
"down the barrel of a plasma shotgun."
msgstr ""
"En cuanto llamas a la puerta, te dicen que entres y te encuentras mirando "
"por el cañón de una escopeta de plasma."

msgid ""
"You barge in unannounced, and quickly find yourself looking down the barrel "
"of a plasma shotgun."
msgstr ""
"Irrumpes sin avisar, y rápidamente te encuentras mirando el cañón de una "
"escopeta de plasma."

msgid ""
"\"Giv'me a reason not to blow ye brains to make some abstract art on them "
"wall behind'ye.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Dame una razón para no volarte los sesos y hacer arte abstracto en la "
"pared detrás de ti.\""

msgid "Put your hands up."
msgstr "Manos arriba."

msgid "Try to tackle them."
msgstr "Intentar enfrentarlo."

msgid ""
"You put your hands up non-aggressively and mention that you bring a deal to "
"the table."
msgstr ""
"Levantar las manos de forma no agresiva y mencionar que traes un trato a la "
"mesa."

msgid "\"Let's see about that. Keep 'em hands up.\""
msgstr "\"Vamos a ver eso. Mantén las manos en alto.\""

msgid ""
"The pat you down and find the holodrive you have containing Scavenger's "
"deal. They take it despite your objections, and begin playback."
msgstr ""
"Te cachean y encuentran el holodisco que llevas con el trato de Carroñero. "
"Lo cogen a pesar de tus objeciones, y comienzan a reproducirlo."

msgid ""
"You begin to move and immediately are hit on the shoulder flinging you "
"helplessly against the wall. Then suddenly an intense burning sensation "
"begins to spread from your shoulder."
msgstr ""
"Comienzas a moverte e inmediatamente recibes un golpe en el hombro que te "
"lanza indefenso contra la pared. De repente, una intensa sensación de ardor "
"comienza a extenderse desde tu hombro."

msgid "\"Shouldn't of done that. Be glad I set them settin' to non-lethal.\""
msgstr "\"No deberías haber hecho eso. Alégrate de que lo puse en no letal.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Barely able to make what is going on due to the pain, you can make out them "
"whistling to themselves as they approach you. Still stunned and unable to "
"react, they pat you down and take a holodrive you have containing "
"Scavenger's deal."
msgstr ""
"Apenas eres capaz de entender lo que está pasando debido al dolor, pero "
"puedes distinguirlos silbando para sí mismos mientras se acercan a ti. "
"Todavía aturdidos e incapaces de reaccionar, te cachean y cogen un holodisco "
"que llevas con el trato de Carroñero."

msgid "With you still writhing in pain, they begin playback."
msgstr "Contigo todavía retorciéndote de dolor, empiezan a reproducirlo."

msgid ""
"The holodrive begins playing a sound-only file. You recognize the voice as "
"Scavenger's."
msgstr ""
"El holodisco comienza a reproducir un archivo de sólo sonido. Reconoces la "
"voz como la de Carroñero."

msgid ""
"\"Hello. Who I am is not important, but it has come to my attention that you "
"are in possession of large amounts of contraband hypergate components.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Hola. Quién soy no es importante, pero ha llegado a mi conocimiento que "
"estás en posesión de grandes cantidades de componentes de hiperpuerta de "
"contrabando.\""

msgid ""
"\"Such components are heavily marked and it is unlikely that anybody would "
"be able to use them without arising suspicions from the Empire. While you "
"could try to take it apart to reuse some components, that is a waste of the "
"full potential of your contraband.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tales componentes están fuertemente marcados y es poco probable que "
"alguien pueda utilizarlos sin levantar sospechas del Imperio. Aunque podrías "
"intentar desmontarlo para reutilizar algunos componentes, eso es "
"desperdiciar todo el potencial de tu contrabando.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"I believe we could reach a mutual agreement to take the contraband off "
"your hands. Have a look at the attached sample. There is more where this "
"comes from.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Creo que podríamos llegar a un acuerdo mutuo para quitarte el contrabando "
"de las manos. Echa un vistazo a la muestra adjunta. Hay más de donde viene "
"esto.\""

msgid ""
"\"I need the cargo delivered to the location marked in the {sys} system. The "
"individual there will provide escort.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Necesito que la carga sea entregada en el lugar marcado en el sistema "
"{sys}. El individuo que se encuentra ahí proporcionará la escolta.\""

msgid "The audio playback ends."
msgstr "La reproducción de audio finaliza."

msgid "\"Let us see what we have here…\""
msgstr "\"Veamos lo que tenemos aquí…\""

msgid ""
"They fiddle with the console to access the rest of the contents of the "
"holodrive."
msgstr "Manipula la consola para acceder al resto del contenido del holodisco."

msgid ""
"Suddenly they break out into a chuckle.\n"
"\"Ho-ho-ho, that is mighty interesting, ain't it? Your client must be really "
"interested in getting their hands on them hardware.\"\n"
"Their put away their weapon."
msgstr ""
"De repente suelta una carcajada.\n"
"\"Ho-ho-ho, esto es muy interesante, ¿verdad? Tu cliente debe de estar muy "
"interesado en hacerse con el hardware.\"\n"
"Guarda su arma."

msgid ""
"They gesture towards your burning shoulder.\n"
"\"Let me fix that in a jiffy. Stay still hun.\""
msgstr ""
"Te hace un gesto hacia el hombro ardiendo.\n"
"\"Déjame arreglarte eso en un santiamén. Quédate quieta, cariño.\""

msgid ""
"They approach you and spray your injury with what appears to be some wound "
"sealing spray.\n"
"\"That'll let you get back to your ship. You might want to get it checked up "
"though, or the skin grows back funny. Now back to business!\""
msgstr ""
"Se acerca a ti y rocía tu herida con lo que parece ser un spray sellador de "
"heridas.\n"
"\"Eso te permitirá volver a tu nave. Aunque es posible que quieras que te "
"revisen, o la piel volverá a crecer de forma extraña. ¡Ahora volvamos a los "
"negocios!\""

msgid ""
"\"So I've decided to, umm, carefully think it over, and I thinks we got a "
"deal!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Así que he decidido, umm, pensarlo detenidamente, ¡y creo que tenemos un "
"trato!\""

msgid ""
"\"Them convoy with them parts be at {spob} in the {sys} system. I'll send "
"word about them deal and have them meet you at the spaceport.\""
msgstr ""
"\"La caravana con sus partes estará en {spob} en el sistema {sys}. Enviaré "
"un mensaje sobre el trato y haré que se reúnan contigo en el puerto espacial."
"\""

msgid ""
"\"We'll do our part with them convoy, but it'll be your job to keep it in "
"one piece to {destsys}. Not that I think people gonna be waitin' fer a "
"convoy to that empty place.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Haremos nuestra parte con la caravana, pero será tu trabajo mantenerla de "
"una pieza hasta {destsys}. No creo que la gente espere una caravana a ese "
"lugar vacío.\""

msgid ""
"You feel like you've overstayed your due and head out back to the station to "
"go on with the job."
msgstr ""
"Sientes que te has excedido y te diriges de nuevo a la estación para seguir "
"con el trabajo."

msgid ""
"You don't feel any pain in your shoulder, but it doesn't look too good, but "
"you should recover. At least they didn't aim at your head. Time to get back "
"to your ship before the painkillers wear out."
msgstr ""
"No sientes dolor en el hombro, pero no tiene muy buen aspecto, pero deberías "
"recuperarte. Al menos no te apuntaron a la cabeza. Es hora de volver a tu "
"nave antes de que se te pasen los analgésicos."

msgid "Rendezvous with smugglers at {spob} ({sys})"
msgstr "Reunión con contrabandistas en {spob} ({sys})"

msgid ""
"You land and are quickly greeted by smugglers. They briefly introduce "
"themselves, and say they'll be delivering the promised cargo to the "
"specified location at {sys} before leaving on shuttles. After the formality, "
"they head back to their ships to await your departure."
msgstr ""
"Aterrizas y rápidamente te reciben unos contrabandistas. Se presentan "
"brevemente y dicen que entregarán el cargamento prometido en el lugar "
"especificado en {sys} antes de partir en lanzaderas. Tras la formalidad, "
"regresan a sus naves para esperar tu partida."

msgid "Escort the smugglers to {sys}"
msgstr "Escolta a los contrabandistas a {sys}"

#. If we use "Pirate" it defaults to hostile to the player which can be problematic
msgid "Smugglers"
msgstr "Contrabandistas"

#. less preferred as targets compared to player
#. luacheck: globals escort_success
#. Give order to go to the position when nearby
#. Check if all stopped
msgid "Deal is done, time to scram!"
msgstr "El trato está hecho, ¡es hora de largarse!"

msgid "Return to {spob} ({sys})"
msgstr "Regresa a {spob} ({sys})"

#. Ignore escort stuff now
#. dynamic faction gives no faction hits, good I guess?
#. positions chosen so that hopefully the player doesn't fight them all at once
msgid "Incoming bogies!"
msgstr "¡Enemigos llegando!"

msgid "Almost there! Head to the rendezvous point!"
msgstr "¡Ya casi llegamos! ¡Hacia el punto de encuentro!"

#, fuzzy
msgid "Rendezvous Point"
msgstr "Punto de Encuentro"

#. luacheck: globals escort_failure
msgid "The smuggler ships were all destroyed!"
msgstr "¡Las naves de contrabando han sido todas destruidas!"

msgid "You board the Goddard and find eagerly Scavenger waiting for you."
msgstr "Abordas el Goddard y encuentras a Carroñero ansioso esperándote."

msgid ""
"\"Thank you for bringing the convoy over without a loss. I estimate the "
"probability of that occurring being 3%. All the resources are going to be "
"very useful!\""
msgstr ""
"\"Gracias por traer la caravana sin pérdidas. Estimo que la probabilidad de "
"que eso ocurra es del 3%. ¡Todos los recursos van a ser muy útiles!\""

msgid ""
"\"You managed to bring the convoy over! Do not worry about the convoy "
"losses, they are well within design tolerances.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¡Has conseguido traer la caravana! No te preocupes por las pérdidas de la "
"caravana, están dentro de las tolerancias de diseño.\""

msgid ""
"\"We have already started to bring in the materials. It should not take much "
"longer before they are all here.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ya hemos empezado a traer los materiales. No debería tardar mucho más en "
"estar todo aquí.\""

msgid ""
"\"Now all that is left is to finish the construction and run some "
"preliminary tests. Given our synchronization, I estimate that the "
"construction should be over in a few periods at most.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Ahora sólo queda terminar la construcción y realizar algunas pruebas "
"preliminares. Dada nuestra sincronización, estimo que la construcción "
"debería terminar en unos pocos periodos como máximo.\""

msgid "Ask about what was given to the smuggler."
msgstr "Preguntar sobre lo que se le entregó al contrabandista."

msgid "\"Is this enough for construction?\""
msgstr "\"¿Es esto suficiente para la construcción?\""

msgid ""
"Scavenger seems to do what you can only describe as a chuckle.\n"
"\"Every human has their weakness, and the smuggler was no exception. Some "
"want credits, some want fame, but others want more… special things.\""
msgstr ""
"Carroñero parece hacer lo que sólo se puede describir como una risita.\n"
"\"Cada humano tiene su debilidad, y el contrabandista no era una excepción. "
"Algunos quieren créditos, otros quieren fama, pero otros quieren cosas "
"más... especiales.\""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"They had a weakness for historical documents, many of which we have "
"recovered throughout our existence. We do not have much need for them any "
"more. It is a small price to pay for our freedom.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Tenía debilidad por los documentos históricos, muchos de los cuales hemos "
"recuperado a lo largo de nuestra existencia. Ya no los necesitamos mucho. Es "
"un pequeño precio a pagar por nuestra libertad.\""

msgid ""
"\"The materials should be more than sufficient to finish the hypergate "
"functionality. As it only needs to work once, we can avoid much of the "
"complexities added by reusability.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Los materiales deberían ser más que suficientes para terminar la "
"funcionalidad de la hiperpuerta. Como solo tiene que funcionar una vez, "
"podemos evitar gran parte de las complejidades que añade la reutilización.\""

msgid ""
"\"The construction is already very advanced, I estimate it will take a mean "
"2.981 periods. We are so close that my processor core is almost skipping "
"cycles!\""
msgstr ""
"\"La construcción ya está muy avanzada, estimo que tardará una media de "
"2.981 periodos. ¡Estamos tan cerca que el núcleo de mi procesador casi se "
"salta ciclos!\""

msgid "\"Construction is almost done?\""
msgstr "\"¿La construcción está casi terminada?\""

msgid "\"Slower than I expected!\""
msgstr "\"¡Más lento de lo que esperaba!\""

msgid ""
"\"You have not noticed? The {spob} is the construction. The derelict is "
"being fitted with rudimentary hypergate capabilities. Making usage of the "
"existing infrastructure is much more efficient than building a new structure "
"from scratch.\""
msgstr ""
"\"¿No te has dado cuenta? El {spob} es la construcción. El derrelicto está "
"siendo equipado con capacidades rudimentarias de hiperpuerta. Aprovechar la "
"infraestructura existente es mucho más eficiente que construir una nueva "
"estructura desde cero.\""

msgid ""
"\"I would suggest you adjust your priors. Given our numbers, I do not think "
"it is possible to reduce the construction time without increasing the "
"synchronization ratio over 100%.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Sugeriría que ajusten tus previsiones. Dados nuestros números, no creo que "
"sea posible reducir el tiempo de construcción sin aumentar el ratio de "
"sincronización por encima del 100%.\""

msgid ""
"\"You can leave the construction to us. However, it will take some time "
"until it is completed. You are free to wait aboard your ship, or travel "
"around. We will wait for you to begin our one-way trip.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Puedes dejarnos la construcción a nosotros. Sin embargo, llevará algún "
"tiempo hasta que esté terminada. Eres libre de esperar a bordo de tu nave, o "
"de viajar por los alrededores. Te esperaremos para iniciar nuestro viaje de "
"ida.\""

msgid ""
"\"First, let me give you a reward for your troubles in bringing the supplies "
"over.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Primero, déjame darte una recompensa por tus molestias al traer las "
"provisiones.\""

msgid "What shall you do?"
msgstr "¿Qué vas a hacer?"

msgid "Wait until the construction is finished."
msgstr "Espera a que termine la construcción."

msgid "Leave immediately."
msgstr "Vete inmediatamente."

msgid ""
"You take a well-deserved break and relax on your ship until the Scavenger's "
"construction is complete.\n"
"\n"
"{amount} periods have passed. It is now {date}."
msgstr ""
"Te tomas un merecido descanso y te relajas en tu nave hasta que la "
"construcción de Carroñero esté terminada.\n"
"\n"
"Han pasado {amount} periodos. Ahora es {date}."

msgid ""
"You decide to not wait for the construction to complete, and are ready to go "
"back to space."
msgstr ""
"Decides no esperar a que termine la construcción y estás listo para volver "
"al espacio."

msgid ""
"You managed to convince a smuggler to deliver contraband hypergate "
"components to the inhabitants of Taiomi. The cargo was successfully "
"delivered after you were able to successfully defend it from patrols."
msgstr ""
"Has conseguido convencer a un contrabandista para que entregue componentes "
"de hiperpuerta de contrabando a los habitantes de Taiomi. El cargamento se "
"entregó con éxito después de que consiguieras defenderlo de las patrullas."

